/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 7 — PRELIMINARY DECISION ROUTING LAYER
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Convert overlapping Section 6 rule-trigger flags into one transparent preliminary strategy route.

    Section 7 answers:

        "Based on current simulated strategy triggers, what path should this synthetic applicant be
         routed toward before approved exposure, approved affordability, approved Expected Loss, and
         counteroffer feasibility are evaluated?"

    Section 7 does not answer:

        "What is the final simulated strategy outcome?"

    Section 7 is the route-priority layer.

    It converts many overlapping trigger signals from Section 6 into one preliminary route that
    Section 8 can use for approved-exposure and counteroffer-feasibility evaluation.

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm required Section 7 dependency objects exist.
    2. Read from tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags.
    3. Preserve all prior source, lineage, Module 2 strategy metadata, segmentation, threshold,
       product-policy, and rule-trigger fields.
    4. Create the severe requested-structure diagnostic trigger used by routing.
    5. Apply a transparent preliminary routing hierarchy.
    6. Create:
            preliminary_decision_outcome
            preliminary_decision_path
            preliminary_decision_priority_rank
            preliminary_route_reason_family
            preliminary_route_trigger_count
    7. Create preliminary-only outcome flags:
            preliminary_decline_flag
            preliminary_counteroffer_flag
            preliminary_manual_review_flag
            preliminary_approve_flag
    8. Create exposure-routing flags:
            requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag
            requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag
    9. Validate routing completeness, preliminary flag reconciliation, hierarchy consistency, and
       exposure-routing flag consistency.
    10. Confirm that final decision fields, simulated reason-code fields, and approved-exposure
        economics fields are not created in this section.
    11. Provide local preliminary-routing diagnostics before Section 8 exposure-treatment logic runs.

WHO SHOULD REVIEW THIS SECTION:
    Credit strategy reviewers:
        Confirm that the route-priority hierarchy reflects the intended simulated strategy posture:
        severe policy stops first, severe synthetic estimated-risk and DTI before counteroffer,
        counteroffer feasibility testing before final counteroffer, unresolved severe requested
        structure to review, clean approval only after material triggers have cleared.

    Model governance / validation reviewers:
        Confirm that Section 7 remains preliminary routing only and does not prematurely assign final
        decisions, approved exposure, approved Expected Loss, or reason codes.

    SQL reviewers:
        Confirm that the routing hierarchy is explicit, deterministic, auditable, and enforced with
        local gatekeepers.

    Portfolio / executive reviewers:
        Use Section 7 diagnostics to understand how the rule-trigger population is being directed
        into preliminary route families before final outcome economics are calculated.

WHEN TO RUN THIS SECTION:
    Run Section 7 after:

        Section 6 — Rule Flag Construction Layer

    Section 7 should be run before:

        Section 8 — Approved Exposure and Counteroffer Feasibility Layer

    Section 7 depends on:

        tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags

HOW TO INTERPRET THIS SECTION:
    Passing Section 7 means:
        row count is preserved from Section 6;
        application_id remains unique;
        every row has exactly one preliminary route;
        preliminary flags reconcile to preliminary_decision_outcome;
        the route-priority hierarchy is enforced;
        preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows are marked for counteroffer feasibility testing;
        preliminary APPROVE and preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows are marked for approved-exposure
        calculation;
        and no final outcome / reason-code / approved-exposure fields were created early.

    Passing Section 7 does not mean:
        a final decision has been assigned;
        a counteroffer is feasible;
        approved amount exists;
        approved monthly payment exists;
        approved PTI exists;
        approved Expected Loss exists;
        simulated offer exposure exists;
        reason codes are assigned;
        archive persistence worked;
        or full validation has passed.

INPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags

OUTPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GRAIN:
    One row per application_id for the selected Module 1 scenario / population and active Module 2
    strategy.

PRELIMINARY ROUTING HIERARCHY:
    Priority 1:
        Hard simulated policy stop route.

    Priority 2:
        Severe synthetic estimated-risk route.

    Priority 3:
        Severe DTI capacity route.

    Priority 4:
        Counteroffer feasibility-check route.

    Priority 5:
        Severe requested-structure review route.

    Priority 6:
        Manual-review candidate route.

    Priority 7:
        Clean approval candidate route.

    Priority 8:
        Residual strategy review fallback.

WHY THIS IS PRELIMINARY ROUTING, NOT FINAL DECISIONING:
    Section 6 identifies which simulated policy conditions are triggered.

    Section 7 prioritizes those overlapping triggers into one preliminary route.

    Final decision_outcome is deferred because preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows require Section 8
    approved-exposure and feasibility testing before they can become final COUNTEROFFER outcomes.

WHY COUNTEROFFER FEASIBILITY CANNOT BE FINALIZED HERE:
    A preliminary COUNTEROFFER route only means:

        "This row should be tested for reduced-exposure feasibility."

    It does not mean:
        approved_amount exists,
        counteroffer_amount exists,
        approved monthly payment proxy exists,
        approved PTI exists,
        approved Expected Loss exists,
        or a viable counteroffer has been created.

    Those fields are calculated in later sections.

WHY HARD SIMULATED POLICY STOPS OVERRIDE OTHER TRIGGERS:
    Severe simulated policy-stop conditions are intentionally routed before affordability or exposure
    treatment because they represent high-priority simulated strategy stops in the routing hierarchy.

    Section 7 makes that priority explicit rather than allowing lower-priority triggers to obscure
    severe stop conditions.

WHY SEVERE SYNTHETIC ESTIMATED-RISK IS NOT SOLVED BY EXPOSURE REDUCTION:
    Module 2 V1.0 does not create a post-decision risk model and does not recalculate estimated_pd.

    estimated_pd remains the Module 1 SQL field and is interpreted as the synthetic estimated-PD
    proxy input.

    Severe synthetic estimated-risk is therefore treated as a preliminary no-offer route before
    counteroffer testing.

WHY SEVERE DTI IS TREATED AS EXISTING-OBLIGATION CAPACITY:
    DTI reflects existing-obligation capacity.

    Reducing the requested exposure may improve requested PTI, but it does not directly change the
    synthetic applicant's existing obligations.

    For that reason, severe DTI routes ahead of counteroffer feasibility in Module 2 V1.0.

WHY REQUESTED-STRUCTURE SEVERE STRESS MAY ROUTE TO REVIEW:
    Requested PTI, requested Expected Loss, and requested exposure stress may be addressable through
    exposure treatment in some cases.

    Section 8 has not yet tested that feasibility.

    If a row is not a clean counteroffer candidate and is not routed by a higher-priority simulated
    no-offer condition, unresolved severe requested-structure stress routes to preliminary review.

WHY CLEAN APPROVAL IS STILL PRELIMINARY:
    A clean approval candidate still requires later population of:
        approved_amount,
        approved monthly payment proxy,
        approved PTI,
        approved Expected Loss,
        final decision flags,
        simulated offer-exposure flag,
        and simulated reason codes.

    Section 7 therefore creates preliminary APPROVE routing only, not final APPROVE output.

WHY RESIDUAL CASES ROUTE TO REVIEW:
    Unclassified synthetic profiles should not silently become approvals or declines.

    Residual preliminary review is intentionally conservative and audit-readable.

REQUESTED-STRUCTURE BOUNDARY:
    Severe requested-structure trigger fields are based on requested structure only.

    They use:
        requested_pti_decline_trigger_flag
        requested_el_decline_trigger_flag
        requested_exposure_extreme_flag
        exposure_policy_stop_candidate_flag

    Approved exposure has not yet been calculated.

COUNTEROFFER CANDIDATE BOUNDARY:
    counteroffer_candidate_flag means the row should be tested for reduced-exposure feasibility.

    It does not mean the counteroffer will pass feasibility.

MANUAL REVIEW CANDIDATE BOUNDARY:
    manual_review_candidate_flag means review-oriented trigger evidence exists.

    It does not assign final MANUAL_REVIEW.

CLEAN APPROVAL CANDIDATE BOUNDARY:
    clean_approval_candidate_flag is diagnostic route evidence.

    It does not assign final APPROVE.

REASON-CODE BOUNDARY:
    Section 7 does not assign simulated reason codes.

    It does not create:
        primary_reason_code
        secondary_reason_code
        tertiary_reason_code
        triggered_reason_code_list
        reason_priority_rank
        primary_reason_family
        reason_code_count

APPROVED-EXPOSURE BOUNDARY:
    Section 7 does not calculate:
        approved_amount
        counteroffer_amount
        approved_monthly_payment_proxy
        approved_payment_to_income_ratio
        approved_expected_loss_amount

FINAL OUTCOME BOUNDARY:
    Section 7 does not create:
        decision_outcome
        decision_path
        approval_flag
        decline_flag
        manual_review_flag
        counteroffer_flag
        simulated_offer_exposure_flag

SQL CONCEPTS TAUGHT IN THIS SECTION:
    CTE chain:
        route_inputs
            preserves Section 6 output and adds severe requested-structure diagnostics.

        route_assignment
            applies deterministic preliminary route priority.

        preliminary_flags
            adds preliminary outcome flags and exposure-routing flags.

    CASE hierarchy:
        Encodes the route-priority order.

        The first TRUE route condition wins.

    Boolean route flags:
        Translate preliminary_decision_outcome into downstream processing instructions.

    COUNT and COUNT(DISTINCT):
        Confirm row-count preservation and application_id uniqueness.

    pg_attribute:
        Confirms downstream-only final outcome, reason-code, and approved-exposure fields were not
        created too early.

GOVERNANCE ROLE:
    Section 7 makes the route-priority hierarchy explicit and reviewable.

    It prevents the engine from hiding route logic inside final decision resolution.

COMMON MISUSE TO AVOID:
    Do not interpret preliminary_decision_outcome as final decision_outcome.
    Do not interpret preliminary COUNTEROFFER as a feasible counteroffer.
    Do not interpret preliminary APPROVE as a completed positive offer exposure.
    Do not interpret preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW as completed operational review.
    Do not infer approved exposure, approved PTI, approved Expected Loss, or simulated reason-code
    assignment from Section 7.

TESTING RELEVANCE:
    Section 7 local diagnostics help reviewers verify:
        row-count preservation,
        application_id uniqueness,
        preliminary route coverage,
        preliminary flag reconciliation,
        priority hierarchy behavior,
        counteroffer feasibility routing requirements,
        approved-exposure calculation routing requirements,
        and absence of final outcome / reason-code / approved-exposure fields.

DOWNSTREAM DEPENDENCY:
    Section 8 consumes tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing.

    Section 8 uses:
        requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag
        requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag

    to determine which rows require exposure-treatment evaluation.

***************************************************************************************************/



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 7.0 — SECTION 7 DEPENDENCY PREFLIGHT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that Section 6 rule-trigger output exists and is populated before preliminary routing
    begins.

    Section 7.0 answers:

        "Can Section 7 safely convert Section 6 trigger evidence into preliminary routes?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags exists.
    2. Confirm tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags contains rows.
    3. Confirm application_id is unique before preliminary routing fields are added.
    4. Confirm key Section 6 route-driving fields are populated.
    5. Fail clearly if Section 6 has not been run.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 7.0 does not create preliminary routes.
    Section 7.0 does not assign final outcomes.
    Section 7.0 does not calculate approved exposure.
    Section 7.0 does not assign reason codes.
    Section 7.0 does not modify persistent tables.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_stage3_exists BOOLEAN;
    v_stage3_row_count BIGINT;
    v_stage3_distinct_application_count BIGINT;
    v_required_trigger_gap_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Dependency check: Section 6 rule-trigger stage must exist.

    SQL mechanics:
        TO_REGCLASS checks whether the temporary object exists.

    Business interpretation:
        Section 7 must consume the Section 6 trigger layer, not earlier segmentation or source-stage
        tables.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COALESCE(
        TO_REGCLASS('pg_temp.tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags'),
        TO_REGCLASS('tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags')
    ) IS NOT NULL
    INTO v_stage3_exists;

    IF v_stage3_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags is required. Run Section 6 before Section 7.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: Section 6 rule-trigger stage must contain rows.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage3_row_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags;

    IF v_stage3_row_count <= 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags contains zero rows.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id must be unique before preliminary routing is added.

    Section 7 should add route fields only.

    It should not repair upstream row-grain problems.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_stage3_distinct_application_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags;

    IF v_stage3_distinct_application_count <> v_stage3_row_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags is not unique at application_id. Rows=%, distinct application_id=%.',
            v_stage3_row_count,
            v_stage3_distinct_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: key route-driving Section 6 flags must be populated.

    Business interpretation:
        These are the trigger inputs used directly by the Section 7 route hierarchy.

        NULL values would make route priority ambiguous.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_required_trigger_gap_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags
    WHERE hard_policy_stop_flag IS NULL
       OR synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS NULL
       OR dti_decline_trigger_flag IS NULL
       OR counteroffer_candidate_flag IS NULL
       OR manual_review_candidate_flag IS NULL
       OR clean_approval_candidate_flag IS NULL
       OR requested_pti_decline_trigger_flag IS NULL
       OR requested_el_decline_trigger_flag IS NULL
       OR requested_exposure_extreme_flag IS NULL
       OR exposure_policy_stop_candidate_flag IS NULL
       OR hard_policy_stop_count IS NULL
       OR synthetic_risk_trigger_count IS NULL
       OR dti_trigger_count IS NULL
       OR counteroffer_candidate_trigger_count IS NULL
       OR manual_review_candidate_trigger_count IS NULL;

    IF v_required_trigger_gap_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: % Section 6 row(s) are missing rule-trigger fields required for preliminary routing.',
            v_required_trigger_gap_count;
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 7.1 — CLEAN RESET OF SECTION 7 STAGING OBJECT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Drop the Section 7 preliminary-routing stage before rebuilding it.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Remove only the temporary Section 7 staging table.

WHY THIS MATTERS:
    A partial rerun should not allow stale preliminary-routing rows to remain available to Section 8.

    Section 8 assumes tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing reflects the current:
        Section 6 rule-trigger output,
        active strategy parameter state already carried forward,
        product policy thresholds already carried forward,
        and route-priority hierarchy.

SQL MECHANICS:
    DROP TABLE IF EXISTS makes the reset rerunnable.

    If the table does not exist, PostgreSQL does not error.

BOUNDARY:
    This drop affects only the temporary Section 7 staging object.

    It does not modify Module 1 outputs.
    It does not modify Module 2 latest-run output.
    It does not modify Module 2 archive output.
    It does not modify evidence tables.
    It does not modify registry tables.

****************************************************************************************************/

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 7.2 — CREATE PRELIMINARY DECISION ROUTING TABLE
****************************************************************************************************

TABLE:
    tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GRAIN:
    One row per application_id for the selected Module 1 scenario / population and active Module 2
    strategy.

INPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags

OUTPUT:
    All Section 6 fields plus preliminary-routing fields only.

FIELDS CREATED:
    severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag
    severe_requested_structure_trigger_count

    preliminary_decision_outcome
    preliminary_decision_path
    preliminary_decision_priority_rank
    preliminary_route_reason_family
    preliminary_route_trigger_count

    preliminary_decline_flag
    preliminary_counteroffer_flag
    preliminary_manual_review_flag
    preliminary_approve_flag

    requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag
    requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag

SQL DESIGN:
    This section uses a short CTE chain so the routing process is readable and reviewable.

    The chain is:

        route_inputs
            preserves Section 6 output and adds severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag.

        route_assignment
            applies the preliminary routing hierarchy.

        preliminary_flags
            adds preliminary outcome flags and exposure-routing flags.

WHY SELECT * IS ACCEPTABLE HERE:
    This is a temporary staging layer, not a permanent output table.

    Section 7 intentionally preserves all prior fields plus preliminary-routing diagnostics for
    Section 8 exposure treatment.

    Permanent output selection is handled later with an explicit field list in Section 11.

***************************************************************************************************/

CREATE TEMP TABLE tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing
ON COMMIT PRESERVE ROWS
AS
WITH route_inputs AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: route_inputs

    Purpose:
        Preserve all Section 6 rule-trigger fields and create severe requested-structure diagnostics.

    Why this CTE exists:
        Section 6 creates individual trigger families.

        Section 7 needs a compact route-driving signal for unresolved severe requested-structure
        pressure that is not already counteroffer-eligible and not already routed by higher-priority
        no-offer conditions.

    Credit risk interpretation:
        Severe requested-structure pressure includes severe requested PTI, severe requested Expected
        Loss, extreme requested exposure, and requested exposure policy-stop candidacy.

        These are based on requested structure, not approved exposure.

        Section 8 has not yet calculated whether reduced exposure can solve any of these pressures.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        rf.*,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag.

        TRUE when any severe requested-structure pressure indicator is active.

        This is not a final decision.
        It is a route-priority input.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (
            rf.requested_pti_decline_trigger_flag
            OR rf.requested_el_decline_trigger_flag
            OR rf.requested_exposure_extreme_flag
            OR rf.exposure_policy_stop_candidate_flag
        ) AS severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        severe_requested_structure_trigger_count.

        Counts the number of severe requested-structure pressure indicators.

        This count supports route interpretation and later reason-code transparency.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (
            rf.requested_pti_decline_trigger_flag::INT
            + rf.requested_el_decline_trigger_flag::INT
            + rf.requested_exposure_extreme_flag::INT
            + rf.exposure_policy_stop_candidate_flag::INT
        ) AS severe_requested_structure_trigger_count

    FROM tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags rf
),

route_assignment AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: route_assignment

    Purpose:
        Apply the deterministic preliminary routing hierarchy.

    SQL mechanics:
        CASE evaluates from top to bottom.
        The first TRUE condition wins.

    Business interpretation:
        This converts overlapping trigger evidence into one preliminary route.

    Boundary:
        These preliminary route labels are not final decision outcomes.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        ri.*,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        preliminary_decision_outcome.

        Allowed preliminary values:
            APPROVE
            COUNTEROFFER
            MANUAL_REVIEW
            DECLINE

        Important:
            These are preliminary route labels only.

            Final decision_outcome is created later after approved exposure, approved PTI, approved
            Expected Loss, and counteroffer feasibility have been resolved.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ri.hard_policy_stop_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'DECLINE'

            WHEN ri.synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'DECLINE'

            WHEN ri.dti_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'DECLINE'

            WHEN ri.counteroffer_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER'

            WHEN ri.severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS TRUE
             AND ri.counteroffer_candidate_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                THEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.manual_review_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.clean_approval_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'APPROVE'

            ELSE 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
        END AS preliminary_decision_outcome,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        preliminary_decision_path.

        This is the route-path label explaining which hierarchy branch assigned the preliminary
        outcome.

        It supports:
            Section 8 exposure-treatment interpretation;
            Section 9 final decision resolution;
            Section 10 reason-code assignment;
            Section 14 QA diagnostics.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ri.hard_policy_stop_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'HARD_POLICY_STOP'

            WHEN ri.synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'SEVERE_SYNTHETIC_RISK'

            WHEN ri.dti_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'SEVERE_DTI_CAPACITY'

            WHEN ri.counteroffer_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBILITY_CHECK'

            WHEN ri.severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS TRUE
             AND ri.counteroffer_candidate_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                THEN 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_STRUCTURE_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.manual_review_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW_CANDIDATE'

            WHEN ri.clean_approval_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'CLEAN_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE'

            ELSE 'RESIDUAL_STRATEGY_REVIEW'
        END AS preliminary_decision_path,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        preliminary_decision_priority_rank.

        Lower rank = higher routing priority.

        This is a route-priority diagnostic, not a final decision severity score.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ri.hard_policy_stop_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 1

            WHEN ri.synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 2

            WHEN ri.dti_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 3

            WHEN ri.counteroffer_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 4

            WHEN ri.severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS TRUE
             AND ri.counteroffer_candidate_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                THEN 5

            WHEN ri.manual_review_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 6

            WHEN ri.clean_approval_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 7

            ELSE 8
        END AS preliminary_decision_priority_rank,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        preliminary_route_reason_family.

        This family label groups preliminary route paths into broad interpretive families.

        These are not final reason-code families.
        Final simulated reason-code families are assigned in Section 10.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ri.hard_policy_stop_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'POLICY_STOP'

            WHEN ri.synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'POLICY_STOP'

            WHEN ri.dti_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'POLICY_STOP'

            WHEN ri.counteroffer_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER'

            WHEN ri.severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS TRUE
             AND ri.counteroffer_candidate_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                THEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.manual_review_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.clean_approval_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'APPROVAL'

            ELSE 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
        END AS preliminary_route_reason_family,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        preliminary_route_trigger_count.

        Counts the trigger dimensions most directly associated with the selected route.

        This is not total_rule_trigger_count.

        It is a route-specific diagnostic count that helps explain why the route was selected.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ri.hard_policy_stop_flag IS TRUE
                THEN ri.hard_policy_stop_count

            WHEN ri.synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
                THEN ri.synthetic_risk_trigger_count

            WHEN ri.dti_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
                THEN ri.dti_trigger_count

            WHEN ri.counteroffer_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN ri.counteroffer_candidate_trigger_count

            WHEN ri.severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS TRUE
             AND ri.counteroffer_candidate_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                THEN ri.severe_requested_structure_trigger_count

            WHEN ri.manual_review_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN ri.manual_review_candidate_trigger_count

            WHEN ri.clean_approval_candidate_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 0

            ELSE 0
        END AS preliminary_route_trigger_count

    FROM route_inputs ri
),

preliminary_flags AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: preliminary_flags

    Purpose:
        Create preliminary outcome flags and downstream exposure-routing flags.

    Boundary:
        These are preliminary flags only.

        Final decision flags are created in Section 9.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        ra.*,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Preliminary outcome flags.

        Exactly one should be TRUE per row.

        These flags are used for staging diagnostics and do not represent final outcomes.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (ra.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE')
            AS preliminary_decline_flag,

        (ra.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
            AS preliminary_counteroffer_flag,

        (ra.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW')
            AS preliminary_manual_review_flag,

        (ra.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE')
            AS preliminary_approve_flag,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag.

        TRUE only for preliminary COUNTEROFFER.

        Meaning:
            Section 8 should test whether reduced-exposure treatment is feasible.

        Boundary:
            This does not mean the counteroffer is feasible.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (ra.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
            AS requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag.

        TRUE for preliminary APPROVE and preliminary COUNTEROFFER.

        APPROVE:
            requires as-requested approved exposure calculation later.

        COUNTEROFFER:
            requires reduced-exposure feasibility and approved exposure calculation later.

        MANUAL_REVIEW / DECLINE:
            do not require approved exposure calculation at this stage.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (ra.preliminary_decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER'))
            AS requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag

    FROM route_assignment ra
)

SELECT *
FROM preliminary_flags;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 7.3 — LOCAL FAIL-FAST CHECKS FOR PRELIMINARY DECISION ROUTING
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that preliminary routing is complete, internally consistent, and still within the
    preliminary-routing boundary before Section 8 creates exposure-treatment fields.

    Section 7.3 answers:

        "Did Section 7 preserve applicant grain, assign exactly one preliminary route, enforce the
         route hierarchy, and avoid creating final outcome / reason-code / approved-exposure fields?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm row count is unchanged from tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags.
    2. Confirm application_id remains unique.
    3. Confirm preliminary routing fields are complete and valid.
    4. Confirm exactly one preliminary outcome flag is TRUE per row.
    5. Confirm preliminary outcome flags reconcile to preliminary_decision_outcome.
    6. Confirm the route hierarchy is enforced.
    7. Confirm counteroffer and approved-exposure routing flags are consistent.
    8. Confirm final decision, reason-code, and approved-exposure fields were not created.

LOCAL GATEKEEPER BOUNDARY:
    These are local Section 7 staging gatekeepers only.

    They are not:
        final decision validation,
        reason-code validation,
        approved-exposure validation,
        archive validation,
        matched strategy comparison,
        full Module 2 QA,
        strategy frontier review,
        or Validation Summary evidence by themselves.

SQL MECHANICS:
    This block uses PL/pgSQL because it needs multiple diagnostic counts and fail-fast exceptions.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Row-grain diagnostics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    v_stage3_count BIGINT;
    v_stage4_count BIGINT;
    v_stage4_distinct_app_count BIGINT;
    v_duplicate_application_count BIGINT;

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Preliminary routing diagnostics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    v_preliminary_completeness_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_preliminary_flag_reconciliation_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_priority_hierarchy_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_feasibility_flag_failure_count BIGINT;

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Section boundary diagnostic.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    v_forbidden_column_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: row count must be unchanged from Section 6 to Section 7.

    Business purpose:
        Section 7 should add preliminary-routing fields only.

        It should not filter applicants or duplicate applicants.

    SQL mechanics:
        Compare Stage 3 row count to Stage 4 row count.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage3_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags;

    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage4_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing;

    IF v_stage4_count <> v_stage3_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: row count changed from Section 6 to Section 7. Stage 3 rows: %, Stage 4 rows: %.',
            v_stage3_count,
            v_stage4_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id remains unique.

    Business purpose:
        Duplicate application_id values would duplicate downstream exposure-treatment calculations,
        final decisions, approved exposure, Expected Loss, and reason-code counts.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_stage4_distinct_app_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing;

    IF v_stage4_distinct_app_count <> v_stage4_count THEN
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_duplicate_application_count
        FROM (
            SELECT application_id
            FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing
            GROUP BY application_id
            HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
        ) d;

        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: application_id uniqueness was not preserved. Stage 4 rows: %, distinct application_id count: %, duplicate application_id group count: %.',
            v_stage4_count,
            v_stage4_distinct_app_count,
            v_duplicate_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: preliminary routing fields must be complete and valid.

    Required preliminary routing fields:
        preliminary_decision_outcome,
        preliminary_decision_path,
        preliminary_decision_priority_rank,
        preliminary_route_reason_family,
        preliminary_route_trigger_count,
        severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag,
        severe_requested_structure_trigger_count.

    Business interpretation:
        Every row should have one explainable preliminary route before exposure treatment begins.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_preliminary_completeness_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing
    WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome IS NULL
       OR preliminary_decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
       OR preliminary_decision_path IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(preliminary_decision_path), '') IS NULL
       OR preliminary_decision_priority_rank IS NULL
       OR preliminary_decision_priority_rank < 1
       OR preliminary_route_reason_family IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(preliminary_route_reason_family), '') IS NULL
       OR preliminary_route_trigger_count IS NULL
       OR preliminary_route_trigger_count < 0
       OR severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS NULL
       OR severe_requested_structure_trigger_count IS NULL
       OR severe_requested_structure_trigger_count < 0;

    IF v_preliminary_completeness_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: % row(s) have incomplete or invalid preliminary routing fields.',
            v_preliminary_completeness_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: preliminary outcome flags must reconcile to preliminary_decision_outcome.

    Expected:
        exactly one preliminary flag is TRUE per row.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_preliminary_flag_reconciliation_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing
    WHERE
        (
            COALESCE(preliminary_decline_flag::INT, 0)
            + COALESCE(preliminary_counteroffer_flag::INT, 0)
            + COALESCE(preliminary_manual_review_flag::INT, 0)
            + COALESCE(preliminary_approve_flag::INT, 0)
        ) <> 1
       OR preliminary_decline_flag
          IS DISTINCT FROM (preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE')
       OR preliminary_counteroffer_flag
          IS DISTINCT FROM (preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
       OR preliminary_manual_review_flag
          IS DISTINCT FROM (preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW')
       OR preliminary_approve_flag
          IS DISTINCT FROM (preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE');

    IF v_preliminary_flag_reconciliation_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: % row(s) have preliminary flag reconciliation failures.',
            v_preliminary_flag_reconciliation_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: priority hierarchy enforcement.

    This validates the accepted preliminary routing hierarchy without forcing mutual exclusivity
    across underlying rule-trigger families.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_priority_hierarchy_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing
    WHERE
        /* Priority 1: hard policy stop. */
        (
            hard_policy_stop_flag IS TRUE
            AND NOT (
                preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                AND preliminary_decision_path = 'HARD_POLICY_STOP'
                AND preliminary_decision_priority_rank = 1
            )
        )

        OR

        /* Priority 2: severe synthetic estimated-risk after no hard stop. */
        (
            hard_policy_stop_flag IS FALSE
            AND synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
            AND NOT (
                preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                AND preliminary_decision_path = 'SEVERE_SYNTHETIC_RISK'
                AND preliminary_decision_priority_rank = 2
            )
        )

        OR

        /* Priority 3: severe DTI after no higher-priority decline route. */
        (
            hard_policy_stop_flag IS FALSE
            AND synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND dti_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
            AND NOT (
                preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                AND preliminary_decision_path = 'SEVERE_DTI_CAPACITY'
                AND preliminary_decision_priority_rank = 3
            )
        )

        OR

        /* Priority 4: counteroffer candidate after no higher-priority decline route. */
        (
            hard_policy_stop_flag IS FALSE
            AND synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND dti_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND counteroffer_candidate_flag IS TRUE
            AND NOT (
                preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                AND preliminary_decision_path = 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBILITY_CHECK'
                AND preliminary_decision_priority_rank = 4
            )
        )

        OR

        /* Priority 5: severe requested-structure review when not counteroffer-eligible. */
        (
            hard_policy_stop_flag IS FALSE
            AND synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND dti_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND counteroffer_candidate_flag IS FALSE
            AND severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS TRUE
            AND NOT (
                preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                AND preliminary_decision_path = 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_STRUCTURE_REVIEW'
                AND preliminary_decision_priority_rank = 5
            )
        )

        OR

        /* Priority 6: manual-review candidate after higher routes are cleared. */
        (
            hard_policy_stop_flag IS FALSE
            AND synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND dti_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND counteroffer_candidate_flag IS FALSE
            AND severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND manual_review_candidate_flag IS TRUE
            AND NOT (
                preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                AND preliminary_decision_path = 'MANUAL_REVIEW_CANDIDATE'
                AND preliminary_decision_priority_rank = 6
            )
        )

        OR

        /* Priority 7: clean approval candidate after higher routes are cleared. */
        (
            hard_policy_stop_flag IS FALSE
            AND synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND dti_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND counteroffer_candidate_flag IS FALSE
            AND severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND manual_review_candidate_flag IS FALSE
            AND clean_approval_candidate_flag IS TRUE
            AND NOT (
                preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                AND preliminary_decision_path = 'CLEAN_APPROVAL_CANDIDATE'
                AND preliminary_decision_priority_rank = 7
            )
        )

        OR

        /* Priority 8: residual strategy review fallback. */
        (
            hard_policy_stop_flag IS FALSE
            AND synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND dti_decline_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND counteroffer_candidate_flag IS FALSE
            AND severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS FALSE
            AND manual_review_candidate_flag IS FALSE
            AND clean_approval_candidate_flag IS FALSE
            AND NOT (
                preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                AND preliminary_decision_path = 'RESIDUAL_STRATEGY_REVIEW'
                AND preliminary_decision_priority_rank = 8
            )
        );

    IF v_priority_hierarchy_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: % row(s) violate preliminary route-priority hierarchy.',
            v_priority_hierarchy_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: exposure and counteroffer feasibility routing flags.

    Expected:
        requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag = TRUE only for preliminary COUNTEROFFER.

        requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag = TRUE for preliminary APPROVE and preliminary
        COUNTEROFFER.

        requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag = FALSE for preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW and
        preliminary DECLINE.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_feasibility_flag_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing
    WHERE (
            preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
    )
    OR (
            preliminary_decision_outcome <> 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
    )
    OR (
            preliminary_decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER')
            AND requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
    )
    OR (
            preliminary_decision_outcome IN ('DECLINE', 'MANUAL_REVIEW')
            AND requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
    );

    IF v_feasibility_flag_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: % row(s) have exposure / counteroffer feasibility routing flag failures.',
            v_feasibility_flag_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: Section 7 must not create final decision, reason-code, or approved-exposure fields.

    Exact column-name checks are used.

    Preliminary fields are allowed.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_forbidden_column_count
    FROM pg_attribute
    WHERE attrelid = 'tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing'::REGCLASS
      AND attnum > 0
      AND NOT attisdropped
      AND attname IN (
            'decision_outcome',
            'decision_path',
            'approval_flag',
            'decline_flag',
            'manual_review_flag',
            'counteroffer_flag',
            'simulated_offer_exposure_flag',

            'primary_reason_code',
            'secondary_reason_code',
            'tertiary_reason_code',
            'triggered_reason_code_list',
            'reason_priority_rank',
            'primary_reason_family',
            'reason_code_count',

            'approved_amount',
            'counteroffer_amount',
            'approved_monthly_payment_proxy',
            'approved_payment_to_income_ratio',
            'approved_expected_loss_amount'
      );

    IF v_forbidden_column_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 7 failure: forbidden final decision, reason-code, or approved-exposure field(s) were created in preliminary routing stage.';
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 7.4 — LOCAL PRELIMINARY ROUTING SANITY CHECKS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide lightweight diagnostics for the Section 7 preliminary routing layer.

    Section 7.4 answers:

        "What preliminary routes did Section 7 assign, and does the route distribution look ready for
         Section 8 exposure-treatment logic?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    Display review outputs for:
        preliminary outcome distribution,
        preliminary path distribution,
        preliminary priority-rank distribution,
        preliminary route-family distribution,
        product × preliminary outcome,
        score band × preliminary outcome,
        requested PTI bucket × preliminary outcome,
        synthetic risk tier × preliminary outcome,
        requested exposure tier × preliminary outcome,
        requested Expected Loss tier × preliminary outcome,
        mixed-signal profile × preliminary outcome,
        borderline profile × preliminary outcome,
        hard policy stop × preliminary outcome,
        synthetic-risk decline trigger × preliminary outcome,
        DTI decline trigger × preliminary outcome,
        counteroffer candidate × preliminary outcome,
        manual-review candidate × preliminary outcome,
        clean approval candidate × preliminary outcome,
        counteroffer feasibility routing flag × preliminary outcome,
        approved exposure routing flag × preliminary outcome,
        and one compact readiness summary.

INTERPRETATION:
    These are staging diagnostics only.

    They should not be interpreted as:
        final strategy validation,
        final decision distribution,
        reason-code coverage,
        approved-exposure validation,
        archive validation,
        matched strategy comparison,
        strategy frontier evidence,
        or Validation Summary acceptance.

SQL TEACHING POINT:
    These SELECT statements are read-only diagnostics.

    GROUP BY summarizes how the route hierarchy distributed the population.

    AVG fields help reviewers understand whether the preliminary route is directionally coherent with
    the underlying risk, affordability, or exposure values.

****************************************************************************************************/



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.1 Count by preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Show the population distribution across the four preliminary route outcomes.

Expected:
    Each row should have exactly one preliminary outcome.

Boundary:
    preliminary_decision_outcome is not final decision_outcome.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    preliminary_decision_outcome,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.2 Count by preliminary_decision_path.

Purpose:
    Show which preliminary route labels are active before approved-exposure feasibility is tested.

Interpretation:
    This is the clearest early read of the route hierarchy.

Boundary:
    preliminary_decision_path is not final decision_path.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    preliminary_decision_path,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY preliminary_decision_path

ORDER BY preliminary_decision_path;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.3 Count by preliminary_decision_priority_rank.

Purpose:
    Show route-priority distribution.

Interpretation:
    Lower rank means higher-priority preliminary route.

    This query helps reviewers see how much of the population is being routed by severe stop
    conditions versus counteroffer feasibility, manual review, clean approval, or residual review.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    preliminary_decision_priority_rank,
    preliminary_decision_path,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    preliminary_decision_priority_rank,
    preliminary_decision_path

ORDER BY
    preliminary_decision_priority_rank,
    preliminary_decision_path;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.4 Count by preliminary_route_reason_family.

Purpose:
    Show broad preliminary route-family distribution.

Boundary:
    preliminary_route_reason_family is not final primary_reason_family.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    preliminary_route_reason_family,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY preliminary_route_reason_family

ORDER BY preliminary_route_reason_family;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.5 Product × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Show how preliminary route outcomes distribute by product.

Interpretation:
    Product route concentrations may reflect product-specific exposure, affordability, Expected Loss,
    and counteroffer constraints.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    product_type_policy_key,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.6 Score band × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review whether preliminary routes align directionally with borrower-quality segmentation.

Boundary:
    Score band is not the final decision.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    score_band_policy_key,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(credit_score) AS avg_credit_score,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    score_band_policy_key,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE score_band_policy_key
        WHEN 'SUPER_PRIME' THEN 1
        WHEN 'PRIME' THEN 2
        WHEN 'NEAR_PRIME' THEN 3
        WHEN 'SUBPRIME' THEN 4
        WHEN 'DEEP_SUBPRIME' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.7 Requested PTI bucket × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review how requested affordability pressure maps into preliminary route assignment.

Boundary:
    This is requested PTI, not approved PTI.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    requested_pti_bucket,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(affordability_trigger_count) AS avg_affordability_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    requested_pti_bucket,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE requested_pti_bucket
        WHEN 'LOW_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.8 Synthetic risk tier × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review how synthetic estimated-risk tier maps into preliminary route assignment.

Boundary:
    estimated_pd is interpreted as the synthetic estimated-PD proxy.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    strategy_risk_tier,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(synthetic_risk_trigger_count) AS avg_synthetic_risk_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    strategy_risk_tier,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE strategy_risk_tier
        WHEN 'LOW_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.9 Requested exposure tier × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review how requested exposure intensity maps into preliminary route assignment.

Boundary:
    Requested exposure is not approved exposure.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    requested_exposure_tier,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(exposure_trigger_count) AS avg_exposure_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    requested_exposure_tier,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE requested_exposure_tier
        WHEN 'BELOW_PRODUCT_MINIMUM' THEN 1
        WHEN 'LOW_REQUESTED_EXPOSURE' THEN 2
        WHEN 'WITHIN_PRODUCT_APPROVAL_CAP' THEN 3
        WHEN 'WITHIN_PRODUCT_LIMITS' THEN 4
        WHEN 'ABOVE_PRODUCT_APPROVAL_CAP' THEN 5
        WHEN 'EXTREME_REQUESTED_EXPOSURE' THEN 6
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.10 Requested Expected Loss tier × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review how requested-exposure Expected Loss tier maps into preliminary routing.

Boundary:
    requested_expected_loss_amount is requested-exposure Expected Loss.

    approved_expected_loss_amount does not exist yet.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    requested_expected_loss_tier,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(requested_el_trigger_count) AS avg_requested_el_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    requested_expected_loss_tier,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE requested_expected_loss_tier
        WHEN 'LOW_REQUESTED_EL' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_REQUESTED_EL' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_REQUESTED_EL' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_REQUESTED_EL' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_EL' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.11 Mixed-signal profile × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review how realistic overlapping profiles route before exposure treatment.

Interpretation:
    Mixed-signal profiles are diagnostic and may route differently depending on which trigger family
    wins the preliminary hierarchy.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    mixed_signal_profile_type,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(mixed_signal_condition_count) AS avg_mixed_signal_condition_count,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    mixed_signal_profile_type,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    mixed_signal_profile_type,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.12 Borderline profile × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review how threshold-adjacent profiles route before final outcome assignment.

Boundary:
    borderline_profile_flag is diagnostic only.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    borderline_profile_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    borderline_profile_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    borderline_profile_flag,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.13 Hard policy stop × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Confirm hard simulated policy stops route to preliminary DECLINE.

Expected:
    hard_policy_stop_flag = TRUE should appear only with preliminary DECLINE.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    hard_policy_stop_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(hard_policy_stop_count) AS avg_hard_policy_stop_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    hard_policy_stop_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    hard_policy_stop_flag,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.14 Synthetic-risk decline trigger × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Confirm severe synthetic estimated-risk routes to preliminary DECLINE unless a higher-priority
    hard policy stop already routed it.

Expected:
    synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag = TRUE should appear only with preliminary DECLINE.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.15 DTI decline trigger × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Confirm severe DTI routes to preliminary DECLINE unless a higher-priority hard policy stop or
    synthetic-risk decline route already applies.

Expected:
    dti_decline_trigger_flag = TRUE should appear only with preliminary DECLINE.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    dti_decline_trigger_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(debt_to_income_ratio) AS avg_debt_to_income_ratio

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    dti_decline_trigger_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    dti_decline_trigger_flag,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.16 Counteroffer candidate × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Confirm counteroffer_candidate_flag routes to preliminary COUNTEROFFER when no higher-priority
    preliminary DECLINE route applies.

Boundary:
    preliminary COUNTEROFFER still requires Section 8 feasibility testing.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    counteroffer_candidate_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(counteroffer_candidate_trigger_count) AS avg_counteroffer_candidate_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    counteroffer_candidate_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    counteroffer_candidate_flag,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.17 Manual-review candidate × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review how manual-review candidate triggers route after higher-priority stop and counteroffer
    routes have been applied.

Boundary:
    preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW is not final MANUAL_REVIEW.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    manual_review_candidate_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(manual_review_candidate_trigger_count) AS avg_manual_review_candidate_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    manual_review_candidate_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    manual_review_candidate_flag,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.18 Clean approval candidate × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Confirm clean approval candidates route to preliminary APPROVE only after higher-priority route
    conditions are cleared.

Boundary:
    preliminary APPROVE is not final APPROVE.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    clean_approval_candidate_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    clean_approval_candidate_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    clean_approval_candidate_flag,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.19 requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Confirm counteroffer feasibility routing flag behavior.

Expected:
    requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag = TRUE only for preliminary COUNTEROFFER.

Boundary:
    This does not mean the counteroffer is feasible.

    It means Section 8 should test feasibility.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.20 requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag × preliminary_decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Confirm approved-exposure calculation routing flag behavior.

Expected:
    TRUE for preliminary APPROVE and preliminary COUNTEROFFER.

    FALSE for preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW and preliminary DECLINE.

Boundary:
    This flag tells Section 8 which rows need approved-exposure calculations.

    It does not calculate approved exposure in Section 7.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

GROUP BY
    requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag,
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.4.21 Section 7 readiness summary.

Purpose:
    Provide one compact readiness row for the preliminary-routing stage.

Expected:
    section_7_preliminary_routing_status =
        SECTION_7_PRELIMINARY_ROUTING_READY_FOR_EXPOSURE_TREATMENT

Interpretation:
    This confirms only that Section 7 is ready for Section 8.

    It does not validate final strategy outcomes.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH routing_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS stage4_row_count,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome IS NULL
               OR preliminary_decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
               OR preliminary_decision_path IS NULL
               OR preliminary_decision_priority_rank IS NULL
               OR preliminary_route_reason_family IS NULL
               OR preliminary_route_trigger_count IS NULL
        ) AS preliminary_routing_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE (
                    COALESCE(preliminary_decline_flag::INT, 0)
                    + COALESCE(preliminary_counteroffer_flag::INT, 0)
                    + COALESCE(preliminary_manual_review_flag::INT, 0)
                    + COALESCE(preliminary_approve_flag::INT, 0)
                  ) <> 1
        ) AS preliminary_flag_reconciliation_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
        ) AS counteroffer_feasibility_flag_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome <> 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
        ) AS counteroffer_feasibility_false_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER')
              AND requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
        ) AS approved_exposure_calc_true_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome IN ('DECLINE', 'MANUAL_REVIEW')
              AND requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
        ) AS approved_exposure_calc_false_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
        ) AS preliminary_approve_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS preliminary_counteroffer_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
        ) AS preliminary_manual_review_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
        ) AS preliminary_decline_rows,

        AVG(preliminary_route_trigger_count) AS avg_preliminary_route_trigger_count

    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing
)

SELECT
    stage4_row_count,
    distinct_application_id_count,

    preliminary_routing_gap_rows,
    preliminary_flag_reconciliation_gap_rows,
    counteroffer_feasibility_flag_gap_rows,
    counteroffer_feasibility_false_gap_rows,
    approved_exposure_calc_true_gap_rows,
    approved_exposure_calc_false_gap_rows,

    preliminary_approve_rows,
    preliminary_counteroffer_rows,
    preliminary_manual_review_rows,
    preliminary_decline_rows,

    avg_preliminary_route_trigger_count,

    CASE
        WHEN stage4_row_count > 0
         AND stage4_row_count = distinct_application_id_count
         AND preliminary_routing_gap_rows = 0
         AND preliminary_flag_reconciliation_gap_rows = 0
         AND counteroffer_feasibility_flag_gap_rows = 0
         AND counteroffer_feasibility_false_gap_rows = 0
         AND approved_exposure_calc_true_gap_rows = 0
         AND approved_exposure_calc_false_gap_rows = 0
            THEN 'SECTION_7_PRELIMINARY_ROUTING_READY_FOR_EXPOSURE_TREATMENT'
        ELSE 'REVIEW_SECTION_7_PRELIMINARY_ROUTING_BEFORE_EXPOSURE_TREATMENT'
    END AS section_7_preliminary_routing_status

FROM routing_summary;



/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 7 — PRELIMINARY DECISION ROUTING LAYER

If execution reaches this point:
    1. Section 7 dependency preflight passed.
    2. tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing exists.
    3. Row count is unchanged from tmp_m2_stage_3_rule_flags.
    4. application_id remains unique.
    5. Module 1 lineage remains preserved.
    6. Module 2 strategy metadata remains preserved.
    7. All Section 6 rule flags remain preserved.
    8. severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag is populated.
    9. severe_requested_structure_trigger_count is populated.
    10. preliminary_decision_outcome is populated for every row.
    11. preliminary_decision_outcome is one of APPROVE, COUNTEROFFER, MANUAL_REVIEW, DECLINE.
    12. preliminary_decision_path is populated.
    13. preliminary_decision_priority_rank is populated.
    14. preliminary_route_reason_family is populated.
    15. preliminary_route_trigger_count is populated.
    16. Exactly one preliminary outcome flag is TRUE per row.
    17. hard_policy_stop_flag routes to preliminary DECLINE.
    18. Severe synthetic estimated-risk routes to preliminary DECLINE unless hard policy stop already
        routed it.
    19. Severe DTI routes to preliminary DECLINE unless a higher-priority route already routed it.
    20. counteroffer_candidate_flag routes to preliminary COUNTEROFFER when no higher-priority
        decline route applies.
    21. Severe requested-structure stress routes to preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW when not already
        counteroffer-eligible and no higher-priority route applies.
    22. manual_review_candidate_flag routes to preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW after higher-priority
        routes are cleared.
    23. clean_approval_candidate_flag routes to preliminary APPROVE after material route triggers are
        cleared.
    24. Residual cases route to preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW.
    25. requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag is TRUE only for preliminary COUNTEROFFER.
    26. requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag is TRUE only for preliminary APPROVE and
        preliminary COUNTEROFFER.
    27. No final decision, final reason-code, or approved-exposure fields were created.
    28. Section 7 local preliminary-routing diagnostics are available for review.

Section 7 established:
    1. The deterministic preliminary route-priority layer.
    2. Severe-policy-stop routing.
    3. Severe synthetic estimated-risk routing.
    4. Severe DTI routing.
    5. Counteroffer feasibility-check routing.
    6. Severe requested-structure review routing.
    7. Manual-review candidate routing.
    8. Clean approval candidate routing.
    9. Residual strategy review routing.
    10. Exposure-treatment routing flags for Section 8.

No final decision_outcome has been created.
No final decision_path has been created.
No final approval / decline / manual review / counteroffer flags have been created.
No simulated_offer_exposure_flag has been created.
No simulated reason codes have been assigned.
No approved_amount has been calculated.
No counteroffer_amount has been calculated.
No approved payment proxy has been calculated.
No approved payment-to-income ratio has been calculated.
No approved Expected Loss has been calculated.
No latest-run strategy decision output has been created.
No strategy archive rows have been inserted.
No evidence rows have been inserted.
No matched comparison has been performed.
No strategy frontier has been calculated.
No full QA framework has been built.

Next section:
    Section 8 should consume tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing and calculate approved
    exposure treatment, approved payment proxy, approved PTI, approved Expected Loss, and
    counteroffer feasibility diagnostics.

***************************************************************************************************/


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 8 — APPROVED EXPOSURE AND COUNTEROFFER FEASIBILITY LAYER
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Calculate preliminary approved-exposure economics and counteroffer feasibility after preliminary
    routing has identified which rows require exposure treatment.

    Section 8 answers:

        "Given the preliminary route, what approved exposure treatment would be economically and
         structurally feasible?"

    Section 8 does not answer:

        "What is the final simulated strategy outcome?"

    This section is the exposure-treatment layer.

    It converts preliminary routing into preliminary approved exposure, preliminary approved payment,
    preliminary approved PTI, preliminary approved Expected Loss, and counteroffer feasibility
    diagnostics.

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm required Section 8 dependency objects exist.
    2. Read from tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing.
    3. Preserve all prior source, lineage, Module 2 strategy metadata, segmentation, rule-trigger,
       and preliminary routing fields.
    4. Calculate preliminary approved exposure treatment by preliminary route.
    5. Evaluate reduced-exposure counteroffer feasibility for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    6. Calculate preliminary approved payment proxy and preliminary approved PTI only where
       appropriate.
    7. Calculate preliminary approved Expected Loss only where appropriate.
    8. Preserve failed counteroffers as unresolved for later final decision resolution.
    9. Validate exposure-treatment conventions and feasibility logic.
    10. Confirm that final decision fields and simulated reason-code fields are not created yet.
    11. Provide local exposure-treatment diagnostics before Section 9 final decision resolution.

WHO SHOULD REVIEW THIS SECTION:
    Credit strategy reviewers:
        Confirm that exposure treatment, counteroffer feasibility, product caps, PTI targets,
        approved Expected Loss caps, minimum counteroffer rules, and maximum exposure-reduction rules
        behave as intended.

    Model governance / validation reviewers:
        Confirm that Section 8 remains a preliminary exposure-treatment layer and does not assign
        final simulated outcomes or reason codes.

    SQL reviewers:
        Confirm that the CTE chain makes counteroffer feasibility auditable and avoids same-SELECT
        alias reuse problems.

    Portfolio / executive reviewers:
        Use Section 8 diagnostics to understand how much approved exposure, payment burden, and
        approved Expected Loss would be reduced before final outcome assignment.

WHEN TO RUN THIS SECTION:
    Run Section 8 after:

        Section 7 — Preliminary Decision Routing Layer

    Section 8 should be run before:

        Section 9 — Final Decision Resolution Layer

    Section 8 depends on:

        tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

INPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

OUTPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

GRAIN:
    One row per application_id for the selected Module 1 scenario / population and active Module 2
    strategy.

WHY APPROVED EXPOSURE TREATMENT IS SEPARATED FROM PRELIMINARY ROUTING:
    Section 7 identifies the preliminary route.

    Section 8 tests whether the preliminary route can support coherent approved-exposure treatment.

    This separation matters because route assignment and exposure feasibility are different questions:

        Section 7 asks:
            "Where should the row go next?"

        Section 8 asks:
            "What exposure treatment is economically and structurally feasible?"

    The separation makes counteroffer behavior transparent, testable, and auditable.

WHY PRELIMINARY COUNTEROFFER DOES NOT GUARANTEE A VIABLE COUNTEROFFER:
    A preliminary COUNTEROFFER route only means:

        "This row should be tested for reduced-exposure feasibility."

    It does not mean:
        approved_amount exists,
        counteroffer_amount exists,
        approved monthly payment proxy exists,
        approved PTI exists,
        approved Expected Loss exists,
        or a viable counteroffer has been created.

    A viable preliminary counteroffer must satisfy:
        product counteroffer permission,
        product maximum approved amount,
        product minimum approved amount,
        minimum counteroffer percent,
        maximum exposure reduction,
        approved PTI target,
        approved Expected Loss cap,
        and product rounding requirements.

WHY APPROVED AMOUNT IS STILL PRELIMINARY:
    Section 8 calculates approved_amount_preliminary.

    Section 9 later resolves final decision_outcome and final approved exposure fields.

    This distinction prevents the module from treating a feasibility calculation as a completed final
    simulated strategy outcome.

WHY APPROVED PAYMENT AND APPROVED PTI ARE STRATEGY-SIMULATION PROXIES:
    approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary scales the requested monthly payment proxy
    proportionally with preliminary approved exposure.

    approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary then compares that preliminary payment proxy to
    income through the already-staged requested PTI relationship.

    This is not:
        a contractual amortization schedule,
        a servicing calculation,
        a billing-engine output,
        or a production payment quote.

    It is a strategy-simulation affordability proxy.

WHY APPROVED EXPECTED LOSS IS BASED ON APPROVED EXPOSURE:
    requested_expected_loss_amount uses requested exposure from Module 1.

    approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary uses preliminary approved exposure from Module 2.

    Conceptual formula:
        approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary
            = approved_amount_preliminary × estimated_pd × estimated_lgd

    estimated_pd remains the Module 1 SQL field and is interpreted as the synthetic estimated-PD
    proxy.

WHY ESTIMATED_PD IS NOT RECALCULATED:
    Module 2 V1.0 does not create a post-decision risk model.

    Exposure treatment changes approved exposure and simulated approved-exposure Expected Loss.

    It does not recalculate the synthetic estimated-PD proxy.

WHY FAILED COUNTEROFFERS ARE NOT RESOLVED HERE:
    Failed counteroffers require a governed final-resolution policy:

        MANUAL_REVIEW
        or
        DECLINE

    That final resolution occurs in Section 9 using failed_counteroffer_resolution.

    Section 8 only identifies whether preliminary COUNTEROFFER exposure treatment passed or failed.

MANUAL REVIEW BOUNDARY:
    Preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW rows remain unresolved by design.

    They receive:
        approved_amount_preliminary = NULL
        counteroffer_amount_preliminary = NULL
        approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary = NULL
        approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary = NULL
        approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary = NULL

DECLINE BOUNDARY:
    Preliminary DECLINE rows receive the zero-exposure convention in this exposure-treatment stage.

    Final DECLINE is still not assigned until Section 9.

REASON-CODE BOUNDARY:
    Section 8 does not assign simulated reason codes.

    It does not create:
        primary_reason_code
        secondary_reason_code
        tertiary_reason_code
        triggered_reason_code_list
        reason_priority_rank
        primary_reason_family
        reason_code_count

    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason is a diagnostic field only.

    It is not a final simulated reason code.
    It is not customer communication language.
    It is not an adverse-action reason.

FINAL OUTCOME BOUNDARY:
    Section 8 does not create:
        decision_outcome
        decision_path
        approval_flag
        decline_flag
        manual_review_flag
        counteroffer_flag
        simulated_offer_exposure_flag

APPROVED-EXPOSURE BOUNDARY:
    Section 8 creates preliminary exposure-treatment fields only.

    Final approved exposure fields are created later:
        approved_amount
        counteroffer_amount
        approved_monthly_payment_proxy
        approved_payment_to_income_ratio
        approved_expected_loss_amount

SQL CONCEPTS TAUGHT IN THIS SECTION:
    CTE chain:
        Breaks feasibility testing into auditable steps:
            exposure_inputs
            counteroffer_components
            counteroffer_raw
            counteroffer_rounding
            counteroffer_test_economics
            counteroffer_feasibility
            exposure_amount_assignment
            approved_affordability
            approved_economics
            final_exposure_treatment

    LEAST:
        Chooses the most conservative upper bound among product cap, PTI target amount, and approved
        Expected Loss cap amount.

    GREATEST:
        Chooses the strictest minimum viable counteroffer amount across product minimum, minimum
        counteroffer percent, and maximum exposure-reduction constraints.

    FLOOR:
        Rounds the raw counteroffer amount down to the governed product rounding increment.

    NULLIF:
        Prevents divide-by-zero behavior when scaling payment, PTI, or Expected Loss values.

    CASE:
        Applies route-specific exposure-treatment conventions.

    IS DISTINCT FROM:
        Used in gatekeepers to compare NULL safely.

GOVERNANCE ROLE:
    Section 8 makes counteroffer feasibility transparent.

    It shows which constraints created a feasible reduced-exposure treatment and which constraints
    caused preliminary counteroffers to fail.

COMMON MISUSE TO AVOID:
    Do not interpret approved_amount_preliminary as final approved_amount.
    Do not interpret counteroffer_amount_preliminary as final counteroffer_amount.
    Do not interpret counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason as a final reason code.
    Do not interpret preliminary DECLINE exposure convention as final decision_outcome.
    Do not interpret preliminary approved PTI as a contractual payment obligation.
    Do not interpret preliminary approved Expected Loss as a production forecast.
    Do not treat Section 8 as latest-run output.
    Do not treat Section 8 as archive persistence.
    Do not treat Section 8 as final QA.

***************************************************************************************************/



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 8.0 — SECTION 8 DEPENDENCY PREFLIGHT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that Section 7 preliminary-routing output exists and is populated before exposure
    treatment begins.

    Section 8.0 answers:

        "Can Section 8 safely calculate approved-exposure treatment and counteroffer feasibility from
         the Section 7 preliminary-routing layer?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing exists.
    2. Confirm tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing contains rows.
    3. Confirm application_id is unique before exposure-treatment fields are added.
    4. Confirm key Section 7 exposure-routing fields are populated.
    5. Confirm requested exposure, payment, PTI, synthetic risk, LGD, Expected Loss, and product-policy
       controls needed by exposure treatment are populated.
    6. Fail clearly if Section 7 has not been run.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 8.0 does not create exposure treatment.
    Section 8.0 does not assign final outcomes.
    Section 8.0 does not assign reason codes.
    Section 8.0 does not modify persistent tables.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_stage4_exists BOOLEAN;
    v_stage4_row_count BIGINT;
    v_stage4_distinct_application_count BIGINT;
    v_required_exposure_input_gap_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Dependency check: Section 7 preliminary-routing stage must exist.

    SQL mechanics:
        TO_REGCLASS checks whether the temporary object exists.

    Business interpretation:
        Section 8 must consume preliminary routing from Section 7, not earlier rule flags or
        segmentation tables.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COALESCE(
        TO_REGCLASS('pg_temp.tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing'),
        TO_REGCLASS('tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing')
    ) IS NOT NULL
    INTO v_stage4_exists;

    IF v_stage4_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing is required. Run Section 7 before Section 8.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: Section 7 preliminary-routing stage must contain rows.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage4_row_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing;

    IF v_stage4_row_count <= 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing contains zero rows.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id must be unique before exposure treatment is added.

    Section 8 should add exposure-treatment fields only.

    It should not repair upstream row-grain problems.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_stage4_distinct_application_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing;

    IF v_stage4_distinct_application_count <> v_stage4_row_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing is not unique at application_id. Rows=%, distinct application_id=%.',
            v_stage4_row_count,
            v_stage4_distinct_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: required exposure-treatment input fields must be populated.

    Business interpretation:
        Section 8 needs both:
            route instructions from Section 7;
            product-policy controls carried forward from Section 5;
            borrower / requested-structure values from Module 1.

    Missing values here would make approved exposure, approved PTI, or approved Expected Loss
    partially undefined.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_required_exposure_input_gap_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing
    WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome IS NULL
       OR preliminary_decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
       OR preliminary_decision_path IS NULL
       OR requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag IS NULL
       OR requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag IS NULL

       OR requested_amount IS NULL
       OR requested_amount <= 0
       OR requested_monthly_payment_proxy IS NULL
       OR requested_payment_to_income_ratio IS NULL
       OR requested_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
       OR estimated_pd IS NULL
       OR estimated_lgd IS NULL

       OR product_min_approved_amount IS NULL
       OR product_max_approved_amount IS NULL
       OR product_min_approved_amount <= 0
       OR product_max_approved_amount <= product_min_approved_amount

       OR counteroffer_allowed_flag IS NULL
       OR product_min_counteroffer_pct IS NULL
       OR product_min_counteroffer_pct < 0
       OR product_min_counteroffer_pct > 1

       OR product_max_exposure_reduction_pct IS NULL
       OR product_max_exposure_reduction_pct < 0
       OR product_max_exposure_reduction_pct > 1

       OR counteroffer_target_pti IS NULL
       OR counteroffer_target_pti < 0

       OR product_approved_el_cap IS NULL
       OR product_approved_el_cap < 0

       OR approved_amount_rounding_increment IS NULL
       OR approved_amount_rounding_increment <= 0;

    IF v_required_exposure_input_gap_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: % Section 7 row(s) are missing required exposure-treatment inputs.',
            v_required_exposure_input_gap_count;
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 8.1 — CLEAN RESET OF SECTION 8 STAGING OBJECT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Drop the Section 8 exposure-treatment stage before rebuilding it.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Remove only the temporary Section 8 staging table.

WHY THIS MATTERS:
    A partial rerun should not allow stale exposure-treatment rows to remain available to Section 9.

    Section 9 assumes tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment reflects the current:
        Section 7 preliminary routing output,
        active strategy parameter state already carried forward,
        product policy thresholds already carried forward,
        and current exposure-treatment logic.

SQL MECHANICS:
    DROP TABLE IF EXISTS makes the reset rerunnable.

    If the table does not exist, PostgreSQL does not error.

BOUNDARY:
    This drop affects only the temporary Section 8 staging object.

    It does not modify Module 1 outputs.
    It does not modify Module 2 latest-run output.
    It does not modify Module 2 archive output.
    It does not modify evidence tables.
    It does not modify registry tables.

****************************************************************************************************/

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 8.2 — CREATE APPROVED EXPOSURE AND COUNTEROFFER FEASIBILITY TABLE
****************************************************************************************************

TABLE:
    tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

GRAIN:
    One row per application_id for the selected Module 1 scenario / population and active Module 2
    strategy.

INPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing

OUTPUT:
    All Section 7 fields plus:
        exposure_treatment_status
        exposure_treatment_path
        approved_amount_preliminary
        counteroffer_amount_preliminary
        exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary
        exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary
        exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary
        approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary
        approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary
        approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary
        approved_el_reduction_amount_preliminary
        approved_el_reduction_pct_preliminary
        counteroffer feasibility component fields
        counteroffer feasibility diagnostics

SQL DESIGN:
    This section uses a CTE chain so each exposure-treatment calculation is visible.

    The chain is:

        exposure_inputs
            preserves Section 7 output.

        counteroffer_components
            calculates the product cap, PTI target amount, approved Expected Loss cap amount, and
            minimum viable counteroffer amount.

        counteroffer_raw
            identifies the most conservative raw feasible amount.

        counteroffer_rounding
            rounds the raw amount down using the product rounding increment.

        counteroffer_test_economics
            calculates test payment, test PTI, and test approved Expected Loss for the rounded
            counteroffer amount.

        counteroffer_feasibility
            evaluates pass / fail and assigns feasibility failure diagnostics.

        exposure_amount_assignment
            assigns preliminary approved amount, counteroffer amount, and exposure reduction fields.

        approved_affordability
            assigns preliminary approved payment and preliminary approved PTI.

        approved_economics
            assigns preliminary approved Expected Loss and preliminary EL reduction diagnostics.

        final_exposure_treatment
            assigns exposure_treatment_status and exposure_treatment_path.

WHY SELECT * IS ACCEPTABLE HERE:
    This is a temporary staging layer, not a permanent output table.

    Section 8 intentionally preserves all prior fields plus exposure-treatment diagnostics for
    Section 9 final decision resolution.

    Permanent output selection is handled later with an explicit field list in Section 11.

***************************************************************************************************/

CREATE TEMP TABLE tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
ON COMMIT PRESERVE ROWS
AS
WITH exposure_inputs AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: exposure_inputs

    Purpose:
        Preserve all Section 7 preliminary-routing rows and fields.

    Boundary:
        No exposure treatment is calculated here.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        r.*
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing r
),

counteroffer_components AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: counteroffer_components

    Purpose:
        Calculate independent counteroffer amount constraints for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.

    Counteroffer upper bounds:
        product cap amount;
        PTI target amount;
        approved Expected Loss cap amount.

    Counteroffer minimum viable amount:
        strictest of product minimum, minimum counteroffer percent, and maximum exposure-reduction
        constraint.

    Boundary:
        These are feasibility components only.

        They do not assign final counteroffer outcomes.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        ei.*,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Product cap amount.

        The preliminary approved exposure cannot exceed:
            original requested_amount
            or product_max_approved_amount.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ei.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN LEAST(ei.requested_amount, ei.product_max_approved_amount)
            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_product_cap_amount,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        PTI target amount.

        Because Module 2 V1.0 scales payment proportionally with exposure, this estimates the
        exposure amount that would bring requested PTI down to the product-specific counteroffer
        target PTI.

        Formula:
            requested_amount × counteroffer_target_pti / requested_payment_to_income_ratio

        If requested PTI is zero or lower, PTI does not constrain the counteroffer amount.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ei.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ei.requested_payment_to_income_ratio > 0
                THEN ei.requested_amount
                     * ei.counteroffer_target_pti
                     / NULLIF(ei.requested_payment_to_income_ratio, 0)

            WHEN ei.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN ei.requested_amount

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_pti_target_amount,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Approved Expected Loss cap amount.

        Conceptual formula:
            approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary
                = approved_amount_preliminary × estimated_pd × estimated_lgd

        Rearranged cap amount:
            product_approved_el_cap / (estimated_pd × estimated_lgd)

        If estimated_pd × estimated_lgd is zero, approved Expected Loss does not constrain exposure.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ei.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND (ei.estimated_pd * ei.estimated_lgd) > 0
                THEN ei.product_approved_el_cap
                     / NULLIF((ei.estimated_pd * ei.estimated_lgd), 0)

            WHEN ei.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN LEAST(ei.requested_amount, ei.product_max_approved_amount)

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_el_cap_amount,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Minimum viable counteroffer amount.

        A feasible counteroffer must be large enough to satisfy:
            product minimum approved amount;
            minimum counteroffer percent;
            maximum exposure-reduction limit.

        Example:
            product_max_exposure_reduction_pct = 0.60

            The approved amount must be at least:
                requested_amount × (1 - 0.60)
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ei.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN GREATEST(
                    ei.product_min_approved_amount,
                    ei.requested_amount * ei.product_min_counteroffer_pct,
                    ei.requested_amount * (1.0 - ei.product_max_exposure_reduction_pct)
                )
            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_min_viable_amount

    FROM exposure_inputs ei
),

counteroffer_raw AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: counteroffer_raw

    Purpose:
        Select the most conservative raw maximum feasible counteroffer amount.

    SQL mechanics:
        LEAST chooses the lowest upper bound.

    Business interpretation:
        A counteroffer must satisfy all upper-bound constraints at once, so the most conservative
        upper bound controls the raw feasible amount.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        cc.*,

        CASE
            WHEN cc.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN LEAST(
                    cc.counteroffer_product_cap_amount,
                    cc.counteroffer_pti_target_amount,
                    cc.counteroffer_el_cap_amount
                )
            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount

    FROM counteroffer_components cc
),

counteroffer_rounding AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: counteroffer_rounding

    Purpose:
        Round the raw maximum feasible counteroffer amount down to the governed product rounding
        increment.

    Why round down:
        Rounding down prevents the rounded amount from accidentally exceeding the raw feasible amount.

    Boundary:
        A rounded amount can become infeasible if rounding pushes it below the minimum viable amount.
        The next CTE tests that explicitly.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        cr.*,

        CASE
            WHEN cr.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND cr.counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount IS NOT NULL
             AND cr.approved_amount_rounding_increment > 0
                THEN FLOOR(
                        cr.counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount
                        / NULLIF(cr.approved_amount_rounding_increment, 0)
                     )
                     * cr.approved_amount_rounding_increment

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_rounded_amount

    FROM counteroffer_raw cr
),

counteroffer_test_economics AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: counteroffer_test_economics

    Purpose:
        Calculate payment, PTI, and Expected Loss for the rounded counteroffer amount.

    Credit risk interpretation:
        This is where reduced exposure is translated into:
            lower payment burden;
            lower approved PTI;
            lower approved Expected Loss.

    Boundary:
        These are test economics for feasibility.

        They become preliminary approved economics only if the counteroffer passes.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        crd.*,

        CASE
            WHEN crd.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND crd.counteroffer_rounded_amount IS NOT NULL
             AND crd.requested_amount > 0
                THEN crd.requested_monthly_payment_proxy
                     * crd.counteroffer_rounded_amount
                     / NULLIF(crd.requested_amount, 0)

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_test_monthly_payment_proxy,


        CASE
            WHEN crd.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND crd.counteroffer_rounded_amount IS NOT NULL
             AND crd.requested_amount > 0
                THEN crd.requested_payment_to_income_ratio
                     * crd.counteroffer_rounded_amount
                     / NULLIF(crd.requested_amount, 0)

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_test_payment_to_income_ratio,


        CASE
            WHEN crd.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND crd.counteroffer_rounded_amount IS NOT NULL
                THEN crd.counteroffer_rounded_amount
                     * crd.estimated_pd
                     * crd.estimated_lgd

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount

    FROM counteroffer_rounding crd
),

counteroffer_feasibility AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: counteroffer_feasibility

    Purpose:
        Evaluate whether the rounded counteroffer amount is feasible.

    A preliminary counteroffer passes only when it satisfies:
        product counteroffer permission,
        positive rounded amount,
        reduction below requested amount,
        product minimum,
        minimum counteroffer percent,
        maximum exposure-reduction limit,
        product maximum approved amount,
        counteroffer target PTI,
        product approved Expected Loss cap.

    Boundary:
        counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag is not final decision_outcome.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        cte.*,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag.

        TRUE / FALSE only for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.

        NULL for non-counteroffer preliminary routes.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN cte.preliminary_decision_outcome <> 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN NULL::BOOLEAN

            ELSE (
                cte.counteroffer_allowed_flag IS TRUE
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount IS NOT NULL
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount > 0
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount < cte.requested_amount
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount >= cte.product_min_approved_amount
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount >= cte.requested_amount * cte.product_min_counteroffer_pct
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount >= cte.requested_amount * (1.0 - cte.product_max_exposure_reduction_pct)
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount <= cte.product_max_approved_amount
                AND cte.counteroffer_test_payment_to_income_ratio <= cte.counteroffer_target_pti
                AND cte.counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount <= cte.product_approved_el_cap
            )
        END AS counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count.

        Counts how many feasibility constraints failed.

        NULL for non-counteroffer preliminary routes.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN cte.preliminary_decision_outcome <> 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN NULL::INTEGER

            ELSE
                (
                    CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_allowed_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount <= 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount >= cte.requested_amount THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount < cte.product_min_approved_amount THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount < cte.requested_amount * cte.product_min_counteroffer_pct THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount < cte.requested_amount * (1.0 - cte.product_max_exposure_reduction_pct) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount > cte.product_max_approved_amount THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_test_payment_to_income_ratio IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_test_payment_to_income_ratio > cte.counteroffer_target_pti THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                    + CASE WHEN cte.counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount > cte.product_approved_el_cap THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                )
        END AS counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason.

        First failing constraint in priority order.

        This is a feasibility diagnostic only.
        It is not a final simulated reason code.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN cte.preliminary_decision_outcome <> 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN NULL::TEXT

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_allowed_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_ALLOWED_BY_PRODUCT_POLICY'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount IS NULL
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_RAW_AMOUNT_NULL'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount IS NULL
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_ROUNDED_AMOUNT_NULL'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount <= 0
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_ROUNDED_AMOUNT_NONPOSITIVE'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount >= cte.requested_amount
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_BELOW_REQUESTED_AMOUNT'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount < cte.product_min_approved_amount
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_BELOW_PRODUCT_MINIMUM'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount < cte.requested_amount * cte.product_min_counteroffer_pct
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_BELOW_MINIMUM_REQUESTED_PERCENT'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount < cte.requested_amount * (1.0 - cte.product_max_exposure_reduction_pct)
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_EXCEEDS_MAX_REDUCTION'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount > cte.product_max_approved_amount
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_EXCEEDS_PRODUCT_CAP'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_test_payment_to_income_ratio IS NULL
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_TEST_PTI_NULL'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_test_payment_to_income_ratio > cte.counteroffer_target_pti
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_PTI_STILL_ABOVE_TARGET'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_TEST_EXPECTED_LOSS_NULL'

            WHEN cte.counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount > cte.product_approved_el_cap
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_APPROVED_EL_ABOVE_CAP'

            WHEN NOT (
                cte.counteroffer_allowed_flag IS TRUE
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount IS NOT NULL
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount > 0
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount < cte.requested_amount
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount >= cte.product_min_approved_amount
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount >= cte.requested_amount * cte.product_min_counteroffer_pct
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount >= cte.requested_amount * (1.0 - cte.product_max_exposure_reduction_pct)
                AND cte.counteroffer_rounded_amount <= cte.product_max_approved_amount
                AND cte.counteroffer_test_payment_to_income_ratio <= cte.counteroffer_target_pti
                AND cte.counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount <= cte.product_approved_el_cap
            )
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBILITY_UNKNOWN'

            ELSE NULL::TEXT
        END AS counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason

    FROM counteroffer_test_economics cte
),

exposure_amount_assignment AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: exposure_amount_assignment

    Purpose:
        Assign preliminary approved exposure and exposure-reduction fields by preliminary route.

    Route conventions:
        APPROVE:
            approve as requested.

        COUNTEROFFER:
            use rounded feasible reduced exposure only if feasibility passes.

        DECLINE:
            apply preliminary zero-exposure convention.

        MANUAL_REVIEW:
            remain unresolved with NULL exposure economics.

        Failed COUNTEROFFER:
            remain unresolved with NULL exposure economics until Section 9 resolves the final outcome.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        cf.*,

        CASE
            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN cf.requested_amount

            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND cf.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN cf.counteroffer_rounded_amount

            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_amount_preliminary,


        CASE
            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND cf.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN cf.counteroffer_rounded_amount
            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_amount_preliminary,


        CASE
            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND cf.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN TRUE
            ELSE FALSE
        END AS exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary,


        CASE
            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND cf.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN cf.requested_amount - cf.counteroffer_rounded_amount

            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN cf.requested_amount

            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary,


        CASE
            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND cf.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN (cf.requested_amount - cf.counteroffer_rounded_amount)
                     / NULLIF(cf.requested_amount, 0)

            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 1.0::NUMERIC

            WHEN cf.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary

    FROM counteroffer_feasibility cf
),

approved_affordability AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: approved_affordability

    Purpose:
        Assign preliminary approved payment proxy and preliminary approved PTI.

    Boundary:
        These remain preliminary exposure-treatment values.

        Final approved payment and final approved PTI are created in Section 9.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        eaa.*,

        CASE
            WHEN eaa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN eaa.requested_monthly_payment_proxy

            WHEN eaa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND eaa.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN eaa.counteroffer_test_monthly_payment_proxy

            WHEN eaa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN eaa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary,


        CASE
            WHEN eaa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN eaa.requested_payment_to_income_ratio

            WHEN eaa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND eaa.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN eaa.counteroffer_test_payment_to_income_ratio

            WHEN eaa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN eaa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary

    FROM exposure_amount_assignment eaa
),

approved_economics AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: approved_economics

    Purpose:
        Assign preliminary approved Expected Loss and approved Expected Loss reduction fields.

    Boundary:
        These are preliminary strategy-simulation economics.

        Final approved Expected Loss is created in Section 9.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        aa.*,

        CASE
            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN aa.requested_expected_loss_amount

            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND aa.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN aa.counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount

            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary,


        CASE
            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND aa.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN aa.requested_expected_loss_amount - aa.counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount

            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN aa.requested_expected_loss_amount

            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_el_reduction_amount_preliminary,


        CASE
            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND aa.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN (aa.requested_expected_loss_amount - aa.counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount)
                     / NULLIF(aa.requested_expected_loss_amount, 0)

            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN CASE
                    WHEN aa.requested_expected_loss_amount > 0 THEN 1.0::NUMERIC
                    ELSE 0::NUMERIC
                END

            WHEN aa.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_el_reduction_pct_preliminary

    FROM approved_affordability aa
),

final_exposure_treatment AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: final_exposure_treatment

    Purpose:
        Assign compact preliminary exposure-treatment status and path labels.

    Boundary:
        These labels are not final decision_outcome and not final decision_path.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        ae.*,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Only preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows receive feasibility evaluation.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
            AS counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag,


        CASE
            WHEN ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 'APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED_PRELIMINARY'

            WHEN ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 'NO_OFFER_PRELIMINARY_DECLINE'

            WHEN ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN 'UNRESOLVED_MANUAL_REVIEW'

            WHEN ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ae.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBLE_PRELIMINARY'

            WHEN ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ae.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE_PRELIMINARY'

            ELSE 'EXPOSURE_TREATMENT_UNKNOWN'
        END AS exposure_treatment_status,


        CASE
            WHEN ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 'APPROVE_AS_REQUESTED'

            WHEN ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 'NO_OFFER'

            WHEN ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW_UNRESOLVED'

            WHEN ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ae.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBLE'

            WHEN ae.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ae.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE'

            ELSE 'EXPOSURE_TREATMENT_UNKNOWN'
        END AS exposure_treatment_path

    FROM approved_economics ae
)

SELECT *
FROM final_exposure_treatment;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 8.3 — LOCAL FAIL-FAST CHECKS FOR EXPOSURE TREATMENT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that preliminary exposure treatment, approved affordability proxies, approved Expected
    Loss proxies, and counteroffer feasibility diagnostics are internally consistent before Section 9
    resolves final decision_outcome.

    Section 8.3 answers:

        "Did Section 8 preserve applicant grain, calculate preliminary exposure treatment correctly,
         evaluate preliminary counteroffers, and avoid creating final decision / reason-code fields?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm row count is unchanged from tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing.
    2. Confirm application_id remains unique.
    3. Confirm required Section 8 fields are complete.
    4. Confirm APPROVE preliminary exposure convention.
    5. Confirm DECLINE preliminary zero-exposure convention.
    6. Confirm MANUAL_REVIEW unresolved convention.
    7. Confirm preliminary COUNTEROFFER feasibility evaluation.
    8. Confirm feasible preliminary COUNTEROFFER convention.
    9. Confirm infeasible preliminary COUNTEROFFER convention.
    10. Confirm final decision, final exposure, latest-run, archive, and reason-code fields were not
        created.

LOCAL GATEKEEPER BOUNDARY:
    These are local Section 8 staging gatekeepers only.

    They are not:
        final decision validation,
        reason-code validation,
        archive validation,
        matched strategy comparison,
        full Module 2 QA,
        strategy frontier review,
        or Validation Summary evidence by themselves.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_stage4_count BIGINT;
    v_stage5_count BIGINT;
    v_stage5_distinct_app_count BIGINT;
    v_duplicate_application_count BIGINT;

    v_exposure_treatment_completeness_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_approve_convention_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_decline_convention_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_manual_review_convention_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_counteroffer_route_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_counteroffer_pass_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_counteroffer_fail_failure_count BIGINT;

    v_forbidden_column_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: row count must be unchanged from Section 7 to Section 8.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage4_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing;

    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage5_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment;

    IF v_stage5_count <> v_stage4_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: row count changed from Section 7 to Section 8. Stage 4 rows: %, Stage 5 rows: %.',
            v_stage4_count,
            v_stage5_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id remains unique.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_stage5_distinct_app_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment;

    IF v_stage5_distinct_app_count <> v_stage5_count THEN
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_duplicate_application_count
        FROM (
            SELECT application_id
            FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
            GROUP BY application_id
            HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
        ) d;

        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: application_id uniqueness was not preserved. Stage 5 rows: %, distinct application_id count: %, duplicate application_id group count: %.',
            v_stage5_count,
            v_stage5_distinct_app_count,
            v_duplicate_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: required Section 8 output fields must be complete.

    Non-counteroffer rows are allowed to have NULL counteroffer-specific diagnostic fields.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_exposure_treatment_completeness_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
    WHERE exposure_treatment_status IS NULL
       OR exposure_treatment_path IS NULL
       OR exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary IS NULL
       OR counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag IS NULL

       OR (
            preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND (
                counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS NULL
             OR counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count IS NULL
             OR counteroffer_product_cap_amount IS NULL
             OR counteroffer_pti_target_amount IS NULL
             OR counteroffer_el_cap_amount IS NULL
             OR counteroffer_min_viable_amount IS NULL
            )
       );

    IF v_exposure_treatment_completeness_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: % row(s) have incomplete exposure-treatment fields.',
            v_exposure_treatment_completeness_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: preliminary APPROVE convention.

    APPROVE remains preliminary but should preserve requested exposure and requested economics.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_approve_convention_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
    WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
      AND (
            approved_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM requested_amount
         OR counteroffer_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
         OR exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM requested_monthly_payment_proxy
         OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM requested_payment_to_income_ratio
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM requested_expected_loss_amount
         OR approved_el_reduction_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_el_reduction_pct_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_treatment_status <> 'APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED_PRELIMINARY'
         OR exposure_treatment_path <> 'APPROVE_AS_REQUESTED'
      );

    IF v_approve_convention_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: % preliminary APPROVE row(s) violate exposure-treatment convention.',
            v_approve_convention_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: preliminary DECLINE convention.

    DECLINE is still preliminary, but the exposure-treatment convention is zero exposure.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_decline_convention_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
    WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND (
            approved_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR counteroffer_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
         OR exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM requested_amount
         OR exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 1.0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_el_reduction_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM requested_expected_loss_amount
         OR approved_el_reduction_pct_preliminary IS NULL
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_treatment_status <> 'NO_OFFER_PRELIMINARY_DECLINE'
         OR exposure_treatment_path <> 'NO_OFFER'
      );

    IF v_decline_convention_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: % preliminary DECLINE row(s) violate zero-exposure treatment convention.',
            v_decline_convention_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW convention.

    Manual review remains unresolved by design.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_manual_review_convention_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
    WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            approved_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
         OR exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_el_reduction_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_el_reduction_pct_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_treatment_status <> 'UNRESOLVED_MANUAL_REVIEW'
         OR exposure_treatment_path <> 'MANUAL_REVIEW_UNRESOLVED'
      );

    IF v_manual_review_convention_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: % preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW row(s) violate unresolved convention.',
            v_manual_review_convention_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows must be explicitly evaluated for feasibility.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_counteroffer_route_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
    WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND (
            counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS NULL
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count IS NULL
         OR exposure_treatment_status NOT IN (
                'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBLE_PRELIMINARY',
                'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE_PRELIMINARY'
            )
         OR exposure_treatment_path NOT IN (
                'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBLE',
                'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE'
            )
      );

    IF v_counteroffer_route_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: % preliminary COUNTEROFFER row(s) were not explicitly evaluated for feasibility.',
            v_counteroffer_route_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: feasible preliminary COUNTEROFFER convention.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_counteroffer_pass_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
    WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
      AND (
            approved_amount_preliminary IS NULL
         OR counteroffer_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM approved_amount_preliminary
         OR approved_amount_preliminary <= 0
         OR approved_amount_preliminary >= requested_amount
         OR exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
         OR exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary <= 0
         OR exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary <= 0
         OR approved_amount_preliminary < product_min_approved_amount
         OR approved_amount_preliminary > product_max_approved_amount
         OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary > counteroffer_target_pti
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary > product_approved_el_cap
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_treatment_status <> 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBLE_PRELIMINARY'
         OR exposure_treatment_path <> 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBLE'
      );

    IF v_counteroffer_pass_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: % feasible preliminary COUNTEROFFER row(s) violate counteroffer feasibility convention.',
            v_counteroffer_pass_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: infeasible preliminary COUNTEROFFER convention.

    Infeasible preliminary counteroffers remain unresolved in Section 8.

    Section 9 later resolves the final outcome using failed_counteroffer_resolution.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_counteroffer_fail_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
    WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
      AND (
            approved_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
         OR exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_el_reduction_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_el_reduction_pct_preliminary IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason IS NULL
         OR exposure_treatment_status <> 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE_PRELIMINARY'
         OR exposure_treatment_path <> 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE'
      );

    IF v_counteroffer_fail_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: % infeasible preliminary COUNTEROFFER row(s) violate failed-counteroffer convention.',
            v_counteroffer_fail_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: Section 8 must not create final decision, final flags, final exposure fields,
    simulated reason-code fields, latest-run output, or archive logic.

    Exact final field names are checked. Preliminary exposure-treatment fields are allowed.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_forbidden_column_count
    FROM pg_attribute
    WHERE attrelid = 'tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment'::REGCLASS
      AND attnum > 0
      AND NOT attisdropped
      AND attname IN (
            'decision_outcome',
            'decision_path',
            'approval_flag',
            'decline_flag',
            'manual_review_flag',
            'counteroffer_flag',
            'simulated_offer_exposure_flag',

            'primary_reason_code',
            'secondary_reason_code',
            'tertiary_reason_code',
            'triggered_reason_code_list',
            'reason_priority_rank',
            'primary_reason_family',
            'reason_code_count',

            'approved_amount',
            'counteroffer_amount',
            'approved_monthly_payment_proxy',
            'approved_payment_to_income_ratio',
            'approved_expected_loss_amount'
      );

    IF v_forbidden_column_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 8 failure: forbidden final decision, final exposure, or reason-code field(s) were created in exposure-treatment stage.';
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 8.4 — LOCAL EXPOSURE-TREATMENT SANITY CHECKS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide lightweight diagnostics for Section 8 exposure treatment and counteroffer feasibility.

    Section 8.4 answers:

        "What exposure treatment did Section 8 calculate, how many preliminary counteroffers were
         feasible, and which constraints explain failed counteroffers?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    Display review outputs for:
        preliminary outcome × exposure-treatment status,
        exposure-treatment path,
        counteroffer feasibility evaluation,
        counteroffer feasibility pass / fail,
        counteroffer failure reason,
        product × counteroffer feasibility,
        score band × counteroffer feasibility,
        requested PTI bucket × counteroffer feasibility,
        strategy risk tier × counteroffer feasibility,
        requested vs approved amount by exposure-treatment status,
        requested vs approved PTI by exposure-treatment status,
        requested vs approved Expected Loss by exposure-treatment status,
        exposure reduction by product for feasible counteroffers,
        counteroffer failures by product and failure reason,
        counteroffer feasibility constraint counts,
        and one compact Section 8 readiness summary.

INTERPRETATION:
    These are staging diagnostics only.

    They should not be interpreted as:
        final strategy validation,
        final decision distribution,
        simulated reason-code validation,
        archive validation,
        matched strategy comparison,
        strategy frontier evidence,
        or Validation Summary acceptance.

****************************************************************************************************/



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.1 Count by preliminary_decision_outcome × exposure_treatment_status.

Purpose:
    Show how each preliminary route was translated into exposure-treatment status.

Boundary:
    preliminary_decision_outcome is not final decision_outcome.
    exposure_treatment_status is not final decision_path.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    preliminary_decision_outcome,
    exposure_treatment_status,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

GROUP BY
    preliminary_decision_outcome,
    exposure_treatment_status

ORDER BY
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END,
    exposure_treatment_status;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.2 Count by exposure_treatment_path.

Purpose:
    Review compact exposure-treatment path labels.

Interpretation:
    This is useful for confirming how many rows were approved as requested, tested as counteroffer,
    left unresolved, or given preliminary zero-exposure treatment.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    exposure_treatment_path,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

GROUP BY exposure_treatment_path

ORDER BY exposure_treatment_path;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.3 Count by counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag.

Purpose:
    Confirm that feasibility was evaluated only for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.

Expected:
    TRUE only for preliminary_decision_outcome = COUNTEROFFER.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
GROUP BY
    counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome
ORDER BY
    counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag,
    preliminary_decision_outcome;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.4 Count by counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag.

Purpose:
    Review preliminary COUNTEROFFER feasibility pass / fail results.

Boundary:
    Feasible preliminary counteroffer is not final COUNTEROFFER until Section 9.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
GROUP BY counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag
ORDER BY counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.5 Count by counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason.

Purpose:
    Show why preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows failed feasibility testing.

Boundary:
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason is a diagnostic field, not a final simulated reason code.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count)
        AS avg_counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
  AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE

GROUP BY counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason

ORDER BY
    row_count DESC,
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.6 Product × counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag.

Purpose:
    Review whether counteroffer feasibility concentrates by product.

Interpretation:
    Product concentration may reflect product caps, minimums, PTI targets, approved Expected Loss caps,
    rounding increments, or exposure-reduction limits.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    product_type_policy_key,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,

    COUNT(*) AS preliminary_counteroffer_rows,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(approved_amount_preliminary) AS avg_approved_amount_preliminary,
    AVG(exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary) AS avg_exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary,

    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary) AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary,

    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'

GROUP BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag

ORDER BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.7 Score band × counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag.

Purpose:
    Review whether counteroffer feasibility differs by borrower-quality segment.

Boundary:
    Score band is diagnostic. Feasibility is still driven by exposure, PTI, Expected Loss, and product
    constraints.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    score_band_policy_key,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,

    COUNT(*) AS preliminary_counteroffer_rows,

    AVG(credit_score) AS avg_credit_score,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(approved_amount_preliminary) AS avg_approved_amount_preliminary

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'

GROUP BY
    score_band_policy_key,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag

ORDER BY
    CASE score_band_policy_key
        WHEN 'SUPER_PRIME' THEN 1
        WHEN 'PRIME' THEN 2
        WHEN 'NEAR_PRIME' THEN 3
        WHEN 'SUBPRIME' THEN 4
        WHEN 'DEEP_SUBPRIME' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.8 Requested PTI bucket × counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag.

Purpose:
    Review how requested affordability pressure affects counteroffer feasibility.

Boundary:
    Requested PTI is the requested structure.

    Approved PTI is calculated only after exposure treatment.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    requested_pti_bucket,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,

    COUNT(*) AS preliminary_counteroffer_rows,

    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary) AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary,
    AVG(counteroffer_target_pti) AS avg_counteroffer_target_pti

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'

GROUP BY
    requested_pti_bucket,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag

ORDER BY
    CASE requested_pti_bucket
        WHEN 'LOW_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.9 Strategy risk tier × counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag.

Purpose:
    Review whether synthetic estimated-risk tiers affect counteroffer feasibility.

Boundary:
    estimated_pd remains the synthetic estimated-PD proxy and is not recalculated by exposure
    treatment.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    strategy_risk_tier,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,

    COUNT(*) AS preliminary_counteroffer_rows,

    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(estimated_lgd) AS avg_estimated_lgd,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'

GROUP BY
    strategy_risk_tier,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag

ORDER BY
    CASE strategy_risk_tier
        WHEN 'LOW_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.10 Requested amount versus preliminary approved amount by exposure_treatment_status.

Purpose:
    Review exposure capture and reduction by treatment status.

Interpretation:
    APPROVE should preserve requested amount.
    Feasible COUNTEROFFER should reduce amount.
    Preliminary DECLINE should use zero approved exposure.
    MANUAL_REVIEW and failed COUNTEROFFER should remain unresolved.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    exposure_treatment_status,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(approved_amount_preliminary) AS avg_approved_amount_preliminary,

    SUM(requested_amount) AS total_requested_amount,
    SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount_preliminary, 0)) AS total_approved_amount_preliminary,

    AVG(exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary) AS avg_exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary,
    AVG(exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary) AS avg_exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

GROUP BY exposure_treatment_status

ORDER BY exposure_treatment_status;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.11 Requested PTI versus preliminary approved PTI by exposure_treatment_status.

Purpose:
    Review affordability impact of exposure treatment.

Boundary:
    approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary is a strategy-simulation proxy.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    exposure_treatment_status,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary) AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary,

    AVG(
        requested_payment_to_income_ratio - approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary
    ) AS avg_pti_reduction_preliminary

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

GROUP BY exposure_treatment_status

ORDER BY exposure_treatment_status;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.12 Requested Expected Loss versus preliminary approved Expected Loss by exposure_treatment_status.

Purpose:
    Review Expected Loss impact of preliminary exposure treatment.

Boundary:
    requested_expected_loss_amount is requested-exposure Expected Loss.
    approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary is preliminary approved-exposure Expected Loss.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    exposure_treatment_status,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary,

    SUM(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS total_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary, 0)) AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary,

    AVG(approved_el_reduction_amount_preliminary) AS avg_approved_el_reduction_amount_preliminary,
    AVG(approved_el_reduction_pct_preliminary) AS avg_approved_el_reduction_pct_preliminary

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

GROUP BY exposure_treatment_status

ORDER BY exposure_treatment_status;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.13 Average exposure reduction percentage by product for feasible counteroffers.

Purpose:
    Show product-level counteroffer reduction behavior.

Interpretation:
    Higher reduction percentages may be expected where product caps, affordability targets, or
    approved Expected Loss caps bind more tightly.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    product_type_policy_key,

    COUNT(*) AS feasible_counteroffer_rows,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(approved_amount_preliminary) AS avg_counteroffer_amount_preliminary,
    AVG(exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary) AS avg_exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary,
    AVG(exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary) AS avg_exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary,

    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary) AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary,
    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
  AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE

GROUP BY product_type_policy_key

ORDER BY product_type_policy_key;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.14 Counteroffer failures by product and failure reason.

Purpose:
    Identify which products and constraints explain failed preliminary counteroffers.

Boundary:
    Failure reasons are feasibility diagnostics only.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    product_type_policy_key,
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason,

    COUNT(*) AS failed_counteroffer_rows,

    AVG(counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count)
        AS avg_counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount) AS avg_counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount,
    AVG(counteroffer_rounded_amount) AS avg_counteroffer_rounded_amount,
    AVG(counteroffer_min_viable_amount) AS avg_counteroffer_min_viable_amount

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
  AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE

GROUP BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason

ORDER BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    failed_counteroffer_rows DESC,
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.15 Counteroffer feasibility constraint count distribution.

Purpose:
    Review whether failed counteroffers usually fail one constraint or multiple constraints.

Interpretation:
    Multiple failed constraints suggest the requested structure is far from feasible.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,
    counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count,

    COUNT(*) AS preliminary_counteroffer_rows,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount

FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'

GROUP BY
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,
    counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count

ORDER BY
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,
    counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4.16 Section 8 readiness summary.

Purpose:
    Provide one compact readiness row for the exposure-treatment stage.

Expected:
    section_8_exposure_treatment_status =
        SECTION_8_EXPOSURE_TREATMENT_READY_FOR_FINAL_DECISION_RESOLUTION

Interpretation:
    This confirms only that Section 8 is ready for Section 9.

    It does not validate final strategy outcomes.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH exposure_treatment_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS stage5_row_count,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE exposure_treatment_status IS NULL
               OR exposure_treatment_path IS NULL
               OR exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary IS NULL
               OR counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag IS NULL
        ) AS exposure_treatment_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND (
                    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS NULL
                 OR counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count IS NULL
              )
        ) AS counteroffer_feasibility_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
              AND approved_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM requested_amount
        ) AS approve_amount_convention_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
              AND (
                    approved_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
                 OR approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
              )
        ) AS decline_zero_exposure_convention_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND (
                    approved_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
                 OR approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary IS NOT NULL
              )
        ) AS manual_review_unresolved_convention_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
        ) AS feasible_preliminary_counteroffer_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
        ) AS infeasible_preliminary_counteroffer_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
        ) AS preliminary_approve_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS preliminary_counteroffer_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
        ) AS preliminary_manual_review_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
        ) AS preliminary_decline_rows

    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
)

SELECT
    stage5_row_count,
    distinct_application_id_count,

    exposure_treatment_gap_rows,
    counteroffer_feasibility_gap_rows,
    approve_amount_convention_gap_rows,
    decline_zero_exposure_convention_gap_rows,
    manual_review_unresolved_convention_gap_rows,

    preliminary_approve_rows,
    preliminary_counteroffer_rows,
    feasible_preliminary_counteroffer_rows,
    infeasible_preliminary_counteroffer_rows,
    preliminary_manual_review_rows,
    preliminary_decline_rows,

    CASE
        WHEN stage5_row_count > 0
         AND stage5_row_count = distinct_application_id_count
         AND exposure_treatment_gap_rows = 0
         AND counteroffer_feasibility_gap_rows = 0
         AND approve_amount_convention_gap_rows = 0
         AND decline_zero_exposure_convention_gap_rows = 0
         AND manual_review_unresolved_convention_gap_rows = 0
            THEN 'SECTION_8_EXPOSURE_TREATMENT_READY_FOR_FINAL_DECISION_RESOLUTION'
        ELSE 'REVIEW_SECTION_8_EXPOSURE_TREATMENT_BEFORE_FINAL_DECISION_RESOLUTION'
    END AS section_8_exposure_treatment_status

FROM exposure_treatment_summary;



/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 8 — APPROVED EXPOSURE AND COUNTEROFFER FEASIBILITY LAYER

If execution reaches this point:
    1. Section 8 dependency preflight passed.
    2. tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment exists.
    3. Row count is unchanged from tmp_m2_stage_4_preliminary_decision_routing.
    4. application_id remains unique.
    5. All Section 7 preliminary routing fields remain preserved.
    6. Counteroffer product cap amount was calculated for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    7. Counteroffer PTI target amount was calculated for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    8. Counteroffer approved Expected Loss cap amount was calculated for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    9. Counteroffer minimum viable amount was calculated for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    10. Counteroffer raw maximum feasible amount was calculated for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    11. Counteroffer rounded amount was calculated for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    12. Counteroffer test payment, test PTI, and test approved Expected Loss were calculated.
    13. counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag is populated.
    14. counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag is populated for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    15. counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason is populated for infeasible preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    16. counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count is populated for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    17. approved_amount_preliminary is populated according to preliminary route convention.
    18. counteroffer_amount_preliminary is populated only for feasible preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    19. approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary is populated according to preliminary route convention.
    20. approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary is populated according to preliminary route convention.
    21. approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary is populated according to preliminary route convention.
    22. exposure_treatment_status and exposure_treatment_path are populated.
    23. APPROVE preliminary convention was validated.
    24. DECLINE preliminary zero-exposure convention was validated.
    25. MANUAL_REVIEW unresolved convention was validated.
    26. Feasible and infeasible preliminary COUNTEROFFER conventions were validated.
    27. No final decision, final reason-code, final approved-exposure, latest-run, archive, or evidence
        fields were created.
    28. Section 8 local exposure-treatment diagnostics are available for review.

Section 8 established:
    1. The preliminary exposure-treatment layer.
    2. Preliminary approved exposure for preliminary APPROVE rows.
    3. Reduced-exposure feasibility testing for preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows.
    4. Preliminary zero-exposure treatment for preliminary DECLINE rows.
    5. Unresolved exposure treatment for preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW rows.
    6. Approved payment proxy and approved PTI proxy calculations.
    7. Approved Expected Loss proxy calculations.
    8. Counteroffer feasibility failure diagnostics.
    9. The exposure-treatment foundation Section 9 needs for final decision resolution.

No final decision_outcome has been created.
No final decision_path has been created.
No final approval / decline / manual review / counteroffer flags have been created.
No simulated_offer_exposure_flag has been created.
No simulated reason codes have been assigned.
No final approved_amount has been created.
No final counteroffer_amount has been created.
No final approved payment proxy has been created.
No final approved payment-to-income ratio has been created.
No final approved Expected Loss has been created.
No latest-run strategy decision output has been created.
No strategy archive rows have been inserted.
No evidence rows have been inserted.
No matched comparison has been performed.
No strategy frontier has been calculated.
No full QA framework has been built.

Next section:
    Section 9 should consume tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment and resolve final simulated decision
    outcomes, final decision paths, final outcome flags, final approved exposure, final approved
    affordability, and final approved Expected Loss fields.

***************************************************************************************************/


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 9 — FINAL DECISION RESOLUTION LAYER
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Resolve preliminary routing plus exposure-treatment feasibility into final simulated strategy
    outcomes for each synthetic applicant.

    Section 9 answers:

        "Given preliminary routing and exposure-treatment feasibility, what is the final simulated
         strategy outcome for this synthetic applicant?"

    Section 9 does not answer:

        "What simulated reason codes explain the outcome?"

    Section 9 is the final outcome-resolution layer.

    It converts:
        Section 7 preliminary route
        +
        Section 8 exposure-treatment / counteroffer feasibility evidence

    into:
        final simulated decision_outcome,
        final decision_path,
        final decision flags,
        final simulated offer-exposure flag,
        final approved exposure,
        final approved affordability proxy,
        and final approved Expected Loss.

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm required Section 9 dependencies exist.
    2. Read from tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment.
    3. Attach the governed failed_counteroffer_resolution strategy parameter.
    4. Convert preliminary_decision_outcome and counteroffer feasibility into final:
            decision_outcome
            decision_path
            decision_priority_rank
            decision_resolution_source
    5. Create final decision flags:
            approval_flag
            counteroffer_flag
            manual_review_flag
            decline_flag
            simulated_offer_exposure_flag
    6. Create final approved exposure, approved affordability, and approved economics fields:
            approved_amount
            counteroffer_amount
            exposure_reduction_flag
            exposure_reduction_amount
            exposure_reduction_pct
            approved_monthly_payment_proxy
            approved_payment_to_income_ratio
            approved_expected_loss_amount
            approved_el_reduction_amount
            approved_el_reduction_pct
    7. Preserve preliminary routing and exposure-treatment diagnostics.
    8. Validate final outcome and final exposure conventions before simulated reason-code assignment.
    9. Confirm that simulated reason-code fields are not created yet.
    10. Confirm that latest-run table materialization remains deferred to Section 11.
    11. Provide local final decision-resolution diagnostics before Section 10 reason-code assignment.

WHO SHOULD REVIEW THIS SECTION:
    Credit strategy reviewers:
        Confirm that preliminary routes and exposure-treatment feasibility resolve into intuitive final
        simulated strategy outcomes.

    Model governance / validation reviewers:
        Confirm that Section 9 finalizes simulated outcomes without assigning customer-facing
        explanations, modifying archive history, or overstating simulated outputs as operational
        underwriting decisions.

    SQL reviewers:
        Confirm that the final outcome CASE logic is deterministic, parameter-governed, and locally
        validated through final convention checks.

    Portfolio / executive reviewers:
        Use Section 9 diagnostics to understand how the strategy’s final outcome mix emerges after
        counteroffer feasibility and failed-counteroffer resolution are applied.

WHEN TO RUN THIS SECTION:
    Run Section 9 after:

        Section 8 — Approved Exposure and Counteroffer Feasibility Layer

    Section 9 should be run before:

        Section 10 — Simulated Reason-Code Assignment Layer

    Section 9 depends on:

        tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
        tmp_module2_strategy_params

INPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

OUTPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GRAIN:
    One row per application_id for the selected Module 1 scenario / population and active Module 2
    strategy.

FINAL DECISION TAXONOMY:
    Section 9 creates exactly four allowed final decision_outcome values:

        APPROVE
        COUNTEROFFER
        MANUAL_REVIEW
        DECLINE

FINAL RESOLUTION HIERARCHY:
    1. Preliminary APPROVE resolves to final APPROVE.
    2. Preliminary COUNTEROFFER with passed feasibility resolves to final COUNTEROFFER.
    3. Preliminary COUNTEROFFER with failed feasibility resolves using failed_counteroffer_resolution:
            MANUAL_REVIEW
            or
            DECLINE
    4. Preliminary MANUAL_REVIEW resolves to final MANUAL_REVIEW.
    5. Preliminary DECLINE resolves to final DECLINE.
    6. Any unexpected residual path resolves conservatively to final MANUAL_REVIEW.

WHY FINAL DECISION RESOLUTION IS SEPARATED FROM PRELIMINARY ROUTING:
    Section 7 creates preliminary routes before approved exposure exists.

    Section 8 evaluates approved exposure treatment and counteroffer feasibility.

    Section 9 resolves final simulated outcomes using both prior layers.

    This separation protects interpretability:
        preliminary routing explains where the row was sent;
        exposure treatment explains what exposure was feasible;
        final decision resolution explains what simulated strategy outcome remains after feasibility.

WHY SECTION 8 EXPOSURE FEASIBILITY IS REQUIRED BEFORE FINAL COUNTEROFFER RESOLUTION:
    A preliminary COUNTEROFFER route is not final.

    It must pass reduced-exposure feasibility tests before becoming a final COUNTEROFFER outcome.

    Feasibility tests include:
        product maximum approved amount,
        product minimum approved amount,
        minimum counteroffer percent,
        maximum exposure-reduction limit,
        approved PTI target,
        approved Expected Loss cap,
        and rounding convention.

WHY FAILED COUNTEROFFERS USE A GOVERNED RESOLUTION PARAMETER:
    Infeasible counteroffers can resolve to:

        MANUAL_REVIEW
        or
        DECLINE

    The active strategy controls this through:

        failed_counteroffer_resolution

    Default posture:
        MANUAL_REVIEW

    Strategic interpretation:
        MANUAL_REVIEW preserves unresolved failed-counteroffer cases for interpretation.
        DECLINE tests operational review-burden reduction by converting failed counteroffers to
        final no-offer outcomes.

    This is a simulated strategy-control parameter, not production underwriting policy.

WHY DECISION_OUTCOME BECOMES FINAL HERE BUT REASON CODES REMAIN DEFERRED:
    Section 9 establishes the final simulated strategy outcome and final approved-exposure economics.

    Section 10 explains those outcomes using:
        final decision outcome,
        final decision path,
        preliminary routing diagnostics,
        rule-trigger diagnostics,
        exposure-treatment diagnostics,
        counteroffer feasibility diagnostics,
        mixed-signal diagnostics,
        and borderline diagnostics.

    Keeping final outcome assignment separate from simulated reason-code assignment makes both layers
    easier to validate.

APPROVE BOUNDARY:
    APPROVE is a simulated positive offer-exposure outcome.

    APPROVE rows preserve requested exposure and requested-exposure economics:
        approved_amount = requested_amount
        approved_monthly_payment_proxy = requested_monthly_payment_proxy
        approved_payment_to_income_ratio = requested_payment_to_income_ratio
        approved_expected_loss_amount = requested_expected_loss_amount

COUNTEROFFER BOUNDARY:
    COUNTEROFFER is a simulated positive offer-exposure outcome with reduced approved exposure.

    COUNTEROFFER rows should show:
        approved_amount > 0
        approved_amount < requested_amount
        counteroffer_amount = approved_amount
        approved_payment_to_income_ratio <= counteroffer_target_pti
        approved_expected_loss_amount <= product_approved_el_cap
        counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag = TRUE

    COUNTEROFFER does not imply:
        operational negotiation,
        customer acceptance,
        booked exposure,
        funded exposure,
        production approval,
        account creation,
        or real applicant treatment.

MANUAL_REVIEW BOUNDARY:
    MANUAL_REVIEW remains unresolved by design.

    Manual-review rows retain:
        approved_amount = NULL
        counteroffer_amount = NULL
        approved_monthly_payment_proxy = NULL
        approved_payment_to_income_ratio = NULL
        approved_expected_loss_amount = NULL

DECLINE BOUNDARY:
    DECLINE follows the locked zero-exposure convention.

    Decline rows receive:
        approved_amount = 0
        counteroffer_amount = NULL
        approved_monthly_payment_proxy = 0
        approved_payment_to_income_ratio = 0
        approved_expected_loss_amount = 0

SIMULATED OFFER EXPOSURE BOUNDARY:
    simulated_offer_exposure_flag means the simulated strategy output includes positive offer exposure
    for the synthetic applicant.

    It is TRUE for:
        APPROVE
        COUNTEROFFER

    It is FALSE for:
        MANUAL_REVIEW
        DECLINE

    It does not imply:
        operational account creation,
        booked exposure,
        funded exposure,
        production approval,
        customer treatment,
        or real applicant treatment.

REQUESTED VS APPROVED EXPECTED LOSS:
    requested_expected_loss_amount is requested-exposure Expected Loss from Module 1.

    approved_expected_loss_amount is approved-exposure Expected Loss from Module 2 after final
    simulated exposure treatment.

    Section 9 finalizes approved Expected Loss convention, but it does not recalculate estimated_pd.

ESTIMATED_PD BOUNDARY:
    estimated_pd remains the finalized Module 1 SQL field and is interpreted as the synthetic
    estimated-PD proxy.

    Module 2 does not recalculate estimated_pd.

REASON-CODE BOUNDARY:
    Section 9 does not assign simulated reason codes.

    It does not create:
        primary_reason_code
        secondary_reason_code
        tertiary_reason_code
        triggered_reason_code_list
        reason_priority_rank
        primary_reason_family
        reason_code_count

LATEST-RUN / ARCHIVE BOUNDARY:
    Section 9 does not create:

        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

    Section 9 does not insert rows into:

        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive

    Latest-run output materialization remains deferred to Section 11.
    Archive persistence remains deferred to Section 12.

SQL CONCEPTS TAUGHT IN THIS SECTION:
    CTE chain:
        active_strategy_params
            selects the final-resolution strategy control.

        resolution_inputs
            attaches the governed failed_counteroffer_resolution value.

        decision_core
            converts preliminary route + feasibility into final outcome labels.

        decision_flags
            creates reconciled Boolean outcome flags.

        final_exposure_assignment
            applies final exposure, affordability, and Expected Loss conventions.

    CASE hierarchy:
        Encodes final simulated outcome resolution.

    CROSS JOIN:
        Attaches one active strategy parameter row to every exposure-treatment row.

    IS DISTINCT FROM:
        Used in gatekeepers to compare NULL safely.

    pg_attribute:
        Confirms simulated reason-code fields and latest-run materialization did not appear early.

GOVERNANCE ROLE:
    Section 9 locks the final simulated outcome taxonomy and final output conventions before
    explanation codes, latest-run materialization, archive persistence, comparison, QA, and evidence
    capture occur.

COMMON MISUSE TO AVOID:
    Do not interpret decision_outcome as a real applicant decision.
    Do not interpret decision_path as customer communication.
    Do not interpret simulated_offer_exposure_flag as booked or funded exposure.
    Do not interpret approved_expected_loss_amount as a production loss forecast.
    Do not interpret MANUAL_REVIEW as completed operational review.
    Do not infer reason-code explanations before Section 10.

***************************************************************************************************/



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 9.0 — SECTION 9 DEPENDENCY PREFLIGHT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that Section 8 exposure-treatment output and the active failed-counteroffer strategy
    control are available before final decision resolution begins.

    Section 9.0 answers:

        "Can Section 9 safely convert Section 8 exposure treatment into final simulated outcomes?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment exists.
    2. Confirm tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment contains rows.
    3. Confirm application_id is unique before final decision fields are added.
    4. Confirm tmp_module2_strategy_params exists.
    5. Confirm exactly one active strategy parameter row exists.
    6. Confirm failed_counteroffer_resolution is populated and valid.
    7. Confirm key Section 8 fields required for final resolution are populated.
    8. Fail clearly if Section 8 or Section 2 has not been run.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 9.0 does not create final decisions.
    Section 9.0 does not assign reason codes.
    Section 9.0 does not create latest-run output.
    Section 9.0 does not insert archive rows.
    Section 9.0 does not modify persistent tables.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_stage5_exists BOOLEAN;
    v_strategy_params_exists BOOLEAN;

    v_stage5_row_count BIGINT;
    v_stage5_distinct_application_count BIGINT;

    v_active_strategy_count BIGINT;
    v_bad_failed_counteroffer_resolution_count BIGINT;
    v_required_stage5_gap_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Dependency check: Section 8 exposure-treatment stage must exist.

    SQL mechanics:
        TO_REGCLASS checks whether the temporary object exists.

    Business interpretation:
        Section 9 must consume the exposure-treatment layer, not preliminary routing directly.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COALESCE(
        TO_REGCLASS('pg_temp.tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment'),
        TO_REGCLASS('tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment')
    ) IS NOT NULL
    INTO v_stage5_exists;

    IF v_stage5_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment is required. Run Section 8 before Section 9.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Dependency check: active strategy parameter table must exist.

    Business interpretation:
        Section 9 needs failed_counteroffer_resolution from the active strategy card.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COALESCE(
        TO_REGCLASS('pg_temp.tmp_module2_strategy_params'),
        TO_REGCLASS('tmp_module2_strategy_params')
    ) IS NOT NULL
    INTO v_strategy_params_exists;

    IF v_strategy_params_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: tmp_module2_strategy_params is required. Run Section 2 before Section 9.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: Section 8 exposure-treatment stage must contain rows.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage5_row_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment;

    IF v_stage5_row_count <= 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment contains zero rows.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id must be unique before final outcome fields are added.

    Section 9 should add final decision-resolution fields only.

    It should not repair upstream row-grain problems.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_stage5_distinct_application_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment;

    IF v_stage5_distinct_application_count <> v_stage5_row_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment is not unique at application_id. Rows=%, distinct application_id=%.',
            v_stage5_row_count,
            v_stage5_distinct_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: exactly one active strategy parameter row.

    Business interpretation:
        Final resolution must use one and only one failed-counteroffer strategy control.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_active_strategy_count
    FROM tmp_module2_strategy_params
    WHERE active_strategy_flag IS TRUE;

    IF v_active_strategy_count <> 1 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: expected exactly one active strategy parameter row, found %.',
            v_active_strategy_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: failed_counteroffer_resolution must be valid.

    Allowed values:
        MANUAL_REVIEW
        DECLINE
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_bad_failed_counteroffer_resolution_count
    FROM tmp_module2_strategy_params
    WHERE active_strategy_flag IS TRUE
      AND (
            failed_counteroffer_resolution IS NULL
         OR failed_counteroffer_resolution NOT IN ('MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
      );

    IF v_bad_failed_counteroffer_resolution_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: active failed_counteroffer_resolution must be MANUAL_REVIEW or DECLINE.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: key Section 8 fields required for final resolution must be populated.

    Non-counteroffer rows are allowed to have NULL counteroffer-specific fields.

    Manual-review rows are expected to have unresolved preliminary exposure fields.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_required_stage5_gap_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment
    WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome IS NULL
       OR preliminary_decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
       OR preliminary_decision_path IS NULL
       OR preliminary_decision_priority_rank IS NULL
       OR preliminary_route_reason_family IS NULL
       OR preliminary_route_trigger_count IS NULL

       OR exposure_treatment_status IS NULL
       OR exposure_treatment_path IS NULL
       OR exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary IS NULL
       OR counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag IS NULL

       OR requested_amount IS NULL
       OR requested_monthly_payment_proxy IS NULL
       OR requested_payment_to_income_ratio IS NULL
       OR requested_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
       OR estimated_pd IS NULL
       OR estimated_lgd IS NULL

       OR (
            preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
            AND (
                approved_amount_preliminary IS NULL
             OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary IS NULL
             OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary IS NULL
             OR approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary IS NULL
            )
       )

       OR (
            preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
            AND (
                approved_amount_preliminary IS NULL
             OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary IS NULL
             OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary IS NULL
             OR approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary IS NULL
            )
       )

       OR (
            preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND (
                counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS NULL
             OR counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count IS NULL
             OR (
                    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                AND (
                        approved_amount_preliminary IS NULL
                     OR counteroffer_amount_preliminary IS NULL
                     OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary IS NULL
                     OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary IS NULL
                     OR approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary IS NULL
                   )
                )
             OR (
                    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
                AND counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason IS NULL
                )
            )
       );

    IF v_required_stage5_gap_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: % Section 8 row(s) are missing fields required for final decision resolution.',
            v_required_stage5_gap_count;
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 9.1 — CLEAN RESET OF SECTION 9 STAGING OBJECT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Drop the Section 9 final decision-resolution stage before rebuilding it.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Remove only the temporary Section 9 staging table.

WHY THIS MATTERS:
    A partial rerun should not allow stale final decision-resolution rows to remain available to
    Section 10.

    Section 10 assumes tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution reflects the current:
        Section 8 exposure-treatment output,
        active failed-counteroffer resolution setting,
        and final outcome convention logic.

SQL MECHANICS:
    DROP TABLE IF EXISTS makes the reset rerunnable.

    If the table does not exist, PostgreSQL does not error.

BOUNDARY:
    This drop affects only the temporary Section 9 staging object.

    It does not modify Module 1 outputs.
    It does not modify Module 2 latest-run output.
    It does not modify Module 2 archive output.
    It does not modify evidence tables.
    It does not modify registry tables.

****************************************************************************************************/

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 9.2 — CREATE FINAL DECISION RESOLUTION TABLE
****************************************************************************************************

TABLE:
    tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GRAIN:
    One row per application_id for the selected Module 1 scenario / population and active Module 2
    strategy.

INPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment

OUTPUT:
    All Section 8 fields plus final decision, final flag, final approved exposure, final approved
    affordability, and final approved economics fields.

SQL DESIGN:
    This section uses a CTE chain so final outcome resolution is readable and auditable.

    The chain is:

        active_strategy_params
            selects failed_counteroffer_resolution from the active strategy card.

        resolution_inputs
            attaches the governed failed-counteroffer final-resolution parameter.

        decision_core
            resolves final outcome labels, paths, priorities, and resolution sources.

        decision_flags
            creates final outcome flags and simulated_offer_exposure_flag.

        final_exposure_assignment
            applies final approved exposure, affordability, and Expected Loss conventions.

WHY SELECT * IS ACCEPTABLE HERE:
    This is a temporary staging layer, not a permanent output table.

    Section 9 intentionally preserves all prior diagnostics plus final decision-resolution fields for
    Section 10 reason-code assignment.

    Permanent output selection is handled later with an explicit field list in Section 11.

***************************************************************************************************/

CREATE TEMP TABLE tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
ON COMMIT PRESERVE ROWS
AS
WITH active_strategy_params AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: active_strategy_params

    Purpose:
        Select the governed failed-counteroffer resolution strategy control.

    Business interpretation:
        This parameter decides how a preliminary COUNTEROFFER row resolves when Section 8 determines
        that no feasible reduced-exposure offer exists.

    Allowed values:
        MANUAL_REVIEW
        DECLINE
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        failed_counteroffer_resolution
    FROM tmp_module2_strategy_params
    WHERE active_strategy_flag IS TRUE
    LIMIT 1
),

resolution_inputs AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: resolution_inputs

    Purpose:
        Attach failed_counteroffer_resolution to every Section 8 row.

    SQL mechanics:
        CROSS JOIN is safe because Section 9.0 confirms exactly one active strategy parameter row.

    Boundary:
        No final outcome is assigned in this CTE.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        et.*,
        p.failed_counteroffer_resolution
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment et

    CROSS JOIN active_strategy_params p
),

decision_core AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: decision_core

    Purpose:
        Resolve final decision labels from preliminary route + counteroffer feasibility.

    SQL mechanics:
        CASE evaluates top to bottom.

    Business interpretation:
        This is where final simulated decision_outcome becomes locked for the current row.

    Boundary:
        Reason codes are still not assigned here.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        ri.*,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final decision_outcome.

        Allowed final values:
            APPROVE
            COUNTEROFFER
            MANUAL_REVIEW
            DECLINE
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 'APPROVE'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
             AND ri.failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
             AND ri.failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 'DECLINE'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 'DECLINE'

            ELSE 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
        END AS decision_outcome,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final decision_path.

        decision_path is an internal simulated strategy path label.

        It is not:
            customer communication,
            regulatory notice language,
            adverse-action reason text,
            or production compliance language.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 'APPROVE_AS_REQUESTED'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBLE'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
             AND ri.failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
             AND ri.failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE_DECLINE'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
             AND ri.preliminary_decision_path = 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_STRUCTURE_REVIEW'
                THEN 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_STRUCTURE_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
             AND ri.preliminary_decision_path = 'MANUAL_REVIEW_CANDIDATE'
                THEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW_CANDIDATE'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
             AND ri.preliminary_decision_path = 'RESIDUAL_STRATEGY_REVIEW'
                THEN 'RESIDUAL_STRATEGY_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW_UNRESOLVED'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
             AND ri.preliminary_decision_path IN (
                    'HARD_POLICY_STOP',
                    'SEVERE_SYNTHETIC_RISK',
                    'SEVERE_DTI_CAPACITY'
                 )
                THEN ri.preliminary_decision_path

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 'PRELIMINARY_DECLINE_RESOLVED'

            ELSE 'RESIDUAL_FINAL_REVIEW'
        END AS decision_path,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final decision_priority_rank.

        Lower values represent more severe or higher-priority final resolution paths.

        This rank is an internal diagnostic.
        It is not a regulatory severity score.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
             AND ri.preliminary_decision_path = 'HARD_POLICY_STOP'
                THEN 1

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
             AND ri.preliminary_decision_path = 'SEVERE_SYNTHETIC_RISK'
                THEN 2

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
             AND ri.preliminary_decision_path = 'SEVERE_DTI_CAPACITY'
                THEN 3

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 4

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
             AND ri.failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 5

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
             AND ri.failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN 6

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN 7

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 8

            ELSE 9
        END AS decision_priority_rank,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        decision_resolution_source.

        This describes which upstream layer / control resolved the final outcome.

        It helps Section 10 reason-code logic and Section 14 QA explain the final output.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 'PRELIMINARY_APPROVE_ROUTE'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBILITY_PASSED'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
             AND ri.failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBILITY_FAILED_TO_REVIEW'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
             AND ri.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
             AND ri.failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBILITY_FAILED_TO_DECLINE'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN 'PRELIMINARY_MANUAL_REVIEW_ROUTE'

            WHEN ri.preliminary_decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 'PRELIMINARY_DECLINE_ROUTE'

            ELSE 'FINAL_RESOLUTION_FALLBACK_TO_REVIEW'
        END AS decision_resolution_source

    FROM resolution_inputs ri
),

decision_flags AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: decision_flags

    Purpose:
        Convert final decision_outcome into final Boolean flags.

    SQL mechanics:
        Each flag is defined directly from decision_outcome.

        The Section 9.3 gatekeeper later confirms exactly one final decision flag is TRUE per row.

    Business interpretation:
        simulated_offer_exposure_flag is TRUE only for positive simulated offer-exposure outcomes:
            APPROVE
            COUNTEROFFER
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        dc.*,

        (dc.decision_outcome = 'APPROVE')
            AS approval_flag,

        (dc.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
            AS counteroffer_flag,

        (dc.decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW')
            AS manual_review_flag,

        (dc.decision_outcome = 'DECLINE')
            AS decline_flag,

        (dc.decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER'))
            AS simulated_offer_exposure_flag

    FROM decision_core dc
),

final_exposure_assignment AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: final_exposure_assignment

    Purpose:
        Apply final approved exposure, affordability, and approved Expected Loss conventions.

    Business interpretation:
        APPROVE:
            preserve requested exposure and requested economics.

        COUNTEROFFER:
            use feasible reduced-exposure economics from Section 8.

        MANUAL_REVIEW:
            remain unresolved with NULL final approved exposure economics.

        DECLINE:
            use locked zero-exposure convention.

    Boundary:
        These are simulated strategy output fields.

        They are not booked balances, funded exposures, or operational account records.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        df.*,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final approved_amount.

        APPROVE:
            requested amount.

        COUNTEROFFER:
            feasible reduced amount from Section 8.

        MANUAL_REVIEW:
            unresolved.

        DECLINE:
            zero exposure.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN df.requested_amount

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN df.approved_amount_preliminary

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_amount,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final counteroffer_amount.

        Populated only for final COUNTEROFFER.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN df.counteroffer_amount_preliminary
            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS counteroffer_amount,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final exposure_reduction_flag.

        TRUE only when a positive simulated offer exists with reduced exposure.

        DECLINE has 100% no-offer exposure reduction amount, but it is not a reduced positive offer.
        Therefore exposure_reduction_flag remains FALSE for DECLINE.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN TRUE
            ELSE FALSE
        END AS exposure_reduction_flag,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final exposure_reduction_amount.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN df.exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN df.requested_amount

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS exposure_reduction_amount,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final exposure_reduction_pct.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN df.exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 1.0::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS exposure_reduction_pct,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final approved_monthly_payment_proxy.

        Boundary:
            This remains a strategy-simulation payment proxy, not a contractual payment schedule.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN df.requested_monthly_payment_proxy

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN df.approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_monthly_payment_proxy,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final approved_payment_to_income_ratio.

        Boundary:
            This is the simulated approved-exposure affordability proxy.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN df.requested_payment_to_income_ratio

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN df.approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_payment_to_income_ratio,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final approved_expected_loss_amount.

        APPROVE:
            requested-exposure Expected Loss.

        COUNTEROFFER:
            reduced approved-exposure Expected Loss from Section 8.

        MANUAL_REVIEW:
            unresolved.

        DECLINE:
            zero approved exposure Expected Loss.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN df.requested_expected_loss_amount

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN df.approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_expected_loss_amount,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final approved_el_reduction_amount.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN df.approved_el_reduction_amount_preliminary

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN df.requested_expected_loss_amount

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_el_reduction_amount,


        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final approved_el_reduction_pct.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                THEN 0::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                THEN df.approved_el_reduction_pct_preliminary

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                THEN NULL::NUMERIC

            WHEN df.decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                THEN CASE
                    WHEN df.requested_expected_loss_amount > 0 THEN 1.0::NUMERIC
                    ELSE 0::NUMERIC
                END

            ELSE NULL::NUMERIC
        END AS approved_el_reduction_pct

    FROM decision_flags df
)

SELECT *
FROM final_exposure_assignment;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 9.3 — LOCAL FAIL-FAST CHECKS FOR FINAL DECISION RESOLUTION
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that Section 9 produced complete, internally consistent, final simulated strategy
    outcomes before Section 10 assigns simulated reason codes.

    Section 9.3 answers:

        "Did Section 9 preserve applicant grain, assign exactly one final outcome, apply final
         exposure conventions, apply failed-counteroffer resolution, and avoid creating reason-code
         or latest-run output fields too early?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm row count is unchanged from tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment.
    2. Confirm application_id remains unique.
    3. Confirm final decision fields are complete and valid.
    4. Confirm exactly one final decision flag is TRUE per row.
    5. Confirm simulated_offer_exposure_flag reconciles to final decision_outcome.
    6. Confirm final APPROVE convention.
    7. Confirm final COUNTEROFFER convention.
    8. Confirm final MANUAL_REVIEW unresolved convention.
    9. Confirm final DECLINE zero-exposure convention.
    10. Confirm failed_counteroffer_resolution was applied correctly.
    11. Confirm Section 9 did not create simulated reason-code fields.
    12. Confirm Section 9 did not create latest-run output.

LOCAL GATEKEEPER BOUNDARY:
    These are local Section 9 staging gatekeepers only.

    They are not:
        simulated reason-code validation,
        latest-run materialization validation,
        archive validation,
        matched strategy comparison,
        full Module 2 QA,
        strategy frontier review,
        or Validation Summary evidence by themselves.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_stage5_count BIGINT;
    v_stage6_count BIGINT;
    v_stage6_distinct_app_count BIGINT;
    v_duplicate_application_count BIGINT;

    v_decision_completeness_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_flag_reconciliation_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_offer_flag_failure_count BIGINT;

    v_approve_convention_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_counteroffer_convention_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_manual_review_convention_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_decline_convention_failure_count BIGINT;

    v_failed_counteroffer_resolution_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_forbidden_reason_column_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: row count must be unchanged from Section 8 to Section 9.

    Business purpose:
        Section 9 should add final decision-resolution fields only.

        It should not filter applicants or duplicate applicants.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage5_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment;

    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage6_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution;

    IF v_stage6_count <> v_stage5_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: row count changed from Section 8 to Section 9. Stage 5 rows: %, Stage 6 rows: %.',
            v_stage5_count,
            v_stage6_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id remains unique.

    Business purpose:
        Duplicate application_id values would duplicate simulated reason codes, latest-run output
        rows, archive rows, QA counts, comparison results, and evidence capture.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_stage6_distinct_app_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution;

    IF v_stage6_distinct_app_count <> v_stage6_count THEN
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_duplicate_application_count
        FROM (
            SELECT application_id
            FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
            GROUP BY application_id
            HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
        ) d;

        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: application_id uniqueness was not preserved. Stage 6 rows: %, distinct application_id count: %, duplicate application_id group count: %.',
            v_stage6_count,
            v_stage6_distinct_app_count,
            v_duplicate_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: final decision fields must be complete and valid.

    Expected:
        decision_outcome is one of:
            APPROVE,
            COUNTEROFFER,
            MANUAL_REVIEW,
            DECLINE.

        decision_path, decision_priority_rank, and decision_resolution_source are populated.

        failed_counteroffer_resolution is attached and valid.

    Boundary:
        These are internal simulated strategy labels, not customer communications.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_decision_completeness_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
    WHERE decision_outcome IS NULL
       OR decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
       OR decision_path IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(decision_path), '') IS NULL
       OR decision_priority_rank IS NULL
       OR decision_priority_rank <= 0
       OR decision_resolution_source IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(decision_resolution_source), '') IS NULL
       OR failed_counteroffer_resolution IS NULL
       OR failed_counteroffer_resolution NOT IN ('MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE');

    IF v_decision_completeness_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: % row(s) have null or invalid final decision fields.',
            v_decision_completeness_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: exactly one final decision flag must be TRUE and all flags must reconcile to
    decision_outcome.

    Expected:
        approval_flag TRUE only for APPROVE.
        counteroffer_flag TRUE only for COUNTEROFFER.
        manual_review_flag TRUE only for MANUAL_REVIEW.
        decline_flag TRUE only for DECLINE.

    SQL mechanics:
        Boolean flags are cast to INT and summed.
        Exactly one TRUE flag should produce a sum of 1.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_flag_reconciliation_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
    WHERE (
            COALESCE(approval_flag::INT, 0)
            + COALESCE(counteroffer_flag::INT, 0)
            + COALESCE(manual_review_flag::INT, 0)
            + COALESCE(decline_flag::INT, 0)
          ) <> 1
       OR approval_flag IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome = 'APPROVE')
       OR counteroffer_flag IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
       OR manual_review_flag IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW')
       OR decline_flag IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome = 'DECLINE');

    IF v_flag_reconciliation_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: % row(s) have final decision flag reconciliation failures.',
            v_flag_reconciliation_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: simulated_offer_exposure_flag must reconcile to decision_outcome.

    Expected:
        TRUE for APPROVE and COUNTEROFFER.

        FALSE for MANUAL_REVIEW and DECLINE.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_offer_flag_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
    WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag
          IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER'));

    IF v_offer_flag_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: % row(s) have simulated_offer_exposure_flag reconciliation failures.',
            v_offer_flag_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: APPROVE final convention.

    Business interpretation:
        APPROVE preserves requested exposure and requested-exposure economics.

    Expected:
        approved_amount = requested_amount.
        counteroffer_amount IS NULL.
        approved payment / PTI / Expected Loss equal requested equivalents.
        simulated_offer_exposure_flag = TRUE.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_approve_convention_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
      AND (
            approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_amount
         OR counteroffer_amount IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
         OR exposure_reduction_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR exposure_reduction_pct IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS DISTINCT FROM requested_monthly_payment_proxy
         OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS DISTINCT FROM requested_payment_to_income_ratio
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_expected_loss_amount
         OR approved_el_reduction_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_el_reduction_pct IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
      );

    IF v_approve_convention_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: % final APPROVE row(s) violate as-requested approval conventions.',
            v_approve_convention_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: COUNTEROFFER final convention.

    Business interpretation:
        COUNTEROFFER is a feasible reduced-exposure positive simulated offer.

    Expected:
        approved_amount > 0.
        approved_amount < requested_amount.
        counteroffer_amount = approved_amount.
        approved PTI <= counteroffer_target_pti.
        approved Expected Loss <= product_approved_el_cap.
        counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag = TRUE.
        simulated_offer_exposure_flag = TRUE.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_counteroffer_convention_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND (
            preliminary_decision_outcome <> 'COUNTEROFFER'
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
         OR counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_amount IS NULL
         OR approved_amount <= 0
         OR approved_amount >= requested_amount
         OR counteroffer_amount IS DISTINCT FROM approved_amount
         OR exposure_reduction_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
         OR exposure_reduction_amount IS NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_amount <= 0
         OR exposure_reduction_pct IS NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_pct <= 0
         OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS NULL
         OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS NULL
         OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio > counteroffer_target_pti
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount < 0
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount > requested_expected_loss_amount
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount > product_approved_el_cap
         OR approved_el_reduction_amount IS NULL
         OR approved_el_reduction_amount < 0
         OR (
                requested_expected_loss_amount > 0
            AND approved_el_reduction_pct IS NULL
            )
         OR simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
      );

    IF v_counteroffer_convention_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: % final COUNTEROFFER row(s) violate reduced-exposure counteroffer conventions.',
            v_counteroffer_convention_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: MANUAL_REVIEW final convention.

    Business interpretation:
        MANUAL_REVIEW is unresolved by design.

    Expected:
        final approved exposure fields remain NULL.
        simulated_offer_exposure_flag = FALSE.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_manual_review_convention_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            approved_amount IS NOT NULL
         OR counteroffer_amount IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
         OR exposure_reduction_amount IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_pct IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_el_reduction_amount IS NOT NULL
         OR approved_el_reduction_pct IS NOT NULL
         OR simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
      );

    IF v_manual_review_convention_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: % final MANUAL_REVIEW row(s) violate unresolved conventions.',
            v_manual_review_convention_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: DECLINE final convention.

    Business interpretation:
        DECLINE is a final no-offer outcome using locked zero-exposure conventions.

    Expected:
        approved_amount = 0.
        approved payment / PTI / Expected Loss = 0.
        simulated_offer_exposure_flag = FALSE.

    Note:
        exposure_reduction_flag remains FALSE because DECLINE is not a reduced positive offer.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_decline_convention_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND (
            approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR counteroffer_amount IS NOT NULL
         OR exposure_reduction_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
         OR exposure_reduction_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_amount
         OR exposure_reduction_pct IS DISTINCT FROM 1.0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
         OR approved_el_reduction_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_expected_loss_amount
         OR approved_el_reduction_pct IS DISTINCT FROM CASE
                WHEN requested_expected_loss_amount > 0 THEN 1.0::NUMERIC
                ELSE 0::NUMERIC
            END
         OR simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
      );

    IF v_decline_convention_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: % final DECLINE row(s) violate zero-exposure conventions.',
            v_decline_convention_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: failed counteroffer resolution must follow governed parameter.

    For preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows where counteroffer feasibility failed:
        failed_counteroffer_resolution = MANUAL_REVIEW
            must resolve to MANUAL_REVIEW.

        failed_counteroffer_resolution = DECLINE
            must resolve to DECLINE.

    This check ensures the active strategy parameter, not hidden downstream logic, controls failed
    counteroffer final resolution.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_failed_counteroffer_resolution_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
    WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
      AND (
            (
                failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                AND NOT (
                    decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                    AND decision_path = 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE_REVIEW'
                    AND decision_resolution_source = 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBILITY_FAILED_TO_REVIEW'
                )
            )
         OR (
                failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'DECLINE'
                AND NOT (
                    decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                    AND decision_path = 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE_DECLINE'
                    AND decision_resolution_source = 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBILITY_FAILED_TO_DECLINE'
                )
            )
      );

    IF v_failed_counteroffer_resolution_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: % failed preliminary COUNTEROFFER row(s) violate failed_counteroffer_resolution conventions.',
            v_failed_counteroffer_resolution_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: Section 9 must not create simulated reason-code fields yet.

    Business purpose:
        Simulated reason codes are assigned in Section 10, after final decision_outcome and final
        exposure fields exist.

    SQL mechanics:
        pg_attribute inspects the physical columns of the temporary table.

        If any reason-code field exists, Section 9 has crossed its boundary.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_forbidden_reason_column_count
    FROM pg_attribute
    WHERE attrelid = 'tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution'::REGCLASS
      AND attnum > 0
      AND NOT attisdropped
      AND attname IN (
            'primary_reason_code',
            'secondary_reason_code',
            'tertiary_reason_code',
            'triggered_reason_code_list',
            'reason_priority_rank',
            'primary_reason_family',
            'reason_code_count'
      );

    IF v_forbidden_reason_column_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: simulated reason-code field(s) were created before Section 10.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: latest-run output table must not exist yet.

    Section 11 creates credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions.

    Why this matters:
        If latest-run output already exists while Section 9 is being rerun, a user could accidentally
        review stale Section 11 output instead of the current staging output.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    IF TO_REGCLASS('credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions') IS NOT NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 9 failure: final latest-run strategy_decisions table exists before Section 11. Run the pipeline from Section 1 or drop/rebuild latest-run output through Section 11.';
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 9.4 — LOCAL FINAL DECISION RESOLUTION SANITY CHECKS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide lightweight diagnostics for Section 9 final decision resolution.

    Section 9.4 answers:

        "What final simulated outcomes did Section 9 assign, how were failed preliminary
         counteroffers resolved, and do final exposure conventions look ready for reason-code
         assignment?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    Display review outputs for:
        final decision outcome distribution,
        final decision path distribution,
        decision resolution source,
        simulated offer-exposure flag,
        preliminary × final decision migration,
        failed counteroffer resolution,
        final decision by product,
        final decision by score band,
        final decision by product × score,
        final decision by synthetic risk tier,
        final decision by requested PTI bucket,
        final decision by DTI bucket,
        final decision by requested exposure tier,
        final decision by requested Expected Loss tier,
        mixed-signal final decision behavior,
        borderline final decision behavior,
        final requested vs approved exposure behavior,
        final requested vs approved affordability behavior,
        final requested vs approved Expected Loss behavior,
        and one compact readiness summary.

INTERPRETATION:
    These are staging diagnostics only.

    They should not be interpreted as:
        simulated reason-code validation,
        latest-run output validation,
        archive validation,
        matched strategy comparison,
        strategy frontier evidence,
        full Module 2 QA,
        or Validation Summary acceptance.

****************************************************************************************************/



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.1 Count by decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Show the final simulated strategy outcome distribution.

Boundary:
    decision_outcome is final for this simulated strategy run, but it is not a real applicant decision.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.2 Count by decision_path.

Purpose:
    Show final internal decision path labels.

Boundary:
    decision_path is internal strategy explanation support.

    It is not customer communication language.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_path,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY decision_path

ORDER BY decision_path;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.3 Count by decision_resolution_source.

Purpose:
    Show which upstream source resolved the final decision.

Interpretation:
    This helps reviewers distinguish:
        preliminary approval route;
        preliminary decline route;
        passed counteroffer feasibility;
        failed counteroffer to review;
        failed counteroffer to decline;
        preliminary manual review route.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_resolution_source,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY decision_resolution_source

ORDER BY decision_resolution_source;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.4 Count by simulated_offer_exposure_flag.

Purpose:
    Review simulated positive offer-exposure rows.

Expected:
    TRUE only for APPROVE and COUNTEROFFER.

Boundary:
    simulated_offer_exposure_flag does not imply booked or funded exposure.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    simulated_offer_exposure_flag,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY simulated_offer_exposure_flag

ORDER BY simulated_offer_exposure_flag;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.5 Preliminary decision outcome × final decision outcome.

Purpose:
    Show how preliminary routes resolved into final outcomes.

Key interpretation:
    Preliminary COUNTEROFFER can resolve to:
        final COUNTEROFFER when feasibility passes;
        final MANUAL_REVIEW or DECLINE when feasibility fails, depending on failed_counteroffer_resolution.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    preliminary_decision_outcome,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(
            SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (PARTITION BY preliminary_decision_outcome),
            0
        ),
        2
    ) AS pct_within_preliminary_outcome

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    preliminary_decision_outcome,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE preliminary_decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.6 Failed counteroffer final resolution summary.

Purpose:
    Review how infeasible preliminary counteroffers resolved.

Expected:
    If failed_counteroffer_resolution = MANUAL_REVIEW:
        failed preliminary counteroffers resolve to MANUAL_REVIEW.

    If failed_counteroffer_resolution = DECLINE:
        failed preliminary counteroffers resolve to DECLINE.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    failed_counteroffer_resolution,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason,
    decision_outcome,
    decision_path,
    decision_resolution_source,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'

GROUP BY
    failed_counteroffer_resolution,
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason,
    decision_outcome,
    decision_path,
    decision_resolution_source

ORDER BY
    counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,
    decision_outcome,
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.7 Product × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final simulated outcome distribution by product.

Interpretation:
    Product behavior should be explainable through product policy, requested exposure, affordability,
    LGD, requested Expected Loss, and counteroffer feasibility.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    product_type_policy_key,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(approved_amount) AS avg_approved_amount,
    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.8 Score band × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcome behavior by score-band policy key.

Boundary:
    score band supports borrower-quality interpretation but is not the only decision driver.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    score_band_policy_key,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(credit_score) AS avg_credit_score,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    score_band_policy_key,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE score_band_policy_key
        WHEN 'SUPER_PRIME' THEN 1
        WHEN 'PRIME' THEN 2
        WHEN 'NEAR_PRIME' THEN 3
        WHEN 'SUBPRIME' THEN 4
        WHEN 'DEEP_SUBPRIME' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.9 Product × score segment × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcome behavior across the key product × score evidence dimension.

Interpretation:
    This preview supports later Section 16 product × score segment evidence.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    product_type_policy_key,
    score_band_policy_key,
    product_score_policy_segment,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS avg_approved_amount_all_rows,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0)) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_all_rows

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    score_band_policy_key,
    product_score_policy_segment,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    CASE score_band_policy_key
        WHEN 'SUPER_PRIME' THEN 1
        WHEN 'PRIME' THEN 2
        WHEN 'NEAR_PRIME' THEN 3
        WHEN 'SUBPRIME' THEN 4
        WHEN 'DEEP_SUBPRIME' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.10 Synthetic risk tier × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcomes by synthetic estimated-risk tier.

Boundary:
    estimated_pd remains the Module 1 SQL field and is interpreted as the synthetic estimated-PD
    proxy.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    strategy_risk_tier,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(synthetic_risk_trigger_count) AS avg_synthetic_risk_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    strategy_risk_tier,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE strategy_risk_tier
        WHEN 'LOW_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.11 Requested PTI bucket × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcomes by requested-structure affordability bucket.

Boundary:
    requested_payment_to_income_ratio is requested PTI.

    approved_payment_to_income_ratio is final approved-exposure PTI proxy.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    requested_pti_bucket,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    requested_pti_bucket,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE requested_pti_bucket
        WHEN 'LOW_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.12 DTI bucket × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcomes by existing-obligation capacity bucket.

Boundary:
    DTI is not directly counteroffer-adjustable in Module 2 V1.0.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    dti_bucket,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(debt_to_income_ratio) AS avg_debt_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(dti_trigger_count) AS avg_dti_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    dti_bucket,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE dti_bucket
        WHEN 'LOW_DTI' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_DTI' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_DTI' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_DTI' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_DTI' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.13 Requested exposure tier × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcomes by requested exposure tier.

Boundary:
    requested_amount is original requested exposure.

    approved_amount is final simulated approved exposure.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    requested_exposure_tier,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(approved_amount) AS avg_approved_amount,
    AVG(exposure_reduction_pct) AS avg_exposure_reduction_pct

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    requested_exposure_tier,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE requested_exposure_tier
        WHEN 'BELOW_PRODUCT_MINIMUM' THEN 1
        WHEN 'LOW_REQUESTED_EXPOSURE' THEN 2
        WHEN 'WITHIN_PRODUCT_APPROVAL_CAP' THEN 3
        WHEN 'WITHIN_PRODUCT_LIMITS' THEN 4
        WHEN 'ABOVE_PRODUCT_APPROVAL_CAP' THEN 5
        WHEN 'EXTREME_REQUESTED_EXPOSURE' THEN 6
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.14 Requested Expected Loss tier × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcomes by requested-exposure Expected Loss tier.

Boundary:
    requested_expected_loss_amount is requested-exposure Expected Loss.

    approved_expected_loss_amount is final approved-exposure Expected Loss.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    requested_expected_loss_tier,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(approved_el_reduction_pct) AS avg_approved_el_reduction_pct

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    requested_expected_loss_tier,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE requested_expected_loss_tier
        WHEN 'LOW_REQUESTED_EL' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_REQUESTED_EL' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_REQUESTED_EL' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_REQUESTED_EL' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_EL' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.15 Mixed-signal profile × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcome behavior for realistic overlapping applicant profiles.

Boundary:
    mixed_signal_profile_type is diagnostic, not final route logic by itself.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    mixed_signal_profile_type,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(mixed_signal_condition_count) AS avg_mixed_signal_condition_count,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    mixed_signal_profile_type,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    mixed_signal_profile_type,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.16 Borderline profile flag × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcome behavior for threshold-adjacent profiles.

Boundary:
    borderline_profile_flag is diagnostic only.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    borderline_profile_flag,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY
    borderline_profile_flag,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    borderline_profile_flag,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.17 Average requested_amount by decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review original requested exposure by final simulated outcome.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    SUM(requested_amount) AS total_requested_amount
FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
GROUP BY decision_outcome
ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.18 Average approved_amount by decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final approved exposure by final simulated outcome.

Expected:
    APPROVE:
        approved_amount equals requested_amount.

    COUNTEROFFER:
        approved_amount is positive and below requested_amount.

    MANUAL_REVIEW:
        approved_amount is NULL.

    DECLINE:
        approved_amount is zero.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(approved_amount) AS avg_approved_amount,
    SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS total_approved_amount
FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
GROUP BY decision_outcome
ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.19 Average requested PTI and approved PTI by decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final affordability treatment by outcome.

Boundary:
    approved_payment_to_income_ratio is a final strategy-simulation affordability proxy.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio)
        AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,

    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio)
        AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio,

    AVG(
        requested_payment_to_income_ratio - approved_payment_to_income_ratio
    ) FILTER (
        WHERE approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS NOT NULL
    ) AS avg_pti_reduction_where_approved_pti_exists

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.20 Average requested Expected Loss and approved Expected Loss by decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final requested-versus-approved Expected Loss by outcome.

Boundary:
    requested_expected_loss_amount is requested-exposure Expected Loss.

    approved_expected_loss_amount is final approved-exposure Expected Loss.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount)
        AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,

    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount)
        AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount,

    SUM(requested_expected_loss_amount)
        AS total_requested_expected_loss_amount,

    SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
        AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount

FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

GROUP BY decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4.21 Section 9 readiness summary.

Purpose:
    Provide one compact readiness row for the final decision-resolution stage.

Expected:
    section_9_final_decision_resolution_status =
        SECTION_9_FINAL_DECISION_RESOLUTION_READY_FOR_REASON_CODE_ASSIGNMENT

Interpretation:
    This confirms only that Section 9 is ready for Section 10.

    It does not validate simulated reason codes, latest-run output, archive persistence, comparison,
    QA, frontier, or evidence capture.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH final_resolution_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS stage6_row_count,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome IS NULL
               OR decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
               OR decision_path IS NULL
               OR decision_priority_rank IS NULL
               OR decision_resolution_source IS NULL
        ) AS final_decision_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE (
                    COALESCE(approval_flag::INT, 0)
                    + COALESCE(counteroffer_flag::INT, 0)
                    + COALESCE(manual_review_flag::INT, 0)
                    + COALESCE(decline_flag::INT, 0)
                  ) <> 1
        ) AS final_flag_reconciliation_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag
                  IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER'))
        ) AS simulated_offer_exposure_flag_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
              AND approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_amount
        ) AS approve_amount_convention_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND (
                    approved_amount IS NULL
                 OR approved_amount <= 0
                 OR approved_amount >= requested_amount
                 OR counteroffer_amount IS DISTINCT FROM approved_amount
                 OR counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
              )
        ) AS counteroffer_convention_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND (
                    approved_amount IS NOT NULL
                 OR approved_expected_loss_amount IS NOT NULL
              )
        ) AS manual_review_unresolved_convention_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
              AND (
                    approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
                 OR approved_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
              )
        ) AS decline_zero_exposure_convention_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
              AND failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND decision_outcome <> 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
        ) AS failed_counteroffer_to_review_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
              AND failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'DECLINE'
              AND decision_outcome <> 'DECLINE'
        ) AS failed_counteroffer_to_decline_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
        ) AS final_approve_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS final_counteroffer_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
        ) AS final_manual_review_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
        ) AS final_decline_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE
        ) AS simulated_offer_exposure_rows

    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
)

SELECT
    stage6_row_count,
    distinct_application_id_count,

    final_decision_gap_rows,
    final_flag_reconciliation_gap_rows,
    simulated_offer_exposure_flag_gap_rows,

    approve_amount_convention_gap_rows,
    counteroffer_convention_gap_rows,
    manual_review_unresolved_convention_gap_rows,
    decline_zero_exposure_convention_gap_rows,

    failed_counteroffer_to_review_gap_rows,
    failed_counteroffer_to_decline_gap_rows,

    final_approve_rows,
    final_counteroffer_rows,
    final_manual_review_rows,
    final_decline_rows,
    simulated_offer_exposure_rows,

    CASE
        WHEN stage6_row_count > 0
         AND stage6_row_count = distinct_application_id_count
         AND final_decision_gap_rows = 0
         AND final_flag_reconciliation_gap_rows = 0
         AND simulated_offer_exposure_flag_gap_rows = 0
         AND approve_amount_convention_gap_rows = 0
         AND counteroffer_convention_gap_rows = 0
         AND manual_review_unresolved_convention_gap_rows = 0
         AND decline_zero_exposure_convention_gap_rows = 0
         AND failed_counteroffer_to_review_gap_rows = 0
         AND failed_counteroffer_to_decline_gap_rows = 0
            THEN 'SECTION_9_FINAL_DECISION_RESOLUTION_READY_FOR_REASON_CODE_ASSIGNMENT'
        ELSE 'REVIEW_SECTION_9_FINAL_DECISION_RESOLUTION_BEFORE_REASON_CODE_ASSIGNMENT'
    END AS section_9_final_decision_resolution_status

FROM final_resolution_summary;



/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 9 — FINAL DECISION RESOLUTION LAYER

If execution reaches this point:
    1. Section 9 dependency preflight passed.
    2. tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution exists.
    3. Row count is unchanged from tmp_m2_stage_5_exposure_treatment.
    4. application_id remains unique.
    5. final decision_outcome is populated.
    6. decision_outcome is one of APPROVE, COUNTEROFFER, MANUAL_REVIEW, DECLINE.
    7. decision_path is populated.
    8. decision_priority_rank is populated.
    9. decision_resolution_source is populated.
    10. failed_counteroffer_resolution is attached and valid.
    11. approval_flag, counteroffer_flag, manual_review_flag, and decline_flag reconcile to
        decision_outcome.
    12. Exactly one final decision flag is TRUE per row.
    13. simulated_offer_exposure_flag is TRUE only for APPROVE and COUNTEROFFER.
    14. simulated_offer_exposure_flag is FALSE for MANUAL_REVIEW and DECLINE.
    15. Final APPROVE rows preserve requested exposure and requested-exposure economics.
    16. Final COUNTEROFFER rows use feasible reduced-exposure economics.
    17. Final MANUAL_REVIEW rows remain unresolved with NULL approved-exposure economics.
    18. Final DECLINE rows use locked zero-exposure conventions.
    19. Infeasible preliminary COUNTEROFFER rows resolve according to failed_counteroffer_resolution.
    20. estimated_pd remains the Module 1 SQL field and is interpreted as the synthetic estimated-PD
        proxy.
    21. requested_expected_loss_amount remains requested-exposure Expected Loss.
    22. approved_expected_loss_amount is now final approved-exposure Expected Loss.
    23. No simulated reason-code fields were created.
    24. No latest-run strategy_decisions output table was created.
    25. Section 9 local final decision-resolution diagnostics are available for review.

Section 9 established:
    1. The final simulated decision outcome layer.
    2. Final decision path labels.
    3. Final decision priority ranks.
    4. Final decision resolution source labels.
    5. Final approval / counteroffer / manual review / decline flags.
    6. Final simulated offer-exposure flag.
    7. Final approved exposure fields.
    8. Final approved affordability proxy fields.
    9. Final approved Expected Loss fields.
    10. Parameter-governed failed-counteroffer resolution.

No simulated reason codes have been assigned.
No primary_reason_code has been created.
No secondary_reason_code has been created.
No tertiary_reason_code has been created.
No triggered_reason_code_list has been created.
No reason_priority_rank has been created.
No primary_reason_family has been created.
No reason_code_count has been created.
No latest-run strategy_decisions table has been created.
No strategy archive rows have been inserted.
No evidence rows have been inserted.
No matched comparison has been performed.
No strategy frontier has been calculated.
No full QA framework has been built.

Next section:
    Section 10 should consume tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution and assign deterministic
    simulated strategy explanation codes using final decision outcomes, final decision paths, rule
    triggers, preliminary routing diagnostics, exposure-treatment diagnostics, and counteroffer
    feasibility diagnostics.

***************************************************************************************************/


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 10 — SIMULATED REASON-CODE ASSIGNMENT LAYER
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Assign deterministic simulated strategy explanation codes after final decision resolution.

    Section 10 answers:

        "Why did this synthetic applicant receive this simulated strategy outcome?"

    Section 10 does not answer:

        "What real applicant communication would be sent?"
        "What regulatory notice would be produced?"
        "What compliance conclusion should be drawn?"
        "What happened to an actual applicant?"

    Section 10 is the explanation-code layer.

    It explains final simulated strategy outcomes after Section 9 has already resolved:
        final decision_outcome,
        final decision_path,
        final decision flags,
        simulated_offer_exposure_flag,
        final approved exposure,
        final approved affordability proxy,
        and final approved Expected Loss.

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm required Section 10 dependency objects exist.
    2. Read from tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution.
    3. Preserve all prior source, lineage, Module 2 strategy metadata, thresholds, segmentation,
       rule flags, preliminary routing diagnostics, exposure-treatment diagnostics, and final
       decision fields.
    4. Create one candidate simulated reason-code row per applicable rule / route / treatment driver.
    5. Filter reason-code candidates by final decision_outcome family.
    6. Deduplicate repeated candidate reason codes.
    7. Rank candidate reasons deterministically using governed priority ranges.
    8. Pivot ranked candidate reasons into:
            primary_reason_code
            secondary_reason_code
            tertiary_reason_code
            primary_reason_family
            triggered_reason_code_list
            reason_priority_rank
            reason_code_count
    9. Validate reason-code completeness, outcome-family alignment, reason-code priority ranges,
       reason-code uniqueness, and staging integrity.
    10. Confirm latest-run output creation and archive persistence remain deferred.
    11. Provide local reason-code diagnostics before Section 11 materializes the latest-run output.

WHO SHOULD REVIEW THIS SECTION:
    Credit strategy reviewers:
        Confirm that the assigned explanation codes reflect the simulated strategy drivers behind
        APPROVE, COUNTEROFFER, MANUAL_REVIEW, and DECLINE outcomes.

    Model governance / validation reviewers:
        Confirm that reason codes are deterministic, bounded, internally consistent, and clearly
        labeled as simulated strategy explanation codes rather than customer-facing explanations.

    SQL reviewers:
        Confirm that the candidate → deduplicate → rank → pivot pattern is deterministic and avoids
        hiding overlapping strategy drivers inside one opaque CASE block.

    Portfolio / executive reviewers:
        Use Section 10 diagnostics to understand which strategy explanation themes dominate the
        current run before latest-run output, archive persistence, QA, frontier analysis, and evidence
        capture.

WHEN TO RUN THIS SECTION:
    Run Section 10 after:

        Section 9 — Final Decision Resolution Layer

    Section 10 should be run before:

        Section 11 — Latest-Run Strategy Decision Output Table

    Section 10 depends on:

        tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

INPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

OUTPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment

GRAIN:
    One row per application_id for the selected Module 1 scenario / population and active Module 2
    strategy.

WHY REASON-CODE ASSIGNMENT IS SEPARATED FROM FINAL DECISION RESOLUTION:
    Section 9 creates final simulated strategy outcomes and final approved-exposure economics.

    Section 10 explains those outcomes.

    Keeping explanation logic separate allows the reason-code layer to use:
        final decision_outcome,
        decision_path,
        decision_resolution_source,
        Section 6 rule-trigger flags,
        Section 7 preliminary routing diagnostics,
        Section 8 counteroffer feasibility diagnostics,
        final exposure-treatment fields,
        mixed-signal diagnostics,
        borderline diagnostics,
        and product-policy controls.

    This separation also makes the reason-code layer easier to validate because Section 10 does not
    recalculate final decisions or exposure fields.

WHY THE CANDIDATE → RANK → PIVOT PATTERN IS USED:
    A single row can have multiple valid explanatory drivers.

    Example:
        A final COUNTEROFFER row may be driven by:
            product exposure limits,
            requested affordability pressure,
            requested Expected Loss pressure,
            and elevated synthetic estimated-risk.

    A single large CASE expression would hide that overlap.

    Section 10 therefore:
        creates candidate reasons,
        deduplicates repeated candidate reason codes,
        ranks them deterministically,
        assigns primary / secondary / tertiary reason fields,
        and preserves the full triggered reason-code list.

OUTCOME-SPECIFIC FILTERING:
    Candidate reasons are filtered by final decision_outcome family so that:

        APPROVE rows receive APPROVAL reasons.
        COUNTEROFFER rows receive COUNTEROFFER reasons.
        MANUAL_REVIEW rows receive MANUAL_REVIEW reasons.
        DECLINE rows receive POLICY_STOP reasons.

REASON PRIORITY RANGES:
    POLICY_STOP / DECLINE reasons:
        100–199

    MANUAL_REVIEW reasons:
        300–399

    COUNTEROFFER reasons:
        500–599

    APPROVAL reasons:
        900–999

    Lower numeric rank means higher priority.

APPROVAL REASON BOUNDARY:
    APPROVE rows receive:

        APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED

    This indicates that the synthetic applicant passed the simulated strategy conditions required for
    an as-requested positive offer-exposure outcome.

COUNTEROFFER REASON BOUNDARY:
    COUNTEROFFER reason codes explain which simulated strategy constraints drove reduced-exposure
    treatment.

    They do not imply:
        operational negotiation,
        customer acceptance,
        booked exposure,
        funded exposure,
        production approval,
        account creation,
        or real applicant treatment.

MANUAL REVIEW REASON BOUNDARY:
    MANUAL_REVIEW reason codes explain why the simulated strategy outcome remains unresolved.

    They do not represent completed operational review.

DECLINE / POLICY STOP REASON BOUNDARY:
    POLICY_STOP reason codes explain final simulated no-offer paths for synthetic applicants.

    They are simulated strategy explanation codes only.

REASON-CODE BOUNDARY:
    The fields created in Section 10 are simulated strategy explanation codes.

    They support:
        transparency,
        QA review,
        strategy interpretation,
        portfolio diagnostics,
        decision-path traceability,
        matched comparison,
        executive evidence capture,
        validation documentation,
        README summaries,
        and LinkedIn campaign storytelling.

    They are not:
        customer communications,
        regulatory notices,
        production compliance determinations,
        real applicant treatment explanations,
        adverse-action notices,
        or fair-lending conclusions.

SECONDARY AND TERTIARY REASONS:
    secondary_reason_code and tertiary_reason_code are additional diagnostics only.

    They do not change:
        decision_outcome,
        decision_path,
        approved exposure,
        approved PTI,
        approved Expected Loss,
        simulated offer exposure,
        or archive behavior.

TRIGGERED REASON LIST:
    triggered_reason_code_list contains all applicable candidate reason codes after filtering to the
    final decision_outcome family.

    This field is useful for QA and documentation because it preserves more explanatory detail than
    the primary / secondary / tertiary fields alone.

ESTIMATED_PD BOUNDARY:
    estimated_pd remains the finalized Module 1 SQL field and is interpreted as the synthetic
    estimated-PD proxy.

    Section 10 does not recalculate estimated_pd.

REQUESTED VS APPROVED EXPECTED LOSS:
    requested_expected_loss_amount is requested-exposure Expected Loss from Module 1.

    approved_expected_loss_amount is approved-exposure Expected Loss after Module 2 final exposure
    treatment.

    Section 10 explains outcomes but does not recalculate either value.

COUNTEROFFER FEASIBILITY FAILURE BOUNDARY:
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason is a Section 8 feasibility diagnostic.

    It is not a final simulated reason code.

    Section 10 may use that diagnostic to assign an internal MANUAL_REVIEW or POLICY_STOP explanation
    when failed counteroffer resolution produces final MANUAL_REVIEW or final DECLINE.

LATEST-RUN / ARCHIVE BOUNDARY:
    Section 10 creates only a temporary reason-code staging table.

    Section 10 does not create:

        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

    Section 10 does not insert rows into:

        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive

GOVERNANCE ROLE:
    Section 10 makes strategy explanations deterministic, reviewable, and tied to the final outcome
    taxonomy.

    It ensures the latest-run table is not materialized until every row has an outcome-family-aligned
    simulated explanation code.

COMMON MISUSE TO AVOID:
    Do not treat primary_reason_code as customer-facing language.
    Do not treat triggered_reason_code_list as adverse-action notices.
    Do not treat reason_priority_rank as a regulatory severity score.
    Do not treat reason codes as fair-lending conclusions.
    Do not infer production compliance approval from reason-code completeness.
    Do not use Section 10 to recalculate decisions or approved exposure.

***************************************************************************************************/



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 10.0 — SECTION 10 DEPENDENCY PREFLIGHT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that Section 9 final decision-resolution output exists and is populated before simulated
    reason-code assignment begins.

    Section 10.0 answers:

        "Can Section 10 safely assign simulated reason codes from the final decision-resolution layer?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution exists.
    2. Confirm tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution contains rows.
    3. Confirm application_id is unique before reason-code fields are added.
    4. Confirm final decision fields required for reason assignment are populated.
    5. Confirm final exposure convention fields required for reason diagnostics are present.
    6. Confirm Section 9 did not already create reason-code fields.
    7. Fail clearly if Section 9 has not been run.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 10.0 does not create reason codes.
    Section 10.0 does not create latest-run output.
    Section 10.0 does not insert archive rows.
    Section 10.0 does not modify persistent tables.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_stage6_exists BOOLEAN;
    v_stage6_row_count BIGINT;
    v_stage6_distinct_application_count BIGINT;
    v_required_stage6_gap_count BIGINT;
    v_existing_reason_column_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Dependency check: Section 9 final decision-resolution stage must exist.

    SQL mechanics:
        TO_REGCLASS checks whether the temporary object exists.

    Business interpretation:
        Section 10 must consume the final decision-resolution layer, not preliminary routing,
        exposure treatment, or rule flags.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COALESCE(
        TO_REGCLASS('pg_temp.tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution'),
        TO_REGCLASS('tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution')
    ) IS NOT NULL
    INTO v_stage6_exists;

    IF v_stage6_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution is required. Run Section 9 before Section 10.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: Section 9 final decision-resolution stage must contain rows.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage6_row_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution;

    IF v_stage6_row_count <= 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution contains zero rows.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id must be unique before reason-code assignment.

    Section 10 should add explanation fields only.

    It should not repair upstream row-grain problems.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_stage6_distinct_application_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution;

    IF v_stage6_distinct_application_count <> v_stage6_row_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution is not unique at application_id. Rows=%, distinct application_id=%.',
            v_stage6_row_count,
            v_stage6_distinct_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: final decision-resolution fields required for reason assignment must be populated.

    Business interpretation:
        Simulated explanation codes should be assigned after final decision resolution, not before.

        Missing final outcome or final path fields would make the explanation layer ambiguous.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_required_stage6_gap_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution
    WHERE decision_outcome IS NULL
       OR decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
       OR decision_path IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(decision_path), '') IS NULL
       OR decision_priority_rank IS NULL
       OR decision_resolution_source IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(decision_resolution_source), '') IS NULL

       OR approval_flag IS NULL
       OR counteroffer_flag IS NULL
       OR manual_review_flag IS NULL
       OR decline_flag IS NULL
       OR simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS NULL

       OR requested_amount IS NULL
       OR requested_payment_to_income_ratio IS NULL
       OR requested_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
       OR estimated_pd IS NULL
       OR estimated_lgd IS NULL

       OR product_type_policy_key IS NULL
       OR score_band_policy_key IS NULL
       OR strategy_risk_tier IS NULL
       OR requested_pti_bucket IS NULL
       OR dti_bucket IS NULL
       OR requested_exposure_tier IS NULL
       OR requested_expected_loss_tier IS NULL

       OR hard_policy_stop_flag IS NULL
       OR synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS NULL
       OR dti_decline_trigger_flag IS NULL
       OR counteroffer_candidate_flag IS NULL
       OR manual_review_candidate_flag IS NULL
       OR clean_approval_candidate_flag IS NULL

       OR (
            decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'DECLINE')
            AND approved_amount IS NULL
       )

       OR (
            decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'DECLINE')
            AND approved_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
       );

    IF v_required_stage6_gap_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: % Section 9 row(s) are missing fields required for simulated reason-code assignment.',
            v_required_stage6_gap_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: Section 9 should not already have reason-code fields.

    Business purpose:
        Protect the staged architecture.

        Reason-code assignment belongs in Section 10.

    SQL mechanics:
        pg_attribute inspects the physical columns of the temp table.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_existing_reason_column_count
    FROM pg_attribute
    WHERE attrelid = 'tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution'::REGCLASS
      AND attnum > 0
      AND NOT attisdropped
      AND attname IN (
            'primary_reason_code',
            'secondary_reason_code',
            'tertiary_reason_code',
            'triggered_reason_code_list',
            'reason_priority_rank',
            'primary_reason_family',
            'reason_code_count'
      );

    IF v_existing_reason_column_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: reason-code fields already exist before Section 10 assignment.';
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 10.1 — CLEAN RESET OF SECTION 10 STAGING OBJECT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Drop the Section 10 reason-code assignment stage before rebuilding it.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Remove only the temporary Section 10 staging table.

WHY THIS MATTERS:
    A partial rerun should not allow stale reason-code rows to remain available to Section 11.

    Section 11 assumes tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment reflects the current:
        Section 9 final decision-resolution output,
        final decision taxonomy,
        and reason-code assignment logic.

SQL MECHANICS:
    DROP TABLE IF EXISTS makes the reset rerunnable.

    If the table does not exist, PostgreSQL does not error.

BOUNDARY:
    This drop affects only the temporary Section 10 staging object.

    It does not modify Module 1 outputs.
    It does not modify Module 2 latest-run output.
    It does not modify Module 2 archive output.
    It does not modify evidence tables.
    It does not modify registry tables.

****************************************************************************************************/

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 10.2 — CREATE SIMULATED REASON-CODE ASSIGNMENT TABLE
****************************************************************************************************

TABLE:
    tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment

GRAIN:
    One row per application_id for the selected Module 1 scenario / population and active Module 2
    strategy.

INPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution

OUTPUT:
    All Section 9 fields plus:
        primary_reason_code
        secondary_reason_code
        tertiary_reason_code
        primary_reason_family
        triggered_reason_code_list
        reason_priority_rank
        reason_code_count

IMPLEMENTATION PATTERN:
    reason_candidate_base:
        preserves the Section 9 final decision record.

    reason_candidates_raw:
        creates one row per application_id per candidate simulated strategy explanation code.

    reason_candidates:
        deduplicates repeated candidate reason codes and keeps the best rank for each code.

    ranked_reasons:
        assigns deterministic rank order within application_id.

    reason_pivot:
        converts candidate rows back to one row per application_id.

    final_reason_assignment:
        preserves all Section 9 fields and adds final Section 10 reason-code fields.

WHY SELECT * IS ACCEPTABLE HERE:
    This is a temporary staging layer, not a permanent output table.

    Section 10 intentionally preserves all prior fields plus explanation-code diagnostics for Section
    11 latest-run materialization.

    Permanent output selection is handled later with an explicit field list in Section 11.

***************************************************************************************************/

CREATE TEMP TABLE tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
ON COMMIT PRESERVE ROWS
AS
WITH reason_candidate_base AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: reason_candidate_base

    Purpose:
        Preserve the final decision-resolution row from Section 9.

    Boundary:
        No reason candidates are created in this CTE.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        f.*
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution f
),

reason_candidates_raw AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    APPROVAL REASONS — PRIORITY 900–999

    APPROVE rows receive APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED as the required approval explanation code.

    Boundary:
        This is a simulated strategy explanation code, not external approval language.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        application_id,
        'APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED'::TEXT AS candidate_reason_code,
        'APPROVAL'::TEXT AS candidate_reason_family,
        900::INTEGER AS candidate_reason_priority_rank,
        'decision_outcome_APPROVE'::TEXT AS candidate_reason_source
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'


    /***********************************************************************************************
    COUNTEROFFER REASONS — PRIORITY 500–599

    These reasons explain why final COUNTEROFFER rows received reduced-exposure treatment.

    A final COUNTEROFFER row may have several valid drivers. The ranking rules decide which driver is
    primary while preserving all candidates in triggered_reason_code_list.
    ***********************************************************************************************/

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'COUNTEROFFER_PRODUCT_EXPOSURE_LIMIT',
        'COUNTEROFFER',
        500,
        'exposure_counteroffer_candidate_or_product_cap_binding'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND (
            exposure_counteroffer_candidate_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_exposure_above_product_cap_flag IS TRUE
         OR (
                counteroffer_product_cap_amount IS NOT NULL
            AND counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount IS NOT NULL
            AND counteroffer_product_cap_amount = counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount
            AND requested_amount > product_max_approved_amount
         )
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'COUNTEROFFER_AFFORDABILITY_ADJUSTMENT',
        'COUNTEROFFER',
        510,
        'requested_pti_or_pti_target_binding'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND (
            counteroffer_affordability_candidate_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_pti_counteroffer_candidate_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_pti_review_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_pti_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR (
                counteroffer_pti_target_amount IS NOT NULL
            AND counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount IS NOT NULL
            AND counteroffer_pti_target_amount = counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount
         )
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'COUNTEROFFER_EXPECTED_LOSS_LIMIT',
        'COUNTEROFFER',
        520,
        'requested_expected_loss_or_approved_el_cap_binding'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND (
            counteroffer_expected_loss_candidate_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_el_counteroffer_candidate_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_el_review_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_el_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR (
                counteroffer_el_cap_amount IS NOT NULL
            AND counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount IS NOT NULL
            AND counteroffer_el_cap_amount = counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount
         )
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'COUNTEROFFER_ELEVATED_SYNTHETIC_RISK',
        'COUNTEROFFER',
        530,
        'synthetic_risk_counteroffer_band'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND (
            synthetic_risk_counteroffer_band_flag IS TRUE
         OR counteroffer_risk_band_eligible_flag IS TRUE
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'COUNTEROFFER_MULTIPLE_CONSTRAINTS',
        'COUNTEROFFER',
        590,
        'multiple_counteroffer_candidate_drivers'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND COALESCE(counteroffer_candidate_trigger_count, 0) > 1

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBLE_REDUCED_EXPOSURE',
        'COUNTEROFFER',
        599,
        'counteroffer_feasibility_passed_fallback'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'


    /***********************************************************************************************
    MANUAL REVIEW REASONS — PRIORITY 300–399

    These reasons explain unresolved final MANUAL_REVIEW outcomes.

    MANUAL_REVIEW can result from:
        failed counteroffer routed to review;
        severe requested-structure stress;
        synthetic-risk review band;
        affordability review;
        DTI review;
        requested Expected Loss review;
        mixed-signal profile;
        borderline threshold proximity;
        supplemental review diagnostics;
        residual strategy review.
    ***********************************************************************************************/

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_FAILED_COUNTEROFFER',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        300,
        'failed_counteroffer_resolution_to_manual_review'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            decision_resolution_source = 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBILITY_FAILED_TO_REVIEW'
         OR decision_path = 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE_REVIEW'
         OR (
                preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
            AND failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
         )
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_SEVERE_REQUESTED_STRUCTURE',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        310,
        'severe_requested_structure_review'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            decision_path = 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_STRUCTURE_REVIEW'
         OR severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag IS TRUE
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_SYNTHETIC_RISK_REVIEW',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        320,
        'synthetic_risk_review_band'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            manual_review_risk_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR synthetic_risk_review_band_flag IS TRUE
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_AFFORDABILITY_REVIEW',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        330,
        'requested_pti_review_trigger'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            manual_review_affordability_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_pti_review_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_pti_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_DTI_REVIEW',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        340,
        'dti_review_trigger'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            manual_review_dti_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR dti_review_trigger_flag IS TRUE
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_EXPECTED_LOSS_REVIEW',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        350,
        'requested_expected_loss_review_trigger'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            manual_review_expected_loss_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_el_review_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_el_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_MIXED_SIGNAL_PROFILE',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        360,
        'mixed_signal_profile'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            manual_review_mixed_signal_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR mixed_signal_profile_type <> 'NO_MIXED_SIGNAL_PROFILE'
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_BORDERLINE_PROFILE',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        370,
        'borderline_profile_flag'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            manual_review_borderline_trigger_flag IS TRUE
         OR borderline_profile_flag IS TRUE
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_HIGH_UTILIZATION',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        380,
        'high_utilization_review_trigger'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND high_utilization_review_trigger_flag IS TRUE

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_LOW_SCORE',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        385,
        'low_score_review_trigger'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND low_score_review_trigger_flag IS TRUE

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'MANUAL_REVIEW_RESIDUAL_STRATEGY_REVIEW',
        'MANUAL_REVIEW',
        399,
        'manual_review_fallback'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'


    /***********************************************************************************************
    POLICY STOP / DECLINE REASONS — PRIORITY 100–199

    These reasons explain final simulated no-offer outcomes.

    POLICY_STOP codes are internal simulated strategy explanation codes only.
    They are not adverse-action notices.
    ***********************************************************************************************/

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'POLICY_STOP_BANKRUPTCY',
        'POLICY_STOP',
        100,
        'bankruptcy_policy_stop_flag'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND bankruptcy_policy_stop_flag IS TRUE

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'POLICY_STOP_MAJOR_DEROGATORY',
        'POLICY_STOP',
        110,
        'major_derogatory_policy_stop_flag'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND major_derogatory_policy_stop_flag IS TRUE

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'POLICY_STOP_SEVERE_DELINQUENCY',
        'POLICY_STOP',
        120,
        'severe_delinquency_policy_stop_flag'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND severe_delinquency_policy_stop_flag IS TRUE

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'POLICY_STOP_SEVERE_SYNTHETIC_RISK',
        'POLICY_STOP',
        130,
        'synthetic_risk_decline_trigger'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'POLICY_STOP_SEVERE_DTI',
        'POLICY_STOP',
        140,
        'dti_decline_trigger'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND dti_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'POLICY_STOP_FAILED_COUNTEROFFER',
        'POLICY_STOP',
        150,
        'failed_counteroffer_resolution_to_decline'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND (
            decision_resolution_source = 'COUNTEROFFER_FEASIBILITY_FAILED_TO_DECLINE'
         OR decision_path = 'COUNTEROFFER_NOT_FEASIBLE_DECLINE'
         OR (
                preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
            AND failed_counteroffer_resolution = 'DECLINE'
         )
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'POLICY_STOP_REQUESTED_PTI_SEVERE',
        'POLICY_STOP',
        160,
        'requested_pti_decline_trigger'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND requested_pti_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'POLICY_STOP_REQUESTED_EL_SEVERE',
        'POLICY_STOP',
        170,
        'requested_expected_loss_decline_trigger'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND requested_el_decline_trigger_flag IS TRUE

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'POLICY_STOP_EXPOSURE_POLICY',
        'POLICY_STOP',
        180,
        'exposure_policy_stop_or_extreme_exposure'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND (
            exposure_policy_stop_candidate_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_exposure_extreme_flag IS TRUE
         OR requested_exposure_below_product_minimum_flag IS TRUE
      )

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        application_id,
        'POLICY_STOP_NO_OFFER',
        'POLICY_STOP',
        199,
        'decline_fallback'
    FROM reason_candidate_base
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
),

reason_candidates AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: reason_candidates

    Purpose:
        Deduplicate candidate reasons.

    Why deduplication matters:
        The same conceptual driver can be created by multiple related trigger fields.

        Example:
            requested Expected Loss pressure and approved EL cap binding can both support
            COUNTEROFFER_EXPECTED_LOSS_LIMIT.

    SQL mechanics:
        GROUP BY application_id / reason code / family.
        MIN(priority) retains the strongest rank.
        STRING_AGG preserves source diagnostics for internal review if needed.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        application_id,
        candidate_reason_code,
        candidate_reason_family,
        MIN(candidate_reason_priority_rank) AS candidate_reason_priority_rank,

        STRING_AGG(
            DISTINCT candidate_reason_source,
            '|' ORDER BY candidate_reason_source
        ) AS candidate_reason_source_list

    FROM reason_candidates_raw

    GROUP BY
        application_id,
        candidate_reason_code,
        candidate_reason_family
),

ranked_reasons AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: ranked_reasons

    Purpose:
        Rank reason candidates within each application.

    SQL mechanics:
        ROW_NUMBER provides deterministic primary / secondary / tertiary ordering.

        Tie-breakers:
            candidate_reason_priority_rank,
            candidate_reason_family,
            candidate_reason_code.

    Interpretation:
        Lower candidate_reason_priority_rank means higher priority.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        rc.*,

        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
            PARTITION BY rc.application_id
            ORDER BY
                rc.candidate_reason_priority_rank,
                rc.candidate_reason_family,
                rc.candidate_reason_code
        ) AS reason_rank

    FROM reason_candidates rc
),

reason_pivot AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: reason_pivot

    Purpose:
        Pivot ranked reason candidates back to one row per application_id.

    SQL mechanics:
        MAX(CASE WHEN reason_rank = n THEN candidate_reason_code END) creates primary, secondary,
        and tertiary reason fields.

        STRING_AGG preserves the full deterministic triggered reason list.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        rr.application_id,

        MAX(CASE WHEN rr.reason_rank = 1 THEN rr.candidate_reason_code END)
            AS primary_reason_code,

        MAX(CASE WHEN rr.reason_rank = 2 THEN rr.candidate_reason_code END)
            AS secondary_reason_code,

        MAX(CASE WHEN rr.reason_rank = 3 THEN rr.candidate_reason_code END)
            AS tertiary_reason_code,

        MAX(CASE WHEN rr.reason_rank = 1 THEN rr.candidate_reason_family END)
            AS primary_reason_family,

        STRING_AGG(
            rr.candidate_reason_code,
            '|' ORDER BY
                rr.reason_rank,
                rr.candidate_reason_priority_rank,
                rr.candidate_reason_code
        ) AS triggered_reason_code_list,

        MAX(CASE WHEN rr.reason_rank = 1 THEN rr.candidate_reason_priority_rank END)
            AS reason_priority_rank,

        COUNT(*) AS reason_code_count

    FROM ranked_reasons rr

    GROUP BY
        rr.application_id
),

final_reason_assignment AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: final_reason_assignment

    Purpose:
        Preserve all Section 9 fields and add final simulated reason-code fields.

    Boundary:
        This still creates only a temporary staging table.

        Permanent latest-run output is created in Section 11.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        b.*,

        rp.primary_reason_code,
        rp.secondary_reason_code,
        rp.tertiary_reason_code,
        rp.primary_reason_family,
        rp.triggered_reason_code_list,
        rp.reason_priority_rank,
        rp.reason_code_count

    FROM reason_candidate_base b

    LEFT JOIN reason_pivot rp
        ON rp.application_id = b.application_id
)

SELECT *
FROM final_reason_assignment;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 10.3 — LOCAL FAIL-FAST CHECKS FOR SIMULATED REASON CODES
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that Section 10 produced complete, deterministic, outcome-family-aligned simulated
    explanation codes before Section 11 materializes the latest-run output.

    Section 10.3 answers:

        "Did Section 10 preserve applicant grain, assign complete reason-code fields, align reason
         family to final outcome, and avoid creating latest-run or archive output early?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm row count is unchanged from tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution.
    2. Confirm application_id remains unique.
    3. Confirm required reason-code fields are complete.
    4. Confirm APPROVE reason-code convention.
    5. Confirm COUNTEROFFER reason-code convention.
    6. Confirm MANUAL_REVIEW reason-code convention.
    7. Confirm DECLINE reason-code convention.
    8. Confirm primary reason family reconciles to final decision outcome.
    9. Confirm reason-code priority range reconciles to reason family.
    10. Confirm reason-code count and triggered list are coherent.
    11. Confirm Section 10 did not create permanent latest-run output.
    12. Confirm Section 10 did not insert archive rows.

LOCAL GATEKEEPER BOUNDARY:
    These are local Section 10 staging gatekeepers only.

    They are not:
        latest-run materialization validation,
        archive validation,
        matched strategy comparison,
        full Module 2 QA,
        strategy frontier review,
        or Validation Summary evidence by themselves.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_stage6_count BIGINT;
    v_stage7_count BIGINT;
    v_stage7_distinct_app_count BIGINT;
    v_duplicate_application_count BIGINT;

    v_required_reason_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_approval_reason_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_counteroffer_reason_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_manual_review_reason_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_decline_reason_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_reason_family_alignment_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_reason_priority_range_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_reason_list_coherence_failure_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: row count must be unchanged from Section 9 to Section 10.

    Business purpose:
        Section 10 should add reason-code fields only.

        It should not filter applicants or duplicate applicants.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage6_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution;

    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage7_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment;

    IF v_stage7_count <> v_stage6_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: row count changed from Section 9 to Section 10. Stage 6 rows: %, Stage 7 rows: %.',
            v_stage6_count,
            v_stage7_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id remains unique.

    Business purpose:
        Duplicate application_id values would duplicate latest-run output rows, archive rows, QA
        counts, comparison results, and evidence capture.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_stage7_distinct_app_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment;

    IF v_stage7_distinct_app_count <> v_stage7_count THEN
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_duplicate_application_count
        FROM (
            SELECT application_id
            FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
            GROUP BY application_id
            HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
        ) d;

        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: application_id uniqueness was not preserved. Stage 7 rows: %, distinct application_id count: %, duplicate application_id group count: %.',
            v_stage7_count,
            v_stage7_distinct_app_count,
            v_duplicate_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: required reason-code fields must be complete.

    Business purpose:
        Every row must be explainable before the latest-run table is materialized.

    Expected:
        primary_reason_code populated,
        primary_reason_family populated,
        reason_priority_rank positive,
        triggered_reason_code_list populated,
        reason_code_count at least 1.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_required_reason_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
    WHERE primary_reason_code IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(primary_reason_code), '') IS NULL
       OR primary_reason_family IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(primary_reason_family), '') IS NULL
       OR reason_priority_rank IS NULL
       OR reason_priority_rank <= 0
       OR triggered_reason_code_list IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(triggered_reason_code_list), '') IS NULL
       OR reason_code_count IS NULL
       OR reason_code_count < 1;

    IF v_required_reason_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: % row(s) have missing or invalid required simulated reason-code fields.',
            v_required_reason_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: APPROVE reason convention.

    Business interpretation:
        APPROVE rows should receive exactly one approval explanation code unless approval diagnostics
        are explicitly expanded in a future design.

    Expected:
        primary_reason_code = APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED
        primary_reason_family = APPROVAL
        reason_priority_rank = 900
        no secondary / tertiary reason
        triggered_reason_code_list = APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED
        reason_code_count = 1
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_approval_reason_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
      AND (
            primary_reason_code <> 'APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED'
         OR primary_reason_family <> 'APPROVAL'
         OR reason_priority_rank <> 900
         OR secondary_reason_code IS NOT NULL
         OR tertiary_reason_code IS NOT NULL
         OR triggered_reason_code_list <> 'APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED'
         OR reason_code_count <> 1
      );

    IF v_approval_reason_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: % APPROVE row(s) violate approval reason-code conventions.',
            v_approval_reason_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: COUNTEROFFER reason convention.

    Final COUNTEROFFER rows must receive a COUNTEROFFER-family primary reason.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_counteroffer_reason_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
      AND (
            primary_reason_family <> 'COUNTEROFFER'
         OR primary_reason_code NOT LIKE 'COUNTEROFFER_%'
         OR reason_priority_rank < 500
         OR reason_priority_rank >= 600
      );

    IF v_counteroffer_reason_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: % COUNTEROFFER row(s) violate counteroffer reason-code conventions.',
            v_counteroffer_reason_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: MANUAL_REVIEW reason convention.

    Final MANUAL_REVIEW rows must receive a MANUAL_REVIEW-family primary reason.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_manual_review_reason_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
      AND (
            primary_reason_family <> 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
         OR primary_reason_code NOT LIKE 'MANUAL_REVIEW_%'
         OR reason_priority_rank < 300
         OR reason_priority_rank >= 400
      );

    IF v_manual_review_reason_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: % MANUAL_REVIEW row(s) violate manual-review reason-code conventions.',
            v_manual_review_reason_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: DECLINE reason convention.

    Final DECLINE rows must receive a POLICY_STOP-family primary reason.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_decline_reason_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
    WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
      AND (
            primary_reason_family <> 'POLICY_STOP'
         OR primary_reason_code NOT LIKE 'POLICY_STOP_%'
         OR reason_priority_rank < 100
         OR reason_priority_rank >= 200
      );

    IF v_decline_reason_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: % DECLINE row(s) violate policy-stop reason-code conventions.',
            v_decline_reason_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: primary reason family must reconcile to final decision_outcome.

    Expected mapping:
        APPROVE       → APPROVAL
        COUNTEROFFER  → COUNTEROFFER
        MANUAL_REVIEW → MANUAL_REVIEW
        DECLINE       → POLICY_STOP
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_reason_family_alignment_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
    WHERE (
            decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
            AND primary_reason_family <> 'APPROVAL'
          )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND primary_reason_family <> 'COUNTEROFFER'
          )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
            AND primary_reason_family <> 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
          )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
            AND primary_reason_family <> 'POLICY_STOP'
          );

    IF v_reason_family_alignment_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: % row(s) have primary_reason_family misaligned to decision_outcome.',
            v_reason_family_alignment_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: reason priority rank must fall inside the expected range for the primary family.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_reason_priority_range_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
    WHERE (
            primary_reason_family = 'POLICY_STOP'
            AND reason_priority_rank NOT BETWEEN 100 AND 199
          )
       OR (
            primary_reason_family = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
            AND reason_priority_rank NOT BETWEEN 300 AND 399
          )
       OR (
            primary_reason_family = 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND reason_priority_rank NOT BETWEEN 500 AND 599
          )
       OR (
            primary_reason_family = 'APPROVAL'
            AND reason_priority_rank NOT BETWEEN 900 AND 999
          );

    IF v_reason_priority_range_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: % row(s) have reason_priority_rank outside the expected family range.',
            v_reason_priority_range_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: reason-code count and triggered reason list must be coherent.

    This is a practical string-list check.

    It verifies:
        reason_code_count is positive;
        primary_reason_code appears in triggered_reason_code_list;
        secondary_reason_code appears when populated;
        tertiary_reason_code appears when populated.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_reason_list_coherence_failure_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
    WHERE reason_code_count < 1
       OR triggered_reason_code_list NOT LIKE '%' || primary_reason_code || '%'
       OR (
            secondary_reason_code IS NOT NULL
            AND triggered_reason_code_list NOT LIKE '%' || secondary_reason_code || '%'
          )
       OR (
            tertiary_reason_code IS NOT NULL
            AND triggered_reason_code_list NOT LIKE '%' || tertiary_reason_code || '%'
          );

    IF v_reason_list_coherence_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: % row(s) have incoherent triggered_reason_code_list / reason_code_count fields.',
            v_reason_list_coherence_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: latest-run output must still be deferred to Section 11.

    This protects the run sequence.

    If strategy_decisions already exists here, the user may be rerunning Section 10 after Section 11
    without clearing the latest-run output.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    IF TO_REGCLASS('credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions') IS NOT NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 10 failure: credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions exists before Section 11 materialization. Drop/rebuild latest-run output through Section 11 or rerun from Section 1.';
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 10.4 — LOCAL SIMULATED REASON-CODE SANITY CHECKS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide lightweight diagnostics for Section 10 simulated reason-code assignment.

    Section 10.4 answers:

        "What explanation-code themes were assigned, and do they align with final simulated outcomes,
         decision paths, products, score bands, and exposure-treatment diagnostics?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    Display review outputs for:
        reason-code assignment row count,
        final decision outcome × reason family,
        primary reason-code distribution,
        product × primary reason-code,
        score band × primary reason-code,
        product × score × primary reason-code,
        counteroffer reason-code drivers,
        manual-review reason-code drivers,
        decline / policy-stop reason-code drivers,
        failed-counteroffer failure reason × primary reason-code,
        decision path × primary reason-code,
        decision resolution source × primary reason-code,
        mixed-signal profile × primary reason-code,
        borderline profile × primary reason-code,
        sample reason-code trace,
        and one compact readiness summary.

INTERPRETATION:
    These are staging diagnostics only.

    They should not be interpreted as:
        final latest-run validation,
        archive validation,
        matched strategy comparison,
        strategy frontier evidence,
        full Module 2 QA,
        customer communication language,
        adverse-action language,
        or Validation Summary acceptance.

****************************************************************************************************/



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.1 Row count and distinct application_id count.

Purpose:
    Confirm the reason-code layer is still one row per application.

Expected:
    stage7_row_count = distinct_application_id_count.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS stage7_row_count,
    COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.2 Final decision outcome × primary reason family.

Purpose:
    Confirm outcome-family alignment.

Expected:
    APPROVE       → APPROVAL
    COUNTEROFFER  → COUNTEROFFER
    MANUAL_REVIEW → MANUAL_REVIEW
    DECLINE       → POLICY_STOP
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,
    primary_reason_family,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (PARTITION BY decision_outcome), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_within_decision_outcome

FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment

GROUP BY
    decision_outcome,
    primary_reason_family

ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END,
    primary_reason_family;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.3 Primary reason-code distribution.

Purpose:
    Show the main simulated explanation-code distribution.

Interpretation:
    This is the central reason-code QA output for the current staging layer.

Boundary:
    These are simulated strategy explanation codes only.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_stage

FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment

GROUP BY
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code

ORDER BY
    CASE primary_reason_family
        WHEN 'POLICY_STOP' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 2
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 3
        WHEN 'APPROVAL' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.4 Reason-code count distribution.

Purpose:
    Show how many explanation drivers were available per row after outcome-family filtering.

Interpretation:
    Higher reason_code_count means more overlapping same-family explanation drivers existed.

    It does not mean the final outcome is more severe.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,
    reason_code_count,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
GROUP BY
    decision_outcome,
    reason_code_count
ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END,
    reason_code_count;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.5 Product × primary reason-code distribution.

Purpose:
    Review whether explanation-code themes concentrate by product.

Interpretation:
    Product concentration may reflect product caps, LGD, requested exposure, PTI, requested Expected
    Loss, and counteroffer feasibility behavior.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    product_type_policy_key,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS avg_approved_amount_all_rows,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0)) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_all_rows
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
GROUP BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.6 Score band × primary reason-code distribution.

Purpose:
    Review whether explanation-code themes concentrate by borrower-quality segment.

Boundary:
    Score band supports interpretation but is not itself a reason-code family.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    score_band_policy_key,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(credit_score) AS avg_credit_score,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
GROUP BY
    score_band_policy_key,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    CASE score_band_policy_key
        WHEN 'SUPER_PRIME' THEN 1
        WHEN 'PRIME' THEN 2
        WHEN 'NEAR_PRIME' THEN 3
        WHEN 'SUBPRIME' THEN 4
        WHEN 'DEEP_SUBPRIME' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.7 Product × score × primary reason-code distribution.

Purpose:
    Review the core product × score segment explanation-code matrix.

Interpretation:
    This previews the segment-level evidence that later sections use for executive story capture.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    product_type_policy_key,
    score_band_policy_key,
    product_score_policy_segment,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS avg_approved_amount_all_rows
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
GROUP BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    score_band_policy_key,
    product_score_policy_segment,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    CASE score_band_policy_key
        WHEN 'SUPER_PRIME' THEN 1
        WHEN 'PRIME' THEN 2
        WHEN 'NEAR_PRIME' THEN 3
        WHEN 'SUBPRIME' THEN 4
        WHEN 'DEEP_SUBPRIME' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.8 Counteroffer primary reason-code distribution.

Purpose:
    Review why final COUNTEROFFER rows were explained as reduced-exposure treatments.

Boundary:
    These are simulated strategy explanation codes, not customer-facing counteroffer explanations.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS final_counteroffer_rows,
    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(approved_amount) AS avg_approved_amount,
    AVG(exposure_reduction_pct) AS avg_exposure_reduction_pct,
    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
GROUP BY primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    final_counteroffer_rows DESC,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.9 Manual-review primary reason-code distribution.

Purpose:
    Review why final MANUAL_REVIEW rows remained unresolved.

Boundary:
    MANUAL_REVIEW is unresolved simulated strategy routing.

    It is not completed operational review.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS final_manual_review_rows,
    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(debt_to_income_ratio) AS avg_debt_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
GROUP BY primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    final_manual_review_rows DESC,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.10 Decline / policy-stop primary reason-code distribution.

Purpose:
    Review why final DECLINE rows were explained as simulated no-offer outcomes.

Boundary:
    POLICY_STOP reason codes are internal simulated explanation codes only.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS final_decline_rows,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(debt_to_income_ratio) AS avg_debt_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
GROUP BY primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    final_decline_rows DESC,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.11 Triggered reason-code list sample by outcome.

Purpose:
    Show compact examples of how primary, secondary, tertiary, and full triggered reason lists appear.

Interpretation:
    triggered_reason_code_list preserves all same-family reason candidates after filtering.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,
    application_id,
    product_type_policy_key,
    score_band_policy_key,
    decision_path,
    decision_resolution_source,

    primary_reason_code,
    secondary_reason_code,
    tertiary_reason_code,
    primary_reason_family,
    reason_priority_rank,
    reason_code_count,
    triggered_reason_code_list

FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment

ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END,
    primary_reason_code,
    application_id

LIMIT 100;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.12 Counteroffer feasibility failure reason × primary_reason_code.

Purpose:
    Review how failed preliminary counteroffer diagnostics align to final explanation codes.

Boundary:
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason is a feasibility diagnostic, not a final reason code.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason,
    decision_outcome,
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
  AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
GROUP BY
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason,
    decision_outcome,
    primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason,
    decision_outcome,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.13 Decision path × primary_reason_code.

Purpose:
    Review whether the assigned primary explanation code aligns with the final internal decision path.

Interpretation:
    decision_path is an internal simulated strategy path label.
    primary_reason_code is the simulated strategy explanation code assigned after final outcome
    resolution.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_path,
    decision_outcome,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
GROUP BY
    decision_path,
    decision_outcome,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    decision_path,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.14 Decision resolution source × primary_reason_code.

Purpose:
    Review whether the assigned primary explanation code aligns with the final resolution source.

Interpretation:
    decision_resolution_source documents how final outcome resolution occurred.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_resolution_source,
    decision_outcome,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
GROUP BY
    decision_resolution_source,
    decision_outcome,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    decision_resolution_source,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.15 Mixed-signal profile × primary_reason_code.

Purpose:
    Review how realistic overlapping applicant profiles explain final outcomes.

Boundary:
    mixed_signal_profile_type remains diagnostic.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    mixed_signal_profile_type,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(reason_code_count) AS avg_reason_code_count,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
GROUP BY
    mixed_signal_profile_type,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    CASE mixed_signal_profile_type
        WHEN 'NO_MIXED_SIGNAL_PROFILE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'STRONG_CREDIT_HIGH_PTI' THEN 2
        WHEN 'WEAK_CREDIT_LOW_PTI' THEN 3
        WHEN 'LARGE_EXPOSURE_LOW_RISK' THEN 4
        WHEN 'HIGH_RISK_LOW_EXPOSURE' THEN 5
        WHEN 'HIGH_DTI_LOW_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 6
        WHEN 'MULTIPLE_MIXED_SIGNALS' THEN 7
        ELSE 99
    END,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.16 Borderline profile flag × primary_reason_code.

Purpose:
    Review whether threshold-adjacent profiles concentrate in particular explanation-code themes.

Boundary:
    borderline_profile_flag uses governed threshold proximity logic and remains diagnostic.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    borderline_profile_flag,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    AVG(reason_code_count) AS avg_reason_code_count,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
GROUP BY
    borderline_profile_flag,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    borderline_profile_flag,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.17 Reason-code priority-rank distribution.

Purpose:
    Confirm priority ranks stay inside the intended family ranges.

Expected:
    POLICY_STOP   100–199
    MANUAL_REVIEW 300–399
    COUNTEROFFER  500–599
    APPROVAL      900–999
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    primary_reason_family,
    reason_priority_rank,
    primary_reason_code,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
GROUP BY
    primary_reason_family,
    reason_priority_rank,
    primary_reason_code
ORDER BY
    reason_priority_rank,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
10.4.18 Section 10 readiness summary.

Purpose:
    Provide one compact readiness row for the reason-code assignment stage.

Expected:
    section_10_reason_code_assignment_status =
        SECTION_10_REASON_CODES_READY_FOR_LATEST_RUN_MATERIALIZATION

Interpretation:
    This confirms only that Section 10 is ready for Section 11.

    It does not validate latest-run materialization, archive persistence, matched comparison,
    Section 14 QA, Section 15 frontier, or Section 16 evidence capture.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH reason_code_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS stage7_row_count,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE primary_reason_code IS NULL
               OR primary_reason_family IS NULL
               OR triggered_reason_code_list IS NULL
               OR reason_priority_rank IS NULL
               OR reason_code_count IS NULL
               OR reason_code_count < 1
        ) AS required_reason_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
              AND primary_reason_family <> 'APPROVAL'
        ) AS approve_family_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND primary_reason_family <> 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS counteroffer_family_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND primary_reason_family <> 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
        ) AS manual_review_family_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
              AND primary_reason_family <> 'POLICY_STOP'
        ) AS decline_family_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE primary_reason_family = 'POLICY_STOP'
              AND reason_priority_rank NOT BETWEEN 100 AND 199
        ) AS policy_stop_priority_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE primary_reason_family = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND reason_priority_rank NOT BETWEEN 300 AND 399
        ) AS manual_review_priority_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE primary_reason_family = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND reason_priority_rank NOT BETWEEN 500 AND 599
        ) AS counteroffer_priority_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE primary_reason_family = 'APPROVAL'
              AND reason_priority_rank NOT BETWEEN 900 AND 999
        ) AS approval_priority_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
        ) AS final_approve_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS final_counteroffer_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
        ) AS final_manual_review_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
        ) AS final_decline_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT primary_reason_code) AS distinct_primary_reason_code_count

    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
)

SELECT
    stage7_row_count,
    distinct_application_id_count,

    required_reason_gap_rows,
    approve_family_gap_rows,
    counteroffer_family_gap_rows,
    manual_review_family_gap_rows,
    decline_family_gap_rows,

    policy_stop_priority_gap_rows,
    manual_review_priority_gap_rows,
    counteroffer_priority_gap_rows,
    approval_priority_gap_rows,

    final_approve_rows,
    final_counteroffer_rows,
    final_manual_review_rows,
    final_decline_rows,
    distinct_primary_reason_code_count,

    CASE
        WHEN stage7_row_count > 0
         AND stage7_row_count = distinct_application_id_count
         AND required_reason_gap_rows = 0
         AND approve_family_gap_rows = 0
         AND counteroffer_family_gap_rows = 0
         AND manual_review_family_gap_rows = 0
         AND decline_family_gap_rows = 0
         AND policy_stop_priority_gap_rows = 0
         AND manual_review_priority_gap_rows = 0
         AND counteroffer_priority_gap_rows = 0
         AND approval_priority_gap_rows = 0
            THEN 'SECTION_10_REASON_CODES_READY_FOR_LATEST_RUN_MATERIALIZATION'
        ELSE 'REVIEW_SECTION_10_REASON_CODES_BEFORE_LATEST_RUN_MATERIALIZATION'
    END AS section_10_reason_code_assignment_status

FROM reason_code_summary;



/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 10 — SIMULATED REASON-CODE ASSIGNMENT LAYER

If execution reaches this point:
    1. Section 10 dependency preflight passed.
    2. tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment exists.
    3. Row count is unchanged from tmp_m2_stage_6_final_decision_resolution.
    4. application_id remains unique.
    5. All Section 9 final decision, final flag, approved-exposure, approved-affordability, and
       approved-economics fields are preserved.
    6. primary_reason_code is populated for every row.
    7. secondary_reason_code and tertiary_reason_code are populated when additional diagnostics exist.
    8. primary_reason_family is populated for every row.
    9. triggered_reason_code_list is populated for every row.
    10. reason_priority_rank is populated and positive for every row.
    11. reason_code_count is populated and at least 1 for every row.
    12. APPROVE rows align to APPROVAL reason family.
    13. COUNTEROFFER rows align to COUNTEROFFER reason family.
    14. MANUAL_REVIEW rows align to MANUAL_REVIEW reason family.
    15. DECLINE rows align to POLICY_STOP reason family.
    16. reason_priority_rank falls inside the expected range for the primary reason family.
    17. APPROVE rows receive the locked APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED convention.
    18. triggered_reason_code_list preserves all applicable same-family explanation candidates.
    19. secondary_reason_code and tertiary_reason_code are diagnostics only.
    20. Simulated reason codes are deterministic strategy explanation codes.
    21. Simulated reason codes are not customer communications, regulatory notices, adverse-action
        notices, production compliance determinations, fair-lending conclusions, or real applicant
        treatment explanations.
    22. Section 10 local reason-code diagnostics are available for review.

Section 10 established:
    1. The final simulated explanation-code staging layer.
    2. Outcome-family-filtered reason-code assignment.
    3. Deterministic reason-code ranking.
    4. Primary, secondary, and tertiary reason-code diagnostics.
    5. Full triggered reason-code list.
    6. Reason-code family alignment to final decision_outcome.
    7. The staging foundation Section 11 needs for latest-run materialization.

No latest-run strategy_decisions table has been created.
No strategy archive rows have been inserted.
No evidence rows have been inserted.
No matched comparison has been performed.
No strategy frontier has been calculated.
No full Module 2 QA framework has been built.
No BRD or Validation Summary documentation has been drafted.

Next section:
    Section 11 should consume tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment and materialize the permanent
    latest-run output table:

        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

***************************************************************************************************/


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 11 — LATEST-RUN STRATEGY DECISION OUTPUT TABLE
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Materialize the completed Module 2 latest-run strategy output table.

    Section 11 answers:

        "What is the current final simulated strategy output for the selected Module 1 source
         population / scenario and active Module 2 strategy?"

    Section 11 does not answer:

        "What historical strategy runs exist?"
        "How does this run compare to an archived baseline?"
        "Has the latest-run output passed the full validation framework?"
        "Has executive evidence been captured?"

    This section is the permanent latest-run output materialization layer.

    Section 10 created the final temporary reason-code assignment stage.
    Section 11 turns that completed staging layer into the governed current-run output surface.

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm required Section 11 dependencies exist.
    2. Consume tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment.
    3. Create credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions as the replaceable latest-run output.
    4. Use an explicit SELECT list rather than SELECT *.
    5. Preserve Module 2 strategy metadata and archive controls.
    6. Preserve Module 1 lineage.
    7. Preserve application, borrower, product, requested-structure, affordability, synthetic
       estimated-risk proxy, LGD, and requested Expected Loss fields.
    8. Preserve strategy segmentation, rule-trigger, preliminary routing, exposure-treatment,
       counteroffer feasibility, final decision, final exposure, and simulated reason-code fields.
    9. Add latest_output_created_ts as latest-run audit metadata.
    10. Create practical latest-run indexes.
    11. Validate latest-run output integrity through local gatekeepers.
    12. Provide lightweight latest-run diagnostics before archive persistence.

WHO SHOULD REVIEW THIS SECTION:
    Credit strategy reviewers:
        Confirm that the latest-run output contains the final simulated decision, offer-exposure,
        approved exposure, approved affordability, approved Expected Loss, and explanation fields
        needed for strategy interpretation.

    Model governance / validation reviewers:
        Confirm that the permanent latest-run output is complete, uniquely keyed at application_id,
        and bounded as a synthetic simulation output rather than an operational underwriting output.

    SQL reviewers:
        Confirm that permanent output materialization uses an explicit field list, preserves intended
        columns, avoids SELECT * schema drift, and validates output integrity before archive
        persistence.

    Portfolio / executive reviewers:
        Use Section 11 diagnostics as the first compact view of the completed current run before
        reviewing Section 14 QA, Section 15 frontier output, and Section 16 evidence capture.

WHEN TO RUN THIS SECTION:
    Run Section 11 after:

        Section 10 — Simulated Reason-Code Assignment Layer

    Section 11 should be run before:

        Section 12 — Strategy Decision Archive Persistence Layer
        Section 14 — Module 2 Validation, QA, and Strategy Outcome Diagnostics
        Section 15 — Strategy Frontier Summary and Executive Comparison View
        Section 16 — Strategy Run Evidence Capture and Executive Story Register

    Section 11 depends on:

        tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
        tmp_module2_strategy_params

HOW TO INTERPRET THIS SECTION:
    Passing Section 11 means:
        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions exists,
        the latest-run output row count matches Section 10 staging,
        application_id remains unique,
        the latest-run table contains exactly one Module 2 strategy slice,
        the latest-run table contains exactly one Module 1 scenario / population slice,
        final decision fields are complete,
        final decision flags reconcile,
        simulated offer-exposure convention holds,
        approved exposure conventions hold,
        approved Expected Loss conventions hold,
        simulated reason-code fields are complete,
        latest-run audit timestamp is populated,
        and practical indexes are available.

    Passing Section 11 does not mean:
        archive persistence has occurred,
        matched comparison has been performed,
        full latest-run validation has passed,
        strategy frontier evidence is complete,
        executive evidence has been captured,
        or documentation is ready to draft.

WHY LATEST-RUN OUTPUT IS SEPARATED FROM STAGING TABLES:
    Temporary staging tables explain the full transformation path.

    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions is the governed latest-run output designed for:
        downstream QA,
        archive persistence,
        reporting,
        review,
        documentation,
        and future validation.

WHY LATEST-RUN OUTPUT IS REPLACED EACH RUN:
    The latest-run output table represents the current completed Module 2 strategy result only.

    Prior completed outputs are preserved through:

        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive

    not through accumulation in the latest-run table.

WHY ARCHIVE PERSISTENCE IS DEFERRED:
    Section 11 creates the latest-run output.

    Section 12 controls:
        archive persistence,
        archive replacement behavior,
        archive skip behavior,
        archive reset behavior,
        archive grain checks,
        and archive persistence fidelity.

WHY EXPLICIT OUTPUT-FIELD SELECTION IS USED:
    The final output schema should be governed, reviewable, and stable.

    Temporary staging tables may carry many diagnostics, but the permanent latest-run table should
    intentionally expose the fields needed for review, validation, archive persistence, comparison,
    frontier analysis, and evidence capture.

    Explicit field selection prevents accidental downstream schema drift if an upstream temporary
    stage later gains a development-only helper field.

WHY CAMPAIGN IDS ARE NOT ADDED TO EVERY LATEST-RUN ROW:
    Campaign IDs such as:
        module1_run_id,
        module2_run_id,
        showcase_id,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,
        readme_storyline_label,
        linkedin_post_sequence,
        validation_summary_section_hint

    are run-level evidence-linkage metadata.

    They are persisted later in Section 16 evidence tables.

    Section 11 preserves technical lineage and applicant-level strategy output fields.

REQUESTED VS APPROVED EXPECTED LOSS:
    requested_expected_loss_amount is the requested-exposure Expected Loss carried from Module 1.

    approved_expected_loss_amount is the approved-exposure Expected Loss calculated by Module 2 after
    final simulated exposure treatment.

ESTIMATED_PD BOUNDARY:
    estimated_pd remains the finalized Module 1 SQL field name.

    In interpretation, estimated_pd means the synthetic estimated-PD proxy.

    Module 2 does not recalculate estimated_pd.

SIMULATED OFFER EXPOSURE BOUNDARY:
    simulated_offer_exposure_flag identifies simulated positive offer exposure for APPROVE and
    COUNTEROFFER outcomes.

    It does not imply:
        operational account creation,
        booked exposure,
        funded exposure,
        production approval,
        customer treatment,
        or real applicant treatment.

SIMULATED REASON-CODE BOUNDARY:
    Reason-code fields are simulated strategy explanation codes only.

    They support:
        strategy transparency,
        QA review,
        decision-path traceability,
        matched comparison,
        executive evidence capture,
        validation documentation,
        README interpretation,
        and LinkedIn campaign storytelling.

    They are not:
        customer communications,
        regulatory notices,
        adverse-action notices,
        production compliance determinations,
        fair-lending conclusions,
        or real applicant treatment explanations.

LATEST_OUTPUT_CREATED_TS BOUNDARY:
    latest_output_created_ts records when the latest-run table was materialized.

    It is audit metadata.

    It is not deterministic comparison evidence.

    Matched strategy comparison should exclude timestamp fields unless specifically validating run
    metadata.

SECTION 11 QA BOUNDARY:
    Section 11 local checks validate latest-run output integrity only.

    They are not the full Module 2 QA framework.

    The full validation and QA framework is built in Section 14.

READ / WRITE BOUNDARY:
    Section 11 drops and recreates only:

        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

    Section 11 does not insert archive rows.
    Section 11 does not delete archive rows.
    Section 11 does not update archive rows.
    Section 11 does not modify campaign registry rows.
    Section 11 does not modify comparison registry rows.
    Section 11 does not insert evidence rows.
    Section 11 does not modify strategy parameters.
    Section 11 does not modify product-policy parameters.

GOVERNANCE ROLE:
    Section 11 creates the stable latest-run output surface consumed by:
        Section 12 archive persistence,
        Section 14 latest-run validation,
        Section 15 strategy frontier summary,
        and Section 16 evidence capture.

COMMON MISUSE TO AVOID:
    Do not treat credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions as historical archive.
    Do not compare multiple completed strategies from the latest-run table.
    Do not interpret latest_output_created_ts as a business outcome.
    Do not interpret simulated_offer_exposure_flag as real operational exposure.
    Do not interpret simulated reason codes as external communication text.
    Do not skip Section 12 if the run should become part of governed campaign history.
    Do not skip Section 14 if the run will support validation or executive documentation.

***************************************************************************************************/



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 11.0 — SECTION 11 DEPENDENCY PREFLIGHT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that Section 10 reason-code assignment output exists, is populated, and is ready to be
    materialized into the latest-run output table.

    Section 11.0 answers:

        "Can Section 11 safely create the permanent latest-run output from the completed Section 10
         reason-code staging layer?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment exists.
    2. Confirm tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment contains rows.
    3. Confirm application_id is unique in Section 10 staging.
    4. Confirm tmp_module2_strategy_params exists.
    5. Confirm exactly one active strategy parameter row exists.
    6. Confirm archive controls are populated and valid.
    7. Confirm required latest-run output fields are available and populated.
    8. Fail clearly if Section 10 or Section 2 has not been run.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 11.0 does not create latest-run output.
    Section 11.0 does not insert archive rows.
    Section 11.0 does not modify evidence tables.
    Section 11.0 does not modify registry tables.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_stage7_exists BOOLEAN;
    v_strategy_params_exists BOOLEAN;

    v_stage7_row_count BIGINT;
    v_stage7_distinct_application_count BIGINT;

    v_active_strategy_count BIGINT;
    v_bad_archive_control_count BIGINT;
    v_required_stage7_gap_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Dependency check: Section 10 reason-code assignment stage must exist.

    SQL mechanics:
        TO_REGCLASS checks whether the temporary object exists.

    Business interpretation:
        Section 11 must consume the completed reason-code assignment layer, not the Section 9 final
        decision layer. The latest-run output should not be materialized until simulated explanation
        codes are complete.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COALESCE(
        TO_REGCLASS('pg_temp.tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment'),
        TO_REGCLASS('tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment')
    ) IS NOT NULL
    INTO v_stage7_exists;

    IF v_stage7_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment is required. Run Section 10 before Section 11.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Dependency check: active strategy parameter table must exist.

    Business interpretation:
        Section 11 needs archive controls from the active strategy parameter card so Section 12 can
        later validate archive behavior from the latest-run output itself.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COALESCE(
        TO_REGCLASS('pg_temp.tmp_module2_strategy_params'),
        TO_REGCLASS('tmp_module2_strategy_params')
    ) IS NOT NULL
    INTO v_strategy_params_exists;

    IF v_strategy_params_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: tmp_module2_strategy_params is required. Run Section 2 before Section 11.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: Section 10 staging must contain rows.

    Business interpretation:
        Materializing an empty latest-run output is not useful and usually indicates an upstream
        source, routing, or reason-code assignment issue.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage7_row_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment;

    IF v_stage7_row_count <= 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment contains zero rows.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id must be unique before latest-run materialization.

    Section 11 should materialize one row per application_id.

    It should not repair upstream row-grain problems.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_stage7_distinct_application_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment;

    IF v_stage7_distinct_application_count <> v_stage7_row_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment is not unique at application_id. Rows=%, distinct application_id=%.',
            v_stage7_row_count,
            v_stage7_distinct_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: exactly one active strategy parameter row.

    Business interpretation:
        Section 11 must attach one archive-control posture to every applicant row.

        More than one active strategy row would duplicate applicant rows when archive controls are
        cross-joined.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_active_strategy_count
    FROM tmp_module2_strategy_params
    WHERE active_strategy_flag IS TRUE;

    IF v_active_strategy_count <> 1 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: expected exactly one active strategy parameter row, found %.',
            v_active_strategy_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: archive controls must be populated and valid.

    Allowed strategy_archive_reset_mode values:
        NONE
        STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY
        STRATEGY_SET_ONLY
        ALL
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_bad_archive_control_count
    FROM tmp_module2_strategy_params
    WHERE active_strategy_flag IS TRUE
      AND (
            archive_run_flag IS NULL
         OR strategy_archive_reset_mode IS NULL
         OR strategy_archive_reset_mode NOT IN (
                'NONE',
                'STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY',
                'STRATEGY_SET_ONLY',
                'ALL'
            )
      );

    IF v_bad_archive_control_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: active archive controls are missing or invalid.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: required Section 10 staging fields must be populated.

    Business interpretation:
        The latest-run output should not be materialized if core identity, lineage, requested-risk,
        final decision, final flag, final exposure, or reason-code fields are missing.

    Important:
        MANUAL_REVIEW rows are unresolved by design, so approved_amount and approved_expected_loss are
        allowed to be NULL for MANUAL_REVIEW.

        APPROVE, COUNTEROFFER, and DECLINE rows must have final approved exposure and approved
        Expected Loss populated according to their conventions.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_required_stage7_gap_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
    WHERE module2_model_version IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module2_model_version), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_set_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_set_name), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_name), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_version IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_version), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_run_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_run_id), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_run_ts IS NULL

       OR module1_model_version IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_model_version), '') IS NULL
       OR module1_scenario_set_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_scenario_set_name), '') IS NULL
       OR module1_scenario_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_scenario_name), '') IS NULL
       OR population_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(population_id), '') IS NULL

       OR application_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(application_id), '') IS NULL
       OR applicant_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(applicant_id), '') IS NULL

       OR product_type_policy_key IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(product_type_policy_key), '') IS NULL
       OR score_band_policy_key IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(score_band_policy_key), '') IS NULL

       OR requested_amount IS NULL
       OR requested_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
       OR estimated_pd IS NULL
       OR estimated_lgd IS NULL

       OR decision_outcome IS NULL
       OR decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
       OR decision_path IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(decision_path), '') IS NULL
       OR decision_resolution_source IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(decision_resolution_source), '') IS NULL

       OR approval_flag IS NULL
       OR counteroffer_flag IS NULL
       OR manual_review_flag IS NULL
       OR decline_flag IS NULL
       OR simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS NULL

       OR primary_reason_code IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(primary_reason_code), '') IS NULL
       OR primary_reason_family IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(primary_reason_family), '') IS NULL
       OR triggered_reason_code_list IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(triggered_reason_code_list), '') IS NULL
       OR reason_priority_rank IS NULL
       OR reason_code_count IS NULL

       OR (
            decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'DECLINE')
            AND approved_amount IS NULL
       )

       OR (
            decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'DECLINE')
            AND approved_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
       );

    IF v_required_stage7_gap_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: % Section 10 staging row(s) are missing required latest-run output fields.',
            v_required_stage7_gap_count;
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 11.1 — CLEAN RESET OF LATEST-RUN OUTPUT TABLE
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Drop the replaceable latest-run output table before rebuilding it from completed Section 10
    staging output.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Remove only:

        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

WHY THIS MATTERS:
    The latest-run table is intentionally current-run only.

    Dropping it prevents a partial or prior latest-run output from being mixed with the current
    completed strategy run.

SQL MECHANICS:
    DROP TABLE IF EXISTS makes the reset rerunnable.

    If the latest-run table does not exist, PostgreSQL does not error.

BOUNDARY:
    This does not drop:
        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_comparison_campaign_registry
        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary
        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence
        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot
        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary

****************************************************************************************************/

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 11.2 — CREATE LATEST-RUN STRATEGY DECISION OUTPUT TABLE
****************************************************************************************************

TABLE:
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GRAIN:
    One row per application_id for the selected Module 1 source scenario / population and active
    Module 2 strategy.

INPUT:
    tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment

OUTPUT:
    Permanent latest-run table with final simulated strategy output and diagnostic trace fields.

IMPORTANT:
    This table does not preserve prior runs.

    Prior completed runs are preserved through Section 12 archive persistence.

SQL DESIGN:
    This section uses:

        CREATE TABLE ... AS
        WITH active_archive_controls AS (...)
        SELECT explicit_field_list
        FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment
        CROSS JOIN active_archive_controls

    The active archive-control CTE is one row because Section 11.0 validated active strategy
    parameter cardinality.

WHY CROSS JOIN IS APPROPRIATE:
    active_archive_controls contains exactly one active strategy control row.

    CROSS JOIN attaches that one archive-control setting to every applicant row in the latest-run
    output.

    If active_archive_controls had more than one row, CROSS JOIN would duplicate applicants.
    Section 11.0 prevents that.

WHY CAMPAIGN IDS ARE NOT SELECTED HERE:
    Campaign registry IDs are run-level evidence metadata.

    They are persisted later in Section 16 evidence tables.

    The latest-run applicant table keeps technical lineage and applicant-level strategy output fields.

***************************************************************************************************/

CREATE TABLE credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions AS
WITH active_archive_controls AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: active_archive_controls

    Purpose:
        Select the active archive persistence controls from the current strategy parameter card.

    SQL mechanics:
        Section 11.0 already validated exactly one active strategy parameter row.

        LIMIT 1 is therefore safe.

    Boundary:
        These controls are carried into the latest-run output so Section 12 can validate archive
        behavior from the completed current-run table.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        archive_run_flag,
        strategy_archive_reset_mode
    FROM tmp_module2_strategy_params
    WHERE active_strategy_flag IS TRUE
    LIMIT 1
)

SELECT
    /***********************************************************************************************
    1. Module 2 strategy metadata.

    These fields identify the downstream simulated strategy applied to the selected Module 1
    population.

    strategy_run_id and strategy_run_ts are audit metadata.

    They support run traceability, but they do not replace the archive replacement / rerun key.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.module2_model_version,
    r.strategy_set_name,
    r.strategy_name,
    r.strategy_version,
    r.strategy_run_id,
    r.strategy_run_ts,
    r.failed_counteroffer_resolution,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    2. Archive controls.

    These are carried from the active strategy parameter card.

    Section 12 uses these fields to govern archive persistence and archive replacement behavior.

    They are not part of applicant grain.
    They are not matched-comparison keys.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    aac.archive_run_flag,
    aac.strategy_archive_reset_mode,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    3. Module 1 source mode and lineage.

    These fields preserve upstream synthetic population and scenario identity.

    They describe where the applicant population came from, not what Module 2 strategy was applied.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.module1_input_source,
    r.module1_source_table_name,

    r.module1_model_version,
    r.module1_scenario_set_name,
    r.module1_scenario_name,
    r.population_id,
    r.anchor_date,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    4. Application lineage.

    Section 11 remains one row per application_id.

    application_id is the row-level key for latest-run QA and matched archive comparison.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.application_seq,
    r.application_id,
    r.applicant_id,
    r.application_date,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    5. Product and score segmentation.

    product_type:
        Original Module 1 product value.

    product_type_policy_key:
        Normalized product-policy key used throughout Module 2.

    score_band:
        Original Module 1 score-band value.

    score_band_policy_key:
        Normalized score-band key used for segment evidence and strategy QA.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.product_type,
    r.product_type_policy_key,
    r.score_band,
    r.score_band_policy_key,
    r.credit_score,
    r.product_score_policy_segment,

    r.product_policy_match_count,
    r.product_policy_config_found_flag,
    r.product_policy_profile_code,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    6. Borrower and behavioral profile.

    prequalified_flag and returning_customer_flag may remain NULL when Module 1 does not provide
    them.

    These are source-profile fields, not final decision fields.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.annual_income,
    r.debt_to_income_ratio,
    r.utilization_rate,
    r.tradeline_count,
    r.months_since_oldest_trade,
    r.recent_inquiry_count,
    r.delinquency_count_12m,
    r.major_derogatory_flag,
    r.bankruptcy_flag,
    r.prequalified_flag,
    r.returning_customer_flag,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    7. Requested structure and requested-exposure economics.

    requested_expected_loss_amount:
        Module 2 alias for Module 1 requested-exposure Expected Loss.

    estimated_pd:
        Finalized Module 1 SQL field name; interpreted as synthetic estimated-PD proxy.

    expected_loss_amount:
        Original Module 1 field retained for traceability.

    monthly_payment_proxy and payment_to_income_ratio:
        Original Module 1 names retained for traceability.

    requested_monthly_payment_proxy and requested_payment_to_income_ratio:
        Module 2 requested-structure aliases used to distinguish requested versus approved terms.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.requested_amount,
    r.loan_term_months,
    r.base_apr_for_payment_calc,

    r.monthly_payment_proxy,
    r.payment_to_income_ratio,
    r.amount_to_income_ratio,

    r.requested_monthly_payment_proxy,
    r.requested_payment_to_income_ratio,

    r.estimated_pd,
    r.estimated_lgd,
    r.expected_loss_amount,
    r.requested_expected_loss_amount,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    8. Global strategy thresholds and product-policy controls.

    These fields make the latest-run output auditable without forcing reviewers to reverse-engineer
    the active temporary parameter tables.

    They are copied as run evidence context.

    They do not make Section 11 a parameter-definition section.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.approve_max_estimated_pd_proxy,
    r.counteroffer_max_estimated_pd_proxy,
    r.review_max_estimated_pd_proxy,
    r.decline_min_estimated_pd_proxy,

    r.global_approve_max_pti,
    r.global_review_max_pti,
    r.global_decline_min_pti,

    r.approve_max_dti,
    r.review_max_dti,
    r.decline_min_dti,

    r.borderline_threshold_buffer_pct,

    r.bankruptcy_policy_stop_enabled,
    r.major_derogatory_policy_stop_enabled,
    r.severe_delinquency_policy_stop_enabled,
    r.severe_delinquency_count_threshold,

    r.high_utilization_review_enabled,
    r.high_utilization_review_threshold,

    r.low_score_review_enabled,
    r.low_score_review_threshold,

    r.product_approve_max_pti,
    r.product_review_max_pti,
    r.product_decline_min_pti,
    r.counteroffer_target_pti,

    r.product_approve_max_requested_el,
    r.product_review_max_requested_el,
    r.product_decline_min_requested_el,
    r.product_approved_el_cap,
    r.requested_el_low_moderate_split,

    r.product_min_approved_amount,
    r.product_max_approved_amount,

    r.counteroffer_allowed_flag,
    r.manual_review_allowed_flag,
    r.product_min_counteroffer_pct,
    r.product_max_exposure_reduction_pct,
    r.exposure_assignment_method,
    r.approved_amount_rounding_increment,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    9. Strategy segmentation diagnostics.

    These fields describe the synthetic applicant before rule hierarchy and final outcome resolution.

    They support downstream QA, product × score evidence, frontier interpretation, and executive
    narrative.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.strategy_risk_tier,
    r.requested_pti_bucket,
    r.dti_bucket,
    r.requested_exposure_tier,
    r.requested_expected_loss_tier,

    r.strong_credit_high_pti_condition,
    r.weak_credit_low_pti_condition,
    r.large_exposure_low_risk_condition,
    r.high_risk_low_exposure_condition,
    r.high_dti_low_requested_pti_condition,

    r.mixed_signal_profile_type,
    r.mixed_signal_condition_count,
    r.borderline_profile_flag,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    10. Rule-trigger diagnostics.

    These fields preserve the trigger evidence behind preliminary routing and simulated reason-code
    assignment.

    These are not customer-facing reasons.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.bankruptcy_policy_stop_flag,
    r.major_derogatory_policy_stop_flag,
    r.severe_delinquency_policy_stop_flag,
    r.hard_policy_stop_flag,
    r.hard_policy_stop_count,

    r.synthetic_risk_clean_approval_band_flag,
    r.synthetic_risk_counteroffer_band_flag,
    r.synthetic_risk_review_band_flag,
    r.synthetic_risk_decline_trigger_flag,
    r.synthetic_risk_band_flag_count,
    r.synthetic_risk_trigger_count,

    r.requested_pti_clean_band_flag,
    r.requested_pti_counteroffer_candidate_flag,
    r.requested_pti_review_trigger_flag,
    r.requested_pti_decline_trigger_flag,
    r.affordability_trigger_count,

    r.dti_clean_band_flag,
    r.dti_review_trigger_flag,
    r.dti_decline_trigger_flag,
    r.dti_band_flag_count,
    r.dti_trigger_count,

    r.requested_el_clean_band_flag,
    r.requested_el_counteroffer_candidate_flag,
    r.requested_el_review_trigger_flag,
    r.requested_el_decline_trigger_flag,
    r.requested_el_trigger_count,

    r.requested_exposure_below_product_minimum_flag,
    r.requested_exposure_within_product_limit_flag,
    r.requested_exposure_above_product_cap_flag,
    r.requested_exposure_extreme_flag,
    r.exposure_counteroffer_candidate_flag,
    r.exposure_policy_stop_candidate_flag,
    r.exposure_trigger_count,

    r.counteroffer_allowed_by_product_flag,
    r.counteroffer_risk_band_eligible_flag,
    r.counteroffer_affordability_candidate_flag,
    r.counteroffer_exposure_candidate_flag,
    r.counteroffer_expected_loss_candidate_flag,
    r.counteroffer_candidate_flag,
    r.counteroffer_candidate_trigger_count,

    r.high_utilization_review_trigger_flag,
    r.low_score_review_trigger_flag,
    r.supplemental_behavioral_review_trigger_flag,
    r.supplemental_behavioral_review_trigger_count,

    r.manual_review_allowed_by_product_flag,
    r.manual_review_risk_trigger_flag,
    r.manual_review_affordability_trigger_flag,
    r.manual_review_dti_trigger_flag,
    r.manual_review_expected_loss_trigger_flag,
    r.manual_review_mixed_signal_trigger_flag,
    r.manual_review_borderline_trigger_flag,
    r.manual_review_candidate_flag,
    r.manual_review_candidate_trigger_count,

    r.clean_approval_candidate_flag,
    r.total_rule_trigger_count,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    11. Preliminary routing fields.

    These fields show how overlapping rule triggers were converted into one preliminary route before
    exposure treatment and final resolution.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.severe_requested_structure_trigger_flag,
    r.severe_requested_structure_trigger_count,

    r.preliminary_decision_outcome,
    r.preliminary_decision_path,
    r.preliminary_decision_priority_rank,
    r.preliminary_route_reason_family,
    r.preliminary_route_trigger_count,

    r.preliminary_decline_flag,
    r.preliminary_counteroffer_flag,
    r.preliminary_manual_review_flag,
    r.preliminary_approve_flag,

    r.requires_counteroffer_feasibility_flag,
    r.requires_approved_exposure_calculation_flag,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    12. Exposure treatment and counteroffer feasibility diagnostics.

    These fields support traceability from preliminary routing through final decision resolution.

    counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason is diagnostic only.
    It is not a simulated final reason code and not customer communication language.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.exposure_treatment_status,
    r.exposure_treatment_path,

    r.approved_amount_preliminary,
    r.counteroffer_amount_preliminary,
    r.exposure_reduction_flag_preliminary,
    r.exposure_reduction_amount_preliminary,
    r.exposure_reduction_pct_preliminary,

    r.approved_monthly_payment_proxy_preliminary,
    r.approved_payment_to_income_ratio_preliminary,

    r.approved_expected_loss_amount_preliminary,
    r.approved_el_reduction_amount_preliminary,
    r.approved_el_reduction_pct_preliminary,

    r.counteroffer_feasibility_evaluated_flag,
    r.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag,
    r.counteroffer_feasibility_failure_reason,
    r.counteroffer_feasibility_constraint_count,

    r.counteroffer_product_cap_amount,
    r.counteroffer_pti_target_amount,
    r.counteroffer_el_cap_amount,
    r.counteroffer_raw_max_feasible_amount,
    r.counteroffer_min_viable_amount,
    r.counteroffer_rounded_amount,
    r.counteroffer_test_monthly_payment_proxy,
    r.counteroffer_test_payment_to_income_ratio,
    r.counteroffer_test_expected_loss_amount,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    13. Final decision outcome fields.

    These fields are the final simulated strategy outcome for the latest-run output.

    They are still synthetic strategy outputs, not real applicant decisions.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.decision_outcome,
    r.decision_path,
    r.decision_priority_rank,
    r.decision_resolution_source,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    14. Final decision flags.

    Exactly one of approval_flag, counteroffer_flag, manual_review_flag, and decline_flag should be
    TRUE per row.

    simulated_offer_exposure_flag is TRUE only for APPROVE and COUNTEROFFER.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.approval_flag,
    r.counteroffer_flag,
    r.manual_review_flag,
    r.decline_flag,
    r.simulated_offer_exposure_flag,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    15. Final approved exposure and approved economics.

    APPROVE:
        approved_amount = requested_amount.

    COUNTEROFFER:
        approved_amount is positive and below requested_amount.

    MANUAL_REVIEW:
        approved fields remain NULL.

    DECLINE:
        approved fields follow the locked zero-exposure convention.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.approved_amount,
    r.counteroffer_amount,
    r.exposure_reduction_flag,
    r.exposure_reduction_amount,
    r.exposure_reduction_pct,

    r.approved_monthly_payment_proxy,
    r.approved_payment_to_income_ratio,

    r.approved_expected_loss_amount,
    r.approved_el_reduction_amount,
    r.approved_el_reduction_pct,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    16. Simulated reason-code fields.

    These are simulated strategy explanation codes, not external communication text.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    r.primary_reason_code,
    r.secondary_reason_code,
    r.tertiary_reason_code,
    r.primary_reason_family,
    r.triggered_reason_code_list,
    r.reason_priority_rank,
    r.reason_code_count,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    17. Latest-run audit timestamp.

    latest_output_created_ts is audit metadata.

    It should not be used as deterministic comparison evidence unless specifically validating run
    metadata.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    CURRENT_TIMESTAMP AS latest_output_created_ts

FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment r

CROSS JOIN active_archive_controls aac;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 11.3 — LATEST-RUN INDEXES
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Create practical indexes for latest-run QA, review, reporting, archive persistence, and matched
    comparison preparation.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Add indexes on common lookup and grouping fields without changing any latest-run rows.

INTERPRETATION:
    Indexes improve query performance and review ergonomics.

    They do not alter:
        row count,
        decision outcomes,
        approved exposure,
        approved Expected Loss,
        reason codes,
        archive state,
        evidence state,
        or registry state.

***************************************************************************************************/

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_application_id
    ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (application_id);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_strategy_identity
    ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version
    );

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_module1_lineage
    ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    );

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_archive_replacement_key
    ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    );

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_decision_outcome
    ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (decision_outcome);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_product_decision
    ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (
        product_type_policy_key,
        decision_outcome
    );

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_score_decision
    ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (
        score_band_policy_key,
        decision_outcome
    );

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_product_score
    ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (
        product_type_policy_key,
        score_band_policy_key
    );

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_primary_reason
    ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (primary_reason_code);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_offer_exposure
    ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (simulated_offer_exposure_flag);



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 11.4 — LOCAL FAIL-FAST CHECKS FOR LATEST-RUN OUTPUT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that the permanent latest-run output table faithfully preserves the completed Section 10
    result and obeys the accepted Module 2 output conventions before archive persistence begins.

    Section 11.4 answers:

        "Is credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions structurally sound and safe to hand to
         archive persistence, QA, frontier review, and evidence capture?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions exists.
    2. Confirm row count matches tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment.
    3. Confirm application_id uniqueness.
    4. Confirm exactly one Module 2 strategy identity exists.
    5. Confirm exactly one Module 1 scenario / population identity exists.
    6. Confirm latest_output_created_ts is populated.
    7. Confirm strategy metadata and Module 1 lineage are populated.
    8. Confirm archive controls are populated and valid.
    9. Confirm final decision fields and final decision flags reconcile.
    10. Confirm simulated_offer_exposure_flag convention.
    11. Confirm approved amount and exposure conventions.
    12. Confirm requested / approved Expected Loss conventions.
    13. Confirm simulated reason-code completeness and family alignment.
    14. Confirm prohibited reason-code terminology controls.

LOCAL GATEKEEPER BOUNDARY:
    These are latest-run output gatekeepers only.

    They are not:
        archive validation,
        matched strategy comparison,
        full Module 2 QA,
        final Validation Summary evidence,
        executive frontier evidence,
        or campaign-run evidence capture.

SQL MECHANICS:
    This block uses PL/pgSQL because it needs multiple diagnostic counts and fail-fast exceptions.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Row-grain diagnostics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    v_stage7_count BIGINT;
    v_latest_count BIGINT;
    v_latest_distinct_app_count BIGINT;
    v_duplicate_application_count BIGINT;

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Object and scope diagnostics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    v_output_table_exists BOOLEAN;
    v_strategy_scope_count BIGINT;
    v_module1_scope_count BIGINT;
    v_latest_output_created_ts_null_count BIGINT;

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Integrity diagnostics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    v_metadata_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_archive_control_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_decision_integrity_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_offer_flag_failure_count BIGINT;

    v_amount_integrity_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_expected_loss_integrity_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_reason_integrity_failure_count BIGINT;
    v_prohibited_reason_term_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: latest-run output table must exist.

    SQL mechanics:
        TO_REGCLASS returns NULL if the table is absent.

    Failure interpretation:
        Section 11.2 did not materialize the output table or was not run.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT TO_REGCLASS('credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions') IS NOT NULL
    INTO v_output_table_exists;

    IF v_output_table_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions does not exist.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: latest-run row count must match Section 10 staging.

    Business purpose:
        Confirm Section 11 materialized the completed reason-code staging layer without dropping,
        duplicating, or filtering rows.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_stage7_count
    FROM tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment;

    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_latest_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;

    IF v_latest_count <> v_stage7_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: latest-run row count (%) does not match Section 10 staging row count (%).',
            v_latest_count,
            v_stage7_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id remains unique.

    Business purpose:
        The latest-run output should be applicant-grain for one selected strategy / scenario slice.

        Duplicate application_id values would duplicate archive rows, QA counts, comparison rows, and
        evidence metrics.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_latest_distinct_app_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;

    IF v_latest_distinct_app_count <> v_latest_count THEN
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_duplicate_application_count
        FROM (
            SELECT application_id
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
            GROUP BY application_id
            HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
        ) d;

        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: application_id uniqueness failed in latest-run output. Rows: %, distinct application_id count: %, duplicate application_id group count: %.',
            v_latest_count,
            v_latest_distinct_app_count,
            v_duplicate_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: exactly one Module 2 strategy identity should exist in latest-run output.

    Business purpose:
        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions represents the current completed latest-run slice,
        not a multi-strategy archive.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT (
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version
    ))
    INTO v_strategy_scope_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;

    IF v_strategy_scope_count <> 1 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: latest-run output contains % Module 2 strategy identities. Expected exactly one.',
            v_strategy_scope_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: exactly one Module 1 scenario / population identity should exist.

    Business purpose:
        Module 2 V1.0 latest-run output is single-scenario / single-population at execution time.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT (
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    ))
    INTO v_module1_scope_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;

    IF v_module1_scope_count <> 1 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: latest-run output contains % Module 1 scenario / population identities. Expected exactly one.',
            v_module1_scope_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: latest_output_created_ts must be populated.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_latest_output_created_ts_null_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE latest_output_created_ts IS NULL;

    IF v_latest_output_created_ts_null_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: % latest-run row(s) have null latest_output_created_ts.',
            v_latest_output_created_ts_null_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: strategy metadata and Module 1 lineage must be populated.

    Business purpose:
        The latest-run output must remain traceable to both:
            upstream Module 1 scenario / population;
            downstream Module 2 strategy.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_metadata_failure_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE module2_model_version IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module2_model_version), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_set_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_set_name), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_name), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_version IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_version), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_run_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_run_id), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_run_ts IS NULL

       OR module1_input_source IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_input_source), '') IS NULL
       OR module1_source_table_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_source_table_name), '') IS NULL
       OR module1_model_version IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_model_version), '') IS NULL
       OR module1_scenario_set_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_scenario_set_name), '') IS NULL
       OR module1_scenario_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_scenario_name), '') IS NULL
       OR population_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(population_id), '') IS NULL
       OR anchor_date IS NULL

       OR application_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(application_id), '') IS NULL
       OR applicant_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(applicant_id), '') IS NULL;

    IF v_metadata_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: % latest-run row(s) have missing strategy metadata, Module 1 lineage, or application identity fields.',
            v_metadata_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: archive controls must be populated and valid.

    Section 11 does not archive rows, but it carries archive controls forward so Section 12 can apply
    governed persistence behavior.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_archive_control_failure_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE archive_run_flag IS NULL
       OR strategy_archive_reset_mode IS NULL
       OR strategy_archive_reset_mode NOT IN (
            'NONE',
            'STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY',
            'STRATEGY_SET_ONLY',
            'ALL'
       );

    IF v_archive_control_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: % latest-run row(s) have invalid archive controls.',
            v_archive_control_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: final decision fields and final decision flags must reconcile.

    Expected:
        Exactly one of approval_flag, counteroffer_flag, manual_review_flag, decline_flag is TRUE.

        Each flag should equal its decision_outcome expression.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_decision_integrity_failure_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE decision_outcome IS NULL
       OR decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
       OR decision_path IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(decision_path), '') IS NULL
       OR decision_priority_rank IS NULL
       OR decision_priority_rank <= 0
       OR decision_resolution_source IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(decision_resolution_source), '') IS NULL
       OR approval_flag IS NULL
       OR counteroffer_flag IS NULL
       OR manual_review_flag IS NULL
       OR decline_flag IS NULL
       OR (
            COALESCE(approval_flag::INT, 0)
            + COALESCE(counteroffer_flag::INT, 0)
            + COALESCE(manual_review_flag::INT, 0)
            + COALESCE(decline_flag::INT, 0)
          ) <> 1
       OR approval_flag IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome = 'APPROVE')
       OR counteroffer_flag IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
       OR manual_review_flag IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW')
       OR decline_flag IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome = 'DECLINE');

    IF v_decision_integrity_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: % latest-run row(s) have final decision or final flag integrity failures.',
            v_decision_integrity_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: simulated_offer_exposure_flag convention.

    Expected:
        TRUE for APPROVE and COUNTEROFFER.

        FALSE for MANUAL_REVIEW and DECLINE.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_offer_flag_failure_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag
          IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER'));

    IF v_offer_flag_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: % latest-run row(s) have simulated_offer_exposure_flag convention failures.',
            v_offer_flag_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: approved amount and exposure conventions by decision outcome.

    APPROVE:
        approved_amount = requested_amount.

    COUNTEROFFER:
        approved_amount > 0 and approved_amount < requested_amount.

    MANUAL_REVIEW:
        approved_amount IS NULL.

    DECLINE:
        approved_amount = 0.

    Note:
        exposure_reduction_flag is TRUE only for final COUNTEROFFER because it means reduced positive
        offer exposure. DECLINE has zero exposure but is not a reduced positive offer.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_amount_integrity_failure_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE requested_amount IS NULL
       OR requested_amount <= 0
       OR (
            approved_amount IS NOT NULL
            AND approved_amount < 0
       )
       OR (
            approved_amount IS NOT NULL
            AND approved_amount > requested_amount
       )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
            AND (
                approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_amount
             OR counteroffer_amount IS NOT NULL
             OR exposure_reduction_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
             OR exposure_reduction_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
             OR exposure_reduction_pct IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
            )
       )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND (
                approved_amount IS NULL
             OR approved_amount <= 0
             OR approved_amount >= requested_amount
             OR counteroffer_amount IS DISTINCT FROM approved_amount
             OR exposure_reduction_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
             OR exposure_reduction_amount IS NULL
             OR exposure_reduction_amount <= 0
             OR exposure_reduction_pct IS NULL
             OR exposure_reduction_pct <= 0
            )
       )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
            AND (
                approved_amount IS NOT NULL
             OR counteroffer_amount IS NOT NULL
             OR exposure_reduction_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
             OR exposure_reduction_amount IS NOT NULL
             OR exposure_reduction_pct IS NOT NULL
            )
       )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
            AND (
                approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
             OR counteroffer_amount IS NOT NULL
             OR exposure_reduction_flag IS DISTINCT FROM FALSE
             OR exposure_reduction_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_amount
             OR exposure_reduction_pct IS DISTINCT FROM 1.0::NUMERIC
            )
       );

    IF v_amount_integrity_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: % latest-run row(s) have approved amount or exposure convention failures.',
            v_amount_integrity_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: requested / approved Expected Loss conventions.

    requested_expected_loss_amount:
        requested-exposure Expected Loss carried from Module 1.

    approved_expected_loss_amount:
        approved-exposure Expected Loss after final Module 2 exposure treatment.

    Expected:
        APPROVE preserves requested Expected Loss.
        COUNTEROFFER should not exceed requested Expected Loss or product approved EL cap.
        MANUAL_REVIEW remains unresolved.
        DECLINE uses zero approved Expected Loss.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_expected_loss_integrity_failure_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE requested_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
       OR estimated_pd IS NULL
       OR estimated_lgd IS NULL
       OR (
            approved_expected_loss_amount IS NOT NULL
            AND approved_expected_loss_amount < 0
       )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
            AND (
                approved_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_expected_loss_amount
             OR approved_el_reduction_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
             OR approved_el_reduction_pct IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
            )
       )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND (
                approved_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
             OR approved_expected_loss_amount < 0
             OR approved_expected_loss_amount > requested_expected_loss_amount
             OR approved_expected_loss_amount > product_approved_el_cap
             OR approved_el_reduction_amount IS NULL
             OR approved_el_reduction_amount < 0
            )
       )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
            AND (
                approved_expected_loss_amount IS NOT NULL
             OR approved_el_reduction_amount IS NOT NULL
             OR approved_el_reduction_pct IS NOT NULL
            )
       )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
            AND (
                approved_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
             OR approved_el_reduction_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_expected_loss_amount
             OR approved_el_reduction_pct IS DISTINCT FROM CASE
                    WHEN requested_expected_loss_amount > 0 THEN 1.0::NUMERIC
                    ELSE 0::NUMERIC
                END
            )
       );

    IF v_expected_loss_integrity_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: % latest-run row(s) have requested / approved Expected Loss convention failures.',
            v_expected_loss_integrity_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: simulated reason-code completeness and family alignment.

    Expected mapping:
        APPROVE       → APPROVAL
        COUNTEROFFER  → COUNTEROFFER
        MANUAL_REVIEW → MANUAL_REVIEW
        DECLINE       → POLICY_STOP
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_reason_integrity_failure_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE primary_reason_code IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(primary_reason_code), '') IS NULL
       OR primary_reason_family IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(primary_reason_family), '') IS NULL
       OR triggered_reason_code_list IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(triggered_reason_code_list), '') IS NULL
       OR reason_priority_rank IS NULL
       OR reason_priority_rank <= 0
       OR reason_code_count IS NULL
       OR reason_code_count < 1
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
            AND primary_reason_family <> 'APPROVAL'
          )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
            AND primary_reason_family <> 'COUNTEROFFER'
          )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
            AND primary_reason_family <> 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
          )
       OR (
            decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
            AND primary_reason_family <> 'POLICY_STOP'
          );

    IF v_reason_integrity_failure_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: % latest-run row(s) have simulated reason-code integrity failures.',
            v_reason_integrity_failure_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: prohibited reason-code terminology controls.

    Business purpose:
        Protect the interpretation boundary that Module 2 reason codes are simulated strategy
        explanation codes only.

    These controls prevent terms that imply:
        adverse-action notice,
        regulatory notice,
        customer notice,
        fair-lending conclusion.

    Boundary:
        This does not make simulated reason codes externally approved communication language.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_prohibited_reason_term_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE COALESCE(primary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%ADVERSE_ACTION%'
       OR COALESCE(secondary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%ADVERSE_ACTION%'
       OR COALESCE(tertiary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%ADVERSE_ACTION%'
       OR COALESCE(triggered_reason_code_list, '') ILIKE '%ADVERSE_ACTION%'

       OR COALESCE(primary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%REGULATORY%'
       OR COALESCE(secondary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%REGULATORY%'
       OR COALESCE(tertiary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%REGULATORY%'
       OR COALESCE(triggered_reason_code_list, '') ILIKE '%REGULATORY%'

       OR COALESCE(primary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%CUSTOMER_NOTICE%'
       OR COALESCE(secondary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%CUSTOMER_NOTICE%'
       OR COALESCE(tertiary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%CUSTOMER_NOTICE%'
       OR COALESCE(triggered_reason_code_list, '') ILIKE '%CUSTOMER_NOTICE%'

       OR COALESCE(primary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%FAIR_LENDING%'
       OR COALESCE(secondary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%FAIR_LENDING%'
       OR COALESCE(tertiary_reason_code, '') ILIKE '%FAIR_LENDING%'
       OR COALESCE(triggered_reason_code_list, '') ILIKE '%FAIR_LENDING%';

    IF v_prohibited_reason_term_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 11 failure: % latest-run row(s) contain prohibited reason-code terminology.',
            v_prohibited_reason_term_count;
    END IF;

    /*
    Archive note:
        Section 11 contains no archive insert logic.
        Archive persistence remains deferred to Section 12.
    */
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 11.5 — LOCAL LATEST-RUN SANITY CHECKS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Let reviewers inspect the newly materialized latest-run output before archive persistence begins.

    Section 11.5 answers:

        "What does the current latest-run output look like at a high level?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    Display lightweight diagnostics for:
        latest-run row count,
        application_id uniqueness,
        current strategy identity,
        current Module 1 lineage,
        decision outcome distribution,
        decision path distribution,
        primary reason-code distribution,
        product × decision outcome,
        score band × decision outcome,
        product × primary reason code,
        score band × primary reason code,
        strategy risk tier × decision outcome,
        requested PTI bucket × decision outcome,
        mixed-signal profile × decision outcome,
        simulated offer-exposure flag,
        requested versus approved amount,
        requested versus approved PTI,
        requested versus approved Expected Loss,
        and one compact readiness row.

INTERPRETATION:
    These diagnostics are local latest-run materialization checks only.

    They are not:
        full Section 14 QA,
        archive validation,
        matched strategy comparison,
        strategy frontier review,
        executive evidence capture,
        or final written validation evidence.

****************************************************************************************************/



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.1 Latest-run row count and distinct application_id count.

Purpose:
    Confirm latest-run applicant grain.

Expected:
    latest_run_rows = distinct_application_id_count.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS latest_run_rows,
    COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count
FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.2 Latest-run strategy identity and Module 1 lineage.

Purpose:
    Display the current strategy / scenario / population slice materialized by Section 11.

Expected:
    exactly one row.

Interpretation:
    Module 2 strategy identifiers describe the downstream strategy.
    Module 1 scenario identifiers describe the upstream synthetic population and risk environment.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    module2_model_version,
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    strategy_run_id,
    strategy_run_ts,

    archive_run_flag,
    strategy_archive_reset_mode,
    failed_counteroffer_resolution,

    module1_input_source,
    module1_source_table_name,

    module1_model_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    anchor_date,

    MIN(latest_output_created_ts) AS min_latest_output_created_ts,
    MAX(latest_output_created_ts) AS max_latest_output_created_ts,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,
    COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    module2_model_version,
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    strategy_run_id,
    strategy_run_ts,

    archive_run_flag,
    strategy_archive_reset_mode,
    failed_counteroffer_resolution,

    module1_input_source,
    module1_source_table_name,

    module1_model_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    anchor_date

ORDER BY
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.3 Count by decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Show the final simulated outcome distribution for the latest-run output.

Boundary:
    decision_outcome is simulated strategy output, not real applicant treatment.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_latest_run,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(approved_amount) AS avg_approved_amount,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.4 Count by decision_path.

Purpose:
    Show internal final decision path labels.

Boundary:
    decision_path is internal simulated strategy traceability, not customer communication language.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_path,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_latest_run

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    decision_path,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    decision_path,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.5 Count by primary_reason_code.

Purpose:
    Show the main simulated explanation-code distribution.

Boundary:
    These are simulated strategy explanation codes only.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_latest_run

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code

ORDER BY
    CASE primary_reason_family
        WHEN 'POLICY_STOP' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 2
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 3
        WHEN 'APPROVAL' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.6 Product × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final simulated outcome distribution by product.

Interpretation:
    Product-level patterns should be explainable through product policy, requested exposure, PTI,
    LGD, Expected Loss, and counteroffer feasibility.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    product_type_policy_key,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(approved_amount) AS avg_approved_amount,
    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.7 Score band × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final simulated outcome distribution by borrower-quality segment.

Boundary:
    Score band supports interpretation but is not the only decision driver.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    score_band_policy_key,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(credit_score) AS avg_credit_score,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    score_band_policy_key,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE score_band_policy_key
        WHEN 'SUPER_PRIME' THEN 1
        WHEN 'PRIME' THEN 2
        WHEN 'NEAR_PRIME' THEN 3
        WHEN 'SUBPRIME' THEN 4
        WHEN 'DEEP_SUBPRIME' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.8 Product × primary_reason_code.

Purpose:
    Review whether simulated explanation-code themes concentrate by product.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    product_type_policy_key,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS avg_approved_amount_all_rows,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0)) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_all_rows

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code

ORDER BY
    product_type_policy_key,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.9 Score band × primary_reason_code.

Purpose:
    Review whether simulated explanation-code themes concentrate by borrower-quality segment.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    score_band_policy_key,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(credit_score) AS avg_credit_score,
    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    score_band_policy_key,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code

ORDER BY
    CASE score_band_policy_key
        WHEN 'SUPER_PRIME' THEN 1
        WHEN 'PRIME' THEN 2
        WHEN 'NEAR_PRIME' THEN 3
        WHEN 'SUBPRIME' THEN 4
        WHEN 'DEEP_SUBPRIME' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    primary_reason_family,
    primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.10 Strategy risk tier × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcomes by synthetic estimated-risk tier.

Boundary:
    estimated_pd remains the Module 1 SQL field and is interpreted as the synthetic estimated-PD
    proxy.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    strategy_risk_tier,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy,
    AVG(synthetic_risk_trigger_count) AS avg_synthetic_risk_trigger_count,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    strategy_risk_tier,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE strategy_risk_tier
        WHEN 'LOW_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_SYNTHETIC_RISK' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.11 Requested PTI bucket × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcomes by requested-structure affordability bucket.

Boundary:
    requested_payment_to_income_ratio is requested PTI.

    approved_payment_to_income_ratio is final simulated approved-exposure PTI proxy.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    requested_pti_bucket,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(affordability_trigger_count) AS avg_affordability_trigger_count

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    requested_pti_bucket,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE requested_pti_bucket
        WHEN 'LOW_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MODERATE_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 2
        WHEN 'ELEVATED_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HIGH_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 4
        WHEN 'SEVERE_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.12 Mixed-signal profile × decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final outcome behavior for realistic overlapping applicant profiles.

Boundary:
    mixed_signal_profile_type is diagnostic, not a final decision reason by itself.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    mixed_signal_profile_type,
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(mixed_signal_condition_count) AS avg_mixed_signal_condition_count,
    AVG(total_rule_trigger_count) AS avg_total_rule_trigger_count

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    mixed_signal_profile_type,
    decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE mixed_signal_profile_type
        WHEN 'NO_MIXED_SIGNAL_PROFILE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'STRONG_CREDIT_HIGH_PTI' THEN 2
        WHEN 'WEAK_CREDIT_LOW_PTI' THEN 3
        WHEN 'LARGE_EXPOSURE_LOW_RISK' THEN 4
        WHEN 'HIGH_RISK_LOW_EXPOSURE' THEN 5
        WHEN 'HIGH_DTI_LOW_REQUESTED_PTI' THEN 6
        WHEN 'MULTIPLE_MIXED_SIGNALS' THEN 7
        ELSE 99
    END,
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.13 Requested versus approved exposure by decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final exposure assignment conventions.

Expected:
    APPROVE preserves requested exposure.
    COUNTEROFFER reduces exposure.
    MANUAL_REVIEW remains unresolved.
    DECLINE uses zero approved exposure.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(approved_amount) AS avg_approved_amount,

    SUM(requested_amount) AS total_requested_amount,
    SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS total_approved_amount,

    AVG(exposure_reduction_amount) AS avg_exposure_reduction_amount,
    AVG(exposure_reduction_pct) AS avg_exposure_reduction_pct

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.14 Requested versus approved PTI by decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final affordability treatment.

Boundary:
    approved_payment_to_income_ratio is a strategy-simulation affordability proxy.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio)
        AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,

    AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio)
        AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio,

    AVG(
        requested_payment_to_income_ratio - approved_payment_to_income_ratio
    ) FILTER (
        WHERE approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS NOT NULL
    ) AS avg_pti_reduction_where_approved_pti_exists

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.15 Requested versus approved Expected Loss by decision_outcome.

Purpose:
    Review final requested-exposure Expected Loss versus approved-exposure Expected Loss.

Boundary:
    approved_expected_loss_amount is a synthetic strategy simulation metric, not a production loss
    forecast.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount)
        AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,

    AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount)
        AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount,

    SUM(requested_expected_loss_amount)
        AS total_requested_expected_loss_amount,

    SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
        AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.16 Simulated offer-exposure profile.

Purpose:
    Review positive simulated offer exposure.

Expected:
    simulated_offer_exposure_flag = TRUE only for APPROVE and COUNTEROFFER.

Boundary:
    This is simulated positive offer exposure, not booked or funded exposure.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    simulated_offer_exposure_flag,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_latest_run,

    AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS avg_approved_amount_all_apps,
    AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0)) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_all_apps

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY simulated_offer_exposure_flag

ORDER BY simulated_offer_exposure_flag;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
11.5.17 Section 11 readiness summary.

Purpose:
    Provide one compact readiness row for latest-run materialization.

Expected:
    section_11_latest_run_status =
        SECTION_11_LATEST_RUN_READY_FOR_ARCHIVE_PERSISTENCE

Interpretation:
    This confirms only that Section 11 is ready for Section 12.

    It does not validate archive persistence, matched comparison, Section 14 QA, Section 15 frontier,
    or Section 16 evidence capture.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH latest_run_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS latest_run_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version
        )) AS distinct_strategy_identity_count,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id
        )) AS distinct_module1_scenario_population_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE latest_output_created_ts IS NULL
        ) AS latest_output_created_ts_null_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome IS NULL
               OR decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
               OR decision_path IS NULL
               OR decision_resolution_source IS NULL
        ) AS final_decision_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE (
                    COALESCE(approval_flag::INT, 0)
                    + COALESCE(counteroffer_flag::INT, 0)
                    + COALESCE(manual_review_flag::INT, 0)
                    + COALESCE(decline_flag::INT, 0)
                  ) <> 1
        ) AS final_flag_reconciliation_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag
                  IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER'))
        ) AS simulated_offer_exposure_flag_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE primary_reason_code IS NULL
               OR primary_reason_family IS NULL
               OR triggered_reason_code_list IS NULL
               OR reason_priority_rank IS NULL
               OR reason_code_count IS NULL
               OR reason_code_count < 1
        ) AS reason_code_gap_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
        ) AS approve_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS counteroffer_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
        ) AS manual_review_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
        ) AS decline_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE
        ) AS simulated_offer_exposure_rows

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
)

SELECT
    latest_run_rows,
    distinct_application_id_count,

    distinct_strategy_identity_count,
    distinct_module1_scenario_population_count,

    latest_output_created_ts_null_rows,
    final_decision_gap_rows,
    final_flag_reconciliation_gap_rows,
    simulated_offer_exposure_flag_gap_rows,
    reason_code_gap_rows,

    approve_rows,
    counteroffer_rows,
    manual_review_rows,
    decline_rows,
    simulated_offer_exposure_rows,

    CASE
        WHEN latest_run_rows > 0
         AND latest_run_rows = distinct_application_id_count
         AND distinct_strategy_identity_count = 1
         AND distinct_module1_scenario_population_count = 1
         AND latest_output_created_ts_null_rows = 0
         AND final_decision_gap_rows = 0
         AND final_flag_reconciliation_gap_rows = 0
         AND simulated_offer_exposure_flag_gap_rows = 0
         AND reason_code_gap_rows = 0
            THEN 'SECTION_11_LATEST_RUN_READY_FOR_ARCHIVE_PERSISTENCE'
        ELSE 'REVIEW_SECTION_11_LATEST_RUN_BEFORE_ARCHIVE_PERSISTENCE'
    END AS section_11_latest_run_status

FROM latest_run_summary;



/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 11 — LATEST-RUN STRATEGY DECISION OUTPUT TABLE

If execution reaches this point:
    1. Section 11 dependency preflight passed.
    2. credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions exists.
    3. Row count matches tmp_m2_stage_7_reason_code_assignment.
    4. application_id remains unique.
    5. Exactly one Module 2 strategy identity is present.
    6. Exactly one Module 1 scenario / population identity is present.
    7. Module 2 strategy metadata is populated.
    8. archive_run_flag and strategy_archive_reset_mode are populated and valid.
    9. Module 1 lineage is populated.
    10. final decision_outcome is populated.
    11. final decision_outcome is one of APPROVE, COUNTEROFFER, MANUAL_REVIEW, DECLINE.
    12. final decision flags reconcile to decision_outcome.
    13. exactly one final decision flag is TRUE per row.
    14. simulated_offer_exposure_flag is TRUE only for APPROVE and COUNTEROFFER.
    15. simulated_offer_exposure_flag is FALSE for MANUAL_REVIEW and DECLINE.
    16. approved_amount conventions hold by decision_outcome.
    17. approved_expected_loss_amount conventions hold by decision_outcome.
    18. primary_reason_code is populated for every row.
    19. primary_reason_family aligns to decision_outcome.
    20. triggered_reason_code_list is populated for every row.
    21. latest_output_created_ts is populated.
    22. Practical latest-run indexes are created.
    23. Campaign registry IDs remain outside the row-level latest-run output and are persisted later
        through Section 16 evidence capture.
    24. Local latest-run diagnostics are available for review.

Section 11 established:
    1. The permanent latest-run output surface.
    2. One current-run row per application_id.
    3. Final simulated decision outcomes.
    4. Final simulated offer-exposure flags.
    5. Final approved exposure fields.
    6. Final approved affordability proxy fields.
    7. Final approved Expected Loss fields.
    8. Simulated strategy explanation-code fields.
    9. Strategy, product-policy, segmentation, rule-trigger, routing, and exposure-treatment trace
       fields needed for downstream QA and evidence capture.
    10. The current-run table Section 12 needs for governed archive persistence.

No archive rows have been inserted.
No matched strategy comparison logic has been created.
No full Module 2 QA framework has been created.
No strategy frontier summary has been created.
No executive evidence rows have been inserted.
No BRD or Validation Summary documentation has been drafted.

Next section:
    Section 12 should consume credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions and apply governed archive
    persistence using archive_run_flag and strategy_archive_reset_mode.

***************************************************************************************************/


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 12 — STRATEGY DECISION ARCHIVE PERSISTENCE LAYER
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Persist completed latest-run Module 2 strategy outputs into the governed strategy archive.

    Section 12 answers:

        "Should this completed Module 2 latest-run strategy output become governed historical
         evidence, and if so, how should the archive handle prior rows for the same strategy /
         Module 1 scenario / population slice?"

    Section 12 is the history-control layer.

    Section 11 created the replaceable latest-run output table.
    Section 12 preserves completed runs in the archive so later sections can compare, validate,
    summarize, and capture evidence across multiple completed strategy slices.

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm the latest-run output exists, is populated, and is unique at application_id.
    2. Confirm the latest-run output contains one unambiguous archive-control configuration.
    3. Confirm the latest-run output contains one unambiguous archive replacement key.
    4. Create or reuse credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive.
    5. Add missing latest-run columns to the archive table when safe.
    6. Add archive_inserted_ts when needed.
    7. Validate latest-run / archive schema alignment.
    8. Capture archive inventory before persistence.
    9. Apply governed archive persistence behavior:
            archive_run_flag = FALSE
            strategy_archive_reset_mode = NONE
            strategy_archive_reset_mode = STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY
            strategy_archive_reset_mode = STRATEGY_SET_ONLY
            strategy_archive_reset_mode = ALL
    10. Insert the current latest-run output into the archive when archive_run_flag = TRUE.
    11. Add archive_inserted_ts as archive persistence audit metadata.
    12. Capture archive inventory after persistence.
    13. Create archive validation indexes before row-level persistence checks.
    14. Validate archive skip / insert / replacement / reset behavior.
    15. Validate archive row-level grain.
    16. Validate current-slice persistence fidelity versus the latest-run table.
    17. Create practical archive review indexes.
    18. Provide lightweight archive diagnostics before Section 13 matched comparison.

WHO SHOULD REVIEW THIS SECTION:
    Credit strategy reviewers:
        Confirm that the completed latest-run strategy slice was archived only when intended and that
        reruns replaced the intended slice.

    Model governance / validation reviewers:
        Confirm that the archive is stable, traceable, unique at archive grain, and not silently
        mixed across strategies, Module 1 scenarios, or populations.

    SQL reviewers:
        Confirm that archive persistence uses explicit column lists, schema checks, safe reset modes,
        row-count audits, and row-level persistence fidelity checks.

    Portfolio / executive reviewers:
        Use Section 12 diagnostics to confirm that a completed strategy run is available for
        Section 13 comparison, Section 15 frontier review, and Section 16 evidence capture.

WHEN TO RUN THIS SECTION:
    Run Section 12 after:

        Section 11 — Latest-Run Strategy Decision Output Table

    Section 12 should be run before:

        Section 13 — Archive Inventory and Matched Strategy Comparison Framework
        Section 14 — Module 2 Validation, QA, and Strategy Outcome Diagnostics
        Section 15 — Strategy Frontier Summary and Executive Comparison View
        Section 16 — Strategy Run Evidence Capture and Executive Story Register

INPUT:
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

OUTPUT:
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive

TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC OUTPUTS:
    tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before
    tmp_m2_archive_inventory_after
    tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit

WHY LATEST-RUN OUTPUT AND ARCHIVE PERSISTENCE ARE SEPARATE:
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions is the current latest-run output.

    It is replaced each run.

    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive is the governed historical evidence layer.

    It supports:
        completed-run retention,
        rerun replacement control,
        matched baseline / challenger comparison,
        strategy frontier analysis,
        validation evidence review,
        executive evidence capture,
        README narrative support,
        LinkedIn campaign narrative support,
        and future Validation Summary drafting.

SECTION 12 DOES NOT RECALCULATE STRATEGY RESULTS:
    Section 12 does not recalculate:
        decision_outcome,
        decision_path,
        approved_amount,
        approved_payment_to_income_ratio,
        approved_expected_loss_amount,
        simulated reason codes,
        trigger flags,
        segmentation fields,
        counteroffer feasibility,
        final outcome flags,
        or simulated offer-exposure flags.

    It persists the already-materialized latest-run output.

ARCHIVE ROW-LEVEL GRAIN:
    One archive row per:

        strategy_set_name
        strategy_name
        strategy_version
        module1_scenario_set_name
        module1_scenario_name
        population_id
        application_id

ARCHIVE REPLACEMENT / RERUN KEY:
    The archive replacement key is:

        strategy_set_name
        strategy_name
        strategy_version
        module1_scenario_set_name
        module1_scenario_name
        population_id

WHY APPLICATION_ID IS EXCLUDED FROM THE REPLACEMENT KEY:
    The replacement key identifies the completed strategy / scenario / population slice.

    application_id identifies each row within that slice.

    Deleting by replacement key clears the prior completed slice before inserting the current
    latest-run slice.

AUDIT METADATA BOUNDARY:
    strategy_run_id:
        run traceability metadata.

    strategy_run_ts:
        run timestamp metadata.

    latest_output_created_ts:
        latest-run table materialization metadata.

    archive_inserted_ts:
        archive persistence metadata.

    None of these timestamp or run-audit fields define archive replacement grain.
    None of these timestamp or run-audit fields should define matched strategy comparison grain.

ARCHIVE CONTROL MODES:
    archive_run_flag = FALSE:
        Skip archive persistence.
        Do not delete archive rows.
        Do not insert archive rows.

    strategy_archive_reset_mode = NONE:
        Append-only mode for the current replacement key.
        Do not delete existing archive rows before insert.
        Fail if the current replacement key already exists.

    strategy_archive_reset_mode = STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY:
        Ordinary governed rerun mode.
        Replace only the current strategy / Module 1 scenario / population slice.

    strategy_archive_reset_mode = STRATEGY_SET_ONLY:
        Broader reset mode.
        Replace all strategy_name / strategy_version outputs within the current strategy_set_name
        for the selected Module 1 scenario and population.

    strategy_archive_reset_mode = ALL:
        Broadest reset mode.
        Delete all archive rows before inserting the current latest-run output.

        Use intentionally.

SCHEMA ALIGNMENT NOTE:
    The archive table is created from the current latest-run output schema when the archive does not
    yet exist.

    If the latest-run schema evolves after the archive already exists, Section 12 safely adds missing
    latest-run columns to the archive table and then validates type alignment.

    Section 12 does not attempt to be a full dynamic schema migration system.

    It provides practical governed archive compatibility checks:
        missing latest-run column checks,
        safe ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS behavior,
        data-type alignment checks,
        unexpected archive column checks,
        and archive_inserted_ts existence checks.

WHY ARCHIVE VALIDATION INDEXES ARE CREATED BEFORE SECTION 12.6:
    Section 12.6 compares the latest-run table to the current archived slice at row-level archive
    grain.

    As the archive grows across strategy and scenario slices, row-level validation can become slow if
    the latest-run and archive tables lack supporting indexes.

    Section 12.5A creates validation indexes before Section 12.6 performs persistence fidelity
    checks.

CAMPAIGN REGISTRY BOUNDARY:
    Campaign IDs such as:
        module1_run_id,
        module2_run_id,
        showcase_id,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,
        readme_storyline_label,
        linkedin_post_sequence,
        validation_summary_section_hint

    are evidence-linkage metadata.

    They are persisted later through Section 16 evidence capture.

    They do not replace archive grain and are not inserted into every archive row in Section 12.

MATCHED COMPARISON BOUNDARY:
    Section 12 persists archive rows.

    It does not compare archived strategies.

    Matched strategy comparison is built in Section 13.

SECTION 14 QA BOUNDARY:
    Section 12 verifies archive persistence fidelity.

    It does not replace latest-run validation.

    Full latest-run validation remains Section 14.

SQL CONCEPTS TAUGHT IN THIS SECTION:
    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ... LIKE:
        Creates the archive table from the latest-run table shape when the archive does not yet exist.

    ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS:
        Adds archive_inserted_ts and missing latest-run columns without failing on reruns.

    pg_attribute + format_type:
        Reads exact PostgreSQL column types so missing archive columns can be added safely.

    information_schema / pg_catalog inspection:
        Validates schema alignment before persistence.

    DO $$ ... END $$:
        Runs procedural archive-control logic with variables, IF statements, dynamic SQL, and explicit
        exceptions.

    SELECT ... INTO:
        Loads counts, archive controls, replacement keys, and diagnostic values into PL/pgSQL
        variables.

    GET DIAGNOSTICS ... ROW_COUNT:
        Captures how many rows were deleted or inserted by the most recent DML statement.

    EXECUTE FORMAT(...):
        Runs a dynamic INSERT statement using an explicit column list derived from the latest-run
        schema.

    IS DISTINCT FROM:
        Performs NULL-safe comparisons when validating latest-run versus archived values.

    FULL OUTER JOIN:
        Compares before / after archive inventory and latest-run / archive row-level persistence even
        when a row exists on only one side.

    CREATE UNIQUE INDEX:
        Enforces the row-level archive grain so matched comparison does not operate on duplicate
        archived applications.

GOVERNANCE ROLE:
    Section 12 protects:
        archive history,
        replacement discipline,
        schema consistency,
        row-level archive grain,
        and persistence fidelity.

COMMON MISUSE TO AVOID:
    Do not use the latest-run table as strategy history.
    Do not manually delete archive rows outside governed archive controls.
    Do not treat timestamp fields as matched-comparison keys.
    Do not interpret archive persistence as recalculation or revalidation of decision logic.
    Do not interpret archive_inserted_ts as a business outcome.
    Do not treat archive_run_flag = TRUE as proof that validation passed.
    Do not treat archive persistence as a substitute for Section 14 QA.

***************************************************************************************************/



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 12.1 — LATEST-RUN SOURCE INTEGRITY AND ARCHIVE-CONTROL PREFLIGHT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that archive persistence is operating on one completed, internally coherent latest-run
    strategy slice.

    Section 12.1 answers:

        "Is credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions safe to archive?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm latest-run table exists.
    2. Confirm latest-run table contains rows.
    3. Confirm latest-run table is unique at application_id.
    4. Confirm the latest-run output contains exactly one archive-control configuration.
    5. Confirm the latest-run output contains exactly one archive replacement key.
    6. Confirm archive controls are populated and valid.
    7. Confirm key identity, lineage, decision, reason-code, requested-risk, and final-output fields
       needed by archive persistence are populated.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 12.1 does not create archive rows.
    Section 12.1 does not delete archive rows.
    Section 12.1 does not update archive rows.
    Section 12.1 does not create comparison outputs.
    Section 12.1 does not run full Section 14 QA.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_latest_count BIGINT;
    v_latest_distinct_app_count BIGINT;
    v_duplicate_application_count BIGINT;

    v_archive_control_null_count BIGINT;
    v_archive_control_invalid_count BIGINT;
    v_archive_control_configuration_count BIGINT;
    v_archive_replacement_key_count BIGINT;

    v_required_latest_output_gap_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: latest-run output table must exist.

    SQL mechanics:
        TO_REGCLASS returns NULL if the table is absent.

    Business interpretation:
        Section 12 must archive the Section 11 latest-run output. If that table is absent, the
        archive step cannot proceed.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    IF TO_REGCLASS('credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions') IS NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions does not exist. Run Section 11 before Section 12.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: latest-run output must contain rows.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_latest_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;

    IF v_latest_count <= 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: latest-run strategy_decisions table contains zero rows.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: application_id must be unique in latest-run output.

    Archive persistence assumes one latest-run row per synthetic application for the current run key.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO v_latest_distinct_app_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;

    IF v_latest_distinct_app_count <> v_latest_count THEN
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_duplicate_application_count
        FROM (
            SELECT application_id
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
            GROUP BY application_id
            HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
        ) d;

        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: latest-run application_id is not unique. Latest rows: %, distinct application_id count: %, duplicate application_id group count: %.',
            v_latest_count,
            v_latest_distinct_app_count,
            v_duplicate_application_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: archive controls must be populated and valid.

    archive_run_flag:
        TRUE or FALSE.

    strategy_archive_reset_mode:
        NONE
        STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY
        STRATEGY_SET_ONLY
        ALL
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_archive_control_null_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE archive_run_flag IS NULL
       OR strategy_archive_reset_mode IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_archive_reset_mode), '') IS NULL;

    IF v_archive_control_null_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: % latest-run row(s) have missing archive controls.',
            v_archive_control_null_count;
    END IF;

    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_archive_control_invalid_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE strategy_archive_reset_mode NOT IN (
        'NONE',
        'STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY',
        'STRATEGY_SET_ONLY',
        'ALL'
    );

    IF v_archive_control_invalid_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: % latest-run row(s) have invalid strategy_archive_reset_mode values.',
            v_archive_control_invalid_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: archive-control configuration must be unambiguous.

    Business interpretation:
        A single latest-run strategy slice cannot contain mixed archive_run_flag or
        strategy_archive_reset_mode values.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT (
        archive_run_flag,
        strategy_archive_reset_mode
    ))
    INTO v_archive_control_configuration_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;

    IF v_archive_control_configuration_count <> 1 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: latest-run output contains % archive-control configurations. Expected exactly one.',
            v_archive_control_configuration_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: archive replacement key must be unambiguous.

    Replacement key:
        strategy_set_name
        strategy_name
        strategy_version
        module1_scenario_set_name
        module1_scenario_name
        population_id
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT (
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    ))
    INTO v_archive_replacement_key_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;

    IF v_archive_replacement_key_count <> 1 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: latest-run output contains % archive replacement keys. Expected exactly one.',
            v_archive_replacement_key_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: required latest-run output fields needed by archive persistence.

    Important:
        MANUAL_REVIEW rows are unresolved by design, so approved_amount and
        approved_expected_loss_amount may be NULL only for MANUAL_REVIEW.

        APPROVE, COUNTEROFFER, and DECLINE rows must have final approved exposure and approved
        Expected Loss populated according to Section 11 conventions.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_required_latest_output_gap_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    WHERE module2_model_version IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module2_model_version), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_set_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_set_name), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_name), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_version IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_version), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_run_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(strategy_run_id), '') IS NULL
       OR strategy_run_ts IS NULL

       OR module1_model_version IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_model_version), '') IS NULL
       OR module1_scenario_set_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_scenario_set_name), '') IS NULL
       OR module1_scenario_name IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(module1_scenario_name), '') IS NULL
       OR population_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(population_id), '') IS NULL

       OR application_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(application_id), '') IS NULL
       OR applicant_id IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(applicant_id), '') IS NULL

       OR requested_amount IS NULL
       OR requested_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
       OR estimated_pd IS NULL
       OR estimated_lgd IS NULL

       OR decision_outcome IS NULL
       OR decision_outcome NOT IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'MANUAL_REVIEW', 'DECLINE')
       OR decision_path IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(decision_path), '') IS NULL

       OR approval_flag IS NULL
       OR counteroffer_flag IS NULL
       OR manual_review_flag IS NULL
       OR decline_flag IS NULL
       OR simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS NULL

       OR primary_reason_code IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(primary_reason_code), '') IS NULL
       OR primary_reason_family IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(primary_reason_family), '') IS NULL
       OR triggered_reason_code_list IS NULL
       OR NULLIF(BTRIM(triggered_reason_code_list), '') IS NULL
       OR reason_priority_rank IS NULL
       OR reason_code_count IS NULL

       OR latest_output_created_ts IS NULL

       OR (
            decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'DECLINE')
            AND approved_amount IS NULL
       )

       OR (
            decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER', 'DECLINE')
            AND approved_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
       );

    IF v_required_latest_output_gap_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: % latest-run row(s) are missing required archive persistence fields.',
            v_required_latest_output_gap_count;
    END IF;
END $$;


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 12.2 — ARCHIVE TABLE SETUP AND SCHEMA ALIGNMENT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Create or reuse the governed strategy decision archive table and align its schema to the current
    latest-run output table before archive persistence occurs.

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Create credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive if it does not already exist.
    2. Ensure archive_inserted_ts exists as archive-only persistence metadata.
    3. Add any latest-run columns missing from the archive table.
    4. Verify no latest-run columns remain missing.
    5. Verify common latest-run / archive columns have matching PostgreSQL data types.
    6. Verify archive contains no unexpected columns except archive_inserted_ts.
    7. Verify archive_inserted_ts exists.

WHY THIS IMPLEMENTATION USES DISTINCT CATALOG ALIASES:
    This block runs inside PL/pgSQL.

    PL/pgSQL variable names and SQL aliases can create name-resolution ambiguity when they share the
    same identifier.

    This implementation avoids that risk by:
        using add_col as the loop record variable;
        using explicit catalog aliases such as lat_cls, arc_cls, and ins_cls;
        avoiding pg_class c aliases inside the DO block.

BOUNDARY:
    This section may create or alter the archive table structure.

    It does not delete archive rows.
    It does not insert archive rows.
    It does not update archive row values.
    It does not recalculate strategy outputs.

****************************************************************************************************/

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    (LIKE credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions INCLUDING DEFAULTS);

ALTER TABLE credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS archive_inserted_ts TIMESTAMP;

DO $$
DECLARE
    add_col RECORD;

    v_missing_archive_column_count BIGINT;
    v_missing_archive_columns TEXT;

    v_type_mismatch_count BIGINT;
    v_type_mismatch_columns TEXT;

    v_unexpected_archive_column_count BIGINT;
    v_unexpected_archive_columns TEXT;

    v_archive_inserted_ts_exists BOOLEAN;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Add missing latest-run columns to the archive table.

    SQL mechanics:
        pg_attribute identifies latest-run columns and their exact PostgreSQL type.

        format_type(atttypid, atttypmod) returns type text such as:
            text
            boolean
            integer
            numeric(12,6)
            timestamp without time zone

        ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS makes reruns safe.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    FOR add_col IN
        SELECT
            latest_att.attname AS column_name,
            pg_catalog.format_type(latest_att.atttypid, latest_att.atttypmod) AS column_type
        FROM pg_attribute latest_att

        JOIN pg_class latest_cls
            ON latest_cls.oid = latest_att.attrelid

        JOIN pg_namespace latest_ns
            ON latest_ns.oid = latest_cls.relnamespace

        WHERE latest_ns.nspname = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
          AND latest_cls.relname = 'strategy_decisions'
          AND latest_att.attnum > 0
          AND latest_att.attisdropped IS FALSE
          AND NOT EXISTS (
              SELECT 1
              FROM pg_attribute archive_att

              JOIN pg_class archive_cls
                  ON archive_cls.oid = archive_att.attrelid

              JOIN pg_namespace archive_ns
                  ON archive_ns.oid = archive_cls.relnamespace

              WHERE archive_ns.nspname = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
                AND archive_cls.relname = 'strategy_decisions_archive'
                AND archive_att.attnum > 0
                AND archive_att.attisdropped IS FALSE
                AND archive_att.attname = latest_att.attname
          )
        ORDER BY latest_att.attnum
    LOOP
        EXECUTE FORMAT(
            'ALTER TABLE credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS %I %s',
            add_col.column_name,
            add_col.column_type
        );
    END LOOP;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Verify no latest-run columns remain missing from archive.

    Business interpretation:
        Every latest-run column should be preservable in the archive.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    WITH latest_columns AS (
        SELECT
            lat_att.attname AS column_name
        FROM pg_attribute lat_att

        JOIN pg_class lat_cls
            ON lat_cls.oid = lat_att.attrelid

        JOIN pg_namespace lat_ns
            ON lat_ns.oid = lat_cls.relnamespace

        WHERE lat_ns.nspname = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
          AND lat_cls.relname = 'strategy_decisions'
          AND lat_att.attnum > 0
          AND lat_att.attisdropped IS FALSE
    ),

    archive_columns AS (
        SELECT
            arc_att.attname AS column_name
        FROM pg_attribute arc_att

        JOIN pg_class arc_cls
            ON arc_cls.oid = arc_att.attrelid

        JOIN pg_namespace arc_ns
            ON arc_ns.oid = arc_cls.relnamespace

        WHERE arc_ns.nspname = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
          AND arc_cls.relname = 'strategy_decisions_archive'
          AND arc_att.attnum > 0
          AND arc_att.attisdropped IS FALSE
    ),

    missing_columns AS (
        SELECT
            l.column_name
        FROM latest_columns l

        LEFT JOIN archive_columns a
            ON a.column_name = l.column_name

        WHERE a.column_name IS NULL
    )

    SELECT
        COUNT(*),
        STRING_AGG(column_name, ', ' ORDER BY column_name)
    INTO
        v_missing_archive_column_count,
        v_missing_archive_columns
    FROM missing_columns;

    IF v_missing_archive_column_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: archive table is missing latest-run column(s): %.',
            v_missing_archive_columns;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Verify PostgreSQL type alignment for common latest-run / archive columns.

    SQL mechanics:
        format_type compares exact rendered PostgreSQL type definitions.

    Business interpretation:
        Archive persistence should not silently coerce or distort latest-run output values.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    WITH latest_columns AS (
        SELECT
            lat_att.attname AS column_name,
            pg_catalog.format_type(lat_att.atttypid, lat_att.atttypmod) AS column_type
        FROM pg_attribute lat_att

        JOIN pg_class lat_cls
            ON lat_cls.oid = lat_att.attrelid

        JOIN pg_namespace lat_ns
            ON lat_ns.oid = lat_cls.relnamespace

        WHERE lat_ns.nspname = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
          AND lat_cls.relname = 'strategy_decisions'
          AND lat_att.attnum > 0
          AND lat_att.attisdropped IS FALSE
    ),

    archive_columns AS (
        SELECT
            arc_att.attname AS column_name,
            pg_catalog.format_type(arc_att.atttypid, arc_att.atttypmod) AS column_type
        FROM pg_attribute arc_att

        JOIN pg_class arc_cls
            ON arc_cls.oid = arc_att.attrelid

        JOIN pg_namespace arc_ns
            ON arc_ns.oid = arc_cls.relnamespace

        WHERE arc_ns.nspname = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
          AND arc_cls.relname = 'strategy_decisions_archive'
          AND arc_att.attnum > 0
          AND arc_att.attisdropped IS FALSE
    ),

    type_mismatches AS (
        SELECT
            l.column_name,
            l.column_type AS latest_type,
            a.column_type AS archive_type
        FROM latest_columns l

        JOIN archive_columns a
            ON a.column_name = l.column_name

        WHERE a.column_type IS DISTINCT FROM l.column_type
    )

    SELECT
        COUNT(*),
        STRING_AGG(
            column_name || ' latest=' || latest_type || ' archive=' || archive_type,
            '; ' ORDER BY column_name
        )
    INTO
        v_type_mismatch_count,
        v_type_mismatch_columns
    FROM type_mismatches;

    IF v_type_mismatch_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: latest-run / archive column type mismatch(es): %.',
            v_type_mismatch_columns;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Verify archive has no unexpected columns other than archive_inserted_ts.

    Business interpretation:
        Unexpected archive columns usually indicate stale schema drift or manual alteration.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    WITH latest_columns AS (
        SELECT
            lat_att.attname AS column_name
        FROM pg_attribute lat_att

        JOIN pg_class lat_cls
            ON lat_cls.oid = lat_att.attrelid

        JOIN pg_namespace lat_ns
            ON lat_ns.oid = lat_cls.relnamespace

        WHERE lat_ns.nspname = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
          AND lat_cls.relname = 'strategy_decisions'
          AND lat_att.attnum > 0
          AND lat_att.attisdropped IS FALSE
    ),

    archive_columns AS (
        SELECT
            arc_att.attname AS column_name
        FROM pg_attribute arc_att

        JOIN pg_class arc_cls
            ON arc_cls.oid = arc_att.attrelid

        JOIN pg_namespace arc_ns
            ON arc_ns.oid = arc_cls.relnamespace

        WHERE arc_ns.nspname = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
          AND arc_cls.relname = 'strategy_decisions_archive'
          AND arc_att.attnum > 0
          AND arc_att.attisdropped IS FALSE
    ),

    unexpected_columns AS (
        SELECT
            a.column_name
        FROM archive_columns a

        LEFT JOIN latest_columns l
            ON l.column_name = a.column_name

        WHERE l.column_name IS NULL
          AND a.column_name <> 'archive_inserted_ts'
    )

    SELECT
        COUNT(*),
        STRING_AGG(column_name, ', ' ORDER BY column_name)
    INTO
        v_unexpected_archive_column_count,
        v_unexpected_archive_columns
    FROM unexpected_columns;

    IF v_unexpected_archive_column_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: archive table contains unexpected column(s): %. Review archive schema before persistence.',
            v_unexpected_archive_columns;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Verify archive_inserted_ts exists.

    archive_inserted_ts is intentionally archive-only.
    It records when archive persistence occurred.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM pg_attribute ins_att

        JOIN pg_class ins_cls
            ON ins_cls.oid = ins_att.attrelid

        JOIN pg_namespace ins_ns
            ON ins_ns.oid = ins_cls.relnamespace

        WHERE ins_ns.nspname = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
          AND ins_cls.relname = 'strategy_decisions_archive'
          AND ins_att.attname = 'archive_inserted_ts'
          AND ins_att.attnum > 0
          AND ins_att.attisdropped IS FALSE
    )
    INTO v_archive_inserted_ts_exists;

    IF v_archive_inserted_ts_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: archive table is missing archive_inserted_ts.';
    END IF;
END $$;


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 12.3 — ARCHIVE INVENTORY SNAPSHOT BEFORE PERSISTENCE
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Capture pre-persistence archive inventory so Section 12 can validate exactly what changed.

    Section 12.3 answers:

        "What archive slices existed before the current archive-control logic ran?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Drop and recreate tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before.
    2. Summarize archive rows by archive replacement slice before Section 12.4.
    3. Drop and recreate tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit.
    4. Prepare a one-row temporary audit table that Section 12.4 will populate.

WHY THIS SECTION EXISTS:
    Archive-control modes should be testable.

    The before snapshot allows later validation that:
        skip mode changed nothing;
        scenario-only mode changed only the current slice;
        strategy-set mode changed only the selected strategy set for the selected scenario/population;
        all mode cleared prior archive state;
        none mode appended only when no prior current-key rows existed.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 12.3 does not modify archive rows.

****************************************************************************************************/

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before;

CREATE TEMP TABLE tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before
ON COMMIT PRESERVE ROWS
AS
SELECT
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
GROUP BY
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id;


DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit;

CREATE TEMP TABLE tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Active archive controls.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    archive_run_flag                         BOOLEAN,
    strategy_archive_reset_mode              TEXT,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Archive replacement / rerun key.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    strategy_set_name                        TEXT,
    strategy_name                            TEXT,
    strategy_version                         TEXT,
    module1_scenario_set_name                TEXT,
    module1_scenario_name                    TEXT,
    population_id                            TEXT,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Latest-run source row counts.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    latest_run_row_count                     BIGINT,
    latest_run_distinct_application_count    BIGINT,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Archive before / delete / insert / after counts.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    archive_row_count_before                 BIGINT,
    archive_deleted_rows                     BIGINT,
    archive_inserted_rows                    BIGINT,
    archive_row_count_after                  BIGINT,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Human-readable archive action label.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    archive_action                           TEXT,
    archive_action_ts                        TIMESTAMP
) ON COMMIT PRESERVE ROWS;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 12.4 — APPLY ARCHIVE CONTROL LOGIC
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Apply the active archive persistence control settings to the governed strategy archive.

    Section 12.4 answers:

        "Should this latest-run strategy slice be inserted into archive history, and what prior
         archive rows should be removed first?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Read the single archive-control configuration and replacement key.
    2. Count latest-run rows and archive rows before persistence.
    3. If archive_run_flag = FALSE, skip delete and insert behavior.
    4. If archive_run_flag = TRUE, apply strategy_archive_reset_mode.
    5. Insert latest-run rows into archive using an explicit dynamic column list.
    6. Capture deleted-row and inserted-row counts.
    7. Insert one audit row into tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit.

WHY DYNAMIC INSERT IS USED:
    The archive is designed to contain all latest-run columns plus archive_inserted_ts.

    Instead of relying on physical column order, Section 12 builds an explicit latest-run column list
    from information_schema.columns.

    This is safer and more auditable than INSERT ... SELECT *.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 12.4 modifies archive rows only according to governed archive controls.

    It does not recalculate decision outcomes.
    It does not recalculate approved exposure.
    It does not recalculate approved Expected Loss.
    It does not reassign simulated reason codes.

****************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_archive_run_flag BOOLEAN;
    v_strategy_archive_reset_mode TEXT;

    v_strategy_set_name TEXT;
    v_strategy_name TEXT;
    v_strategy_version TEXT;
    v_module1_scenario_set_name TEXT;
    v_module1_scenario_name TEXT;
    v_population_id TEXT;

    v_latest_count BIGINT;
    v_latest_distinct_app_count BIGINT;
    v_archive_before_count BIGINT;
    v_archive_after_count BIGINT;
    v_existing_key_count BIGINT;

    v_deleted_rows BIGINT := 0;
    v_inserted_rows BIGINT := 0;

    v_archive_action TEXT;
    v_insert_columns TEXT;
    v_select_columns TEXT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Read the single archive-control configuration and archive replacement key.

    Section 12.1 has already validated that this SELECT resolves to one logical configuration.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT
        archive_run_flag,
        strategy_archive_reset_mode,
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    INTO
        v_archive_run_flag,
        v_strategy_archive_reset_mode,
        v_strategy_set_name,
        v_strategy_name,
        v_strategy_version,
        v_module1_scenario_set_name,
        v_module1_scenario_name,
        v_population_id
    FROM (
        SELECT DISTINCT
            archive_run_flag,
            strategy_archive_reset_mode,
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id
        FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    ) k;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Count latest-run rows.

    These counts become audit evidence for archive persistence.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT
        COUNT(*),
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO
        v_latest_count,
        v_latest_distinct_app_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Count total archive rows before persistence.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_archive_before_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    archive_run_flag = FALSE:
        Skip archive persistence.

    Business purpose:
        Allows development runs or diagnostic runs to materialize latest-run output without
        preserving it as governed archive history.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    IF v_archive_run_flag IS FALSE THEN
        v_archive_action := 'ARCHIVE_SKIPPED_ARCHIVE_RUN_FLAG_FALSE';


    ELSE
        /*---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        archive_run_flag = TRUE:
            Apply governed archive reset / replacement mode before insert.
        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

        IF v_strategy_archive_reset_mode = 'NONE' THEN
            /*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            NONE:
                Append-only behavior for the current replacement key.

                If the key already exists, fail rather than creating duplicate archive grain.
            -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
            SELECT COUNT(*)
            INTO v_existing_key_count
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
            WHERE strategy_set_name = v_strategy_set_name
              AND strategy_name = v_strategy_name
              AND strategy_version = v_strategy_version
              AND module1_scenario_set_name = v_module1_scenario_set_name
              AND module1_scenario_name = v_module1_scenario_name
              AND population_id = v_population_id;

            IF v_existing_key_count > 0 THEN
                RAISE EXCEPTION
                    'Module 2 Section 12 failure: strategy_archive_reset_mode = NONE but archive already contains % row(s) for the current replacement key.',
                    v_existing_key_count;
            END IF;

            v_archive_action := 'ARCHIVE_INSERTED_NONE_MODE_NO_PRIOR_KEY';


        ELSIF v_strategy_archive_reset_mode = 'STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY' THEN
            /*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY:
                Ordinary governed rerun behavior.

                Deletes only the prior archived rows for the current:
                    strategy_set_name,
                    strategy_name,
                    strategy_version,
                    module1_scenario_set_name,
                    module1_scenario_name,
                    population_id.
            -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
            DELETE FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
            WHERE strategy_set_name = v_strategy_set_name
              AND strategy_name = v_strategy_name
              AND strategy_version = v_strategy_version
              AND module1_scenario_set_name = v_module1_scenario_set_name
              AND module1_scenario_name = v_module1_scenario_name
              AND population_id = v_population_id;

            GET DIAGNOSTICS v_deleted_rows = ROW_COUNT;
            v_archive_action := 'ARCHIVE_REPLACED_STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY';


        ELSIF v_strategy_archive_reset_mode = 'STRATEGY_SET_ONLY' THEN
            /*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            STRATEGY_SET_ONLY:
                Broader reset behavior.

                Deletes all archived rows in the current strategy_set_name for the selected Module 1
                scenario and population.

                This supports restarting a strategy-family comparison without disturbing unrelated
                Module 1 scenarios or unrelated populations.
            -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
            DELETE FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
            WHERE strategy_set_name = v_strategy_set_name
              AND module1_scenario_set_name = v_module1_scenario_set_name
              AND module1_scenario_name = v_module1_scenario_name
              AND population_id = v_population_id;

            GET DIAGNOSTICS v_deleted_rows = ROW_COUNT;
            v_archive_action := 'ARCHIVE_REPLACED_STRATEGY_SET_ONLY';


        ELSIF v_strategy_archive_reset_mode = 'ALL' THEN
            /*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
            ALL:
                Broadest reset behavior.

                Deletes all archive rows before inserting the current latest-run output.

                Use intentionally.
            -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
            DELETE FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive;

            GET DIAGNOSTICS v_deleted_rows = ROW_COUNT;
            v_archive_action := 'ARCHIVE_FULL_RESET_ALL_MODE';


        ELSE
            RAISE EXCEPTION
                'Module 2 Section 12 failure: unsupported strategy_archive_reset_mode: %.',
                v_strategy_archive_reset_mode;
        END IF;


        /*---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        Insert current latest-run rows into archive.

        SQL mechanics:
            v_insert_columns:
                target archive columns matching latest-run output columns.

            v_select_columns:
                source expressions from credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions.

            archive_inserted_ts:
                added separately using CURRENT_TIMESTAMP.

        Why this is safer than SELECT *:
            SELECT * depends on physical column order.
            This dynamic insert uses explicit column names.
        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
        SELECT
            STRING_AGG(FORMAT('%I', column_name), ', ' ORDER BY ordinal_position),
            STRING_AGG(FORMAT('sd.%I', column_name), ', ' ORDER BY ordinal_position)
        INTO
            v_insert_columns,
            v_select_columns
        FROM information_schema.columns
        WHERE table_schema = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
          AND table_name = 'strategy_decisions';

        IF v_insert_columns IS NULL OR v_select_columns IS NULL THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION
                'Module 2 Section 12 failure: unable to derive latest-run insert column list for archive persistence.';
        END IF;

        EXECUTE FORMAT(
            'INSERT INTO credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (%s, archive_inserted_ts)
             SELECT %s, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
             FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions sd',
            v_insert_columns,
            v_select_columns
        );

        GET DIAGNOSTICS v_inserted_rows = ROW_COUNT;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Count total archive rows after archive-control behavior.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_archive_after_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Insert one temporary archive persistence audit row.

    Boundary:
        This audit row supports current-run Section 12 validation.

        It is not persistent executive evidence.
        Persistent evidence is captured later in Section 16.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    INSERT INTO tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit (
        archive_run_flag,
        strategy_archive_reset_mode,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        latest_run_row_count,
        latest_run_distinct_application_count,

        archive_row_count_before,
        archive_deleted_rows,
        archive_inserted_rows,
        archive_row_count_after,

        archive_action,
        archive_action_ts
    )
    VALUES (
        v_archive_run_flag,
        v_strategy_archive_reset_mode,

        v_strategy_set_name,
        v_strategy_name,
        v_strategy_version,
        v_module1_scenario_set_name,
        v_module1_scenario_name,
        v_population_id,

        v_latest_count,
        v_latest_distinct_app_count,

        v_archive_before_count,
        v_deleted_rows,
        v_inserted_rows,
        v_archive_after_count,

        v_archive_action,
        CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
    );
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 12.5 — ARCHIVE INVENTORY SNAPSHOT AFTER PERSISTENCE
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Capture post-persistence archive inventory so Section 12 can validate archive-control behavior.

    Section 12.5 answers:

        "What archive slices exist after the current archive-control logic ran?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Drop and recreate tmp_m2_archive_inventory_after.
    2. Summarize archive rows by archive replacement slice after Section 12.4.
    3. Provide comparable inventory grain to tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 12.5 does not modify archive rows.

****************************************************************************************************/

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tmp_m2_archive_inventory_after;

CREATE TEMP TABLE tmp_m2_archive_inventory_after
ON COMMIT PRESERVE ROWS
AS
SELECT
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
GROUP BY
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 12.5A — ARCHIVE VALIDATION INDEX SUPPORT BEFORE FAIL-FAST CHECKS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Support efficient archive persistence validation before Section 12.6 row-level gatekeepers.

    Section 12.5A answers:

        "Are the latest-run and archive tables indexed well enough for archive fidelity checks?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Create latest-run validation-grain index.
    2. Create archive validation-grain index.
    3. Create unique archive row-level grain index.
    4. Analyze latest-run and archive tables for query planning.

UNIQUE ARCHIVE GRAIN ENFORCEMENT:
    The archive should not contain duplicate rows for the same application under the same Module 1
    scenario and Module 2 strategy version.

    If duplicates already exist, unique index creation will fail clearly.

    That is preferable to allowing ambiguous matched comparison later.

BOUNDARY:
    This section does not modify decisions, exposure values, Expected Loss values, reason codes, or
    archive data values.

****************************************************************************************************/

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_validation_grain
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions (
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    application_id
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_decisions_archive_validation_grain
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    application_id
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS uq_m2_strategy_decisions_archive_row_grain
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    application_id
);

ANALYZE credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;
ANALYZE credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 12.6 — LOCAL FAIL-FAST CHECKS FOR ARCHIVE PERSISTENCE
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that Section 12 archive persistence behaved exactly as governed before archive comparison,
    validation, frontier, or evidence capture proceeds.

    Section 12.6 answers:

        "Did Section 12 preserve archive grain, apply the intended archive-control mode, and faithfully
         persist the current latest-run output?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Confirm archive table and archive_inserted_ts exist.
    2. Confirm tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit contains exactly one audit row.
    3. Confirm latest-run source integrity remains valid.
    4. Confirm archive_run_flag = FALSE changed no archive rows.
    5. Confirm archive_run_flag = TRUE inserted exactly latest-run row count.
    6. Confirm current archived slice row count equals latest-run row count.
    7. Confirm current archived slice is unique at application_id.
    8. Confirm archive_inserted_ts is populated for inserted current-slice rows.
    9. Confirm archive row-level grain is unique across the full archive.
    10. Confirm reset modes did not change unintended archive slices.
    11. Confirm archived current-slice values match latest-run values across every latest-run column.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 12.6 does not modify archive rows.
    Section 12.6 does not modify latest-run rows.
    Section 12.6 does not recalculate strategy outputs.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    a RECORD;

    v_audit_count BIGINT;

    v_archive_table_exists BOOLEAN;
    v_archive_inserted_ts_exists BOOLEAN;

    v_latest_count BIGINT;
    v_latest_distinct_app_count BIGINT;

    v_current_archive_count BIGINT;
    v_current_archive_distinct_app_count BIGINT;
    v_current_archive_null_ts_count BIGINT;
    v_current_archive_duplicate_app_count BIGINT;

    v_archive_duplicate_grain_count BIGINT;

    v_inventory_diff_count BIGINT;
    v_after_inventory_group_count BIGINT;

    v_before_current_key_rows BIGINT;
    v_before_current_set_rows BIGINT;

    v_persistence_compare_predicate TEXT;
    v_persistence_mismatch_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: one archive persistence audit row.

    Section 12.3 recreated the audit table.
    Section 12.4 should have inserted exactly one current-run audit row.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_audit_count
    FROM tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit;

    IF v_audit_count <> 1 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: expected exactly one archive persistence audit row, found %.',
            v_audit_count;
    END IF;

    SELECT *
    INTO a
    FROM tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit
    LIMIT 1;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: archive table and archive_inserted_ts must exist.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT TO_REGCLASS('credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive') IS NOT NULL
    INTO v_archive_table_exists;

    IF v_archive_table_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: strategy_decisions_archive does not exist after archive setup.';
    END IF;

    SELECT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM information_schema.columns
        WHERE table_schema = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
          AND table_name = 'strategy_decisions_archive'
          AND column_name = 'archive_inserted_ts'
    )
    INTO v_archive_inserted_ts_exists;

    IF v_archive_inserted_ts_exists IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: archive_inserted_ts column does not exist after archive setup.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: latest-run source integrity remains valid.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT
        COUNT(*),
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id)
    INTO
        v_latest_count,
        v_latest_distinct_app_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions;

    IF v_latest_count <= 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: latest-run table contains zero rows during archive gatekeeper.';
    END IF;

    IF v_latest_distinct_app_count <> v_latest_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: latest-run application_id uniqueness failed during archive gatekeeper.';
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: audit math must reconcile.

    Expected:
        after = before - deleted + inserted.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    IF a.archive_row_count_after
       <> a.archive_row_count_before - a.archive_deleted_rows + a.archive_inserted_rows THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: archive audit row-count math does not reconcile. Before %, deleted %, inserted %, after %.',
            a.archive_row_count_before,
            a.archive_deleted_rows,
            a.archive_inserted_rows,
            a.archive_row_count_after;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: full archive row-level grain must be unique.

    This protects Section 13 matched comparison from duplicate archived application rows.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_archive_duplicate_grain_count
    FROM (
        SELECT
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id,
            application_id,
            COUNT(*) AS row_count
        FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
        GROUP BY
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id,
            application_id
        HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
    ) d;

    IF v_archive_duplicate_grain_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: archive contains % duplicate row-level grain group(s).',
            v_archive_duplicate_grain_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: archive_run_flag = FALSE skip behavior.

    Skip mode should not delete rows.
    Skip mode should not insert rows.
    Skip mode should not change archive inventory.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    IF a.archive_run_flag IS FALSE THEN
        IF a.archive_deleted_rows <> 0
           OR a.archive_inserted_rows <> 0
           OR a.archive_row_count_after <> a.archive_row_count_before THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION
                'Module 2 Section 12 failure: archive_run_flag = FALSE but archive row counts changed.';
        END IF;

        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_inventory_diff_count
        FROM (
            SELECT
                COALESCE(b.strategy_set_name, aft.strategy_set_name) AS strategy_set_name,
                COALESCE(b.strategy_name, aft.strategy_name) AS strategy_name,
                COALESCE(b.strategy_version, aft.strategy_version) AS strategy_version,
                COALESCE(b.module1_scenario_set_name, aft.module1_scenario_set_name) AS module1_scenario_set_name,
                COALESCE(b.module1_scenario_name, aft.module1_scenario_name) AS module1_scenario_name,
                COALESCE(b.population_id, aft.population_id) AS population_id,
                COALESCE(b.row_count, 0) AS before_row_count,
                COALESCE(aft.row_count, 0) AS after_row_count
            FROM tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before b
            FULL OUTER JOIN tmp_m2_archive_inventory_after aft
                ON aft.strategy_set_name = b.strategy_set_name
               AND aft.strategy_name = b.strategy_name
               AND aft.strategy_version = b.strategy_version
               AND aft.module1_scenario_set_name = b.module1_scenario_set_name
               AND aft.module1_scenario_name = b.module1_scenario_name
               AND aft.population_id = b.population_id
        ) x
        WHERE before_row_count <> after_row_count;

        IF v_inventory_diff_count > 0 THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION
                'Module 2 Section 12 failure: archive_run_flag = FALSE but before / after archive inventory changed for % slice(s).',
                v_inventory_diff_count;
        END IF;

        RETURN;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: archive_run_flag = TRUE insert count.

    Expected:
        inserted rows = latest-run rows.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    IF a.archive_inserted_rows <> v_latest_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: archive inserted rows (%) do not equal latest-run rows (%).',
            a.archive_inserted_rows,
            v_latest_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: current archived slice row count, application uniqueness, and archive_inserted_ts.

    Current slice is scoped by the archive replacement key.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT
        COUNT(*),
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id),
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE archive_inserted_ts IS NULL)
    INTO
        v_current_archive_count,
        v_current_archive_distinct_app_count,
        v_current_archive_null_ts_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    WHERE strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
      AND strategy_name = a.strategy_name
      AND strategy_version = a.strategy_version
      AND module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
      AND population_id = a.population_id;

    IF v_current_archive_count <> v_latest_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: current archived slice row count (%) does not equal latest-run row count (%).',
            v_current_archive_count,
            v_latest_count;
    END IF;

    IF v_current_archive_distinct_app_count <> v_current_archive_count THEN
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_current_archive_duplicate_app_count
        FROM (
            SELECT application_id
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
            WHERE strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
              AND strategy_name = a.strategy_name
              AND strategy_version = a.strategy_version
              AND module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
              AND module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
              AND population_id = a.population_id
            GROUP BY application_id
            HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
        ) d;

        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: current archived slice has duplicate application_id values. Duplicate groups: %.',
            v_current_archive_duplicate_app_count;
    END IF;

    IF v_current_archive_null_ts_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: % current archived slice row(s) have null archive_inserted_ts.',
            v_current_archive_null_ts_count;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: reset-mode scope validation.

    STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY:
        Only the current replacement key should change.

    STRATEGY_SET_ONLY:
        Only the current strategy_set_name within the selected Module 1 scenario / population should
        change.

    ALL:
        After persistence, the archive should contain exactly one slice: the current latest-run slice.

    NONE:
        Prior current-key rows should not have existed before insert.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    IF a.strategy_archive_reset_mode = 'NONE' THEN
        SELECT COALESCE(SUM(row_count), 0)
        INTO v_before_current_key_rows
        FROM tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before
        WHERE strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
          AND strategy_name = a.strategy_name
          AND strategy_version = a.strategy_version
          AND module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
          AND module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
          AND population_id = a.population_id;

        IF v_before_current_key_rows > 0 THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION
                'Module 2 Section 12 failure: NONE mode inserted despite prior current-key archive rows existing.';
        END IF;

        IF a.archive_deleted_rows <> 0 THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION
                'Module 2 Section 12 failure: NONE mode deleted % row(s). Expected zero.',
                a.archive_deleted_rows;
        END IF;


    ELSIF a.strategy_archive_reset_mode = 'STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY' THEN
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_inventory_diff_count
        FROM (
            SELECT
                COALESCE(b.strategy_set_name, aft.strategy_set_name) AS strategy_set_name,
                COALESCE(b.strategy_name, aft.strategy_name) AS strategy_name,
                COALESCE(b.strategy_version, aft.strategy_version) AS strategy_version,
                COALESCE(b.module1_scenario_set_name, aft.module1_scenario_set_name) AS module1_scenario_set_name,
                COALESCE(b.module1_scenario_name, aft.module1_scenario_name) AS module1_scenario_name,
                COALESCE(b.population_id, aft.population_id) AS population_id,
                COALESCE(b.row_count, 0) AS before_row_count,
                COALESCE(aft.row_count, 0) AS after_row_count
            FROM tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before b
            FULL OUTER JOIN tmp_m2_archive_inventory_after aft
                ON aft.strategy_set_name = b.strategy_set_name
               AND aft.strategy_name = b.strategy_name
               AND aft.strategy_version = b.strategy_version
               AND aft.module1_scenario_set_name = b.module1_scenario_set_name
               AND aft.module1_scenario_name = b.module1_scenario_name
               AND aft.population_id = b.population_id
        ) x
        WHERE NOT (
                strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
            AND strategy_name = a.strategy_name
            AND strategy_version = a.strategy_version
            AND module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
            AND module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
            AND population_id = a.population_id
        )
          AND before_row_count <> after_row_count;

        IF v_inventory_diff_count > 0 THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION
                'Module 2 Section 12 failure: STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY changed % unrelated archive slice(s).',
                v_inventory_diff_count;
        END IF;


    ELSIF a.strategy_archive_reset_mode = 'STRATEGY_SET_ONLY' THEN
        SELECT COALESCE(SUM(row_count), 0)
        INTO v_before_current_set_rows
        FROM tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before
        WHERE strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
          AND module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
          AND module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
          AND population_id = a.population_id;

        IF a.archive_deleted_rows <> v_before_current_set_rows THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION
                'Module 2 Section 12 failure: STRATEGY_SET_ONLY deleted % row(s), but before-inventory current strategy-set rows were %.',
                a.archive_deleted_rows,
                v_before_current_set_rows;
        END IF;

        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_inventory_diff_count
        FROM (
            SELECT
                COALESCE(b.strategy_set_name, aft.strategy_set_name) AS strategy_set_name,
                COALESCE(b.strategy_name, aft.strategy_name) AS strategy_name,
                COALESCE(b.strategy_version, aft.strategy_version) AS strategy_version,
                COALESCE(b.module1_scenario_set_name, aft.module1_scenario_set_name) AS module1_scenario_set_name,
                COALESCE(b.module1_scenario_name, aft.module1_scenario_name) AS module1_scenario_name,
                COALESCE(b.population_id, aft.population_id) AS population_id,
                COALESCE(b.row_count, 0) AS before_row_count,
                COALESCE(aft.row_count, 0) AS after_row_count
            FROM tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before b
            FULL OUTER JOIN tmp_m2_archive_inventory_after aft
                ON aft.strategy_set_name = b.strategy_set_name
               AND aft.strategy_name = b.strategy_name
               AND aft.strategy_version = b.strategy_version
               AND aft.module1_scenario_set_name = b.module1_scenario_set_name
               AND aft.module1_scenario_name = b.module1_scenario_name
               AND aft.population_id = b.population_id
        ) x
        WHERE NOT (
                strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
            AND module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
            AND module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
            AND population_id = a.population_id
        )
          AND before_row_count <> after_row_count;

        IF v_inventory_diff_count > 0 THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION
                'Module 2 Section 12 failure: STRATEGY_SET_ONLY changed % unrelated archive slice(s).',
                v_inventory_diff_count;
        END IF;


    ELSIF a.strategy_archive_reset_mode = 'ALL' THEN
        SELECT COUNT(*)
        INTO v_after_inventory_group_count
        FROM tmp_m2_archive_inventory_after;

        IF v_after_inventory_group_count <> 1 THEN
            RAISE EXCEPTION
                'Module 2 Section 12 failure: ALL mode should leave one archive slice after insert, found %.',
                v_after_inventory_group_count;
        END IF;
    END IF;


    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Gatekeeper: row-level persistence fidelity.

    Business purpose:
        The current archived slice should match the latest-run table across every latest-run column.

    SQL mechanics:
        Build a dynamic OR predicate:
            ar.<column> IS DISTINCT FROM sd.<column>

        Then FULL OUTER JOIN latest-run rows to current archived-slice rows by application_id.

    Why application_id is enough inside this dynamic query:
        latest-run output is already validated as one replacement key.
        current_archive is filtered to the same replacement key.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT STRING_AGG(
        FORMAT('ar.%1$I IS DISTINCT FROM sd.%1$I', column_name),
        ' OR ' ORDER BY ordinal_position
    )
    INTO v_persistence_compare_predicate
    FROM information_schema.columns
    WHERE table_schema = 'credit_decisioning_sim'
      AND table_name = 'strategy_decisions';

    IF v_persistence_compare_predicate IS NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: unable to build persistence comparison predicate.';
    END IF;

    EXECUTE FORMAT(
        $SQL$
        WITH latest_run AS (
            SELECT *
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
        ),

        current_archive AS (
            SELECT *
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
            WHERE strategy_set_name = %L
              AND strategy_name = %L
              AND strategy_version = %L
              AND module1_scenario_set_name = %L
              AND module1_scenario_name = %L
              AND population_id = %L
        )

        SELECT COUNT(*)
        FROM latest_run sd

        FULL OUTER JOIN current_archive ar
            ON ar.application_id = sd.application_id

        WHERE sd.application_id IS NULL
           OR ar.application_id IS NULL
           OR %s
        $SQL$,
        a.strategy_set_name,
        a.strategy_name,
        a.strategy_version,
        a.module1_scenario_set_name,
        a.module1_scenario_name,
        a.population_id,
        v_persistence_compare_predicate
    )
    INTO v_persistence_mismatch_count;

    IF v_persistence_mismatch_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 12 failure: % row(s) have latest-run versus archived current-slice persistence mismatches.',
            v_persistence_mismatch_count;
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 12.7 — PRACTICAL ARCHIVE REVIEW INDEXES
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Add practical archive indexes for downstream review, comparison, validation, frontier analysis,
    and evidence capture.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Create rerunnable indexes on common archive review dimensions.

BOUNDARY:
    Indexes do not modify archive row values.
    Indexes do not recalculate strategy outcomes.
    Indexes do not change validation results.

****************************************************************************************************/

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_archive_replacement_key
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_archive_strategy_identity
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_archive_module1_lineage
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_archive_decision_outcome
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (decision_outcome);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_archive_product_decision
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (
    product_type_policy_key,
    decision_outcome
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_archive_score_decision
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (
    score_band_policy_key,
    decision_outcome
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_archive_primary_reason
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (primary_reason_code);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_archive_offer_exposure
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (simulated_offer_exposure_flag);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_m2_strategy_archive_inserted_ts
ON credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive (archive_inserted_ts);



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 12.8 — LOCAL ARCHIVE PERSISTENCE SANITY CHECKS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide lightweight archive diagnostics after persistence.

    Section 12.8 answers:

        "What archive action was taken, what does the archive now contain, and does the current slice
         look ready for Section 13 matched comparison and downstream QA?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    Display review outputs for:
        archive inventory,
        current latest-run identity,
        archive audit row,
        before / after inventory movement,
        current archived slice row count,
        current archived slice decision distribution,
        current archived slice product distribution,
        current archived slice reason-code distribution,
        current archived slice exposure / Expected Loss summary,
        archive mode diagnostic,
        and one compact readiness row.

INTERPRETATION:
    These diagnostics are local archive persistence checks only.

    They are not:
        matched strategy comparison,
        full Section 14 QA,
        strategy frontier review,
        or executive evidence capture.

****************************************************************************************************/



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.1 Archive inventory by strategy / Module 1 scenario / population.

Purpose:
    Show all archived strategy slices currently available.

Interpretation:
    This is the first archive view to inspect before Section 13 comparison.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,

    COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
    COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,

    MIN(archive_inserted_ts) AS first_archive_inserted_ts,
    MAX(archive_inserted_ts) AS last_archive_inserted_ts

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive

GROUP BY
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id

ORDER BY
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.2 Latest-run identity prepared for archive.

Purpose:
    Display the current latest-run replacement key and archive controls.

Expected:
    exactly one row.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    module2_model_version,

    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    strategy_run_id,
    strategy_run_ts,

    archive_run_flag,
    strategy_archive_reset_mode,

    module1_input_source,
    module1_source_table_name,

    module1_model_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    anchor_date,

    COUNT(*) AS latest_run_rows,
    COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,

    MIN(latest_output_created_ts) AS min_latest_output_created_ts,
    MAX(latest_output_created_ts) AS max_latest_output_created_ts

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

GROUP BY
    module2_model_version,

    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    strategy_run_id,
    strategy_run_ts,

    archive_run_flag,
    strategy_archive_reset_mode,

    module1_input_source,
    module1_source_table_name,

    module1_model_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    anchor_date

ORDER BY
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.3 Archive persistence audit row.

Purpose:
    Show the action Section 12.4 took.

Interpretation:
    This is the clearest diagnostic for whether Section 12 skipped, appended, replaced, reset, or
    inserted.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    archive_run_flag,
    strategy_archive_reset_mode,

    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,

    latest_run_row_count,
    latest_run_distinct_application_count,

    archive_row_count_before,
    archive_deleted_rows,
    archive_inserted_rows,
    archive_row_count_after,

    archive_action,
    archive_action_ts

FROM tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.4 Archive before / after inventory movement.

Purpose:
    Show archive slice-level inventory changes caused by Section 12.

Interpretation:
    For ordinary STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY reruns, only the current replacement key should change.

    For STRATEGY_SET_ONLY, only slices in the current strategy_set_name under the selected Module 1
    scenario / population should change.

    For ALL, prior archive slices should disappear except the newly inserted current slice.

    For archive_run_flag = FALSE, this output should show no row-count changes.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    COALESCE(b.strategy_set_name, a.strategy_set_name) AS strategy_set_name,
    COALESCE(b.strategy_name, a.strategy_name) AS strategy_name,
    COALESCE(b.strategy_version, a.strategy_version) AS strategy_version,
    COALESCE(b.module1_scenario_set_name, a.module1_scenario_set_name) AS module1_scenario_set_name,
    COALESCE(b.module1_scenario_name, a.module1_scenario_name) AS module1_scenario_name,
    COALESCE(b.population_id, a.population_id) AS population_id,

    COALESCE(b.row_count, 0) AS before_row_count,
    COALESCE(a.row_count, 0) AS after_row_count,

    COALESCE(a.row_count, 0) - COALESCE(b.row_count, 0) AS row_count_delta

FROM tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before b

FULL OUTER JOIN tmp_m2_archive_inventory_after a
    ON a.strategy_set_name = b.strategy_set_name
   AND a.strategy_name = b.strategy_name
   AND a.strategy_version = b.strategy_version
   AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = b.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND a.module1_scenario_name = b.module1_scenario_name
   AND a.population_id = b.population_id

ORDER BY
    ABS(COALESCE(a.row_count, 0) - COALESCE(b.row_count, 0)) DESC,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.5 Archive row-level grain duplicate diagnostic.

Purpose:
    Confirm full archive uniqueness at archive row-level grain.

Expected:
    duplicate_archive_grain_count = 0.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS duplicate_archive_grain_count
FROM (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,
        application_id,
        COUNT(*) AS row_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,
        application_id
    HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
) d;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.6 Current archived slice row-count diagnostic.

Purpose:
    Confirm the archived current slice exists when archive_run_flag = TRUE.

Boundary:
    If archive_run_flag = FALSE, this query may show zero rows for the current slice if it was never
    previously archived.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH archive_context AS (
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit
    LIMIT 1
)

SELECT
    a.archive_run_flag,
    a.strategy_archive_reset_mode,
    a.strategy_set_name,
    a.strategy_name,
    a.strategy_version,
    a.module1_scenario_set_name,
    a.module1_scenario_name,
    a.population_id,

    COUNT(ar.*) AS current_archived_slice_rows,
    COUNT(DISTINCT ar.application_id) AS current_archived_slice_distinct_application_id_count,

    MIN(ar.archive_inserted_ts) AS min_archive_inserted_ts,
    MAX(ar.archive_inserted_ts) AS max_archive_inserted_ts

FROM archive_context a

LEFT JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ar
    ON ar.strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
   AND ar.strategy_name = a.strategy_name
   AND ar.strategy_version = a.strategy_version
   AND ar.module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND ar.module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
   AND ar.population_id = a.population_id

GROUP BY
    a.archive_run_flag,
    a.strategy_archive_reset_mode,
    a.strategy_set_name,
    a.strategy_name,
    a.strategy_version,
    a.module1_scenario_set_name,
    a.module1_scenario_name,
    a.population_id;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.7 Current archived slice decision distribution.

Purpose:
    Review final simulated outcome distribution in the archived current slice.

Boundary:
    decision_outcome remains a simulated strategy outcome, not real applicant treatment.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH archive_context AS (
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit
    LIMIT 1
)

SELECT
    ar.decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_current_archived_slice,

    AVG(ar.requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(ar.approved_amount) AS avg_approved_amount,
    AVG(ar.requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(ar.approved_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount

FROM archive_context a

JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ar
    ON ar.strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
   AND ar.strategy_name = a.strategy_name
   AND ar.strategy_version = a.strategy_version
   AND ar.module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND ar.module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
   AND ar.population_id = a.population_id

GROUP BY ar.decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    CASE ar.decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.8 Current archived slice product × decision distribution.

Purpose:
    Confirm product-level outcome behavior is available in the archive for downstream Section 13,
    Section 14, Section 15, and Section 16 analysis.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH archive_context AS (
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit
    LIMIT 1
)

SELECT
    ar.product_type_policy_key,
    ar.decision_outcome,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    AVG(ar.requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,
    AVG(ar.approved_amount) AS avg_approved_amount,
    AVG(ar.requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(ar.approved_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio,
    AVG(ar.requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    AVG(ar.approved_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_approved_expected_loss_amount

FROM archive_context a

JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ar
    ON ar.strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
   AND ar.strategy_name = a.strategy_name
   AND ar.strategy_version = a.strategy_version
   AND ar.module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND ar.module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
   AND ar.population_id = a.population_id

GROUP BY
    ar.product_type_policy_key,
    ar.decision_outcome

ORDER BY
    ar.product_type_policy_key,
    CASE ar.decision_outcome
        WHEN 'APPROVE' THEN 1
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 3
        WHEN 'DECLINE' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.9 Current archived slice primary reason-code distribution.

Purpose:
    Confirm simulated explanation-code evidence is available in the archive.

Boundary:
    Reason codes remain simulated strategy explanation codes, not customer communications.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH archive_context AS (
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit
    LIMIT 1
)

SELECT
    ar.primary_reason_family,
    ar.primary_reason_code,

    COUNT(*) AS row_count,

    ROUND(
        100.0 * COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0),
        2
    ) AS pct_of_current_archived_slice

FROM archive_context a

JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ar
    ON ar.strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
   AND ar.strategy_name = a.strategy_name
   AND ar.strategy_version = a.strategy_version
   AND ar.module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND ar.module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
   AND ar.population_id = a.population_id

GROUP BY
    ar.primary_reason_family,
    ar.primary_reason_code

ORDER BY
    CASE ar.primary_reason_family
        WHEN 'POLICY_STOP' THEN 1
        WHEN 'MANUAL_REVIEW' THEN 2
        WHEN 'COUNTEROFFER' THEN 3
        WHEN 'APPROVAL' THEN 4
        ELSE 99
    END,
    ar.primary_reason_code;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.10 Current archived slice requested versus approved exposure / Expected Loss summary.

Purpose:
    Review portfolio-impact metrics in the archived current slice.

Interpretation:
    requested_expected_loss_amount is requested-exposure Expected Loss.
    approved_expected_loss_amount is approved-exposure Expected Loss.
    archive_inserted_ts is archive persistence metadata.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH archive_context AS (
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit
    LIMIT 1
)

SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS current_archived_slice_rows,

    SUM(ar.requested_amount) AS total_requested_amount,
    SUM(COALESCE(ar.approved_amount, 0)) AS total_approved_amount,

    SUM(COALESCE(ar.approved_amount, 0))
        / NULLIF(SUM(ar.requested_amount), 0) AS approved_amount_capture_rate,

    SUM(ar.requested_expected_loss_amount) AS total_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    SUM(COALESCE(ar.approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
        AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount,

    SUM(COALESCE(ar.approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
        / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(ar.approved_amount, 0)), 0) AS approved_expected_loss_rate,

    AVG(ar.requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,

    AVG(ar.approved_payment_to_income_ratio)
        FILTER (WHERE ar.simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
        AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_offer_rows,

    MIN(ar.latest_output_created_ts) AS min_latest_output_created_ts,
    MAX(ar.latest_output_created_ts) AS max_latest_output_created_ts,
    MIN(ar.archive_inserted_ts) AS min_archive_inserted_ts,
    MAX(ar.archive_inserted_ts) AS max_archive_inserted_ts

FROM archive_context a

JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ar
    ON ar.strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
   AND ar.strategy_name = a.strategy_name
   AND ar.strategy_version = a.strategy_version
   AND ar.module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND ar.module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
   AND ar.population_id = a.population_id;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.11 Archive mode diagnostic.

Purpose:
    Show the archive action and row-count effect in one compact row.

Interpretation:
    This is the quickest Section 12 audit view.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    archive_run_flag,
    strategy_archive_reset_mode,

    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,

    latest_run_row_count,
    latest_run_distinct_application_count,

    archive_row_count_before,
    archive_deleted_rows,
    archive_inserted_rows,
    archive_row_count_after,

    archive_action,
    archive_action_ts

FROM tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
12.8.12 Section 12 readiness summary.

Purpose:
    Provide one compact readiness row for archive persistence.

Expected:
    If archive_run_flag = TRUE:
        SECTION_12_ARCHIVE_PERSISTENCE_READY_FOR_COMPARISON_AND_QA

    If archive_run_flag = FALSE:
        SECTION_12_ARCHIVE_PERSISTENCE_SKIPPED_BY_CONTROL

Interpretation:
    This confirms only Section 12 archive persistence status.

    It does not validate Section 13 comparison readiness.
    It does not validate Section 14 QA.
    It does not validate Section 15 frontier completeness.
    It does not validate Section 16 evidence capture.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

WITH audit_row AS (
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_archive_persistence_audit
    LIMIT 1
),

current_archive AS (
    SELECT
        a.archive_run_flag,
        a.strategy_archive_reset_mode,
        a.strategy_set_name,
        a.strategy_name,
        a.strategy_version,
        a.module1_scenario_set_name,
        a.module1_scenario_name,
        a.population_id,

        COUNT(ar.*) AS current_archived_slice_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT ar.application_id) AS current_archived_slice_distinct_application_id_count,
        COUNT(ar.*) FILTER (WHERE ar.archive_inserted_ts IS NULL) AS current_archived_slice_null_archive_ts_rows
    FROM audit_row a

    LEFT JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ar
        ON ar.strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
       AND ar.strategy_name = a.strategy_name
       AND ar.strategy_version = a.strategy_version
       AND ar.module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ar.module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
       AND ar.population_id = a.population_id

    GROUP BY
        a.archive_run_flag,
        a.strategy_archive_reset_mode,
        a.strategy_set_name,
        a.strategy_name,
        a.strategy_version,
        a.module1_scenario_set_name,
        a.module1_scenario_name,
        a.population_id
),

archive_duplicates AS (
    SELECT COUNT(*) AS duplicate_archive_grain_count
    FROM (
        SELECT
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id,
            application_id,
            COUNT(*) AS row_count
        FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
        GROUP BY
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id,
            application_id
        HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
    ) d
),

inventory_diff AS (
    SELECT COUNT(*) AS before_after_inventory_diff_count
    FROM (
        SELECT
            COALESCE(b.strategy_set_name, a.strategy_set_name) AS strategy_set_name,
            COALESCE(b.strategy_name, a.strategy_name) AS strategy_name,
            COALESCE(b.strategy_version, a.strategy_version) AS strategy_version,
            COALESCE(b.module1_scenario_set_name, a.module1_scenario_set_name) AS module1_scenario_set_name,
            COALESCE(b.module1_scenario_name, a.module1_scenario_name) AS module1_scenario_name,
            COALESCE(b.population_id, a.population_id) AS population_id,
            COALESCE(b.row_count, 0) AS before_row_count,
            COALESCE(a.row_count, 0) AS after_row_count
        FROM tmp_m2_archive_inventory_before b
        FULL OUTER JOIN tmp_m2_archive_inventory_after a
            ON a.strategy_set_name = b.strategy_set_name
           AND a.strategy_name = b.strategy_name
           AND a.strategy_version = b.strategy_version
           AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = b.module1_scenario_set_name
           AND a.module1_scenario_name = b.module1_scenario_name
           AND a.population_id = b.population_id
    ) x
    WHERE before_row_count <> after_row_count
)

SELECT
    a.archive_run_flag,
    a.strategy_archive_reset_mode,

    a.strategy_set_name,
    a.strategy_name,
    a.strategy_version,
    a.module1_scenario_set_name,
    a.module1_scenario_name,
    a.population_id,

    a.latest_run_row_count,
    a.latest_run_distinct_application_count,

    a.archive_row_count_before,
    a.archive_deleted_rows,
    a.archive_inserted_rows,
    a.archive_row_count_after,
    a.archive_action,

    ca.current_archived_slice_rows,
    ca.current_archived_slice_distinct_application_id_count,
    ca.current_archived_slice_null_archive_ts_rows,

    ad.duplicate_archive_grain_count,
    id.before_after_inventory_diff_count,

    CASE
        WHEN a.archive_run_flag IS FALSE
         AND a.archive_deleted_rows = 0
         AND a.archive_inserted_rows = 0
         AND a.archive_row_count_after = a.archive_row_count_before
         AND id.before_after_inventory_diff_count = 0
            THEN 'SECTION_12_ARCHIVE_PERSISTENCE_SKIPPED_BY_CONTROL'

        WHEN a.archive_run_flag IS TRUE
         AND a.archive_inserted_rows = a.latest_run_row_count
         AND ca.current_archived_slice_rows = a.latest_run_row_count
         AND ca.current_archived_slice_distinct_application_id_count = a.latest_run_row_count
         AND ca.current_archived_slice_null_archive_ts_rows = 0
         AND ad.duplicate_archive_grain_count = 0
            THEN 'SECTION_12_ARCHIVE_PERSISTENCE_READY_FOR_COMPARISON_AND_QA'

        ELSE 'REVIEW_SECTION_12_ARCHIVE_PERSISTENCE_BEFORE_COMPARISON_OR_QA'
    END AS section_12_archive_persistence_status

FROM audit_row a
CROSS JOIN current_archive ca
CROSS JOIN archive_duplicates ad
CROSS JOIN inventory_diff id;



/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 12 — STRATEGY DECISION ARCHIVE PERSISTENCE LAYER

If execution reaches this point:
    1. credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions existed and was populated.
    2. latest-run application_id uniqueness was validated.
    3. latest-run archive controls were populated and unambiguous.
    4. latest-run archive replacement key was populated and unambiguous.
    5. credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive exists.
    6. archive_inserted_ts exists.
    7. Archive table contains all latest-run columns plus archive_inserted_ts.
    8. Missing latest-run columns were added to the archive table where safe.
    9. Common latest-run / archive columns have aligned PostgreSQL data types.
    10. Unexpected archive columns do not exist, except archive_inserted_ts.
    11. Archive inventory before persistence was captured.
    12. Archive control logic was applied.
    13. Archive inventory after persistence was captured.
    14. Archive validation indexes were created.
    15. Archive row-level grain was protected by a unique index.
    16. archive_run_flag = FALSE skipped persistence without deleting or inserting archive rows.
    17. archive_run_flag = TRUE persisted latest-run rows according to strategy_archive_reset_mode.
    18. STRATEGY_SCENARIO_ONLY replaced only the current replacement key.
    19. STRATEGY_SET_ONLY replaced the selected strategy set for the selected Module 1 scenario and
        population.
    20. ALL reset the full archive before inserting the current latest-run output.
    21. NONE inserted only when the current replacement key did not already exist.
    22. Current archived slice row count was validated when archive_run_flag = TRUE.
    23. Current archived slice application_id uniqueness was validated when archive_run_flag = TRUE.
    24. Current archived slice archive_inserted_ts was validated when archive_run_flag = TRUE.
    25. Latest-run values were compared to archived current-slice values when archive_run_flag = TRUE.
    26. Archive diagnostics are available for inventory and current-slice review.

