)
WITH current_key AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: current_key

    Purpose:
        Select the single current run key created in Section 16.0.

    SQL mechanics:
        LIMIT 1 is safe because Section 16.0 gatekeeper already validated that
        tmp_m2_current_run_key contains exactly one row.

    Interpretation:
        This CTE identifies the run being captured.

        It does not calculate metrics.

    Evidence grain:
        strategy_set_name
        strategy_name
        strategy_version
        module1_scenario_set_name
        module1_scenario_name
        population_id
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_key
    LIMIT 1
),

story AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: story

    Purpose:
        Select the single active current-run registry / story metadata row.

    Why this matters:
        Technical identifiers are necessary but not sufficient for executive evidence.

        The story metadata supplies:
            registry match status,
            module1_run_id,
            module2_run_id,
            run_sequence_number,
            showcase_id,
            comparison_group_id,
            validation_evidence_group_id,
            README / LinkedIn labels,
            parameter-family labels,
            expected storyline,
            observed storyline override,
            and validation notes.

    SQL mechanics:
        WHERE active_story_flag IS TRUE ensures only the governed active story row is used.

        LIMIT 1 is safe because Section 16.0 validates that exactly one active story row exists.

    Boundary:
        Story labels do not change decision outcomes, strategy logic, approved exposure, approved
        Expected Loss, or reason codes.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_story_params
    WHERE active_story_flag IS TRUE
    LIMIT 1
),

archive_ts AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: archive_ts

    Purpose:
        Retrieve the most recent archive_inserted_ts for the current archived slice.

    SQL mechanics:
        The archive is applicant-grain, so the current run key is used to isolate the matching slice.

        MAX(archive_inserted_ts) gives one audit timestamp for the slice.

    Interpretation:
        archive_inserted_ts is traceability metadata.

        It is not:
            a strategy metric,
            a comparison grain,
            a business outcome,
            or a run-performance measure.

    Review trigger:
        If archive_inserted_ts is NULL for a formal archived run, review Section 12 archive
        persistence and Section 14 archive-readiness diagnostics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        MAX(ar.archive_inserted_ts) AS archive_inserted_ts

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ar

    JOIN current_key k
        ON ar.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
       AND ar.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
       AND ar.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
       AND ar.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ar.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
       AND ar.population_id = k.population_id
),

portfolio AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: portfolio

    Purpose:
        Calculate core run-level portfolio evidence directly from the latest-run output.

    Why this CTE is large:
        The executive evidence summary is intended to be a single durable row that avoids forcing the
        reviewer to manually collect metrics from many QA outputs.

    Metric groups:
        structural counts,
        decision counts,
        decision rates,
        requested / approved exposure,
        counteroffer exposure treatment,
        manual-review unresolved exposure,
        decline no-offer exposure,
        requested and approved PTI,
        APR proxy,
        term,
        product mix,
        synthetic estimated-risk proxy,
        LGD,
        requested Expected Loss,
        approved Expected Loss,
        approved Expected Loss rate,
        and approved amount per approved Expected Loss dollar.

    Boundary:
        Metrics are aggregations over existing latest-run outputs.

        No applicant-level fields are recalculated.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        /*******************************************************************************************
        Structural counts.

        applications:
            total applicant-level latest-run rows.

        distinct_application_id_count:
            distinct application_id count.

        duplicate_application_count:
            should be zero for accepted evidence.

        Credit risk interpretation:
            All portfolio rates and totals depend on this population denominator being clean.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        COUNT(*) AS applications,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,
        COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS duplicate_application_count,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final decision counts.

        offer_count uses simulated_offer_exposure_flag because positive simulated offer exposure is
        defined as APPROVE + COUNTEROFFER.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE') AS approval_count,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER') AS counteroffer_count,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW') AS manual_review_count,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE') AS decline_count,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE) AS offer_count,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final decision rates.

        Denominator:
            full latest-run population.

        SQL mechanics:
            COUNT(*) FILTER creates each numerator.
            COUNT(*) creates the denominator.
            NULLIF prevents divide-by-zero.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS approval_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS counteroffer_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS manual_review_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS decline_rate,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Simulated positive offer-exposure rate.

        TRUE for:
            APPROVE
            COUNTEROFFER

        FALSE for:
            MANUAL_REVIEW
            DECLINE

        Boundary:
            This is not booked or funded exposure.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS simulated_offer_exposure_rate,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Offer composition.

        Denominator:
            simulated offer-exposure rows only.

        Interpretation:
            approval_share_of_offers shows the clean approval share of positive simulated offers.
            counteroffer_share_of_offers shows reliance on reduced-exposure treatment among positive
            simulated offers.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE), 0)
            AS approval_share_of_offers,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE), 0)
            AS counteroffer_share_of_offers,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Requested and approved exposure metrics.

        COALESCE converts unresolved / no-offer approved exposure to zero only for all-application
        portfolio-impact metrics.

        requested_amount:
            original requested exposure from Module 1.

        approved_amount:
            final simulated approved exposure after Module 2 treatment.

        approved_amount_capture_rate:
            how much requested exposure survived into final simulated approved exposure.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        SUM(requested_amount) AS total_requested_amount,
        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS total_approved_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0))
            / NULLIF(SUM(requested_amount), 0) AS approved_amount_capture_rate,

        AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,

        AVG(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0))
            AS avg_approved_amount_all_apps,

        AVG(approved_amount) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
            AS avg_approved_amount_offer_rows,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Exposure-reduction metrics.

        These help explain counteroffer management and no-offer exposure removal.

        total_exposure_reduction_amount:
            aggregate reduction between requested and approved exposure where such reduction was
            calculated.

        counteroffer_* fields:
            isolate the reduced-exposure treatment population.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        SUM(COALESCE(exposure_reduction_amount, 0)) AS total_exposure_reduction_amount,

        SUM(requested_amount) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
            AS counteroffer_requested_amount,

        SUM(approved_amount) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
            AS counteroffer_approved_amount,

        SUM(exposure_reduction_amount) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
            AS counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount,

        AVG(exposure_reduction_pct) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')
            AS counteroffer_exposure_reduction_pct_avg,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Unresolved manual-review and decline exposure context.

        Manual-review requested values remain useful because manual-review rows are unresolved.

        Decline requested values show the no-offer population's requested exposure and requested
        Expected Loss profile.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        SUM(requested_amount) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW')
            AS manual_review_requested_amount,

        SUM(requested_expected_loss_amount) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW')
            AS manual_review_requested_expected_loss_amount,

        SUM(requested_amount) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE')
            AS decline_requested_amount,

        SUM(requested_expected_loss_amount) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE')
            AS decline_requested_expected_loss_amount,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Requested and approved affordability metrics.

        requested_payment_to_income_ratio:
            original requested-structure PTI from Module 1.

        approved_payment_to_income_ratio:
            final approved-exposure PTI proxy for simulated offer rows.

        Boundary:
            approved_payment_to_income_ratio is a strategy-simulation affordability proxy.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) AS avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,

        AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
            AS avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_offer_rows,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        APR proxy metrics for Module 3 readiness.

        base_apr_for_payment_calc is preserved as an APR proxy input.

        These metrics are preserved for future economics design but are not revenue, yield,
        profitability, or pricing outputs.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        AVG(base_apr_for_payment_calc) AS avg_apr_proxy_all_apps,

        AVG(base_apr_for_payment_calc) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
            AS avg_apr_proxy_offer_rows,

        SUM(requested_amount * base_apr_for_payment_calc)
            / NULLIF(SUM(requested_amount), 0)
            AS requested_amount_weighted_apr_proxy,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0) * base_apr_for_payment_calc)
            / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS approved_amount_weighted_apr_proxy,

        SUM(requested_amount * base_apr_for_payment_calc)
            AS requested_amount_x_apr_proxy_sum,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0) * base_apr_for_payment_calc)
            AS approved_amount_x_apr_proxy_sum,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Term metrics for Module 3 readiness.

        loan_term_months may be NULL or not meaningful for revolving exposure.

        approved_amount_weighted_term_months:
            uses approved amount as the weight and excludes NULL term rows from the denominator.

        term_missing_or_revolving_count:
            preserves evidence that some products may not have installment-style term behavior.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        AVG(loan_term_months) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
            AS avg_loan_term_months_offer_rows,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0) * loan_term_months)
            FILTER (WHERE loan_term_months IS NOT NULL)
            / NULLIF(
                SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) FILTER (WHERE loan_term_months IS NOT NULL),
                0
              )
            AS approved_amount_weighted_term_months,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE loan_term_months IS NULL
               OR product_type_policy_key IN ('REVOLVING_LINE')
        ) AS term_missing_or_revolving_count,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Product approved-exposure composition metrics.

        These fields support future economics interpretation and portfolio mix storytelling.

        Boundary:
            These are exposure-mix fields, not profitability fields.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) FILTER (
            WHERE product_type_policy_key IN ('MORTGAGE', 'HELOC', 'AUTO_LOAN')
        ) / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS secured_approved_amount_share,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) FILTER (
            WHERE product_type_policy_key IN ('REVOLVING_LINE', 'UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN')
        ) / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS unsecured_approved_amount_share,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) FILTER (
            WHERE product_type_policy_key IN ('REVOLVING_LINE', 'HELOC')
        ) / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS revolving_approved_amount_share,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) FILTER (
            WHERE product_type_policy_key IN ('MORTGAGE', 'AUTO_LOAN', 'UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN')
        ) / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS installment_approved_amount_share,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) FILTER (
            WHERE product_type_policy_key = 'MORTGAGE'
        ) / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS mortgage_approved_amount_share,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Synthetic risk and LGD metrics.

        estimated_pd remains the SQL field name and is interpreted as the synthetic estimated-PD
        proxy.

        estimated_lgd remains the synthetic loss-given-default severity approximation.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        AVG(estimated_pd) AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_all_apps,

        AVG(estimated_pd) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
            AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows,

        AVG(estimated_pd) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE')
            AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_declined_rows,

        AVG(estimated_lgd) AS avg_estimated_lgd_all_apps,

        AVG(estimated_lgd) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
            AS avg_estimated_lgd_offer_rows,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Expected Loss metrics.

        requested_expected_loss_amount:
            requested-exposure Expected Loss from Module 1.

        approved_expected_loss_amount:
            approved-exposure Expected Loss after Module 2 final exposure treatment.

        approved_expected_loss_rate:
            approved Expected Loss divided by approved amount.

        Boundary:
            approved_expected_loss_rate is a synthetic strategy evidence metric, not a production
            loss-rate forecast.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        SUM(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS total_requested_expected_loss_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount,

        AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,

        AVG(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            AS avg_approved_expected_loss_all_apps,

        AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
            AS avg_approved_expected_loss_offer_rows,

        SUM(requested_expected_loss_amount)
            / NULLIF(SUM(requested_amount), 0)
            AS requested_expected_loss_rate,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS approved_expected_loss_rate,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0))
            / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS approved_amount_per_approved_expected_loss_dollar

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
),

product_summary AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: product_summary

    Purpose:
        Summarize current-run outcome, exposure, and approved Expected Loss metrics by product.

    Downstream use:
        product_json uses this CTE to create product-mix JSONB evidence.
        product_drivers uses this CTE to populate executive product-driver fields.

    Credit risk interpretation:
        Product type shapes exposure size, payment mechanics, LGD, counteroffer feasibility, and
        approved Expected Loss.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        product_type_policy_key,

        COUNT(*) AS applications,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE) AS offer_count,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER') AS counteroffer_count,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE') AS decline_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS offer_rate,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS total_approved_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS approved_expected_loss_rate

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

    GROUP BY product_type_policy_key
),

product_totals AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: product_totals

    Purpose:
        Provide denominators for product-level approved amount share and approved Expected Loss share.

    SQL mechanics:
        This CTE collapses product_summary to a single row.

    Boundary:
        These totals are current-run totals only.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        SUM(total_approved_amount) AS total_approved_amount,
        SUM(total_approved_expected_loss_amount) AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount
    FROM product_summary
),

product_json AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: product_json

    Purpose:
        Store compact product-level mix evidence as JSONB.

    Why JSONB:
        JSONB lets the one-row executive evidence record retain product-level detail without adding
        a wide set of product-specific columns for every product.

    SQL mechanics:
        jsonb_object_agg creates a JSON object keyed by product_type_policy_key.

        jsonb_build_object stores selected product-level metrics under each product key.

    Boundary:
        This is structured evidence, not a reporting mart and not Module 3 economics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        /*******************************************************************************************
        Product approved amount mix.

        Interpretation:
            Shows how approved exposure is distributed across product types.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        jsonb_object_agg(
            ps.product_type_policy_key,
            jsonb_build_object(
                'applications', ps.applications,
                'offer_count', ps.offer_count,
                'offer_rate', ps.offer_rate,
                'total_approved_amount', ps.total_approved_amount,
                'approved_amount_share', ps.total_approved_amount / NULLIF(pt.total_approved_amount, 0)
            )
        ) AS product_approved_amount_mix_jsonb,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Product approved Expected Loss mix.

        Interpretation:
            Shows which products contribute the most approved-exposure Expected Loss.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        jsonb_object_agg(
            ps.product_type_policy_key,
            jsonb_build_object(
                'total_approved_expected_loss_amount', ps.total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
                'approved_expected_loss_share', ps.total_approved_expected_loss_amount / NULLIF(pt.total_approved_expected_loss_amount, 0),
                'approved_expected_loss_rate', ps.approved_expected_loss_rate
            )
        ) AS product_approved_expected_loss_mix_jsonb,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Product offer-rate summary.

        Interpretation:
            Shows product-level simulated positive offer-exposure behavior.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        jsonb_object_agg(
            ps.product_type_policy_key,
            jsonb_build_object(
                'applications', ps.applications,
                'offer_count', ps.offer_count,
                'offer_rate', ps.offer_rate
            )
        ) AS product_offer_rate_jsonb

    FROM product_summary ps
    CROSS JOIN product_totals pt
),

product_drivers AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: product_drivers

    Purpose:
        Identify compact product-level driver labels for the executive evidence row.

    Driver examples:
        product with largest approved amount;
        product with largest approved Expected Loss;
        product with most counteroffers;
        product with most declines;
        product with highest / lowest simulated offer-exposure rate.

    SQL mechanics:
        Each scalar subquery orders product_summary by a specific metric and returns the top product.

    Interpretation:
        These are driver labels for storytelling and validation review.

        They are not strategy recommendations.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        (SELECT product_type_policy_key
         FROM product_summary
         ORDER BY total_approved_amount DESC NULLS LAST, product_type_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS top_approved_amount_product,

        (SELECT total_approved_amount / NULLIF((SELECT total_approved_amount FROM product_totals), 0)
         FROM product_summary
         ORDER BY total_approved_amount DESC NULLS LAST, product_type_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS top_approved_amount_product_share,

        (SELECT product_type_policy_key
         FROM product_summary
         ORDER BY total_approved_expected_loss_amount DESC NULLS LAST, product_type_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS top_approved_expected_loss_product,

        (SELECT total_approved_expected_loss_amount
                / NULLIF((SELECT total_approved_expected_loss_amount FROM product_totals), 0)
         FROM product_summary
         ORDER BY total_approved_expected_loss_amount DESC NULLS LAST, product_type_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS top_approved_expected_loss_product_share,

        (SELECT product_type_policy_key
         FROM product_summary
         ORDER BY counteroffer_count DESC, product_type_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS top_counteroffer_product,

        (SELECT product_type_policy_key
         FROM product_summary
         ORDER BY decline_count DESC, product_type_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS top_decline_product,

        (SELECT product_type_policy_key
         FROM product_summary
         ORDER BY offer_rate DESC NULLS LAST, product_type_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS highest_offer_rate_product,

        (SELECT product_type_policy_key
         FROM product_summary
         ORDER BY offer_rate ASC NULLS LAST, product_type_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS lowest_offer_rate_product
),

score_summary AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: score_summary

    Purpose:
        Summarize current-run outcome, exposure, and approved Expected Loss metrics by score band.

    Credit risk interpretation:
        Score band is the borrower-quality segmentation layer.

        Reviewing score-band drivers helps identify whether access, approved exposure, and approved
        Expected Loss concentrate in stronger or weaker borrower-quality segments.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        score_band_policy_key,

        COUNT(*) AS applications,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE) AS offer_count,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER') AS counteroffer_count,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE') AS decline_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS offer_rate,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS total_approved_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS approved_expected_loss_rate

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

    GROUP BY score_band_policy_key
),

score_drivers AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: score_drivers

    Purpose:
        Identify compact score-band driver labels for executive evidence.

    Driver examples:
        score band with largest approved amount;
        score band with largest approved Expected Loss;
        score band with highest counteroffer count;
        score band with highest decline count;
        score band with highest / lowest offer rate;
        score band with highest approved Expected Loss rate.

    Interpretation:
        These labels identify concentration and movement by credit-quality segment.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        (SELECT score_band_policy_key
         FROM score_summary
         ORDER BY total_approved_amount DESC NULLS LAST, score_band_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS top_approved_amount_score_band,

        (SELECT score_band_policy_key
         FROM score_summary
         ORDER BY total_approved_expected_loss_amount DESC NULLS LAST, score_band_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS top_approved_expected_loss_score_band,

        (SELECT score_band_policy_key
         FROM score_summary
         ORDER BY counteroffer_count DESC, score_band_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS top_counteroffer_score_band,

        (SELECT score_band_policy_key
         FROM score_summary
         ORDER BY decline_count DESC, score_band_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS top_decline_score_band,

        (SELECT score_band_policy_key
         FROM score_summary
         ORDER BY offer_rate DESC NULLS LAST, score_band_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS highest_offer_rate_score_band,

        (SELECT score_band_policy_key
         FROM score_summary
         ORDER BY offer_rate ASC NULLS LAST, score_band_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS lowest_offer_rate_score_band,

        (SELECT score_band_policy_key
         FROM score_summary
         ORDER BY approved_expected_loss_rate DESC NULLS LAST, score_band_policy_key
         LIMIT 1) AS highest_approved_el_rate_score_band
),

product_score_summary AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: product_score_summary

    Purpose:
        Summarize current-run driver metrics at the product × score level.

    Why this matters:
        Product-only and score-only summaries can hide concentration at their intersection.

        Product × score drivers are often the strongest executive evidence for strategy movement.

    Credit risk interpretation:
        Product × score identifies where product structure and borrower-quality segmentation combine
        to create approved exposure, approved Expected Loss, counteroffer concentration, or decline
        concentration.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        product_type_policy_key,
        score_band_policy_key,
        product_type_policy_key || ' / ' || score_band_policy_key
            AS product_score_policy_segment,

        COUNT(*) AS applications,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE) AS offer_count,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER') AS counteroffer_count,
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE') AS decline_count,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS total_approved_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS approved_expected_loss_rate

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

    GROUP BY
        product_type_policy_key,
        score_band_policy_key
),

product_score_drivers AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: product_score_drivers

    Purpose:
        Identify compact product × score driver labels for the executive evidence row.

    Interpretation:
        These labels identify the segment intersections most important for:
            approved amount,
            approved Expected Loss,
            counteroffer concentration,
            decline concentration,
            and approved Expected Loss rate.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        (SELECT product_score_policy_segment
         FROM product_score_summary
         ORDER BY total_approved_amount DESC NULLS LAST, product_score_policy_segment
         LIMIT 1) AS top_approved_amount_product_score_segment,

        (SELECT product_score_policy_segment
         FROM product_score_summary
         ORDER BY total_approved_expected_loss_amount DESC NULLS LAST, product_score_policy_segment
         LIMIT 1) AS top_approved_el_product_score_segment,

        (SELECT product_score_policy_segment
         FROM product_score_summary
         ORDER BY counteroffer_count DESC, product_score_policy_segment
         LIMIT 1) AS top_counteroffer_product_score_segment,

        (SELECT product_score_policy_segment
         FROM product_score_summary
         ORDER BY decline_count DESC, product_score_policy_segment
         LIMIT 1) AS top_decline_product_score_segment,

        (SELECT product_score_policy_segment
         FROM product_score_summary
         ORDER BY approved_expected_loss_rate DESC NULLS LAST, product_score_policy_segment
         LIMIT 1) AS highest_approved_el_rate_product_score_segment
),

reason_counts AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: reason_counts

    Purpose:
        Count simulated reason-code distribution at the current run level.

    Why this matters:
        The executive evidence row should explain not only rates and amounts, but the reason-code
        drivers behind strategy outcomes.

    SQL mechanics:
        GROUP BY decision_outcome, primary_reason_family, and primary_reason_code creates one row per
        reason-code / outcome combination.

        Window SUM over COUNT(*) creates reason_population_share across the full current run.

    Boundary:
        Reason codes are simulated strategy explanation codes only.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        decision_outcome,
        primary_reason_family,
        primary_reason_code,

        COUNT(*) AS reason_row_count,

        COUNT(*)::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(SUM(COUNT(*)) OVER (), 0) AS reason_population_share

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

    GROUP BY
        decision_outcome,
        primary_reason_family,
        primary_reason_code
),

reason_drivers AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: reason_drivers

    Purpose:
        Identify compact run-level simulated reason-code driver fields.

    Driver fields:
        top overall reason;
        top non-approval reason;
        top policy-stop reason;
        top counteroffer reason;
        top manual-review reason;
        top decline reason.

    Why this matters:
        top_primary_reason_code may often be APPROVED_AS_REQUESTED.

        Non-approval and outcome-specific reason fields better explain friction, constraints, and
        risk-tightening movement.

    SQL mechanics:
        Each scalar subquery orders reason_counts by reason_row_count and deterministic tie-breakers.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        /*******************************************************************************************
        Top reason code across all rows.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (SELECT primary_reason_family
         FROM reason_counts
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_primary_reason_family,

        (SELECT primary_reason_code
         FROM reason_counts
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_primary_reason_code,

        (SELECT reason_population_share
         FROM reason_counts
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_primary_reason_population_share,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Top non-approval reason code.

        This excludes final APPROVE rows so the executive evidence can identify the strongest
        friction / constraint reason.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (SELECT primary_reason_family
         FROM reason_counts
         WHERE decision_outcome <> 'APPROVE'
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_non_approval_primary_reason_family,

        (SELECT primary_reason_code
         FROM reason_counts
         WHERE decision_outcome <> 'APPROVE'
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_non_approval_primary_reason_code,

        (SELECT reason_population_share
         FROM reason_counts
         WHERE decision_outcome <> 'APPROVE'
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_non_approval_reason_population_share,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Top policy-stop reason code.

        This is especially important when decline concentration or risk-tightening behavior is a key
        part of the strategy story.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (SELECT primary_reason_family
         FROM reason_counts
         WHERE primary_reason_family = 'POLICY_STOP'
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_policy_stop_primary_reason_family,

        (SELECT primary_reason_code
         FROM reason_counts
         WHERE primary_reason_family = 'POLICY_STOP'
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_policy_stop_primary_reason_code,

        (SELECT reason_population_share
         FROM reason_counts
         WHERE primary_reason_family = 'POLICY_STOP'
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_policy_stop_reason_population_share,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Outcome-specific reason highlights.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (SELECT primary_reason_code
         FROM reason_counts
         WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_counteroffer_reason_code,

        (SELECT primary_reason_code
         FROM reason_counts
         WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_manual_review_reason_code,

        (SELECT primary_reason_code
         FROM reason_counts
         WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
         ORDER BY reason_row_count DESC, primary_reason_family, primary_reason_code
         LIMIT 1) AS top_decline_reason_code
),

validation_summary AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: validation_summary

    Purpose:
        Roll Section 14 validation rows into executive evidence fields.

    Outputs:
        validation_pass_count;
        validation_review_count;
        validation_not_applicable_count;
        validation_review_items;
        validation_status_summary_jsonb.

    Interpretation:
        REVIEW rows are documentation prompts, not automatic invalidation.

        NOT_APPLICABLE rows identify tests that were not evaluable under the current run context.

    SQL mechanics:
        COUNT(*) FILTER creates status counts.
        STRING_AGG creates a compact readable review-item list.
        jsonb_agg preserves detailed validation rows as structured evidence.

    Boundary:
        This CTE summarizes Section 14 output only.

        It does not rerun validation logic.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE validation_status = 'PASS') AS validation_pass_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE validation_status = 'REVIEW') AS validation_review_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE validation_status = 'NOT_APPLICABLE')
            AS validation_not_applicable_count,

        STRING_AGG(
            validation_area || ': ' || validation_test_name || ' [' || validation_status || ']',
            ' | '
            ORDER BY validation_area, validation_test_name
        ) FILTER (WHERE validation_status IN ('REVIEW', 'NOT_APPLICABLE'))
            AS validation_review_items,

        jsonb_agg(
            jsonb_build_object(
                'validation_area', validation_area,
                'validation_test_name', validation_test_name,
                'validation_category', validation_category,
                'validation_status', validation_status,
                'observed_value', observed_value,
                'expected_behavior', expected_behavior,
                'interpretation', interpretation
            )
            ORDER BY validation_area, validation_test_name
        ) AS validation_status_summary_jsonb

    FROM tmp_m2_validation_status_summary
),

frontier AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: frontier

    Purpose:
        Bring in Section 15 executive frontier fields for the current run key.

    Why this matters:
        Section 15 already calculated archive-backed frontier posture and baseline-relative
        movement. Section 16.6 should persist those results rather than duplicate frontier logic.

    SQL mechanics:
        The JOIN uses the same technical run key as the evidence grain.

    Boundary:
        This CTE reads frontier evidence only.

        It does not recalculate frontier classification.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        f.*
    FROM tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary f
    JOIN current_key k
        ON f.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
       AND f.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
       AND f.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
       AND f.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND f.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
       AND f.population_id = k.population_id
    LIMIT 1
),

baseline_product AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: baseline_product

    Purpose:
        Create product-level baseline reference values from the archive.

    Why baseline comes from archive:
        Baseline-relative deltas should compare current latest-run metrics to the archived baseline
        strategy under the same Module 1 scenario / population and strategy set.

    SQL mechanics:
        The archive is filtered to:
            same strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name = BASELINE_STRATEGY,
            same strategy_version,
            same Module 1 scenario / population.

    Boundary:
        This CTE does not require the current run to be a challenger.

        Delta fields are later set to NULL for BASELINE_STRATEGY.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        ar.product_type_policy_key,
        SUM(COALESCE(ar.approved_amount, 0)) AS baseline_total_approved_amount,
        SUM(COALESCE(ar.approved_expected_loss_amount, 0)) AS baseline_total_approved_el

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ar

    JOIN current_key k
        ON ar.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
       AND ar.strategy_name = 'BASELINE_STRATEGY'
       AND ar.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
       AND ar.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ar.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
       AND ar.population_id = k.population_id

    GROUP BY ar.product_type_policy_key
),

current_product AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: current_product

    Purpose:
        Create product-level current-run values from the latest-run table for baseline-relative
        product deltas.

    Interpretation:
        This is the current strategy's product-level approved exposure and approved Expected Loss
        profile.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        product_type_policy_key,
        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS current_total_approved_amount,
        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0)) AS current_total_approved_el

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

    GROUP BY product_type_policy_key
),

product_delta AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: product_delta

    Purpose:
        Compare current product exposure and approved Expected Loss to the archived baseline product
        profile.

    SQL mechanics:
        INNER JOIN means product deltas are calculated only where both current and baseline product
        rows exist.

    Boundary:
        If no baseline exists, this CTE returns no rows and later driver fields become NULL.

        NULL delta drivers are acceptable for baseline runs or non-baseline-unavailable contexts.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        cp.product_type_policy_key,

        cp.current_total_approved_amount - bp.baseline_total_approved_amount
            AS delta_total_approved_amount,

        cp.current_total_approved_el - bp.baseline_total_approved_el
            AS delta_total_approved_el

    FROM current_product cp

    JOIN baseline_product bp
        ON bp.product_type_policy_key = cp.product_type_policy_key
),

baseline_score AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: baseline_score

    Purpose:
        Create score-band baseline offer-rate and decline-rate reference values from the archive.

    Why this matters:
        Offer-rate movement and decline-rate movement by score band are useful for explaining
        strategy posture and credit-quality effects.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        ar.score_band_policy_key,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE ar.simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS baseline_offer_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE ar.decision_outcome = 'DECLINE')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS baseline_decline_rate

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ar

    JOIN current_key k
        ON ar.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
       AND ar.strategy_name = 'BASELINE_STRATEGY'
       AND ar.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
       AND ar.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ar.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
       AND ar.population_id = k.population_id

    GROUP BY ar.score_band_policy_key
),

current_score AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: current_score

    Purpose:
        Create current score-band offer-rate and decline-rate values from the latest-run table.

    Interpretation:
        These are the current run's access and no-offer rates by borrower-quality segment.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        score_band_policy_key,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS current_offer_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS current_decline_rate

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

    GROUP BY score_band_policy_key
),

score_delta AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: score_delta

    Purpose:
        Compare current offer and decline rates to baseline by score band.

    Interpretation:
        The largest movement score bands help explain whether strategy changes concentrated in
        stronger, weaker, or transitional borrower-quality tiers.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        cs.score_band_policy_key,
        cs.current_offer_rate - bs.baseline_offer_rate AS delta_offer_rate,
        cs.current_decline_rate - bs.baseline_decline_rate AS delta_decline_rate

    FROM current_score cs

    JOIN baseline_score bs
        ON bs.score_band_policy_key = cs.score_band_policy_key
),

baseline_product_score AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: baseline_product_score

    Purpose:
        Create product × score baseline approved Expected Loss values from the archive.

    Why this matters:
        Product × score approved Expected Loss deltas are often the clearest way to explain where a
        strategy moved risk.

    Example interpretation:
        If a tighter strategy reduces approved Expected Loss most in unsecured / subprime segments,
        this CTE supports that evidence trail.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        ar.product_type_policy_key,
        ar.score_band_policy_key,
        ar.product_type_policy_key || ' / ' || ar.score_band_policy_key
            AS product_score_policy_segment,

        SUM(COALESCE(ar.approved_expected_loss_amount, 0)) AS baseline_total_approved_el

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ar

    JOIN current_key k
        ON ar.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
       AND ar.strategy_name = 'BASELINE_STRATEGY'
       AND ar.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
       AND ar.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ar.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
       AND ar.population_id = k.population_id

    GROUP BY
        ar.product_type_policy_key,
        ar.score_band_policy_key
),

current_product_score AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: current_product_score

    Purpose:
        Create current product × score approved Expected Loss values from the latest-run table.

    Interpretation:
        These values show where approved Expected Loss is concentrated in the current strategy run.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        product_type_policy_key,
        score_band_policy_key,
        product_type_policy_key || ' / ' || score_band_policy_key
            AS product_score_policy_segment,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0)) AS current_total_approved_el

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions

    GROUP BY
        product_type_policy_key,
        score_band_policy_key
),

product_score_delta AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: product_score_delta

    Purpose:
        Compare current product × score approved Expected Loss to archived baseline.

    SQL mechanics:
        INNER JOIN means deltas are calculated only where both baseline and current product × score
        segments exist.

    Boundary:
        If no baseline exists, later largest-delta fields become NULL.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        cps.product_score_policy_segment,

        cps.current_total_approved_el - bps.baseline_total_approved_el
            AS delta_total_approved_el

    FROM current_product_score cps

    JOIN baseline_product_score bps
        ON bps.product_type_policy_key = cps.product_type_policy_key
       AND bps.score_band_policy_key = cps.score_band_policy_key
),

delta_drivers AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: delta_drivers

    Purpose:
        Select the largest baseline-relative movement drivers for executive evidence.

    Why baseline rows return NULL:
        A baseline strategy should not report largest baseline-relative deltas against itself.

    Driver fields:
        largest_delta_approved_amount_product,
        largest_delta_approved_el_product,
        largest_delta_offer_rate_score_band,
        largest_delta_decline_rate_score_band,
        largest_delta_approved_el_product_score_segment.

    SQL mechanics:
        Each scalar subquery orders by ABS(delta) so the largest movement is selected regardless of
        direction.

        The field name identifies where movement occurred; the full delta size can be reviewed in
        Section 15 or supporting diagnostics.

    Interpretation:
        These fields help explain where strategy movement concentrated.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        CASE
            WHEN (SELECT strategy_name FROM current_key LIMIT 1) = 'BASELINE_STRATEGY'
                THEN NULL
            ELSE (
                SELECT product_type_policy_key
                FROM product_delta
                ORDER BY
                    ABS(delta_total_approved_amount) DESC NULLS LAST,
                    product_type_policy_key
                LIMIT 1
            )
        END AS largest_delta_approved_amount_product,

        CASE
            WHEN (SELECT strategy_name FROM current_key LIMIT 1) = 'BASELINE_STRATEGY'
                THEN NULL
            ELSE (
                SELECT product_type_policy_key
                FROM product_delta
                ORDER BY
                    ABS(delta_total_approved_el) DESC NULLS LAST,
                    product_type_policy_key
                LIMIT 1
            )
        END AS largest_delta_approved_el_product,

        CASE
            WHEN (SELECT strategy_name FROM current_key LIMIT 1) = 'BASELINE_STRATEGY'
                THEN NULL
            ELSE (
                SELECT score_band_policy_key
                FROM score_delta
                ORDER BY
                    ABS(delta_offer_rate) DESC NULLS LAST,
                    score_band_policy_key
                LIMIT 1
            )
        END AS largest_delta_offer_rate_score_band,

        CASE
            WHEN (SELECT strategy_name FROM current_key LIMIT 1) = 'BASELINE_STRATEGY'
                THEN NULL
            ELSE (
                SELECT score_band_policy_key
                FROM score_delta
                ORDER BY
                    ABS(delta_decline_rate) DESC NULLS LAST,
                    score_band_policy_key
                LIMIT 1
            )
        END AS largest_delta_decline_rate_score_band,

        CASE
            WHEN (SELECT strategy_name FROM current_key LIMIT 1) = 'BASELINE_STRATEGY'
                THEN NULL
            ELSE (
                SELECT product_score_policy_segment
                FROM product_score_delta
                ORDER BY
                    ABS(delta_total_approved_el) DESC NULLS LAST,
                    product_score_policy_segment
                LIMIT 1
            )
        END AS largest_delta_approved_el_product_score_segment
),

module3_readiness AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    CTE: module3_readiness

    Purpose:
        Identify whether the current run has the core fields needed to support future Module 3
        growth / economics logic.

    Availability rule:
        TRUE when at least one simulated offer-exposure row has:
            approved amount,
            APR proxy,
            synthetic estimated-PD proxy,
            LGD,
            and approved Expected Loss.

    Credit strategy interpretation:
        This tells reviewers whether the current Module 2 run has the necessary basis fields for a
        future economics module.

    Boundary:
        This is readiness evidence only.

        It does not calculate revenue, funding cost, fee income, profitability, capital, pricing
        optimization, or risk-adjusted margin.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        CASE
            WHEN SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE) > 0
             AND COUNT(*) FILTER (
                    WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE
                      AND base_apr_for_payment_calc IS NOT NULL
                      AND approved_amount IS NOT NULL
                      AND estimated_pd IS NOT NULL
                      AND estimated_lgd IS NOT NULL
                      AND approved_expected_loss_amount IS NOT NULL
                 ) > 0
                THEN TRUE
            ELSE FALSE
        END AS module3_growth_inputs_available_flag,

        CASE
            WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE) = 0
                THEN 'No simulated offer-exposure rows are available for future Module 3 economics.'

            WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (
                    WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE
                      AND base_apr_for_payment_calc IS NULL
                 ) > 0
                THEN 'One or more offer rows are missing APR proxy values.'

            WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (
                    WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE
                      AND approved_amount IS NULL
                 ) > 0
                THEN 'One or more offer rows are missing approved_amount values.'

            ELSE 'Core Module 3 readiness inputs are available: approved amount, APR proxy, product, synthetic estimated-PD proxy, LGD, and approved Expected Loss. Utilization, funding cost, fee income, and revenue assumptions remain future Module 3 design inputs.'
        END AS module3_growth_input_gap_note,

        TRUE AS module3_revenue_model_required_flag,

        'Earnings, revenue, funding cost, profitability, and risk-adjusted margin logic are intentionally deferred to Module 3. Section 16 captures readiness inputs only.'::TEXT
            AS module3_boundary_note

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
)

SELECT
    CURRENT_TIMESTAMP AS evidence_snapshot_ts,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Evidence snapshot ID.

    SQL mechanics:
        MD5 hashes the technical run key plus CURRENT_TIMESTAMP.

    Interpretation:
        This identifies the evidence-capture event.

        It is not the run key and should not replace strategy / scenario / population lineage.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    MD5(
        k.strategy_set_name || '|'
        || k.strategy_name || '|'
        || k.strategy_version || '|'
        || k.module1_scenario_set_name || '|'
        || k.module1_scenario_name || '|'
        || k.population_id || '|'
        || CURRENT_TIMESTAMP::TEXT
    ) AS evidence_snapshot_id,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Campaign registry / run-story fields.

    These are the primary documentation-linkage fields for run roadmap, Validation Summary, README,
    LinkedIn, and comparison traceability.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    story.campaign_registry_required_flag,
    story.registry_match_count,
    story.run_registry_match_status,

    story.module1_run_id,
    story.module2_run_id,
    story.run_sequence_number,

    story.showcase_id,
    story.showcase_name,
    story.comparison_group_id,
    story.validation_evidence_group_id,

    story.readme_storyline_label,
    story.linkedin_post_sequence,
    story.validation_summary_section_hint,

    story.module1_parameter_family_changed,
    story.module1_parameter_change_summary,
    story.module2_strategy_family_changed,
    story.module2_parameter_change_summary,
    story.expected_storyline,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Observed storyline.

    Registry / story helper observed_storyline is preferred if populated.

    If not populated, Section 15 frontier_interpretation_note provides the best available automated
    observed storyline for the current run.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    COALESCE(story.observed_storyline, f.frontier_interpretation_note) AS observed_storyline,

    story.validation_notes,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Module 2 strategy identity.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    k.module2_model_version,
    k.strategy_set_name,
    k.strategy_name,
    k.strategy_version,
    k.strategy_run_id,
    k.strategy_run_ts,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Output and archive timestamps.

    latest_output_created_ts:
        latest-run table materialization timestamp.

    archive_inserted_ts:
        archive persistence timestamp for the matching archived slice.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    k.latest_output_created_ts,
    ats.archive_inserted_ts,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Archive and resolution controls.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    k.archive_run_flag,
    k.strategy_archive_reset_mode,
    k.failed_counteroffer_resolution,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Module 1 source and lineage.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    k.module1_input_source,
    k.module1_source_table_name,

    k.module1_model_version,
    k.module1_scenario_set_name,
    k.module1_scenario_name,
    k.population_id,
    k.anchor_date,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Structural counts.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    p.applications,
    p.distinct_application_id_count,
    p.duplicate_application_count,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Final outcome counts.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    p.approval_count,
    p.counteroffer_count,
    p.manual_review_count,
    p.decline_count,
    p.offer_count,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Final outcome rates.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    p.approval_rate,
    p.counteroffer_rate,
    p.manual_review_rate,
    p.decline_rate,
    p.simulated_offer_exposure_rate,
    p.approval_share_of_offers,
    p.counteroffer_share_of_offers,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Exposure metrics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    p.total_requested_amount,
    p.total_approved_amount,
    p.approved_amount_capture_rate,

    p.avg_requested_amount,
    p.avg_approved_amount_all_apps,
    p.avg_approved_amount_offer_rows,

    p.total_exposure_reduction_amount,

    p.counteroffer_requested_amount,
    p.counteroffer_approved_amount,
    p.counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount,
    p.counteroffer_exposure_reduction_pct_avg,

    p.manual_review_requested_amount,
    p.manual_review_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    p.decline_requested_amount,
    p.decline_requested_expected_loss_amount,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Affordability metrics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    p.avg_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
    p.avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_offer_rows,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    APR proxy and term metrics for Module 3 readiness.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    p.avg_apr_proxy_all_apps,
    p.avg_apr_proxy_offer_rows,
    p.requested_amount_weighted_apr_proxy,
    p.approved_amount_weighted_apr_proxy,
    p.requested_amount_x_apr_proxy_sum,
    p.approved_amount_x_apr_proxy_sum,

    p.avg_loan_term_months_offer_rows,
    p.approved_amount_weighted_term_months,
    p.term_missing_or_revolving_count,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Product approved-exposure composition.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    p.secured_approved_amount_share,
    p.unsecured_approved_amount_share,
    p.revolving_approved_amount_share,
    p.installment_approved_amount_share,
    p.mortgage_approved_amount_share,

    pj.product_approved_amount_mix_jsonb,
    pj.product_approved_expected_loss_mix_jsonb,
    pj.product_offer_rate_jsonb,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Synthetic risk and LGD metrics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    p.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_all_apps,
    p.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows,
    p.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_declined_rows,

    p.avg_estimated_lgd_all_apps,
    p.avg_estimated_lgd_offer_rows,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Expected Loss metrics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    p.total_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    p.total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    p.avg_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    p.avg_approved_expected_loss_all_apps,
    p.avg_approved_expected_loss_offer_rows,

    p.requested_expected_loss_rate,
    p.approved_expected_loss_rate,
    p.approved_amount_per_approved_expected_loss_dollar,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Top simulated reason-code fields.

    Prefer Section 15 frontier reason fields when available because they may include archive-backed
    frontier context.

    Fall back to current-run reason_drivers when frontier context is NULL.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    COALESCE(f.top_primary_reason_family, rd.top_primary_reason_family),
    COALESCE(f.top_primary_reason_code, rd.top_primary_reason_code),
    COALESCE(f.top_primary_reason_population_share, rd.top_primary_reason_population_share),

    COALESCE(f.top_non_approval_primary_reason_family, rd.top_non_approval_primary_reason_family),
    COALESCE(f.top_non_approval_primary_reason_code, rd.top_non_approval_primary_reason_code),
    COALESCE(f.top_non_approval_reason_population_share, rd.top_non_approval_reason_population_share),

    COALESCE(f.top_policy_stop_primary_reason_family, rd.top_policy_stop_primary_reason_family),
    COALESCE(f.top_policy_stop_primary_reason_code, rd.top_policy_stop_primary_reason_code),
    COALESCE(f.top_policy_stop_reason_population_share, rd.top_policy_stop_reason_population_share),

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Baseline-relative reason-code movement fields from Section 15.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_family,
    f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code,
    f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share,
    f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share,
    f.top_reason_code_delta_population_share,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Outcome-specific reason-code highlights.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    rd.top_counteroffer_reason_code,
    rd.top_manual_review_reason_code,
    rd.top_decline_reason_code,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Frontier posture fields.

    These come from Section 15 and are diagnostic story labels only.

    They are not production recommendations or risk appetite approvals.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    f.frontier_position_type,
    f.executive_frontier_quadrant,
    f.frontier_interpretation_note,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Validation summary fields.

    These summarize Section 14 validation-status evidence.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    vs.validation_pass_count,
    vs.validation_review_count,
    vs.validation_not_applicable_count,
    vs.validation_review_items,
    vs.validation_status_summary_jsonb,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Product driver fields.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    pd.top_approved_amount_product,
    pd.top_approved_amount_product_share,
    pd.top_approved_expected_loss_product,
    pd.top_approved_expected_loss_product_share,
    pd.top_counteroffer_product,
    pd.top_decline_product,
    pd.highest_offer_rate_product,
    pd.lowest_offer_rate_product,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Score-band driver fields.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    sd.top_approved_amount_score_band,
    sd.top_approved_expected_loss_score_band,
    sd.top_counteroffer_score_band,
    sd.top_decline_score_band,
    sd.highest_offer_rate_score_band,
    sd.lowest_offer_rate_score_band,
    sd.highest_approved_el_rate_score_band,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Product × score driver fields.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    psd.top_approved_amount_product_score_segment,
    psd.top_approved_el_product_score_segment,
    psd.top_counteroffer_product_score_segment,
    psd.top_decline_product_score_segment,
    psd.highest_approved_el_rate_product_score_segment,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Baseline-relative driver fields.

    These are NULL for baseline rows and may be NULL when a matching baseline reference is unavailable.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    dd.largest_delta_approved_amount_product,
    dd.largest_delta_approved_el_product,
    dd.largest_delta_offer_rate_score_band,
    dd.largest_delta_decline_rate_score_band,
    dd.largest_delta_approved_el_product_score_segment,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Module 3 readiness fields.

    These are readiness indicators only.

    They are not revenue, profitability, pricing, funding-cost, capital, or risk-adjusted margin
    outputs.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    mr.module3_growth_inputs_available_flag,
    mr.module3_growth_input_gap_note,
    mr.module3_revenue_model_required_flag,
    mr.module3_boundary_note

FROM current_key k

/***************************************************************************************************
The following CROSS JOINs are intentional.

Each CTE is expected to return one row after Section 16.0 gatekeepers and Section 14 / Section 15
dependencies are satisfied.

Together, they assemble one executive evidence row for the current run.

If any of these CTEs unexpectedly returns zero rows, the INSERT will produce no executive evidence row,
and Section 16.7 will raise a clear evidence-capture exception.
***************************************************************************************************/
CROSS JOIN story
CROSS JOIN archive_ts ats
CROSS JOIN portfolio p
CROSS JOIN product_json pj
CROSS JOIN product_drivers pd
CROSS JOIN score_drivers sd
CROSS JOIN product_score_drivers psd
CROSS JOIN reason_drivers rd
CROSS JOIN validation_summary vs
CROSS JOIN delta_drivers dd
CROSS JOIN module3_readiness mr

/***************************************************************************************************
LEFT JOIN frontier:

The frontier table should contain a matching current-run row after Section 15.

LEFT JOIN keeps evidence capture structurally tolerant if the frontier match is absent, while still
allowing run-level evidence to be inserted with NULL frontier fields.

Section 16.0 already requires tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary to exist.
***************************************************************************************************/
LEFT JOIN frontier f
    ON TRUE;



/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 16.6 — CURRENT RUN EXECUTIVE EVIDENCE SUMMARY

If execution reaches this point:
    1. Product × score segment evidence has already been persisted for the current run with registry
       IDs.
    2. One executive evidence summary row has been inserted for the current run key with registry IDs.
    3. Current run story metadata has been captured.
    4. Current run decision outcomes have been summarized.
    5. Current run simulated offer-exposure metrics have been captured.
    6. Requested exposure, approved exposure, and exposure capture metrics have been captured.
    7. Requested Expected Loss, approved Expected Loss, and approved Expected Loss rate have been
       captured.
    8. Synthetic estimated-PD proxy and LGD evidence has been captured.
    9. APR proxy and term fields have been captured for future Module 3 readiness.
    10. Product, score-band, and product × score driver fields have been captured.
    11. Simulated reason-code story fields have been captured.
    12. Section 14 validation status counts and JSONB detail have been captured.
    13. Section 15 frontier posture fields have been captured when the current run has a matching
        frontier row.
    14. Baseline-relative segment movement driver fields have been captured when a baseline reference
        exists.
    15. Module 3 readiness flags and boundary notes have been captured.
    16. Evidence rows now carry module1_run_id, module2_run_id, showcase_id, comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id, README label, LinkedIn sequence, and registry match status.

No latest-run output rows have been modified.
No archive rows have been modified.
No strategy parameter rows have been modified.
No product policy parameter rows have been modified.
No decision outcomes have been recalculated.
No approved exposure values have been recalculated.
No approved Expected Loss values have been recalculated.
No simulated reason codes have been reassigned.
No campaign registry rows have been modified.
No revenue, earnings, funding-cost, pricing, profitability, capital, or risk-adjusted margin logic has
been built.

Next section:
    Section 16.7 should validate that evidence capture produced the expected persistent evidence rows
    for the current run key and that registry-linkage metadata was preserved consistently.

***************************************************************************************************/

/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.7 — LOCAL EVIDENCE CAPTURE GATEKEEPERS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that Section 16 persisted exactly the evidence expected for the current completed Module 2
    strategy run.

    Section 16.7 answers:

        "Did evidence capture create the right persistent evidence rows for this current run key,
         and did those rows preserve the campaign registry identifiers needed for validation-summary,
         README, LinkedIn, and comparison traceability?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Read the current run key from tmp_m2_current_run_key.
    2. Read the current registry / story metadata from tmp_m2_current_run_story_params.
    3. Confirm exactly one executive evidence summary row exists for the current run key.
    4. Confirm validation evidence detail row count matches tmp_m2_validation_status_summary.
    5. Confirm exactly one parameter snapshot row exists for the current run key.
    6. Confirm product × score segment evidence row count matches the latest-run product × score
       segment count.
    7. Confirm required executive summary evidence fields are populated.
    8. Confirm required registry-linkage fields are populated across evidence tables.
    9. Confirm registry-linkage fields stored in evidence tables align to tmp_m2_current_run_story_params.
    10. Confirm parameter snapshot JSONB payloads and hash are populated.
    11. Check Module 3 readiness flag without failing Section 16 solely because Module 3 is future
        scope.

INPUTS:
    tmp_m2_current_run_key
    tmp_m2_current_run_story_params
    tmp_m2_validation_status_summary
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary

OUTPUT:
    No result table is expected.

    This section either:
        completes successfully,
        or raises a clear evidence-capture exception.

WHEN TO RUN THIS SECTION:
    Run after:
        Section 16.3 inserted validation evidence detail.
        Section 16.4 inserted the parameter snapshot.
        Section 16.5 inserted product × score segment evidence.
        Section 16.6 inserted the one-row executive evidence summary.

    Section 16.7 should be the local evidence-capture acceptance gate before Section 16.8 displays
    export-ready diagnostics.

WHY LOCAL GATEKEEPERS ARE NEEDED:
    Sections 16.3 through 16.6 insert persistent evidence.

    Persistent evidence should not be assumed correct merely because INSERT statements completed.

    Section 16.7 verifies that the evidence layer now contains the expected run-level, validation,
    parameter, and segment records for the current run key.

EVIDENCE GRAIN CHECKED:
    Primary current run key:

        strategy_set_name
        strategy_name
        strategy_version
        module1_scenario_set_name
        module1_scenario_name
        population_id

    Segment evidence extends this grain by:

        product_type_policy_key
        score_band_policy_key

WHY EXACTLY ONE EXECUTIVE SUMMARY ROW IS REQUIRED:
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary is the main one-row executive story register.

    For each completed strategy / scenario / population key, there should be exactly one current
    evidence row.

    Zero rows means Section 16.6 did not persist the executive story.

    More than one row means the evidence layer has duplicate or conflicting run-level narratives.

WHY VALIDATION COUNT IS CHECKED AGAINST SECTION 14:
    Section 16.3 should persist every row from tmp_m2_validation_status_summary.

    Matching the persistent validation evidence count to the temporary Section 14 validation summary
    count helps ensure the Validation Summary evidence spine was fully captured.

WHY PARAMETER SNAPSHOT COUNT IS CHECKED:
    Each completed run key should have exactly one persistent parameter snapshot.

    The parameter snapshot preserves:
        the active strategy parameter card,
        the product-policy parameter card,
        and the registry / story metadata payload.

    Without this snapshot, reviewers may know what happened but not what configuration produced it.

WHY SEGMENT COUNT IS CHECKED AGAINST THE LATEST-RUN TABLE:
    Section 16.5 persists one product × score segment evidence row for each product × score
    combination present in the current latest-run output.

    The local gatekeeper compares the persistent segment-evidence count against the distinct current
    latest-run product × score count.

    If the counts differ, the segment companion table is incomplete or overpopulated for the current
    run.

WHY REQUIRED SUMMARY FIELDS ARE CHECKED:
    The executive evidence summary is the primary one-row story record for the current run.

    Core identity, registry linkage, outcome-rate, approved-exposure, approved Expected Loss,
    validation-rollup, and top reason-code fields must be populated before the evidence row is used
    in README, LinkedIn, executive review, or Validation Summary drafting.

REGISTRY PATCH:
    Section 16.7 validates that the same registry linkage carried by Section 16.0 is present in the
    persistent evidence layer:

        campaign_registry_required_flag
        registry_match_count
        run_registry_match_status
        module1_run_id
        module2_run_id
        run_sequence_number
        showcase_id
        showcase_name
        comparison_group_id
        validation_evidence_group_id
        readme_storyline_label
        linkedin_post_sequence
        validation_summary_section_hint

    These fields connect:

        SQL run key
        → campaign roadmap
        → comparison group
        → validation evidence group
        → executive evidence row
        → validation evidence rows
        → parameter snapshot
        → segment evidence
        → final Validation Summary artifact.

WHY REGISTRY COMPLETENESS IS CHECKED:
    Evidence rows may be technically correct but still difficult to document if they do not carry run
    IDs and evidence-group IDs.

    Registry fields make the connection from code output to validation summary clear and reusable.

    This is especially important for formal campaign runs.

WHY REGISTRY ALIGNMENT IS CHECKED:
    A row can have registry fields populated but still carry the wrong values.

    Section 16.7 therefore compares persistent evidence rows back to tmp_m2_current_run_story_params
    using NULL-safe comparisons.

    This confirms that the executive row, validation rows, parameter snapshot, and segment rows are
    all tied to the same run-story metadata.

FORMAL CAMPAIGN EXPECTATION:
    When campaign_registry_required_flag = TRUE:

        run_registry_match_status should equal RUN_REGISTRY_MATCHED.
        registry_match_count should equal 1.
        module2_run_id should be populated.
        run_sequence_number should be populated.
        showcase_id should be populated.
        validation_evidence_group_id should be populated.

    Section 16.0 already fails fast if required registry matching is missing.

    Section 16.7 verifies that the matched registry fields were actually persisted.

AD HOC DEVELOPMENT EXPECTATION:
    When campaign_registry_required_flag = FALSE:

        fallback metadata may be present.

    In that case, Section 16.7 still requires core registry-linkage fields such as module1_run_id,
    module2_run_id, showcase_name, and run_registry_match_status to be populated, but it does not
    require formal campaign fields such as run_sequence_number or validation_evidence_group_id.

MODULE 3 READINESS BOUNDARY:
    Module 3 readiness gaps do not fail Section 16.

    Module 3 is future scope.

    Section 16 captures readiness flags and gap notes so the future economics layer can be designed
    deliberately.

    A missing Module 3 readiness input is evidence to record, not a defect in Module 2 strategy
    simulation.

VALIDATION STATUS INTERPRETATION:
    PASS:
        The validation expectation was satisfied.

    REVIEW:
        The pattern should be interpreted before documentation.
        REVIEW does not automatically mean the strategy run is invalid.

    NOT_APPLICABLE:
        The validation test depends on conditions not present in the current run context.

SQL CONCEPTS TAUGHT IN THIS SECTION:
    PL/pgSQL DO block:
        Runs multiple evidence integrity checks and raises clear exceptions when evidence capture is
        incomplete.

    DECLARE:
        Defines local variables used to hold current-run keys, story metadata, row counts, and
        completeness diagnostics.

    SELECT ... INTO:
        Loads one-row query results into PL/pgSQL variables or records.

    COUNT(*):
        Confirms evidence table row-count expectations.

    COUNT(*) FILTER:
        Counts rows matching specific conditions without changing the underlying evidence table.

    IS DISTINCT FROM:
        Performs NULL-safe comparison.
        This is critical for registry alignment checks because ordinary equality does not treat NULL
        comparisons as true or false in the same way.

    UNION ALL:
        Stacks registry-alignment checks across multiple evidence tables into one compact violation
        count.

    RAISE EXCEPTION:
        Stops execution when persistent evidence is missing, duplicated, incomplete, or inconsistent.

READ-ONLY / PERSISTENCE BOUNDARY:
    Section 16.7 does not insert evidence rows.
    Section 16.7 does not delete evidence rows.
    Section 16.7 does not update evidence rows.
    Section 16.7 does not modify credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions.
    Section 16.7 does not modify credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive.
    Section 16.7 does not modify campaign registry rows.
    Section 16.7 does not modify strategy parameter rows.
    Section 16.7 does not modify product policy parameter rows.
    Section 16.7 does not recalculate decisions.
    Section 16.7 does not recalculate approved exposure.
    Section 16.7 does not recalculate approved Expected Loss.
    Section 16.7 does not reassign simulated reason codes.
    Section 16.7 does not implement Module 3 economics.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Current run key record.

    Section 16.0 already validated that tmp_m2_current_run_key contains exactly one row.

    Section 16.7 reads that one row and uses it to scope every evidence-count check below.

    Technical evidence grain:
        strategy_set_name
        strategy_name
        strategy_version
        module1_scenario_set_name
        module1_scenario_name
        population_id
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    k RECORD;

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Current run story / registry record.

    Section 16.0 already validated that tmp_m2_current_run_story_params contains exactly one active
    row.

    Section 16.7 uses this record as the expected registry-linkage source for persistent evidence
    rows.

    This record is the bridge between:
        technical SQL run key
        and formal campaign / documentation IDs.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    s RECORD;

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Evidence row-count diagnostics.

    These counts confirm that each persistent evidence table contains the expected current-run
    records after Sections 16.3 through 16.6 executed.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    v_summary_count BIGINT;
    v_validation_count BIGINT;
    v_expected_validation_count BIGINT;
    v_parameter_snapshot_count BIGINT;
    v_segment_count BIGINT;
    v_expected_segment_count BIGINT;

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Evidence completeness diagnostics.

    These counts identify whether required fields or required payloads are missing from persistent
    evidence rows.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    v_null_required_summary_count BIGINT;
    v_validation_registry_gap_count BIGINT;
    v_parameter_registry_gap_count BIGINT;
    v_segment_registry_gap_count BIGINT;
    v_parameter_payload_gap_count BIGINT;

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Registry-alignment diagnostic.

    This count identifies evidence rows whose registry values are populated but do not match the
    active current-run story metadata.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    v_registry_alignment_violation_count BIGINT;

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Module 3 readiness diagnostic.

    This count is intentionally not used as a failure condition because Module 3 is future scope.

    The executive evidence row stores Module 3 readiness flags and gap notes for later review.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    v_module3_gap_count BIGINT;

BEGIN
    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7A Load current run key.

    Business purpose:
        Scope all local evidence gatekeepers to the current latest-run strategy / Module 1 scenario /
        population slice.

    SQL mechanics:
        SELECT ... INTO k loads the first row of tmp_m2_current_run_key into a PL/pgSQL record.

    Assumption:
        Section 16.0 already enforced exactly one row in tmp_m2_current_run_key.

    Failure behavior:
        This block still checks that a run key was loaded. If not, the evidence-capture gatekeeper
        raises an explicit exception rather than allowing downstream NULL-key checks to behave
        ambiguously.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT *
    INTO k
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_key
    LIMIT 1;

    IF k.strategy_set_name IS NULL
       OR k.strategy_name IS NULL
       OR k.strategy_version IS NULL
       OR k.module1_scenario_set_name IS NULL
       OR k.module1_scenario_name IS NULL
       OR k.population_id IS NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: current run key is missing or incomplete in tmp_m2_current_run_key.';
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7B Load current run registry / story metadata.

    Business purpose:
        Establish the expected campaign registry fields that should now appear in all persistent
        evidence rows.

    SQL mechanics:
        SELECT ... INTO s loads the active story row into a PL/pgSQL record.

    Assumption:
        Section 16.0 already enforced exactly one active story row.

    Registry interpretation:
        RUN_REGISTRY_MATCHED means the row was tied to the formal campaign registry.

        Fallback statuses may appear only when campaign_registry_required_flag = FALSE.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT *
    INTO s
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_story_params
    WHERE active_story_flag IS TRUE
    LIMIT 1;

    IF s.active_story_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: active current-run story metadata row is missing in tmp_m2_current_run_story_params.';
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7C Executive evidence summary row-count gatekeeper.

    Expected:
        exactly one row in credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary for the current run
        key.

    Why exactly one:
        The executive evidence summary is one-row-per-run-key evidence.

        Multiple rows would create duplicate or conflicting executive stories.

        Zero rows would mean Section 16.6 did not persist the run-level evidence.

    SQL mechanics:
        The WHERE clause repeats the full technical run key so the count is scoped to the current
        completed strategy / scenario / population slice only.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_summary_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e
    WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = k.population_id;

    IF v_summary_count <> 1 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: expected exactly one executive evidence summary row for current run, found %.',
            v_summary_count;
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7D Validation evidence detail row-count gatekeeper.

    Expected:
        persistent validation evidence count should equal tmp_m2_validation_status_summary count.

    Why exact count matters:
        Section 16.3 should persist every Section 14 validation status row.

        A mismatch means the Validation Summary evidence spine is incomplete or overpopulated.

    SQL mechanics:
        First count persistent validation rows for the current run key.
        Then count source validation rows from tmp_m2_validation_status_summary.
        Finally compare the two counts.

    Credit risk / governance interpretation:
        Validation evidence should be reproducible and traceable at the run level.

        A missing validation row could omit a PASS, REVIEW, or NOT_APPLICABLE item from the later
        written Validation Summary.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_validation_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence e
    WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = k.population_id;

    IF v_validation_count <= 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: no validation evidence rows were captured for current run.';
    END IF;

    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_expected_validation_count
    FROM tmp_m2_validation_status_summary;

    IF v_expected_validation_count <= 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: tmp_m2_validation_status_summary contains zero rows.';
    END IF;

    IF v_validation_count <> v_expected_validation_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: validation evidence row count (%) does not match Section 14 validation summary row count (%).',
            v_validation_count,
            v_expected_validation_count;
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7E Parameter snapshot row-count gatekeeper.

    Expected:
        exactly one row in credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot for the current run
        key.

    Why exactly one:
        Each current run key should have one snapshot of:
            active strategy parameters,
            product policy parameters,
            and run-story metadata.

    Failure meaning:
        Zero rows means parameter evidence is missing.

        More than one row means the evidence layer contains duplicate parameter snapshots for the
        same run key.

    SQL mechanics:
        The count is scoped to the same technical run key used by the executive evidence summary.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_parameter_snapshot_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot e
    WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = k.population_id;

    IF v_parameter_snapshot_count <> 1 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: expected exactly one parameter snapshot row for current run, found %.',
            v_parameter_snapshot_count;
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7F Segment evidence row-count gatekeeper.

    Expected:
        Persistent segment evidence row count should equal the number of distinct product × score
        combinations in the current latest-run output.

    Why this matters:
        Section 16.5 is the product × score companion evidence layer.

        If it misses a segment, executive driver fields may not be supported by complete drill-down
        evidence.

        If it overpopulates segments, the evidence layer may be mixing current-run and stale segment
        rows.

    SQL mechanics:
        v_segment_count counts persistent segment evidence rows for the current run key.

        v_expected_segment_count counts the distinct product_type_policy_key × score_band_policy_key
        combinations in credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions.

    Credit risk interpretation:
        Product × score evidence explains where portfolio-level access, exposure, approved Expected
        Loss, counteroffer, and decline behavior is concentrated.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_segment_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary e
    WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = k.population_id;

    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_expected_segment_count
    FROM (
        SELECT DISTINCT
            product_type_policy_key,
            score_band_policy_key
        FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions
    ) d;

    IF v_segment_count <> v_expected_segment_count THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: segment evidence row count (%) does not match expected product × score segment count (%).',
            v_segment_count,
            v_expected_segment_count;
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7G Executive evidence required-field completeness gatekeeper.

    Expected:
        Required executive evidence fields should be populated.

    Required field families:
        evidence capture metadata,
        registry linkage,
        strategy identity,
        Module 1 lineage,
        application count,
        decision rates,
        simulated offer-exposure rate,
        approved amount,
        approved Expected Loss,
        top primary simulated reason code,
        validation status counts,
        and Module 3 boundary fields.

    Registry patch:
        module1_run_id, module2_run_id, and run_registry_match_status are required because the
        executive evidence row should always identify how it links back to the campaign roadmap.

        When campaign_registry_required_flag = TRUE, run_registry_match_status must already be
        RUN_REGISTRY_MATCHED due to Section 16.0.

    SQL mechanics:
        COUNT(*) counts whether the one executive evidence row has any required-field gap.

        Because Section 16.7 already confirmed exactly one executive row exists, any count greater
        than zero means that one row is incomplete.

    Interpretation:
        This check protects against using a half-populated executive evidence row in documentation.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_null_required_summary_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e
    WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = k.population_id
      AND (
             e.evidence_snapshot_ts IS NULL

          OR e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS NULL
          OR e.registry_match_count IS NULL
          OR e.run_registry_match_status IS NULL
          OR e.module1_run_id IS NULL
          OR e.module2_run_id IS NULL
          OR e.showcase_name IS NULL

          OR (
                e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS TRUE
            AND (
                    e.run_registry_match_status <> 'RUN_REGISTRY_MATCHED'
                 OR e.run_sequence_number IS NULL
                 OR e.showcase_id IS NULL
                 OR e.validation_evidence_group_id IS NULL
                )
             )

          OR e.strategy_set_name IS NULL
          OR e.strategy_name IS NULL
          OR e.strategy_version IS NULL
          OR e.module1_scenario_set_name IS NULL
          OR e.module1_scenario_name IS NULL
          OR e.population_id IS NULL

          OR e.applications IS NULL
          OR e.approval_rate IS NULL
          OR e.counteroffer_rate IS NULL
          OR e.manual_review_rate IS NULL
          OR e.decline_rate IS NULL
          OR e.simulated_offer_exposure_rate IS NULL

          OR e.total_approved_amount IS NULL
          OR e.total_approved_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
          OR e.top_primary_reason_code IS NULL

          OR e.validation_pass_count IS NULL
          OR e.validation_review_count IS NULL
          OR e.validation_not_applicable_count IS NULL
          OR e.validation_status_summary_jsonb IS NULL

          OR e.module3_revenue_model_required_flag IS NULL
          OR e.module3_boundary_note IS NULL
      );

    IF v_null_required_summary_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: executive evidence summary has null or invalid required evidence fields.';
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7H Registry-linkage completeness gatekeeper for validation evidence.

    Expected:
        Every persisted validation evidence row for the current run should carry the run ID and
        registry match status fields.

    Why this matters:
        Validation Summary artifacts should be traceable to individual validation evidence rows using
        module2_run_id and validation_evidence_group_id.

    SQL mechanics:
        COUNT(*) identifies validation evidence rows for the current key with missing registry-linkage
        values.

        The formal-campaign branch requires matched registry fields only when
        campaign_registry_required_flag = TRUE.

    Governance interpretation:
        This protects the validation evidence detail layer from becoming disconnected from the
        campaign roadmap.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_validation_registry_gap_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence e
    WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = k.population_id
      AND (
             e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS NULL
          OR e.registry_match_count IS NULL
          OR e.run_registry_match_status IS NULL
          OR e.module1_run_id IS NULL
          OR e.module2_run_id IS NULL
          OR e.showcase_name IS NULL
          OR (
                e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS TRUE
            AND (
                    e.run_registry_match_status <> 'RUN_REGISTRY_MATCHED'
                 OR e.run_sequence_number IS NULL
                 OR e.showcase_id IS NULL
                 OR e.validation_evidence_group_id IS NULL
                )
             )
      );

    IF v_validation_registry_gap_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: % validation evidence row(s) are missing required registry-linkage fields.',
            v_validation_registry_gap_count;
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7I Registry-linkage completeness gatekeeper for parameter snapshot.

    Expected:
        The parameter snapshot row should carry the same registry linkage used by the executive
        evidence row.

    Why this matters:
        Parameter evidence should be traceable to the same run ID and validation evidence group as
        the executive evidence and validation detail rows.

    SQL mechanics:
        The check is scoped to the current run key and requires:
            campaign registry required flag,
            registry match count,
            registry match status,
            module1_run_id,
            module2_run_id,
            showcase_name,
            and, for formal campaigns, formal registry IDs.

    Governance interpretation:
        This ensures that the captured parameter payload can be tied back to the same campaign run
        that produced the executive and validation evidence.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_parameter_registry_gap_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot e
    WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = k.population_id
      AND (
             e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS NULL
          OR e.registry_match_count IS NULL
          OR e.run_registry_match_status IS NULL
          OR e.module1_run_id IS NULL
          OR e.module2_run_id IS NULL
          OR e.showcase_name IS NULL
          OR (
                e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS TRUE
            AND (
                    e.run_registry_match_status <> 'RUN_REGISTRY_MATCHED'
                 OR e.run_sequence_number IS NULL
                 OR e.showcase_id IS NULL
                 OR e.validation_evidence_group_id IS NULL
                )
             )
      );

    IF v_parameter_registry_gap_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: parameter snapshot row is missing required registry-linkage fields.';
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7J Registry-linkage completeness gatekeeper for product × score segment evidence.

    Expected:
        Every product × score segment evidence row should carry the same registry linkage used by the
        executive evidence row.

    Why this matters:
        Segment evidence should be directly usable in the Validation Summary or README without
        manual reconstruction of run IDs.

    SQL mechanics:
        COUNT(*) identifies segment evidence rows with missing registry-linkage values.

        Formal registry fields are required only when campaign_registry_required_flag = TRUE.

    Credit risk interpretation:
        Product × score evidence often explains where the portfolio strategy story is concentrated.
        The registry link ensures those segment claims can be tied to the same completed campaign run.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_segment_registry_gap_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary e
    WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = k.population_id
      AND (
             e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS NULL
          OR e.registry_match_count IS NULL
          OR e.run_registry_match_status IS NULL
          OR e.module1_run_id IS NULL
          OR e.module2_run_id IS NULL
          OR e.showcase_name IS NULL
          OR (
                e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS TRUE
            AND (
                    e.run_registry_match_status <> 'RUN_REGISTRY_MATCHED'
                 OR e.run_sequence_number IS NULL
                 OR e.showcase_id IS NULL
                 OR e.validation_evidence_group_id IS NULL
                )
             )
      );

    IF v_segment_registry_gap_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: % product × score segment evidence row(s) are missing required registry-linkage fields.',
            v_segment_registry_gap_count;
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7K Parameter snapshot payload gatekeeper.

    Expected:
        strategy_params_jsonb, product_policy_params_jsonb, run_story_params_jsonb, and
        parameter_snapshot_hash should all be populated.

    Why this matters:
        The parameter snapshot is the evidence trail from observed strategy outcomes back to active
        strategy parameters, product-policy settings, and registry / story metadata.

    SQL mechanics:
        This check counts the current parameter snapshot row if any required JSONB payload or the
        hash is NULL.

    Interpretation:
        If this gate fails, the run may have an executive result but lacks a complete configuration
        evidence trail.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_parameter_payload_gap_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot e
    WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = k.population_id
      AND (
             e.strategy_params_jsonb IS NULL
          OR e.product_policy_params_jsonb IS NULL
          OR e.run_story_params_jsonb IS NULL
          OR e.parameter_snapshot_hash IS NULL
      );

    IF v_parameter_payload_gap_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: parameter snapshot is missing strategy, product-policy, story JSONB payload, or parameter hash.';
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7L Registry alignment gatekeeper across all evidence tables.

    Expected:
        Persistent evidence rows should align to the active current-run story metadata.

    Why this matters:
        Populated registry fields are not enough.

        They must also match the active current-run story metadata, or the evidence layer could
        connect a strategy result to the wrong roadmap / comparison / validation group.

    SQL mechanics:
        IS DISTINCT FROM performs NULL-safe comparison.

        UNION ALL stacks alignment violations across:
            executive evidence,
            validation evidence,
            parameter snapshot,
            segment evidence.

        SELECT COUNT(*) over the UNION ALL result converts all detected violations into one
        diagnostic count.

    Interpretation:
        Any non-zero count means at least one evidence row has a registry-linkage value that differs
        from tmp_m2_current_run_story_params.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_registry_alignment_violation_count
    FROM (
        /*******************************************************************************************
        Executive summary alignment check.

        Expected:
            one executive evidence row, carrying registry values that match the active story row.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        SELECT 'EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY' AS evidence_table_name
        FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e
        WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
          AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
          AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
          AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
          AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
          AND e.population_id = k.population_id
          AND (
                 e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS DISTINCT FROM s.campaign_registry_required_flag
              OR e.registry_match_count IS DISTINCT FROM s.registry_match_count
              OR e.run_registry_match_status IS DISTINCT FROM s.run_registry_match_status
              OR e.module1_run_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.module1_run_id
              OR e.module2_run_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.module2_run_id
              OR e.run_sequence_number IS DISTINCT FROM s.run_sequence_number
              OR e.showcase_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.showcase_id
              OR e.showcase_name IS DISTINCT FROM s.showcase_name
              OR e.comparison_group_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.comparison_group_id
              OR e.validation_evidence_group_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.validation_evidence_group_id
              OR e.readme_storyline_label IS DISTINCT FROM s.readme_storyline_label
              OR e.linkedin_post_sequence IS DISTINCT FROM s.linkedin_post_sequence
              OR e.validation_summary_section_hint IS DISTINCT FROM s.validation_summary_section_hint
          )

        UNION ALL

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Validation evidence alignment check.

        Expected:
            every validation evidence detail row carries the same registry story metadata.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        SELECT 'VALIDATION_EVIDENCE' AS evidence_table_name
        FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence e
        WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
          AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
          AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
          AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
          AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
          AND e.population_id = k.population_id
          AND (
                 e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS DISTINCT FROM s.campaign_registry_required_flag
              OR e.registry_match_count IS DISTINCT FROM s.registry_match_count
              OR e.run_registry_match_status IS DISTINCT FROM s.run_registry_match_status
              OR e.module1_run_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.module1_run_id
              OR e.module2_run_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.module2_run_id
              OR e.run_sequence_number IS DISTINCT FROM s.run_sequence_number
              OR e.showcase_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.showcase_id
              OR e.showcase_name IS DISTINCT FROM s.showcase_name
              OR e.comparison_group_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.comparison_group_id
              OR e.validation_evidence_group_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.validation_evidence_group_id
              OR e.readme_storyline_label IS DISTINCT FROM s.readme_storyline_label
              OR e.linkedin_post_sequence IS DISTINCT FROM s.linkedin_post_sequence
              OR e.validation_summary_section_hint IS DISTINCT FROM s.validation_summary_section_hint
          )

        UNION ALL

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Parameter snapshot alignment check.

        Expected:
            the parameter payload is linked to the same registry story metadata as the executive and
            validation evidence.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        SELECT 'PARAMETER_SNAPSHOT' AS evidence_table_name
        FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot e
        WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
          AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
          AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
          AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
          AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
          AND e.population_id = k.population_id
          AND (
                 e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS DISTINCT FROM s.campaign_registry_required_flag
              OR e.registry_match_count IS DISTINCT FROM s.registry_match_count
              OR e.run_registry_match_status IS DISTINCT FROM s.run_registry_match_status
              OR e.module1_run_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.module1_run_id
              OR e.module2_run_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.module2_run_id
              OR e.run_sequence_number IS DISTINCT FROM s.run_sequence_number
              OR e.showcase_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.showcase_id
              OR e.showcase_name IS DISTINCT FROM s.showcase_name
              OR e.comparison_group_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.comparison_group_id
              OR e.validation_evidence_group_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.validation_evidence_group_id
              OR e.readme_storyline_label IS DISTINCT FROM s.readme_storyline_label
              OR e.linkedin_post_sequence IS DISTINCT FROM s.linkedin_post_sequence
              OR e.validation_summary_section_hint IS DISTINCT FROM s.validation_summary_section_hint
          )

        UNION ALL

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Segment evidence alignment check.

        Expected:
            every product × score segment row is linked to the same registry story metadata as the
            one-row executive evidence summary.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        SELECT 'SEGMENT_EVIDENCE' AS evidence_table_name
        FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary e
        WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
          AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
          AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
          AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
          AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
          AND e.population_id = k.population_id
          AND (
                 e.campaign_registry_required_flag IS DISTINCT FROM s.campaign_registry_required_flag
              OR e.registry_match_count IS DISTINCT FROM s.registry_match_count
              OR e.run_registry_match_status IS DISTINCT FROM s.run_registry_match_status
              OR e.module1_run_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.module1_run_id
              OR e.module2_run_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.module2_run_id
              OR e.run_sequence_number IS DISTINCT FROM s.run_sequence_number
              OR e.showcase_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.showcase_id
              OR e.showcase_name IS DISTINCT FROM s.showcase_name
              OR e.comparison_group_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.comparison_group_id
              OR e.validation_evidence_group_id IS DISTINCT FROM s.validation_evidence_group_id
              OR e.readme_storyline_label IS DISTINCT FROM s.readme_storyline_label
              OR e.linkedin_post_sequence IS DISTINCT FROM s.linkedin_post_sequence
              OR e.validation_summary_section_hint IS DISTINCT FROM s.validation_summary_section_hint
          )
    ) alignment_violations;

    IF v_registry_alignment_violation_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16 failure: % evidence row(s) have registry-linkage values that do not align to tmp_m2_current_run_story_params.',
            v_registry_alignment_violation_count;
    END IF;



    /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    16.7M Module 3 readiness gap diagnostic.

    Purpose:
        Count whether the executive evidence row indicates that Module 3 growth / economics inputs
        are not fully available.

    Important:
        This is intentionally NOT a failure condition.

    Why not fail:
        Module 3 economics is future scope.

        Section 16 is responsible for preserving readiness evidence and gap notes, not for forcing all
        future economics inputs to be complete today.

    SQL mechanics:
        IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE treats FALSE and NULL as readiness gaps.

    Interpretation:
        If v_module3_gap_count is greater than zero, the gap has already been recorded in the
        executive evidence row through:
            module3_growth_inputs_available_flag
            module3_growth_input_gap_note
            module3_revenue_model_required_flag
            module3_boundary_note

        The correct action is later Module 3 design review, not a Section 16 failure.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_module3_gap_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e
    WHERE e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = k.population_id
      AND e.module3_growth_inputs_available_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE;

    /*
    A Module 3 readiness gap does not fail Section 16 because Module 3 is future scope.

    The evidence row stores:
        module3_growth_inputs_available_flag
        module3_growth_input_gap_note
        module3_revenue_model_required_flag
        module3_boundary_note

    for later Module 3 design review.
    */
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 16.7 — LOCAL EVIDENCE CAPTURE GATEKEEPERS

If execution reaches this point:
    1. The current run key was loaded from tmp_m2_current_run_key.
    2. The current run registry / story metadata was loaded from tmp_m2_current_run_story_params.
    3. Exactly one executive evidence summary row exists for the current run key.
    4. Validation evidence detail rows exist for the current run key.
    5. Validation evidence row count matches tmp_m2_validation_status_summary.
    6. Exactly one parameter snapshot row exists for the current run key.
    7. Product × score segment evidence row count matches the latest-run product × score segment
       count.
    8. Required executive evidence fields are populated.
    9. Required registry-linkage fields are populated in validation evidence rows.
    10. Required registry-linkage fields are populated in the parameter snapshot.
    11. Required registry-linkage fields are populated in product × score segment evidence rows.
    12. Parameter snapshot JSONB payloads and parameter_snapshot_hash are populated.
    13. Registry-linkage values align back to tmp_m2_current_run_story_params across executive,
        validation, parameter, and segment evidence rows.
    14. Module 3 readiness gaps, if present, were recorded but did not fail Section 16.

No latest-run output rows have been modified.
No archive rows have been modified.
No evidence rows have been inserted, deleted, or updated in Section 16.7.
No campaign registry rows have been modified.
No strategy parameter rows have been modified.
No product policy parameter rows have been modified.
No decision outcomes have been recalculated.
No approved exposure values have been recalculated.
No approved Expected Loss values have been recalculated.
No simulated reason codes have been reassigned.
No Module 3 revenue, earnings, pricing, funding-cost, profitability, capital, or risk-adjusted margin
logic has been built.

Next section:
    Section 16.8 should display evidence capture diagnostics and export-ready views for current-run
    review.

***************************************************************************************************/



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.8 — EVIDENCE CAPTURE DIAGNOSTICS AND EXPORT-READY VIEWS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide compact, review-ready outputs after Section 16 evidence capture.

    Section 16.8 answers:

        "What evidence was captured for this current run, what registry IDs identify it, what should
         be reviewed before documentation, and what rows are ready for export or summary?"

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Show evidence row counts for the current run across all Section 16 evidence tables.
    2. Display the current run's one-row executive evidence summary.
    3. Display validation evidence rows with REVIEW or NOT_APPLICABLE status.
    4. Display product × score segment evidence for the current run.
    5. Display parameter snapshot capture flags and parameter snapshot hash.
    6. Display registry-linkage consistency diagnostics across evidence tables.

INPUTS:
    tmp_m2_current_run_key
    tmp_m2_current_run_story_params
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary

OUTPUTS:
    Review result sets only.

WHEN TO RUN THIS SECTION:
    Run Section 16.8 after Section 16.7 has completed successfully.

    Section 16.7 is the local evidence-capture gatekeeper.

    Section 16.8 is the evidence-review and export-readiness display layer.

WHY THIS SECTION EXISTS:
    Section 16.3 through Section 16.6 persist evidence.

    Section 16.7 confirms that the evidence was captured correctly.

    Section 16.8 then displays the captured evidence in review-ready form so the user does not have
    to manually query four different evidence tables after every campaign run.

    This section is especially useful during a multi-run campaign because it gives a consistent
    post-run evidence package for:
        run tracking,
        validation-summary drafting,
        README result summaries,
        LinkedIn storyline preparation,
        executive review,
        and future Module 3 planning.

REGISTRY PATCH:
    Section 16.8 surfaces campaign registry fields in the review outputs:

        module1_run_id
        module2_run_id
        run_sequence_number
        showcase_id
        showcase_name
        comparison_group_id
        validation_evidence_group_id
        readme_storyline_label
        linkedin_post_sequence
        validation_summary_section_hint
        run_registry_match_status

    These fields connect the SQL evidence layer to the formal campaign roadmap.

    They allow the same completed run to be referenced consistently across:
        the SQL output,
        Section 13 comparison,
        Section 14 validation evidence,
        Section 15 frontier evidence,
        Section 16 persistent evidence,
        the future written Validation Summary,
        README documentation,
        LinkedIn campaign posts,
        and executive-facing summaries.

HOW TO USE AFTER EACH MODULE 2 RUN:
    1. Review Section 16.8A to confirm each evidence table has current-run rows.
    2. Review Section 16.8B as the main executive evidence row.
    3. Review Section 16.8C to identify validation items requiring interpretation.
    4. Review Section 16.8D for product × score segment drivers.
    5. Review Section 16.8E to confirm parameter snapshots were captured.
    6. Review Section 16.8F to confirm registry linkage is consistent across evidence tables.

DOCUMENTATION ROLE:
    Section 16.8 outputs are the immediate post-run evidence review package.

    These outputs support:
        validation-summary notes,
        README result summaries,
        LinkedIn storyline preparation,
        campaign-run tracking,
        comparison group review,
        executive strategy review,
        product × score segment explanation,
        and future Module 3 economics planning.

CREDIT RISK INTERPRETATION:
    Section 16.8 helps reviewers interpret the completed strategy run across the main credit strategy
    dimensions:

        Access:
            simulated_offer_exposure_rate, approval_rate, counteroffer_rate.

        Exposure:
            total_requested_amount, total_approved_amount, approved_amount_capture_rate.

        Risk:
            synthetic estimated-PD proxy, LGD, requested Expected Loss, approved Expected Loss.

        Affordability:
            requested PTI and approved PTI evidence.

        Treatment:
            APPROVE, COUNTEROFFER, MANUAL_REVIEW, and DECLINE outcome rates.

        Explainability:
            top reason codes, non-approval reason codes, policy-stop reason codes, and reason-code
            movement versus baseline.

        Segmentation:
            product, score-band, and product × score evidence.

        Validation:
            PASS, REVIEW, and NOT_APPLICABLE evidence from Section 14.

        Future economics:
            APR proxy, term, product mix, approved exposure, and approved Expected Loss readiness
            fields for future Module 3 design.

WHAT TO LOOK FOR:
    Section 16.8A:
        Confirms the four evidence tables contain current-run evidence rows.

    Section 16.8B:
        Main executive evidence row for the completed run.

    Section 16.8C:
        REVIEW and NOT_APPLICABLE validation items that should be interpreted before documentation.

    Section 16.8D:
        Product × score segment evidence, especially high approved Expected Loss segments.

    Section 16.8E:
        Parameter snapshot capture flags and parameter_snapshot_hash.

    Section 16.8F:
        Registry-linkage consistency across evidence tables.

REVIEW TRIGGERS:
    Missing evidence rows:
        Review Sections 16.3 through 16.6 and Section 16.7 gatekeeper output.

    REVIEW validation rows:
        Interpret before writing the Validation Summary, README, or executive narrative.

    NOT_APPLICABLE validation rows:
        Confirm whether the test depended on unavailable comparison setup, unavailable archive slices,
        or non-ready matched comparison context.

    High approved Expected Loss segment:
        Review product, score band, LGD, approved amount, synthetic estimated-risk proxy, and
        reason-code fields.

    Registry linkage review status:
        Confirm that the persistent evidence tables are tied to the intended campaign run IDs.

INTERPRETATION BOUNDARIES:
    REVIEW validation rows are documentation prompts, not automatic invalidation.

    NOT_APPLICABLE validation rows show tests that were not evaluable in the current run context.

    simulated_offer_exposure_rate is simulated positive offer exposure, not booked or funded exposure.

    approved_amount is simulated approved exposure, not booked exposure, funded exposure, account
    creation, or production approval.

    approved_expected_loss_rate is a synthetic strategy evidence metric, not a production loss-rate
    forecast.

    estimated_pd remains the SQL field name and is interpreted as the synthetic estimated-PD proxy.

    Reason-code fields are simulated strategy explanation codes only.

    They are not customer communications, regulatory notices, adverse-action reasons, fair-lending
    conclusions, or production compliance determinations.

    Module 3 readiness fields are readiness indicators only, not revenue or profitability results.

READ-ONLY BOUNDARY:
    Section 16.8 does not insert evidence rows.
    Section 16.8 does not delete evidence rows.
    Section 16.8 does not update evidence rows.
    Section 16.8 does not modify latest-run output.
    Section 16.8 does not modify archive rows.
    Section 16.8 does not modify campaign registry rows.
    Section 16.8 does not modify strategy parameters.
    Section 16.8 does not modify product policy parameters.
    Section 16.8 does not recalculate decisions.
    Section 16.8 does not recalculate approved exposure.
    Section 16.8 does not recalculate approved Expected Loss.
    Section 16.8 does not reassign simulated reason codes.
    Section 16.8 does not implement Module 3 revenue, earnings, pricing, funding-cost, profitability,
    capital, or risk-adjusted margin logic.

SQL CONCEPTS TAUGHT IN THIS SECTION:
    CTE:
        Creates one-row current-run context helpers before each review query.

    JOIN to tmp_m2_current_run_key:
        Scopes persistent evidence tables to the current run key so historical campaign evidence does
        not mix into the current review output.

    CROSS JOIN:
        Attaches the one active story / registry row to object-level diagnostic rows.

    UNION ALL:
        Stacks row-count diagnostics and registry-linkage diagnostics across multiple evidence
        tables.

    COUNT(*):
        Counts evidence rows captured for the current run.

    COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(...)):
        Detects whether registry identity is consistent inside each evidence object.

    FILTER:
        Counts missing critical registry-linkage fields inside each evidence object.

    CASE:
        Converts registry diagnostic counts into readable status labels.

***************************************************************************************************/



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.8A — EVIDENCE OBJECT ROW-COUNT DIAGNOSTIC FOR CURRENT RUN
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Confirm that the current run has persisted evidence rows in each Section 16 evidence table.

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide a compact "did evidence capture land?" diagnostic after Section 16.7 has passed.

EXPECTED INTERPRETATION:
    strategy_run_evidence_summary:
        exactly one row.

    strategy_run_validation_evidence:
        one row per Section 14 validation status summary row.

    strategy_run_parameter_snapshot:
        exactly one row.

    strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary:
        one row per product × score segment present in the latest-run output.

REGISTRY PATCH:
    The diagnostic includes the current run IDs and registry status so evidence object row counts can
    be tied directly to campaign tracking.

WHAT TO LOOK FOR:
    current_run_evidence_rows:
        Confirms how many rows were captured in each evidence object for the current run key.

    module2_run_id:
        Confirms which formal Module 2 campaign run the evidence belongs to.

    validation_evidence_group_id:
        Confirms which future Validation Summary evidence group can reference the output.

REVIEW TRIGGERS:
    strategy_run_evidence_summary <> 1:
        Executive evidence is missing or duplicated.

    strategy_run_parameter_snapshot <> 1:
        Parameter traceability is missing or duplicated.

    strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary = 0:
        Product × score companion evidence was not captured.

    Missing module2_run_id:
        Registry linkage should be reviewed before documentation.

SQL MECHANICS:
    k:
        Loads the current technical run key.

    story:
        Loads the active current-run registry / story metadata row.

    evidence_counts:
        Uses scalar COUNT(*) subqueries so each evidence object is displayed even if a count is zero.

    CROSS JOIN:
        Attaches registry / story fields to each evidence object count.

BOUNDARY:
    This query displays counts only.

    Local gatekeepers in Section 16.7 already enforce critical count expectations.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH k AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Current run key.

    This CTE scopes all evidence counts to the latest completed strategy / Module 1 scenario /
    population slice.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_key
    LIMIT 1
),

story AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Current run registry / story metadata.

    This CTE supplies the formal run IDs and documentation linkage fields shown with the row-count
    diagnostic.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_story_params
    WHERE active_story_flag IS TRUE
    LIMIT 1
),

evidence_counts AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Evidence object counts.

    SQL mechanics:
        Each SELECT returns one row for one persistent evidence object.

        Scalar subqueries count rows for the current technical run key.

    Why this pattern is used:
        It keeps the diagnostic compact and makes missing or zero-row evidence objects visible.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        'strategy_run_evidence_summary' AS evidence_object_name,

        (
            SELECT COUNT(*)
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e
            JOIN k
                ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
               AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
               AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
               AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
               AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
               AND e.population_id = k.population_id
        ) AS current_run_evidence_rows

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        'strategy_run_validation_evidence' AS evidence_object_name,

        (
            SELECT COUNT(*)
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence e
            JOIN k
                ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
               AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
               AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
               AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
               AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
               AND e.population_id = k.population_id
        ) AS current_run_evidence_rows

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        'strategy_run_parameter_snapshot' AS evidence_object_name,

        (
            SELECT COUNT(*)
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot e
            JOIN k
                ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
               AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
               AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
               AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
               AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
               AND e.population_id = k.population_id
        ) AS current_run_evidence_rows

    UNION ALL

    SELECT
        'strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary' AS evidence_object_name,

        (
            SELECT COUNT(*)
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary e
            JOIN k
                ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
               AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
               AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
               AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
               AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
               AND e.population_id = k.population_id
        ) AS current_run_evidence_rows
)

SELECT
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Campaign registry / run-story identity.

    These fields make the row-count diagnostic immediately traceable to the campaign roadmap.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    story.module1_run_id,
    story.module2_run_id,
    story.run_sequence_number,
    story.showcase_id,
    story.showcase_name,
    story.comparison_group_id,
    story.validation_evidence_group_id,
    story.run_registry_match_status,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Evidence object row count.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    c.evidence_object_name,
    c.current_run_evidence_rows

FROM evidence_counts c

CROSS JOIN story

ORDER BY c.evidence_object_name;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.8B — CURRENT RUN EXECUTIVE EVIDENCE SUMMARY ROW
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Display the primary one-row executive evidence record for the current run.

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide the compact current-run story row that can be exported, summarized, or referenced after
    evidence capture.

WHY THIS QUERY IS SCOPED TO tmp_m2_current_run_key:
    The evidence summary table persists rows across the full campaign.

    Filtering to the current run key prevents this diagnostic from accidentally showing a different
    run if historical or later evidence rows also exist.

REGISTRY PATCH:
    The first fields displayed are the registry and campaign linkage fields.

    These fields should be used to tie the SQL evidence row to:
        the run roadmap,
        comparison group,
        validation evidence group,
        README storyline,
        LinkedIn post sequence,
        and Validation Summary section.

HOW TO USE:
    This is the main post-run evidence row to export or summarize.

REVIEW FOCUS:
    registry identity,
    scenario identity,
    strategy identity,
    outcome rates,
    simulated offer exposure,
    approved amount,
    approved Expected Loss,
    top reason-code fields,
    frontier posture,
    product / score / segment drivers,
    validation counts,
    and Module 3 readiness notes.

CREDIT RISK INTERPRETATION:
    This output gives the run-level story across:
        access,
        exposure,
        risk,
        affordability,
        treatment,
        explainability,
        validation,
        and future economics readiness.

SQL MECHANICS:
    k:
        Loads the current technical run key.

    JOIN:
        Filters the persistent evidence table to the current run key.

    ORDER BY evidence_snapshot_ts DESC LIMIT 1:
        Displays the most recent evidence row for the current run key.

        Section 16.7 should already have confirmed exactly one row for the key, but this ordering
        keeps the display deterministic if a development artifact ever left multiple rows behind.

BOUNDARY:
    This query reads persisted executive evidence only.

    It does not recalculate portfolio metrics or frontier fields.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH k AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Current run key.

    This CTE scopes the persistent executive evidence table to the completed latest-run slice.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_key
    LIMIT 1
)

SELECT
    e.evidence_snapshot_ts,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Campaign registry / run-story identity.

    These fields provide the bridge from SQL evidence to the formal run roadmap and later
    documentation artifacts.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.campaign_registry_required_flag,
    e.registry_match_count,
    e.run_registry_match_status,

    e.module1_run_id,
    e.module2_run_id,
    e.run_sequence_number,

    e.showcase_id,
    e.showcase_name,
    e.comparison_group_id,
    e.validation_evidence_group_id,

    e.readme_storyline_label,
    e.linkedin_post_sequence,
    e.validation_summary_section_hint,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Module 1 scenario / population lineage.

    These fields identify the upstream synthetic scenario and population.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.module1_scenario_set_name,
    e.module1_scenario_name,
    e.population_id,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Module 2 strategy identity.

    These fields identify the downstream strategy applied to the Module 1 population.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.strategy_set_name,
    e.strategy_name,
    e.strategy_version,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Story-family labels.

    These fields help reviewers connect parameter changes to the expected and observed run narrative.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.module1_parameter_family_changed,
    e.module2_strategy_family_changed,

    e.expected_storyline,
    e.observed_storyline,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Portfolio size.

    applications should reflect the current latest-run population size.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.applications,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Final decision outcome rates.

    These are run-level final strategy outcome rates.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.approval_rate,
    e.counteroffer_rate,
    e.manual_review_rate,
    e.decline_rate,
    e.simulated_offer_exposure_rate,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Requested and approved exposure.

    approved_amount_capture_rate shows how much requested exposure survived final simulated strategy
    treatment.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.total_requested_amount,
    e.total_approved_amount,
    e.approved_amount_capture_rate,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Offer-row risk and affordability profile.

    These fields focus on rows with simulated positive offer exposure.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows,
    e.avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_offer_rows,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Requested and approved Expected Loss.

    approved_expected_loss_rate is a synthetic strategy evidence metric.

    It is not a production loss-rate forecast.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.total_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    e.total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    e.approved_expected_loss_rate,
    e.approved_amount_per_approved_expected_loss_dollar,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Simulated reason-code story fields.

    These fields explain what most commonly drove the strategy outcomes.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.top_primary_reason_code,
    e.top_primary_reason_population_share,

    e.top_non_approval_primary_reason_code,
    e.top_non_approval_reason_population_share,

    e.top_policy_stop_primary_reason_code,
    e.top_policy_stop_reason_population_share,

    e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code,
    e.top_reason_code_delta_population_share,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Strategy frontier posture.

    These fields come from Section 15 and should be interpreted as diagnostic story labels, not
    production recommendations.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.frontier_position_type,
    e.executive_frontier_quadrant,
    e.frontier_interpretation_note,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Product / score / product × score driver fields.

    These fields identify where the run-level result concentrated.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.top_approved_amount_product,
    e.top_approved_expected_loss_product,

    e.top_approved_amount_score_band,
    e.top_approved_expected_loss_score_band,

    e.top_approved_el_product_score_segment,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Baseline-relative movement drivers.

    These fields may be NULL for baseline runs or when no matching baseline exists.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.largest_delta_approved_amount_product,
    e.largest_delta_approved_el_product,
    e.largest_delta_offer_rate_score_band,
    e.largest_delta_decline_rate_score_band,
    e.largest_delta_approved_el_product_score_segment,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Validation rollup.

    REVIEW and NOT_APPLICABLE items should be interpreted before documentation.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.validation_pass_count,
    e.validation_review_count,
    e.validation_not_applicable_count,
    e.validation_review_items,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Module 3 readiness boundary fields.

    These are readiness indicators only.

    They are not profitability or revenue metrics.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.module3_growth_inputs_available_flag,
    e.module3_growth_input_gap_note,
    e.module3_boundary_note

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e

JOIN k
    ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
   AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
   AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
   AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
   AND e.population_id = k.population_id

ORDER BY e.evidence_snapshot_ts DESC

LIMIT 1;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.8C — CURRENT RUN VALIDATION ITEMS REQUIRING INTERPRETATION
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Display validation evidence rows with REVIEW or NOT_APPLICABLE status for the current run.

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Identify the exact validation evidence rows that should be discussed before documentation.

VALIDATION STATUS INTERPRETATION:
    REVIEW:
        The pattern should be interpreted before documentation.

        REVIEW does not automatically mean the strategy run is invalid.

    NOT_APPLICABLE:
        The test depended on unavailable comparison setup, unavailable archive slices, or conditions
        not present in the current run context.

IMPORTANT:
    REVIEW and NOT_APPLICABLE are not automatic failures.

    They are prompts for validation narrative, evidence review, and documentation discipline.

REGISTRY PATCH:
    Validation rows include module2_run_id and validation_evidence_group_id so each item can be
    carried directly into the future Validation Summary.

WHAT TO LOOK FOR:
    validation_area:
        The broad area of the validation framework.

    validation_test_name:
        The specific check or diagnostic.

    observed_value:
        The evidence value captured from Section 14.

    expected_behavior:
        The intended interpretation boundary or expectation.

    interpretation:
        Plain-English guidance for reviewers.

REVIEW TRIGGERS:
    High manual-review rate:
        Explain operational burden and failed-counteroffer resolution behavior.

    High counteroffer concentration:
        Explain reduced-exposure treatment and product / affordability drivers.

    High reason-code concentration:
        Explain whether the concentration is expected for the selected strategy.

    Comparison not ready:
        Explain missing baseline / challenger readiness before writing comparison claims.

SQL MECHANICS:
    JOIN to k:
        Restricts persistent validation evidence to the current run key.

    WHERE validation_status IN (...):
        Shows only the rows requiring interpretation or context.

    ORDER BY:
        Places REVIEW rows before NOT_APPLICABLE rows.

BOUNDARY:
    This query reads persisted validation evidence only.

    It does not rerun Section 14 validation logic.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH k AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Current run key.

    Used to scope the persistent validation evidence table to the current completed run.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_key
    LIMIT 1
)

SELECT
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Campaign registry / validation evidence linkage.

    These fields let each validation row be tied directly to the formal campaign run and Validation
    Summary evidence group.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.module1_run_id,
    e.module2_run_id,
    e.run_sequence_number,
    e.showcase_id,
    e.showcase_name,
    e.comparison_group_id,
    e.validation_evidence_group_id,
    e.validation_summary_section_hint,
    e.run_registry_match_status,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Validation evidence detail.

    These are the fields most directly reusable in a future written Validation Summary.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.validation_area,
    e.validation_test_name,
    e.validation_category,
    e.validation_status,
    e.observed_value,
    e.expected_behavior,
    e.interpretation

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence e

JOIN k
    ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
   AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
   AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
   AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
   AND e.population_id = k.population_id

WHERE e.validation_status IN ('REVIEW', 'NOT_APPLICABLE')

ORDER BY
    CASE e.validation_status
        WHEN 'REVIEW' THEN 1
        WHEN 'NOT_APPLICABLE' THEN 2
        ELSE 99
    END,
    e.validation_area,
    e.validation_test_name;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.8D — CURRENT RUN PRODUCT × SCORE SEGMENT EVIDENCE
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Display the product × score companion evidence rows captured in Section 16.5.

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide the segment-level drill-down behind the one-row executive evidence summary.

    Section 16.8D answers:

        "Which product × score segments drove approved exposure, approved Expected Loss, offer
         exposure, counteroffer behavior, no-offer behavior, and reason-code concentration?"

WHY PRODUCT × SCORE MATTERS:
    Portfolio-level averages can hide concentration.

    Product type shapes:
        exposure size,
        payment mechanics,
        LGD,
        counteroffer feasibility,
        product caps,
        and approved Expected Loss.

    Score band shapes:
        borrower-quality segmentation,
        synthetic estimated-risk proxy,
        offer-exposure rate,
        policy-stop behavior,
        and no-offer concentration.

    Product × score intersections often explain the true strategy story.

REVIEW FOCUS:
    registry IDs,
    product × score segment,
    applications,
    final decision rates,
    simulated offer-exposure rate,
    total approved amount,
    total approved Expected Loss,
    approved Expected Loss rate,
    APR proxy,
    term,
    offered-population synthetic estimated-risk proxy,
    offered-population approved PTI,
    and segment reason-code fields.

ORDERING:
    Segments are sorted by total approved Expected Loss descending because the highest approved
    Expected Loss segments are typically most important for risk / exposure storytelling.

WHAT TO LOOK FOR:
    High total_approved_expected_loss_amount:
        Segment contributes materially to approved-exposure Expected Loss.

    High approved_expected_loss_rate:
        Segment has high approved Expected Loss per approved exposure dollar.

    High simulated_offer_exposure_rate in weaker score bands:
        Review risk posture and approved Expected Loss.

    High counteroffer or decline rates:
        Review product caps, affordability, approved Expected Loss caps, and reason codes.

MODULE 3 READINESS:
    Segment-level APR proxy and term fields are preserved because future economics assumptions will
    likely vary by product and borrower-quality segment.

    These fields are not revenue or profitability metrics.

BOUNDARY:
    Segment evidence is persistent evidence, not a new decision model.

    It does not imply production segmentation or customer treatment.

SQL MECHANICS:
    JOIN to k:
        Restricts segment evidence to the current run key.

    ORDER BY total_approved_expected_loss_amount DESC:
        Prioritizes the risk-impact segment review.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH k AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Current run key.

    Used to scope the persistent segment evidence table to the current completed run.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_key
    LIMIT 1
)

SELECT
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Campaign registry / segment evidence linkage.

    These fields make every segment row traceable to the formal run and evidence group.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.module1_run_id,
    e.module2_run_id,
    e.showcase_id,
    e.showcase_name,
    e.comparison_group_id,
    e.validation_evidence_group_id,
    e.run_registry_match_status,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Segment identity.

    Product × score is the primary segment drill-down layer for explaining concentration.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.product_type_policy_key,
    e.score_band_policy_key,
    e.product_score_policy_segment,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Segment population and outcome rates.

    These fields show access, counteroffer, review, and no-offer behavior within the segment.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.applications,

    e.approval_rate,
    e.counteroffer_rate,
    e.manual_review_rate,
    e.decline_rate,
    e.simulated_offer_exposure_rate,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Segment exposure and approved Expected Loss.

    These fields identify the exposure and risk contribution of each segment.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.total_approved_amount,
    e.total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    e.approved_expected_loss_rate,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Module 3 readiness inputs by segment.

    These fields are basis inputs only.

    They are not revenue, pricing, yield, profitability, or margin outputs.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.approved_amount_weighted_apr_proxy,
    e.approved_amount_weighted_term_months,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Segment risk and affordability.

    These fields describe offered-population synthetic risk and approved affordability pressure.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows,
    e.avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_offer_rows,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Segment simulated reason-code story.

    These fields help explain why the segment behaved as it did.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.top_primary_reason_code,
    e.top_primary_reason_population_share,
    e.top_non_approval_primary_reason_code,
    e.top_non_approval_reason_population_share

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary e

JOIN k
    ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
   AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
   AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
   AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
   AND e.population_id = k.population_id

ORDER BY
    e.total_approved_expected_loss_amount DESC NULLS LAST,
    e.product_type_policy_key,
    e.score_band_policy_key;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.8E — PARAMETER SNAPSHOT DIAGNOSTIC
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Confirm that the temporary active parameter tables and current-run story metadata were captured
    into persistent evidence.

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    A completed run should be traceable not only to results, but also to the exact strategy and
    product-policy configuration that produced those results.

    Section 16.8E answers:

        "Was the parameter evidence payload captured, and what fingerprint identifies the captured
         strategy / product-policy / story payload?"

WHY PARAMETER SNAPSHOT MATTERS:
    The temporary parameter tables are execution artifacts.

    They can change in later runs.

    The persistent parameter snapshot preserves:
        the active Module 2 strategy parameter card,
        the product-policy parameter card,
        current-run story metadata,
        registry linkage,
        and a compact hash fingerprint.

REGISTRY PATCH:
    The parameter snapshot displays:
        module1_run_id,
        module2_run_id,
        showcase_id,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,
        and run_registry_match_status.

REVIEW FOCUS:
    parameter_snapshot_hash,
    strategy_params_captured_flag,
    product_policy_params_captured_flag,
    run_story_params_captured_flag.

WHAT TO LOOK FOR:
    strategy_params_captured_flag = TRUE:
        Active strategy parameter card was captured.

    product_policy_params_captured_flag = TRUE:
        Product policy parameter card was captured.

    run_story_params_captured_flag = TRUE:
        Current run registry / story metadata was captured.

    parameter_snapshot_hash:
        Compact fingerprint for comparing parameter payloads across evidence rows.

BOUNDARY:
    parameter_snapshot_hash is a compact fingerprint.

    The full JSONB payload remains the authoritative parameter evidence.

SQL MECHANICS:
    IS NOT NULL:
        Converts JSONB payload presence into readable TRUE / FALSE capture flags.

    JOIN to k:
        Restricts parameter snapshot evidence to the current run key.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH k AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Current run key.

    Used to scope the persistent parameter snapshot table to the current completed run.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_key
    LIMIT 1
)

SELECT
    e.evidence_snapshot_ts,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Campaign registry / parameter evidence linkage.

    These fields connect the captured parameter payload to the formal campaign run.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.campaign_registry_required_flag,
    e.registry_match_count,
    e.run_registry_match_status,

    e.module1_run_id,
    e.module2_run_id,
    e.run_sequence_number,

    e.showcase_id,
    e.showcase_name,
    e.comparison_group_id,
    e.validation_evidence_group_id,

    e.readme_storyline_label,
    e.linkedin_post_sequence,
    e.validation_summary_section_hint,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Technical run key.

    These fields preserve the SQL evidence grain alongside the registry metadata.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.strategy_set_name,
    e.strategy_name,
    e.strategy_version,

    e.module1_scenario_set_name,
    e.module1_scenario_name,
    e.population_id,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Parameter snapshot fingerprint and payload flags.

    TRUE values indicate that the JSONB payload was captured.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    e.parameter_snapshot_hash,

    e.strategy_params_jsonb IS NOT NULL AS strategy_params_captured_flag,
    e.product_policy_params_jsonb IS NOT NULL AS product_policy_params_captured_flag,
    e.run_story_params_jsonb IS NOT NULL AS run_story_params_captured_flag

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot e

JOIN k
    ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
   AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
   AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
   AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
   AND e.population_id = k.population_id;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.8F — REGISTRY-LINKAGE CONSISTENCY DIAGNOSTIC ACROSS EVIDENCE TABLES
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Provide a compact post-capture view showing whether each persistent evidence table carries a
    single, consistent registry identity for the current run.

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that the evidence layer does not require manual reconstruction of run IDs.

    Section 16.8F answers:

        "Do the executive, validation, parameter, and segment evidence tables all carry one coherent
         campaign identity for the current run?"

WHY THIS MATTERS:
    Evidence tables are useful for documentation only if they can be tied back to the same completed
    campaign run.

    A mismatch in module2_run_id, registry status, validation_evidence_group_id, or showcase fields
    could cause a future Validation Summary or README note to reference the wrong run.

EXPECTED EVIDENCE OBJECT BEHAVIOR:
    Each evidence object should show:
        at least one current-run row,
        one module2_run_id,
        one registry match status,
        one validation evidence group identity when formal registry evidence is present,
        and zero missing critical registry ID rows.

STATUS LOGIC:
    REGISTRY_LINKAGE_CAPTURED:
        Evidence object has at least one current-run row, one distinct module2_run_id, one distinct
        run_registry_match_status, and no missing critical run ID fields.

    REGISTRY_LINKAGE_REVIEW_REQUIRED:
        Evidence object is missing rows, has multiple registry identities, or has missing critical
        registry fields.

FORMAL CAMPAIGN NOTE:
    Section 16.7 already enforces stronger formal-campaign rules when
    campaign_registry_required_flag = TRUE.

    Section 16.8F is a compact display diagnostic for review and export.

AD HOC DEVELOPMENT NOTE:
    If registry fallback is allowed, validation_evidence_group_id may be NULL.

    In that case, review run_registry_match_status so the output is not mistaken for a formal
    registry-matched campaign run.

SQL MECHANICS:
    registry_profile:
        Uses UNION ALL to stack one registry profile row per evidence table.

    COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(...)):
        Detects whether each evidence object carries one unique value or multiple values.

    COUNT(*) FILTER:
        Counts rows with missing critical registry fields.

    MIN(...):
        Displays representative registry values after consistency counts confirm uniqueness.

    CASE:
        Converts profile counts into a readable registry_linkage_status.

BOUNDARY:
    This query reads evidence tables only.

    It does not modify evidence, archive, latest-run output, or registry rows.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH k AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Current run key.

    Used to scope all evidence-table registry profiles to the current completed run.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT *
    FROM tmp_m2_current_run_key
    LIMIT 1
),

registry_profile AS (
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Registry profile for the executive evidence summary.

    Expected:
        One current-run row and one coherent registry identity.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        'strategy_run_evidence_summary' AS evidence_object_name,

        COUNT(*) AS current_run_evidence_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(module2_run_id, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_module2_run_id_count,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(run_registry_match_status, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_registry_match_status_count,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(validation_evidence_group_id, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_validation_evidence_group_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE module1_run_id IS NULL
               OR module2_run_id IS NULL
               OR run_registry_match_status IS NULL
        ) AS missing_critical_registry_field_rows,

        MIN(module1_run_id) AS module1_run_id,
        MIN(module2_run_id) AS module2_run_id,
        MIN(run_sequence_number) AS run_sequence_number,
        MIN(showcase_id) AS showcase_id,
        MIN(showcase_name) AS showcase_name,
        MIN(comparison_group_id) AS comparison_group_id,
        MIN(validation_evidence_group_id) AS validation_evidence_group_id,
        MIN(run_registry_match_status) AS run_registry_match_status

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e

    JOIN k
        ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
       AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
       AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
       AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
       AND e.population_id = k.population_id

    UNION ALL

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Registry profile for validation evidence detail.

    Expected:
        One coherent registry identity across all validation evidence rows for the current run.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        'strategy_run_validation_evidence' AS evidence_object_name,

        COUNT(*) AS current_run_evidence_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(module2_run_id, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_module2_run_id_count,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(run_registry_match_status, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_registry_match_status_count,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(validation_evidence_group_id, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_validation_evidence_group_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE module1_run_id IS NULL
               OR module2_run_id IS NULL
               OR run_registry_match_status IS NULL
        ) AS missing_critical_registry_field_rows,

        MIN(module1_run_id) AS module1_run_id,
        MIN(module2_run_id) AS module2_run_id,
        MIN(run_sequence_number) AS run_sequence_number,
        MIN(showcase_id) AS showcase_id,
        MIN(showcase_name) AS showcase_name,
        MIN(comparison_group_id) AS comparison_group_id,
        MIN(validation_evidence_group_id) AS validation_evidence_group_id,
        MIN(run_registry_match_status) AS run_registry_match_status

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence e

    JOIN k
        ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
       AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
       AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
       AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
       AND e.population_id = k.population_id

    UNION ALL

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Registry profile for parameter snapshot evidence.

    Expected:
        One current-run row and one coherent registry identity.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        'strategy_run_parameter_snapshot' AS evidence_object_name,

        COUNT(*) AS current_run_evidence_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(module2_run_id, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_module2_run_id_count,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(run_registry_match_status, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_registry_match_status_count,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(validation_evidence_group_id, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_validation_evidence_group_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE module1_run_id IS NULL
               OR module2_run_id IS NULL
               OR run_registry_match_status IS NULL
        ) AS missing_critical_registry_field_rows,

        MIN(module1_run_id) AS module1_run_id,
        MIN(module2_run_id) AS module2_run_id,
        MIN(run_sequence_number) AS run_sequence_number,
        MIN(showcase_id) AS showcase_id,
        MIN(showcase_name) AS showcase_name,
        MIN(comparison_group_id) AS comparison_group_id,
        MIN(validation_evidence_group_id) AS validation_evidence_group_id,
        MIN(run_registry_match_status) AS run_registry_match_status

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot e

    JOIN k
        ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
       AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
       AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
       AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
       AND e.population_id = k.population_id

    UNION ALL

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Registry profile for product × score segment evidence.

    Expected:
        One coherent registry identity across all product × score segment rows for the current run.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT
        'strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary' AS evidence_object_name,

        COUNT(*) AS current_run_evidence_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(module2_run_id, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_module2_run_id_count,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(run_registry_match_status, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_registry_match_status_count,

        COUNT(DISTINCT COALESCE(validation_evidence_group_id, '<NULL>'))
            AS distinct_validation_evidence_group_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE module1_run_id IS NULL
               OR module2_run_id IS NULL
               OR run_registry_match_status IS NULL
        ) AS missing_critical_registry_field_rows,

        MIN(module1_run_id) AS module1_run_id,
        MIN(module2_run_id) AS module2_run_id,
        MIN(run_sequence_number) AS run_sequence_number,
        MIN(showcase_id) AS showcase_id,
        MIN(showcase_name) AS showcase_name,
        MIN(comparison_group_id) AS comparison_group_id,
        MIN(validation_evidence_group_id) AS validation_evidence_group_id,
        MIN(run_registry_match_status) AS run_registry_match_status

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary e

    JOIN k
        ON e.strategy_set_name = k.strategy_set_name
       AND e.strategy_name = k.strategy_name
       AND e.strategy_version = k.strategy_version
       AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = k.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND e.module1_scenario_name = k.module1_scenario_name
       AND e.population_id = k.population_id
)

SELECT
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Evidence object name and row count.

    current_run_evidence_rows should be greater than zero for every evidence object.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    evidence_object_name,
    current_run_evidence_rows,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Representative registry fields.

    These values are shown after distinct-count diagnostics confirm whether each evidence object is
    carrying one coherent registry identity.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    module1_run_id,
    module2_run_id,
    run_sequence_number,
    showcase_id,
    showcase_name,
    comparison_group_id,
    validation_evidence_group_id,
    run_registry_match_status,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Registry consistency counts.

    Counts greater than one suggest mixed registry identities inside the evidence object.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    distinct_module2_run_id_count,
    distinct_registry_match_status_count,
    distinct_validation_evidence_group_id_count,
    missing_critical_registry_field_rows,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Registry linkage status.

    REGISTRY_LINKAGE_CAPTURED:
        Evidence object has current-run rows, one module2_run_id, one registry match status, one
        validation evidence group identity, and no missing critical registry fields.

    REGISTRY_LINKAGE_REVIEW_REQUIRED:
        Evidence object requires review before documentation.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    CASE
        WHEN current_run_evidence_rows > 0
         AND distinct_module2_run_id_count = 1
         AND distinct_registry_match_status_count = 1
         AND distinct_validation_evidence_group_id_count = 1
         AND missing_critical_registry_field_rows = 0
            THEN 'REGISTRY_LINKAGE_CAPTURED'

        ELSE 'REGISTRY_LINKAGE_REVIEW_REQUIRED'
    END AS registry_linkage_status

FROM registry_profile

ORDER BY evidence_object_name;


/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 16.0–16.8 — RUN-LEVEL STRATEGY EVIDENCE CAPTURE AND EXECUTIVE STORY REGISTER

If execution reaches this point:
    1. Persistent executive run evidence summary has been created or reused.
    2. Persistent validation evidence detail has been created or reused.
    3. Persistent strategy and product-policy parameter snapshot evidence has been created or reused.
    4. Persistent product × score segment evidence summary has been created or reused.
    5. Prior evidence rows for the current run key were replaced in the evidence tables only.
    6. Current Section 14 validation evidence detail was persisted.
    7. Current strategy, product-policy, and story parameter snapshots were persisted.
    8. Current product × score segment evidence was persisted.
    9. Current one-row executive evidence summary was persisted.
    10. Local Section 16 evidence-capture gatekeepers passed.
    11. Section 16.8 evidence diagnostics and export-ready review outputs are available.
    12. Module 3 readiness fields have been captured for future growth / economics design.

Registry evidence now carries:
    module1_run_id
    module2_run_id
    run_sequence_number
    showcase_id
    showcase_name
    comparison_group_id
    validation_evidence_group_id
    readme_storyline_label
    linkedin_post_sequence
    validation_summary_section_hint
    run_registry_match_status

Current-run evidence capture boundary:
    Section 16.0–16.8 may create, delete, and replace persistent evidence rows for the current run
    key only.

    Section 16.0–16.8 does not modify latest-run output rows.
    Section 16.0–16.8 does not modify archive rows.
    Section 16.0–16.8 does not modify campaign registry rows.
    Section 16.0–16.8 does not modify comparison registry rows.
    Section 16.0–16.8 does not modify strategy parameter rows.
    Section 16.0–16.8 does not modify product-policy parameter rows.
    Section 16.0–16.8 does not recalculate decision outcomes.
    Section 16.0–16.8 does not recalculate approved exposure values.
    Section 16.0–16.8 does not recalculate approved Expected Loss values.
    Section 16.0–16.8 does not reassign simulated reason codes.
    Section 16.0–16.8 does not implement revenue, earnings, pricing, funding-cost, profitability,
    capital, or risk-adjusted margin logic.

Workflow guidance:
    For a single run:
        Stop here after reviewing Section 16.8 outputs, or proceed to the next selected run.

    For a full campaign:
        After all planned runs have completed through Section 16.8, rerun Section 15 from the
        completed archive, then run Section 16.9, then run Section 17.

Why Section 16.9 remains separate:
    Section 16.0–16.8 captures the current run's evidence at the time the run is completed.

    Section 16.9 refreshes Section 15-derived frontier fields after the full campaign frontier is
    complete.

    Keeping the steps separate makes the workflow clearer:
        run-level capture first;
        campaign-wide synchronization later.

***************************************************************************************************/


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.9 — POST-CAMPAIGN FRONTIER EVIDENCE SYNCHRONIZATION
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Refresh Section 15-derived frontier fields in the persistent executive evidence table after the
    full campaign archive is complete.

    Section 16.9 answers:

        "After the full campaign archive has been finalized and Section 15 has been rerun, do the
         persistent executive evidence rows reflect the newest archive-backed frontier labels,
         executive frontier quadrant, interpretation note, and baseline-relative reason-code movement
         fields?"

WHY THIS SECTION EXISTS:
    Section 15 is archive-wide.

    Section 16 evidence capture is run-level.

    During a full campaign, early evidence rows may be captured before every baseline / challenger
    strategy slice exists in the archive. After additional runs or reruns are completed, a fresh
    Section 15 run may produce improved frontier labels and baseline-relative movement fields.

    Without Section 16.9, the user would need to run an informal manual patch.

    Section 16.9 formalizes that refresh.

WHEN TO RUN:
    Full campaign workflow:
        1. Run each planned campaign run through Section 16.8.
        2. Rerun Section 15 once from the completed archive.
        3. Run Section 16.9.
        4. Run Section 17.

IMPORTANT:
    Do not run Section 1 immediately before Section 16.9 unless Section 15 is rerun afterward.

    Section 16.9 requires:
        tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary

    That table is created by Section 15 and is temporary to the active SQL session.

WHAT THIS SECTION UPDATES:
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary

    Fields refreshed from fresh Section 15 output:
        frontier_position_type
        executive_frontier_quadrant
        frontier_interpretation_note
        top_reason_code_delta_driver_family
        top_reason_code_delta_driver_code
        top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share
        top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share
        top_reason_code_delta_population_share

WHAT THIS SECTION DOES NOT UPDATE:
    This section does not update:
        latest-run outputs,
        archive rows,
        validation status rows,
        parameter snapshots,
        segment evidence rows,
        strategy parameters,
        product-policy parameters,
        decision outcomes,
        approved exposure,
        approved Expected Loss,
        simulated reason codes,
        observed_storyline,
        validation_notes.

WHY observed_storyline IS NOT UPDATED:
    observed_storyline may contain user-authored interpretation from the current run.

    Section 16.9 updates only deterministic Section 15-derived frontier fields. It does not overwrite
    analyst narrative.

EVIDENCE GRAIN:
    Synchronization is matched on the technical run key:

        strategy_set_name
        strategy_name
        strategy_version
        module1_scenario_set_name
        module1_scenario_name
        population_id

SQL TEACHING POINT:
    This section uses a pre-update candidate table and a post-update check.

    The candidate table shows what would change.
    The UPDATE applies only matched rows with field differences.
    The post-check confirms that matched rows now agree with fresh Section 15 output.

INTERPRETATION:
    Rows updated > 0:
        expected when earlier evidence rows had stale frontier fields.

    Rows updated = 0:
        acceptable when evidence already reflects the current Section 15 frontier state.

    Unmatched evidence rows:
        review signal only. They may represent custom / non-archived / old evidence rows.

    Matched rows still mismatched after sync:
        fail-fast condition.

BOUNDARY:
    Section 16.9 is evidence synchronization only.

    It does not recalculate frontier logic.
    It does not rebuild Section 15.
    It does not modify archive history.
    It does not modify latest-run output.
    It does not create or remove campaign registry rows.
    It does not validate final campaign acceptance.

***************************************************************************************************/


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.9A — LOCAL RESET OF FRONTIER SYNCHRONIZATION HELPERS
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Remove prior Section 16.9 helper objects before rebuilding the synchronization audit from the
    current Section 15 frontier output.

***************************************************************************************************/

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_candidates;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_update_result;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_postcheck;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.9B — PREFLIGHT GATEKEEPERS
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Confirm that the persistent evidence table and fresh Section 15 frontier output are available,
    non-empty, and unique at the run key before synchronization starts.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_evidence_table_regclass              REGCLASS;
    v_frontier_table_regclass              REGCLASS;

    v_missing_evidence_columns             TEXT;
    v_missing_frontier_columns             TEXT;

    v_evidence_rows                        BIGINT;
    v_frontier_rows                        BIGINT;

    v_evidence_duplicate_key_count          BIGINT;
    v_frontier_duplicate_key_count          BIGINT;
BEGIN
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Locate the persistent executive evidence table and the temporary Section 15 frontier table.

    to_regclass returns NULL when an object does not exist.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT TO_REGCLASS('credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary')
    INTO v_evidence_table_regclass;

    SELECT TO_REGCLASS('pg_temp.tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary')
    INTO v_frontier_table_regclass;

    IF v_evidence_table_regclass IS NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16.9 failure: credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary does not exist. Run Section 16 evidence capture before synchronization.';
    END IF;

    IF v_frontier_table_regclass IS NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16.9 failure: tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary does not exist. Rerun Section 15 immediately before Section 16.9.';
    END IF;


    /***********************************************************************************************
    Confirm required columns exist in the persistent executive evidence table.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    WITH required_columns AS (
        SELECT *
        FROM (
            VALUES
                ('strategy_set_name'),
                ('strategy_name'),
                ('strategy_version'),
                ('module1_scenario_set_name'),
                ('module1_scenario_name'),
                ('population_id'),

                ('frontier_position_type'),
                ('executive_frontier_quadrant'),
                ('frontier_interpretation_note'),

                ('top_reason_code_delta_driver_family'),
                ('top_reason_code_delta_driver_code'),
                ('top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share'),
                ('top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share'),
                ('top_reason_code_delta_population_share')
        ) AS v(column_name)
    )

    SELECT STRING_AGG(column_name, ', ' ORDER BY column_name)
    INTO v_missing_evidence_columns
    FROM required_columns rc
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM pg_attribute a
        WHERE a.attrelid = v_evidence_table_regclass
          AND a.attname = rc.column_name
          AND a.attisdropped IS FALSE
    );

    IF v_missing_evidence_columns IS NOT NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16.9 failure: strategy_run_evidence_summary is missing required column(s): %.',
            v_missing_evidence_columns;
    END IF;


    /***********************************************************************************************
    Confirm required columns exist in the fresh Section 15 frontier summary.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    WITH required_columns AS (
        SELECT *
        FROM (
            VALUES
                ('strategy_set_name'),
                ('strategy_name'),
                ('strategy_version'),
                ('module1_scenario_set_name'),
                ('module1_scenario_name'),
                ('population_id'),

                ('frontier_position_type'),
                ('executive_frontier_quadrant'),
                ('frontier_interpretation_note'),

                ('top_reason_code_delta_driver_family'),
                ('top_reason_code_delta_driver_code'),
                ('top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share'),
                ('top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share'),
                ('top_reason_code_delta_population_share')
        ) AS v(column_name)
    )

    SELECT STRING_AGG(column_name, ', ' ORDER BY column_name)
    INTO v_missing_frontier_columns
    FROM required_columns rc
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM pg_attribute a
        WHERE a.attrelid = v_frontier_table_regclass
          AND a.attname = rc.column_name
          AND a.attisdropped IS FALSE
    );

    IF v_missing_frontier_columns IS NOT NULL THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16.9 failure: tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary is missing required column(s): %.',
            v_missing_frontier_columns;
    END IF;


    /***********************************************************************************************
    Non-empty evidence and frontier checks.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_evidence_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary;

    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_frontier_rows
    FROM tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary;

    IF v_evidence_rows = 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16.9 failure: strategy_run_evidence_summary contains zero rows. Capture Section 16 evidence before synchronization.';
    END IF;

    IF v_frontier_rows = 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16.9 failure: tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary contains zero rows. Rerun Section 15 from the completed archive.';
    END IF;


    /***********************************************************************************************
    Duplicate-key checks.

    Synchronization must be one frontier row to one evidence row at the technical run key.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_evidence_duplicate_key_count
    FROM (
        SELECT
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id,
            COUNT(*) AS row_count
        FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary
        GROUP BY
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id
        HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
    ) d;

    IF v_evidence_duplicate_key_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16.9 failure: strategy_run_evidence_summary has % duplicate technical run key(s). Resolve duplicate evidence rows before frontier synchronization.',
            v_evidence_duplicate_key_count;
    END IF;

    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO v_frontier_duplicate_key_count
    FROM (
        SELECT
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id,
            COUNT(*) AS row_count
        FROM tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary
        GROUP BY
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id
        HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
    ) d;

    IF v_frontier_duplicate_key_count > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16.9 failure: tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary has % duplicate technical run key(s). Rerun / review Section 15 before synchronization.',
            v_frontier_duplicate_key_count;
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.9C — BUILD PRE-UPDATE SYNCHRONIZATION CANDIDATES
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Compare persistent executive evidence rows to fresh Section 15 frontier rows and identify which
    evidence rows need synchronization.

SQL LOGIC:
    1. Start from persistent strategy_run_evidence_summary.
    2. Left join to tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary on technical run key.
    3. Compare each Section 15-derived field using IS DISTINCT FROM.
    4. Calculate a mismatch count and row-level sync action.

WHY IS DISTINCT FROM:
    IS DISTINCT FROM treats NULLs explicitly.

    NULL versus non-NULL is a mismatch.
    NULL versus NULL is not a mismatch.

***************************************************************************************************/

CREATE TEMP TABLE tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_candidates
ON COMMIT PRESERVE ROWS
AS
WITH field_compare AS (
    SELECT
        /*******************************************************************************************
        Technical run key.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        e.strategy_set_name,
        e.strategy_name,
        e.strategy_version,
        e.module1_scenario_set_name,
        e.module1_scenario_name,
        e.population_id,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Optional campaign IDs for review readability.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        e.module1_run_id,
        e.module2_run_id,
        e.run_sequence_number,
        e.showcase_id,
        e.showcase_name,
        e.comparison_group_id,
        e.validation_evidence_group_id,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Match diagnostic.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        CASE
            WHEN f.strategy_set_name IS NOT NULL
                THEN TRUE
            ELSE FALSE
        END AS frontier_match_flag,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Current persistent evidence values.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        e.frontier_position_type
            AS evidence_frontier_position_type,

        e.executive_frontier_quadrant
            AS evidence_executive_frontier_quadrant,

        e.frontier_interpretation_note
            AS evidence_frontier_interpretation_note,

        e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_family
            AS evidence_top_reason_code_delta_driver_family,

        e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code
            AS evidence_top_reason_code_delta_driver_code,

        e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share
            AS evidence_top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share,

        e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share
            AS evidence_top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share,

        e.top_reason_code_delta_population_share
            AS evidence_top_reason_code_delta_population_share,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Fresh Section 15 values.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        f.frontier_position_type
            AS section15_frontier_position_type,

        f.executive_frontier_quadrant
            AS section15_executive_frontier_quadrant,

        f.frontier_interpretation_note
            AS section15_frontier_interpretation_note,

        f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_family
            AS section15_top_reason_code_delta_driver_family,

        f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code
            AS section15_top_reason_code_delta_driver_code,

        f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share
            AS section15_top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share,

        f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share
            AS section15_top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share,

        f.top_reason_code_delta_population_share
            AS section15_top_reason_code_delta_population_share,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Field-level mismatch flags.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (
            e.frontier_position_type
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.frontier_position_type
        ) AS frontier_position_type_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.executive_frontier_quadrant
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.executive_frontier_quadrant
        ) AS executive_frontier_quadrant_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.frontier_interpretation_note
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.frontier_interpretation_note
        ) AS frontier_interpretation_note_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_family
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_family
        ) AS top_reason_code_delta_driver_family_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code
        ) AS top_reason_code_delta_driver_code_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share
        ) AS top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share
        ) AS top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.top_reason_code_delta_population_share
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.top_reason_code_delta_population_share
        ) AS top_reason_code_delta_population_share_mismatch_flag

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e

    LEFT JOIN tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary f
        ON f.strategy_set_name = e.strategy_set_name
       AND f.strategy_name = e.strategy_name
       AND f.strategy_version = e.strategy_version
       AND f.module1_scenario_set_name = e.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND f.module1_scenario_name = e.module1_scenario_name
       AND f.population_id = e.population_id
)

SELECT
    fc.*,

    /***********************************************************************************************
    Count only mismatches for matched frontier rows.

    Unmatched rows are reviewed separately and are not updated.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    CASE
        WHEN fc.frontier_match_flag IS TRUE
            THEN (
                fc.frontier_position_type_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.executive_frontier_quadrant_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.frontier_interpretation_note_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.top_reason_code_delta_driver_family_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.top_reason_code_delta_population_share_mismatch_flag::INT
            )
        ELSE NULL
    END AS frontier_field_mismatch_count,

    CASE
        WHEN fc.frontier_match_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
            THEN 'NO_MATCHING_SECTION_15_FRONTIER_ROW_REVIEW'

        WHEN (
                fc.frontier_position_type_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.executive_frontier_quadrant_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.frontier_interpretation_note_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.top_reason_code_delta_driver_family_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share_mismatch_flag::INT
                + fc.top_reason_code_delta_population_share_mismatch_flag::INT
             ) > 0
            THEN 'SYNC_FRONTIER_FIELDS_FROM_SECTION_15'

        ELSE 'FRONTIER_FIELDS_ALREADY_CURRENT'
    END AS frontier_sync_action

FROM field_compare fc;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.9D — APPLY FRONTIER FIELD SYNCHRONIZATION
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Update only matched evidence rows where Section 15-derived frontier fields differ.

SQL LOGIC:
    UPDATE uses the candidate table built in Section 16.9C.

    Rows with no matching Section 15 frontier row are not updated.

***************************************************************************************************/

CREATE TEMP TABLE tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_update_result
ON COMMIT PRESERVE ROWS
AS
WITH updated AS (
    UPDATE credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e
    SET
        /*******************************************************************************************
        Frontier posture fields.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        frontier_position_type =
            c.section15_frontier_position_type,

        executive_frontier_quadrant =
            c.section15_executive_frontier_quadrant,

        frontier_interpretation_note =
            c.section15_frontier_interpretation_note,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Baseline-relative reason-code movement fields.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        top_reason_code_delta_driver_family =
            c.section15_top_reason_code_delta_driver_family,

        top_reason_code_delta_driver_code =
            c.section15_top_reason_code_delta_driver_code,

        top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share =
            c.section15_top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share,

        top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share =
            c.section15_top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share,

        top_reason_code_delta_population_share =
            c.section15_top_reason_code_delta_population_share

    FROM tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_candidates c

    WHERE c.frontier_match_flag IS TRUE
      AND c.frontier_field_mismatch_count > 0

      AND e.strategy_set_name = c.strategy_set_name
      AND e.strategy_name = c.strategy_name
      AND e.strategy_version = c.strategy_version
      AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
      AND e.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
      AND e.population_id = c.population_id

    RETURNING
        e.strategy_set_name,
        e.strategy_name,
        e.strategy_version,
        e.module1_scenario_set_name,
        e.module1_scenario_name,
        e.population_id
)

SELECT
    CURRENT_TIMESTAMP AS frontier_evidence_sync_ts,
    COUNT(*) AS evidence_rows_updated
FROM updated;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.9E — POST-SYNCHRONIZATION CHECK
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Confirm that every evidence row with a matching fresh Section 15 frontier row now has aligned
    Section 15-derived frontier fields.

***************************************************************************************************/

CREATE TEMP TABLE tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_postcheck
ON COMMIT PRESERVE ROWS
AS
WITH post_compare AS (
    SELECT
        e.strategy_set_name,
        e.strategy_name,
        e.strategy_version,
        e.module1_scenario_set_name,
        e.module1_scenario_name,
        e.population_id,

        CASE
            WHEN f.strategy_set_name IS NOT NULL
                THEN TRUE
            ELSE FALSE
        END AS frontier_match_flag,

        (
            e.frontier_position_type
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.frontier_position_type
        ) AS frontier_position_type_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.executive_frontier_quadrant
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.executive_frontier_quadrant
        ) AS executive_frontier_quadrant_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.frontier_interpretation_note
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.frontier_interpretation_note
        ) AS frontier_interpretation_note_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_family
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_family
        ) AS top_reason_code_delta_driver_family_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code
        ) AS top_reason_code_delta_driver_code_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share
        ) AS top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share
        ) AS top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share_mismatch_flag,

        (
            e.top_reason_code_delta_population_share
            IS DISTINCT FROM f.top_reason_code_delta_population_share
        ) AS top_reason_code_delta_population_share_mismatch_flag

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e

    LEFT JOIN tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary f
        ON f.strategy_set_name = e.strategy_set_name
       AND f.strategy_name = e.strategy_name
       AND f.strategy_version = e.strategy_version
       AND f.module1_scenario_set_name = e.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND f.module1_scenario_name = e.module1_scenario_name
       AND f.population_id = e.population_id
),

post_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS evidence_rows_after_sync,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE frontier_match_flag IS TRUE
        ) AS matched_evidence_rows_after_sync,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE frontier_match_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
        ) AS unmatched_evidence_rows_after_sync,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE frontier_match_flag IS TRUE
              AND (
                    frontier_position_type_mismatch_flag
                 OR executive_frontier_quadrant_mismatch_flag
                 OR frontier_interpretation_note_mismatch_flag
                 OR top_reason_code_delta_driver_family_mismatch_flag
                 OR top_reason_code_delta_driver_code_mismatch_flag
                 OR top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share_mismatch_flag
                 OR top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share_mismatch_flag
                 OR top_reason_code_delta_population_share_mismatch_flag
              )
        ) AS matched_rows_with_frontier_mismatch_after_sync

    FROM post_compare
)

SELECT
    ps.*,

    u.evidence_rows_updated,

    CASE
        WHEN ps.matched_evidence_rows_after_sync = 0
            THEN 'FRONTIER_EVIDENCE_SYNC_NO_MATCHED_EVIDENCE_ROWS_REVIEW'

        WHEN ps.matched_rows_with_frontier_mismatch_after_sync = 0
         AND ps.unmatched_evidence_rows_after_sync = 0
            THEN 'FRONTIER_EVIDENCE_SYNC_READY_ALL_EVIDENCE_ROWS_MATCH_SECTION_15'

        WHEN ps.matched_rows_with_frontier_mismatch_after_sync = 0
         AND ps.unmatched_evidence_rows_after_sync > 0
            THEN 'FRONTIER_EVIDENCE_SYNC_READY_WITH_UNMATCHED_EVIDENCE_ROWS_REVIEW'

        ELSE 'FRONTIER_EVIDENCE_SYNC_MISMATCH_REVIEW_REQUIRED'
    END AS frontier_evidence_sync_status,

    CASE
        WHEN ps.matched_evidence_rows_after_sync = 0
            THEN 'No persistent executive evidence rows matched the fresh Section 15 frontier output. Confirm Section 15 was rerun from the completed archive and evidence rows use the same technical run keys.'

        WHEN ps.matched_rows_with_frontier_mismatch_after_sync = 0
         AND ps.unmatched_evidence_rows_after_sync = 0
            THEN 'All persistent executive evidence rows match the fresh Section 15 frontier output.'

        WHEN ps.matched_rows_with_frontier_mismatch_after_sync = 0
         AND ps.unmatched_evidence_rows_after_sync > 0
            THEN 'All matched evidence rows were synchronized. Unmatched evidence rows remain for review; these may be custom, non-archived, or legacy evidence rows.'

        ELSE 'One or more matched evidence rows still differ from Section 15 output after synchronization.'
    END AS frontier_evidence_sync_interpretation

FROM post_summary ps

CROSS JOIN tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_update_result u;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.9F — POST-SYNCHRONIZATION FAIL-FAST CHECK
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Fail only when matched evidence rows still disagree with fresh Section 15 output.

BOUNDARY:
    Unmatched evidence rows do not fail this section automatically.

    They are review items because they may represent custom or non-campaign evidence outside the
    current archive frontier.

***************************************************************************************************/

DO $$
DECLARE
    v_matched_rows_after_sync                 BIGINT;
    v_matched_mismatch_rows_after_sync         BIGINT;
    v_sync_status                             TEXT;
BEGIN
    SELECT
        matched_evidence_rows_after_sync,
        matched_rows_with_frontier_mismatch_after_sync,
        frontier_evidence_sync_status
    INTO
        v_matched_rows_after_sync,
        v_matched_mismatch_rows_after_sync,
        v_sync_status
    FROM tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_postcheck
    LIMIT 1;

    IF v_matched_rows_after_sync = 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16.9 failure: no persistent executive evidence rows matched fresh Section 15 frontier output.';
    END IF;

    IF v_matched_mismatch_rows_after_sync > 0 THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION
            'Module 2 Section 16.9 failure: % matched evidence row(s) still disagree with fresh Section 15 frontier output after synchronization. Status: %.',
            v_matched_mismatch_rows_after_sync,
            v_sync_status;
    END IF;
END $$;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 16.9G — FRONTIER SYNCHRONIZATION REVIEW OUTPUTS
****************************************************************************************************

PURPOSE:
    Display the synchronization result and the rows that were updated or still require review.

***************************************************************************************************/



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
16.9G.1 Synchronization status summary.

Expected:
    frontier_evidence_sync_status should be either:
        FRONTIER_EVIDENCE_SYNC_READY_ALL_EVIDENCE_ROWS_MATCH_SECTION_15
        FRONTIER_EVIDENCE_SYNC_READY_WITH_UNMATCHED_EVIDENCE_ROWS_REVIEW

Interpretation:
    evidence_rows_updated:
        number of executive evidence rows refreshed from Section 15.

    unmatched_evidence_rows_after_sync:
        evidence rows with no matching current Section 15 frontier row.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    *
FROM tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_postcheck;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
16.9G.2 Rows updated by synchronization.

Purpose:
    Show the rows whose persistent evidence frontier fields were stale before this sync.

Interpretation:
    These rows are expected after campaign reruns or when early campaign evidence was captured before
    all comparison slices were archived.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    module1_run_id,
    module2_run_id,
    run_sequence_number,
    showcase_id,
    showcase_name,
    comparison_group_id,
    validation_evidence_group_id,

    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,

    evidence_frontier_position_type,
    section15_frontier_position_type,

    evidence_executive_frontier_quadrant,
    section15_executive_frontier_quadrant,

    evidence_frontier_interpretation_note,
    section15_frontier_interpretation_note,

    evidence_top_reason_code_delta_driver_code,
    section15_top_reason_code_delta_driver_code,

    frontier_field_mismatch_count,
    frontier_sync_action

FROM tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_candidates

WHERE frontier_sync_action = 'SYNC_FRONTIER_FIELDS_FROM_SECTION_15'

ORDER BY
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    strategy_set_name,
    run_sequence_number NULLS LAST,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
16.9G.3 Unmatched evidence rows for review.

Purpose:
    Identify persistent executive evidence rows that did not match the fresh Section 15 frontier
    output.

Common causes:
    custom evidence rows,
    non-archived evidence rows,
    older evidence from a prior campaign design,
    archive rows not currently represented in Section 15.

Action:
    Review before final documentation if these are expected to be part of the formal campaign.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    module1_run_id,
    module2_run_id,
    run_sequence_number,
    showcase_id,
    showcase_name,
    comparison_group_id,
    validation_evidence_group_id,

    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,

    evidence_frontier_position_type,
    evidence_executive_frontier_quadrant,
    evidence_top_reason_code_delta_driver_code,

    frontier_sync_action

FROM tmp_m2_frontier_evidence_sync_candidates

WHERE frontier_match_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE

ORDER BY
    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,
    strategy_set_name,
    run_sequence_number NULLS LAST,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version;



/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
16.9G.4 Matched evidence rows after synchronization.

Purpose:
    Show the final synchronized frontier fields that will be consumed by Section 17 and executive
    evidence review.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

SELECT
    e.module1_run_id,
    e.module2_run_id,
    e.run_sequence_number,
    e.showcase_id,
    e.showcase_name,
    e.comparison_group_id,
    e.validation_evidence_group_id,

    e.strategy_set_name,
    e.strategy_name,
    e.strategy_version,
    e.module1_scenario_set_name,
    e.module1_scenario_name,
    e.population_id,

    e.frontier_position_type,
    e.executive_frontier_quadrant,
    e.frontier_interpretation_note,

    e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_family,
    e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code,
    e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share,
    e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share,
    e.top_reason_code_delta_population_share

FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e

JOIN tmp_m2_strategy_frontier_executive_summary f
    ON f.strategy_set_name = e.strategy_set_name
   AND f.strategy_name = e.strategy_name
   AND f.strategy_version = e.strategy_version
   AND f.module1_scenario_set_name = e.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND f.module1_scenario_name = e.module1_scenario_name
   AND f.population_id = e.population_id

ORDER BY
    e.module1_scenario_set_name,
    e.module1_scenario_name,
    e.population_id,
    e.strategy_set_name,
    e.run_sequence_number NULLS LAST,
    CASE
        WHEN e.strategy_name = 'BASELINE_STRATEGY' THEN 1
        ELSE 2
    END,
    e.strategy_name,
    e.strategy_version;



/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 16.9 — POST-CAMPAIGN FRONTIER EVIDENCE SYNCHRONIZATION

If execution reaches this point:
    1. Fresh Section 15 frontier output exists.
    2. Persistent executive evidence exists.
    3. Section 15-derived frontier fields have been refreshed for all matching evidence rows.
    4. Matched evidence rows now align with the fresh Section 15 frontier output.
    5. Unmatched evidence rows, if any, have been surfaced for review.
    6. Section 17 can be run for final post-campaign acceptance.

Post-campaign synchronization boundary:
    Section 16.9 may update only Section 15-derived frontier fields in:

        credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary

    Specifically, Section 16.9 may refresh:
        frontier_position_type
        executive_frontier_quadrant
        frontier_interpretation_note
        top_reason_code_delta_driver_family
        top_reason_code_delta_driver_code
        top_reason_code_delta_driver_baseline_share
        top_reason_code_delta_driver_strategy_share
        top_reason_code_delta_population_share

    Section 16.9 does not modify latest-run output rows.
    Section 16.9 does not modify archive rows.
    Section 16.9 does not modify campaign registry rows.
    Section 16.9 does not modify validation evidence detail rows.
    Section 16.9 does not modify parameter snapshots.
    Section 16.9 does not modify product × score segment evidence.
    Section 16.9 does not modify strategy parameter rows.
    Section 16.9 does not modify product-policy parameter rows.
    Section 16.9 does not recalculate decision outcomes.
    Section 16.9 does not recalculate approved exposure values.
    Section 16.9 does not recalculate approved Expected Loss values.
    Section 16.9 does not reassign simulated reason codes.
    Section 16.9 does not implement revenue, earnings, pricing, funding-cost, profitability, capital,
    or risk-adjusted margin logic.

Next:
    Run Section 17 after reviewing the Section 16.9 synchronization summary.

***************************************************************************************************/


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17 — POST-CAMPAIGN ACCEPTANCE, EXPORT, PARAMETER AUDIT, AND STRATEGY EFFECT REVIEW
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide the final post-campaign control tower after all planned Module 2 campaign runs have been
    completed, archived, validated, compared, summarized, synchronized, and captured into persistent
    evidence.

    Section 17 answers:

        "Is the completed Module 2 campaign structurally complete, registry-aligned,
         evidence-complete, convention-clean, comparison-ready, source-consistent,
         parameter-traceable, product-policy-audited, and analytically ready for final
         interpretation?"

WHY THIS SECTION EXISTS:
    Earlier sections execute, validate, archive, compare, summarize, and capture the strategy
    campaign.

        Section 11:
            materializes the latest-run strategy output.

        Section 12:
            persists completed latest-run output into the governed strategy archive.

        Section 13:
            provides archive-backed matched baseline / challenger comparison.

        Section 14:
            validates latest-run behavior and creates validation evidence.

        Section 15:
            summarizes archive-backed strategy frontier tradeoffs.

        Section 16.0–16.8:
            persists run-level executive evidence, validation evidence, parameter snapshots, and
            product × score segment evidence.

        Section 16.9:
            synchronizes fresh Section 15-derived frontier fields into persistent executive evidence
            after the full campaign archive is complete.

    Section 17 is different.

    Section 17 does not create new strategy output.
    Section 17 does not persist new evidence.
    Section 17 does not synchronize frontier evidence.
    Section 17 reviews the completed campaign from persistent archive, registry, comparison,
    validation, parameter-snapshot, product-policy, and evidence objects.

SECTION 17 WORKFLOW POSITION:
    Section 17 is the final read-only acceptance layer.

    It should be run after:

        1. All planned Module 2 campaign runs have completed through Section 16.8.
        2. Section 15 has been rerun once from the completed campaign archive.
        3. Section 16.9 has synchronized fresh Section 15 frontier fields into:
                credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary
        4. Section 16 evidence rows exist for all accepted campaign runs.
        5. Any known reruns, repair runs, or product-policy corrections have been completed.

WHY SECTION 16.9 MUST COME BEFORE SECTION 17:
    Section 15 is archive-wide.

    Section 16.0–16.8 captures evidence one run at a time.

    If a baseline or challenger was added or rerun after earlier evidence capture, older executive
    evidence rows may still contain stale Section 15-derived frontier labels.

    Section 16.9 formalizes the refresh so Section 17 evaluates the final synchronized evidence
    state rather than a partially stale campaign evidence layer.

DO NOT RUN SECTION 1 IMMEDIATELY BEFORE SECTION 17:
    Section 1 drops the replaceable latest-run table and temporary objects.

    Section 17 is designed to read persistent archive, registry, comparison, and evidence objects.

    If the user needs to refresh frontier evidence before Section 17:
        rerun Section 15 from the completed archive;
        run Section 16.9;
        then run Section 17.

WHAT SECTION 17 INCLUDES:
    17.1  Archive campaign inventory.
    17.2  Archive slice detail.
    17.3  Archive grain duplicate check.
    17.4  Campaign registry to archive reconciliation.
    17.5  Registry runs missing or mismatched in archive.
    17.6  Archive slices without active campaign registry row.
    17.7  Section 16 evidence coverage summary.
    17.8  Section 16 evidence coverage detail by run.
    17.9  Active-campaign archive final-output convention checks.
    17.10 Validation status summary by campaign run.
    17.11 Validation REVIEW / NOT_APPLICABLE concentration.
    17.12 Comparison registry readiness.
    17.13 Matched comparison source-field consistency.
    17.14 Executive evidence campaign summary.
    17.15 Baseline × challenger delta summary.
    17.16 Product guardrail strategy effect check.
    17.17 Counteroffer-first strategy effect check.
    17.18 Parameter snapshot profile audit.
    17.19 Product guardrail policy exact-value audit.
    17.20 Final Module 2 campaign acceptance rollup.

WHY THE FORMER CAMPAIGN QUERIES 16–20 ARE AT THE END:
    The prior standalone campaign QA queries 16–20 are now represented by the closing Section 17
    checks:

        product guardrail strategy effect check,
        counteroffer-first strategy effect check,
        parameter snapshot profile audit,
        product guardrail policy exact-value audit,
        and final campaign acceptance rollup.

    Section 17 adds earlier campaign-wide completeness, reconciliation, evidence, convention, and
    comparison-readiness checks first, then keeps those strategy-effect and acceptance checks as the
    final executive acceptance layer.

DYNAMIC ACCEPTANCE DESIGN:
    Section 17 no longer assumes that every Module 1 source slice has 50,000 rows.

    Instead, for every active campaign registry run, Section 17 derives the expected source population
    row count from:

        credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive

    using:

        module1_scenario_set_name
        module1_scenario_name
        population_id

    Then Section 17 checks whether each archived Module 2 strategy slice has:

        archived_rows = expected_module1_source_rows
        distinct_application_id_count = expected_module1_source_rows

    This allows Module 2 to work with any governed Module 1 population size selected by the user.

VALIDATION EVIDENCE COMPLETENESS DESIGN:
    Section 17 no longer hardcodes the Section 14 validation evidence spine as 18 rows forever.

    Instead, Section 17 derives the validation evidence key set from persisted validation evidence
    across active campaign registry runs:

        validation_area
        validation_test_name
        validation_category

    Each run should contain the full derived validation evidence key set, without duplicate
    validation keys.

SEGMENT EVIDENCE COMPLETENESS DESIGN:
    Section 17 no longer assumes a fixed 25 product × score segment rows.

    Instead, Section 17 derives expected segment evidence count from each archived strategy slice
    using the distinct product × score × product-score segment combinations present in the archive.

WHAT TO LOOK FOR IN SECTION 17 RESULTS:
    Archive inventory:
        Every active campaign registry run should have one matching archived strategy slice, and each
        archived slice should match its selected Module 1 source population row count.

    Archive grain:
        Duplicate archive-grain count should be zero.

    Registry reconciliation:
        Every active campaign registry run should reconcile to the archive.

    Evidence coverage:
        Every accepted campaign run should have one executive evidence row, one parameter snapshot,
        complete validation evidence, and complete segment evidence.

    Final-output conventions:
        Active-campaign archive convention violation counts should be zero.

    Validation status:
        PASS rows are expected.
        REVIEW rows should be interpreted before documentation.
        NOT_APPLICABLE rows should be understood in context.

    Comparison readiness:
        Formal comparison groups should be ready after the full campaign archive is complete.

    Source-field consistency:
        Matched baseline and challenger source fields should match so Module 2 strategy deltas are not
        contaminated by Module 1 population drift.

    Executive evidence:
        Frontier labels should reflect the fresh post-campaign Section 15 state after Section 16.9.

    Parameter snapshots:
        Strategy and product-policy payloads should be present and traceable for every accepted run.

    Product guardrail audit:
        Product-guardrail strategy runs should preserve intended exact UPL and revolving-line policy
        values.

READ-ONLY BOUNDARY:
    Section 17 does not insert archive rows.
    Section 17 does not delete archive rows.
    Section 17 does not update archive rows.
    Section 17 does not modify latest-run rows.
    Section 17 does not modify evidence rows.
    Section 17 does not modify campaign registry rows.
    Section 17 does not modify comparison registry rows.
    Section 17 does not modify strategy parameter rows.
    Section 17 does not modify product-policy parameter rows.
    Section 17 does not recalculate decisions.
    Section 17 does not recalculate approved exposure.
    Section 17 does not recalculate approved Expected Loss.
    Section 17 does not reassign simulated reason codes.
    Section 17 does not draft the BRD.
    Section 17 does not draft the written Validation Summary.

COMMON MISUSE TO AVOID:
    Do not run Section 1 immediately before Section 17.
    Do not interpret Section 17 as creating or repairing evidence.
    Do not interpret Section 17 as recalculating frontier fields.
    Do not interpret Section 17 as replacing Section 14 latest-run QA.
    Do not interpret Section 17 as replacing the written Validation Summary.
    Do not interpret simulated reason-code movement as customer communication language.

***************************************************************************************************/



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.1 — MODULE 2 ARCHIVE CAMPAIGN INVENTORY
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that active campaign registry runs have matching archived strategy slices, and that each
    archived slice matches the row count of its selected Module 1 source population.

SQL PURPOSE:
    1. Read active campaign registry runs.
    2. Derive expected source population row counts from the Module 1 scenario archive.
    3. Read archived Module 2 strategy slice counts.
    4. Compare archived row counts and distinct application_id counts to expected Module 1 source
       counts.
    5. Return one compact campaign inventory status row.

DYNAMIC ACCEPTANCE PRINCIPLE:
    The expected archived row count is not hardcoded.

    For every active campaign registry run:

        expected_module1_source_rows =
            COUNT(*)
            FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
            WHERE scenario_set_name = module1_scenario_set_name
              AND scenario_name = module1_scenario_name
              AND population_id = population_id

EXPECTED RESULT:
    active_campaign_registry_rows > 0
    module1_source_count_missing_runs = 0
    registry_runs_missing_archive_rows = 0
    registry_runs_with_archive_row_count_mismatch = 0
    registry_runs_with_duplicate_application_ids = 0
    archive_campaign_inventory_status = MODULE_2_ARCHIVE_INVENTORY_READY

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_campaign_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module1_run_id,
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

archive_counts AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,

        MIN(archive_inserted_ts) AS first_archive_inserted_ts,
        MAX(archive_inserted_ts) AS last_archive_inserted_ts
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

registry_archive_join AS (
    SELECT
        r.module1_run_id,
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,
        r.showcase_id,
        r.showcase_name,
        r.comparison_group_id,
        r.validation_evidence_group_id,

        r.module1_scenario_set_name,
        r.module1_scenario_name,
        r.population_id,

        r.strategy_set_name,
        r.strategy_name,
        r.strategy_version,

        s.expected_module1_source_rows,
        s.expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(a.archived_rows, 0) AS archived_rows,
        COALESCE(a.distinct_application_id_count, 0) AS distinct_application_id_count,

        a.first_archive_inserted_ts,
        a.last_archive_inserted_ts

    FROM active_campaign_runs r

    LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
        ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = r.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts a
        ON a.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND a.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND a.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND a.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND a.population_id = r.population_id
)

SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS active_campaign_registry_rows,

    COUNT(DISTINCT (
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    )) AS distinct_module1_source_slices,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
    ) AS module1_source_count_missing_runs,

    SUM(COALESCE(expected_module1_source_rows, 0)) AS expected_total_active_campaign_source_rows,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE archived_rows > 0
    ) AS registry_runs_with_archive_rows,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE archived_rows = 0
    ) AS registry_runs_missing_archive_rows,

    SUM(archived_rows) AS total_active_campaign_archived_rows,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
          AND archived_rows <> expected_module1_source_rows
    ) AS registry_runs_with_archive_row_count_mismatch,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
          AND distinct_application_id_count <> expected_module1_source_rows
    ) AS registry_runs_with_duplicate_or_missing_application_ids,

    MIN(first_archive_inserted_ts) AS first_campaign_archive_inserted_ts,
    MAX(last_archive_inserted_ts) AS last_campaign_archive_inserted_ts,

    CASE
        WHEN COUNT(*) = 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_NO_ACTIVE_CAMPAIGN_REGISTRY_RUNS'

        WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL) > 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNTS_MISSING'

        WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE archived_rows = 0) > 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_CAMPAIGN_ARCHIVE_MISSING_RUNS'

        WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
              AND archived_rows <> expected_module1_source_rows
        ) > 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_CAMPAIGN_ARCHIVE_ROW_COUNT_MISMATCH'

        WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
              AND distinct_application_id_count <> expected_module1_source_rows
        ) > 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_CAMPAIGN_ARCHIVE_APPLICATION_ID_GRAIN'

        ELSE 'MODULE_2_ARCHIVE_INVENTORY_READY'
    END AS archive_campaign_inventory_status

FROM registry_archive_join;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.2 — MODULE 2 ARCHIVE SLICE DETAIL
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Display every active campaign registry run and its matching archived strategy slice so reviewers
    can confirm run-by-run archive completeness.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Produce one row per active campaign registry run with:
        registry IDs,
        Module 1 source lineage,
        Module 2 strategy identity,
        expected Module 1 source row count,
        archived row count,
        distinct archived application count,
        row-count gap,
        application-id grain gap,
        and archive readiness status.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    One row per active campaign registry run.

    Each row should generally show:
        archived_rows = expected_module1_source_rows
        distinct_application_id_count = expected_module1_source_rows
        archive_slice_detail_status = ARCHIVE_SLICE_READY

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_campaign_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module1_run_id,
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

archive_counts AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,

        MIN(strategy_run_id) AS min_strategy_run_id,
        MAX(strategy_run_id) AS max_strategy_run_id,

        MIN(archive_inserted_ts) AS first_archive_inserted_ts,
        MAX(archive_inserted_ts) AS last_archive_inserted_ts
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
)

SELECT
    r.run_sequence_number,
    r.module1_run_id,
    r.module2_run_id,
    r.showcase_id,
    r.showcase_name,
    r.comparison_group_id,
    r.validation_evidence_group_id,

    r.module1_scenario_set_name,
    r.module1_scenario_name,
    r.population_id,

    r.strategy_set_name,
    r.strategy_name,
    r.strategy_version,

    s.expected_module1_source_rows,
    s.expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count,

    COALESCE(a.archived_rows, 0) AS archived_rows,
    COALESCE(a.distinct_application_id_count, 0) AS distinct_application_id_count,

    COALESCE(a.archived_rows, 0) - COALESCE(s.expected_module1_source_rows, 0)
        AS archived_row_count_gap,

    COALESCE(a.distinct_application_id_count, 0) - COALESCE(s.expected_module1_source_rows, 0)
        AS distinct_application_id_count_gap,

    a.min_strategy_run_id,
    a.max_strategy_run_id,

    a.first_archive_inserted_ts,
    a.last_archive_inserted_ts,

    CASE
        WHEN s.expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
            THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNT_NOT_FOUND'

        WHEN COALESCE(a.archived_rows, 0) = 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_ARCHIVE_SLICE_MISSING'

        WHEN a.archived_rows <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
            THEN 'REVIEW_ARCHIVE_ROW_COUNT_MISMATCH'

        WHEN a.distinct_application_id_count <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
            THEN 'REVIEW_ARCHIVE_APPLICATION_ID_GRAIN'

        ELSE 'ARCHIVE_SLICE_READY'
    END AS archive_slice_detail_status

FROM active_campaign_runs r

LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
    ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND s.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
   AND s.population_id = r.population_id

LEFT JOIN archive_counts a
    ON a.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
   AND a.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
   AND a.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
   AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND a.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
   AND a.population_id = r.population_id

ORDER BY
    r.run_sequence_number,
    r.module1_scenario_set_name,
    r.module1_scenario_name,
    r.strategy_name,
    r.strategy_version;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.3 — MODULE 2 ARCHIVE GRAIN DUPLICATE CHECK
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm the archive is unique at the governed row-level archive grain.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Count duplicate rows at:

        strategy_set_name
        strategy_name
        strategy_version
        module1_scenario_set_name
        module1_scenario_name
        population_id
        application_id

EXPECTED RESULT:
    duplicate_archive_grain_count = 0
    archive_grain_status = ARCHIVE_GRAIN_READY

***************************************************************************************************/

SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS duplicate_archive_grain_count,

    CASE
        WHEN COUNT(*) = 0
            THEN 'ARCHIVE_GRAIN_READY'
        ELSE 'REVIEW_DUPLICATE_ARCHIVE_GRAIN'
    END AS archive_grain_status

FROM (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        application_id,

        COUNT(*) AS row_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive

    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,
        application_id

    HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
) d;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.4 — CAMPAIGN REGISTRY TO ARCHIVE RECONCILIATION
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm every active campaign registry run has exactly one matching archived strategy slice whose
    row count matches the selected Module 1 source population.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Reconcile active campaign registry runs to archive counts and Module 1 source counts.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    registry_run_count > 0
    registry_runs_with_archive_rows = registry_run_count
    registry_runs_missing_archive_rows = 0
    registry_runs_with_archive_row_count_mismatch = 0
    registry_runs_with_duplicate_or_missing_application_ids = 0
    campaign_registry_archive_status = CAMPAIGN_REGISTRY_RECONCILES_TO_ARCHIVE

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH registry_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module1_run_id,
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

archive_counts AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

registry_archive_join AS (
    SELECT
        r.*,

        s.expected_module1_source_rows,

        COALESCE(a.archived_rows, 0) AS archived_rows,
        COALESCE(a.distinct_application_id_count, 0) AS distinct_application_id_count

    FROM registry_runs r

    LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
        ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = r.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts a
        ON a.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND a.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND a.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND a.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND a.population_id = r.population_id
)

SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS registry_run_count,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
    ) AS registry_runs_missing_module1_source_count,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE archived_rows > 0
    ) AS registry_runs_with_archive_rows,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE archived_rows = 0
    ) AS registry_runs_missing_archive_rows,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
          AND archived_rows <> expected_module1_source_rows
    ) AS registry_runs_with_archive_row_count_mismatch,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
          AND distinct_application_id_count <> expected_module1_source_rows
    ) AS registry_runs_with_duplicate_or_missing_application_ids,

    CASE
        WHEN COUNT(*) = 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_NO_ACTIVE_CAMPAIGN_REGISTRY_RUNS'

        WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL) > 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_REGISTRY_MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNT_MISSING'

        WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE archived_rows = 0) > 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_CAMPAIGN_REGISTRY_ARCHIVE_MISSING_RUNS'

        WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
              AND archived_rows <> expected_module1_source_rows
        ) > 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_CAMPAIGN_REGISTRY_ARCHIVE_ROW_COUNT_MISMATCH'

        WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
              AND distinct_application_id_count <> expected_module1_source_rows
        ) > 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_CAMPAIGN_REGISTRY_ARCHIVE_APPLICATION_ID_GRAIN'

        ELSE 'CAMPAIGN_REGISTRY_RECONCILES_TO_ARCHIVE'
    END AS campaign_registry_archive_status

FROM registry_archive_join;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.5 — REGISTRY RUNS MISSING OR MISMATCHED IN ARCHIVE
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Provide row-level troubleshooting detail for active campaign registry runs that do not reconcile
    to the archive.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Display active registry runs where:
        Module 1 source count is missing,
        archive slice is missing,
        archive row count differs from expected Module 1 source rows,
        or archive distinct application_id count differs from expected Module 1 source rows.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    zero rows.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH registry_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module1_run_id,
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

archive_counts AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

registry_archive_join AS (
    SELECT
        r.*,

        s.expected_module1_source_rows,

        COALESCE(a.archived_rows, 0) AS archived_rows,
        COALESCE(a.distinct_application_id_count, 0) AS distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(a.archived_rows, 0) - COALESCE(s.expected_module1_source_rows, 0)
            AS archived_row_count_gap,

        COALESCE(a.distinct_application_id_count, 0) - COALESCE(s.expected_module1_source_rows, 0)
            AS distinct_application_id_count_gap

    FROM registry_runs r

    LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
        ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = r.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts a
        ON a.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND a.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND a.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND a.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND a.population_id = r.population_id
)

SELECT
    module1_run_id,
    module2_run_id,
    run_sequence_number,
    showcase_id,
    showcase_name,
    comparison_group_id,
    validation_evidence_group_id,

    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,

    strategy_set_name,
    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,

    expected_module1_source_rows,
    archived_rows,
    distinct_application_id_count,
    archived_row_count_gap,
    distinct_application_id_count_gap,

    CASE
        WHEN expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
            THEN 'MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNT_NOT_FOUND'

        WHEN archived_rows = 0
            THEN 'ARCHIVE_SLICE_MISSING'

        WHEN archived_rows <> expected_module1_source_rows
            THEN 'ARCHIVE_ROW_COUNT_MISMATCH'

        WHEN distinct_application_id_count <> expected_module1_source_rows
            THEN 'ARCHIVE_APPLICATION_ID_GRAIN_MISMATCH'

        ELSE 'ARCHIVE_SLICE_READY'
    END AS archive_reconciliation_issue_type

FROM registry_archive_join

WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
   OR archived_rows = 0
   OR archived_rows <> expected_module1_source_rows
   OR distinct_application_id_count <> expected_module1_source_rows

ORDER BY
    run_sequence_number,
    module2_run_id;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.6 — ARCHIVE SLICES WITHOUT ACTIVE CAMPAIGN REGISTRY ROW
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Identify archived strategy slices that are not represented by an active campaign registry row.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Surface archive slices that may be:
        old development runs,
        ad hoc custom experiments,
        inactive campaign runs,
        or archive rows that need documentation review.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    For a clean formal campaign archive, this may return zero rows.

INTERPRETATION:
    Rows returned here are not automatically invalid.

    They should be reviewed because Section 17 acceptance is registry-scoped. Extra archive slices can
    be legitimate historical evidence, but they should not be confused with the active campaign.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH archive_slices AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count,

        MIN(archive_inserted_ts) AS first_archive_inserted_ts,
        MAX(archive_inserted_ts) AS last_archive_inserted_ts
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

active_registry_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
)

SELECT
    a.strategy_set_name,
    a.strategy_name,
    a.strategy_version,

    a.module1_scenario_set_name,
    a.module1_scenario_name,
    a.population_id,

    a.archived_rows,
    a.distinct_application_id_count,

    a.first_archive_inserted_ts,
    a.last_archive_inserted_ts,

    'ARCHIVE_SLICE_WITHOUT_ACTIVE_CAMPAIGN_REGISTRY_ROW' AS archive_registry_status

FROM archive_slices a

LEFT JOIN active_registry_runs r
    ON r.strategy_set_name = a.strategy_set_name
   AND r.strategy_name = a.strategy_name
   AND r.strategy_version = a.strategy_version
   AND r.module1_scenario_set_name = a.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND r.module1_scenario_name = a.module1_scenario_name
   AND r.population_id = a.population_id

WHERE r.module2_run_id IS NULL

ORDER BY
    a.module1_scenario_set_name,
    a.module1_scenario_name,
    a.population_id,
    a.strategy_name,
    a.strategy_version;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.7 — SECTION 16 EVIDENCE COVERAGE SUMMARY
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that persistent Section 16 evidence exists for every active campaign registry run and
    that validation / segment evidence is complete relative to dynamically derived evidence spines.

EVIDENCE TABLES CHECKED:
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot
    credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary

DYNAMIC VALIDATION EVIDENCE DESIGN:
    expected_validation_key_count is derived from distinct validation keys present across active
    campaign runs:

        validation_area
        validation_test_name
        validation_category

    This avoids hardcoding the Section 14 validation spine row count.

DYNAMIC SEGMENT EVIDENCE DESIGN:
    expected_segment_rows is derived for each run from its archived strategy slice:

        product_type_policy_key
        score_band_policy_key
        product_score_policy_segment

    This avoids assuming a fixed product × score segment count.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    registry_run_count > 0
    expected_validation_key_count > 0
    runs_with_one_executive_evidence_row = registry_run_count
    runs_with_one_parameter_snapshot_row = registry_run_count
    runs_with_complete_validation_evidence_rows = registry_run_count
    runs_with_complete_segment_evidence_rows = registry_run_count
    evidence_coverage_issue_count = 0
    evidence_campaign_status = SECTION_16_EVIDENCE_COVERAGE_READY

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH registry_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

archive_segment_expected AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            a.product_type_policy_key,
            a.score_band_policy_key,
            a.product_score_policy_segment
        )) AS expected_segment_rows

    FROM registry_runs r

    LEFT JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive a
        ON a.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND a.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND a.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND a.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND a.population_id = r.population_id

    GROUP BY r.module2_run_id
),

executive_evidence AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,
        COUNT(*) AS executive_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

parameter_evidence AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,
        COUNT(*) AS parameter_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

validation_evidence AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS validation_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            validation_area,
            validation_test_name,
            validation_category
        )) AS validation_distinct_key_count,

        COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT (
            validation_area,
            validation_test_name,
            validation_category
        )) AS duplicate_validation_key_rows

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence

    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

validation_key_catalog AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            v.validation_area,
            v.validation_test_name,
            v.validation_category
        )) AS expected_validation_key_count
    FROM registry_runs r

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence v
        ON v.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND v.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND v.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND v.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND v.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND v.population_id = r.population_id
),

segment_evidence AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS segment_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            product_type_policy_key,
            score_band_policy_key,
            product_score_policy_segment
        )) AS segment_distinct_key_count,

        COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT (
            product_type_policy_key,
            score_band_policy_key,
            product_score_policy_segment
        )) AS duplicate_segment_key_rows

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary

    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

joined AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,

        COALESCE(e.executive_rows, 0) AS executive_rows,
        COALESCE(p.parameter_rows, 0) AS parameter_rows,

        COALESCE(v.validation_rows, 0) AS validation_rows,
        COALESCE(v.validation_distinct_key_count, 0) AS validation_distinct_key_count,
        COALESCE(v.duplicate_validation_key_rows, 0) AS duplicate_validation_key_rows,

        COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0) AS expected_validation_key_count,

        COALESCE(s.segment_rows, 0) AS segment_rows,
        COALESCE(s.segment_distinct_key_count, 0) AS segment_distinct_key_count,
        COALESCE(s.duplicate_segment_key_rows, 0) AS duplicate_segment_key_rows,

        COALESCE(ase.expected_segment_rows, 0) AS expected_segment_rows

    FROM registry_runs r

    CROSS JOIN validation_key_catalog vkc

    LEFT JOIN archive_segment_expected ase
        ON ase.module2_run_id = r.module2_run_id

    LEFT JOIN executive_evidence e
        ON e.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND e.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND e.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND e.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND e.population_id = r.population_id

    LEFT JOIN parameter_evidence p
        ON p.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND p.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND p.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND p.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND p.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND p.population_id = r.population_id

    LEFT JOIN validation_evidence v
        ON v.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND v.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND v.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND v.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND v.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND v.population_id = r.population_id

    LEFT JOIN segment_evidence s
        ON s.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND s.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND s.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND s.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = r.population_id
)

SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS registry_run_count,

    MAX(expected_validation_key_count) AS expected_validation_key_count,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE executive_rows = 1
    ) AS runs_with_one_executive_evidence_row,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE parameter_rows = 1
    ) AS runs_with_one_parameter_snapshot_row,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE expected_validation_key_count > 0
          AND validation_rows = expected_validation_key_count
          AND validation_distinct_key_count = expected_validation_key_count
          AND duplicate_validation_key_rows = 0
    ) AS runs_with_complete_validation_evidence_rows,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE expected_validation_key_count = 0
           OR validation_rows <> expected_validation_key_count
           OR validation_distinct_key_count <> expected_validation_key_count
           OR duplicate_validation_key_rows <> 0
    ) AS runs_with_incomplete_validation_evidence_rows,

    MIN(validation_rows) AS min_validation_rows_per_run,
    MAX(validation_rows) AS max_validation_rows_per_run,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE expected_segment_rows > 0
          AND segment_rows = expected_segment_rows
          AND segment_distinct_key_count = expected_segment_rows
          AND duplicate_segment_key_rows = 0
    ) AS runs_with_complete_segment_evidence_rows,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE expected_segment_rows = 0
           OR segment_rows <> expected_segment_rows
           OR segment_distinct_key_count <> expected_segment_rows
           OR duplicate_segment_key_rows <> 0
    ) AS runs_with_incomplete_segment_evidence_rows,

    MIN(expected_segment_rows) AS min_expected_segment_rows_per_run,
    MAX(expected_segment_rows) AS max_expected_segment_rows_per_run,
    MIN(segment_rows) AS min_actual_segment_rows_per_run,
    MAX(segment_rows) AS max_actual_segment_rows_per_run,

    COUNT(*) FILTER (
        WHERE executive_rows <> 1
           OR parameter_rows <> 1
           OR expected_validation_key_count = 0
           OR validation_rows <> expected_validation_key_count
           OR validation_distinct_key_count <> expected_validation_key_count
           OR duplicate_validation_key_rows <> 0
           OR expected_segment_rows = 0
           OR segment_rows <> expected_segment_rows
           OR segment_distinct_key_count <> expected_segment_rows
           OR duplicate_segment_key_rows <> 0
    ) AS evidence_coverage_issue_count,

    CASE
        WHEN COUNT(*) = 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_NO_ACTIVE_CAMPAIGN_REGISTRY_RUNS'

        WHEN MAX(expected_validation_key_count) = 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE_KEY_CATALOG_MISSING'

        WHEN COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE executive_rows = 1
              AND parameter_rows = 1
              AND expected_validation_key_count > 0
              AND validation_rows = expected_validation_key_count
              AND validation_distinct_key_count = expected_validation_key_count
              AND duplicate_validation_key_rows = 0
              AND expected_segment_rows > 0
              AND segment_rows = expected_segment_rows
              AND segment_distinct_key_count = expected_segment_rows
              AND duplicate_segment_key_rows = 0
        ) = COUNT(*)
            THEN 'SECTION_16_EVIDENCE_COVERAGE_READY'

        ELSE 'REVIEW_SECTION_16_EVIDENCE_COVERAGE'
    END AS evidence_campaign_status

FROM joined;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.8 — SECTION 16 EVIDENCE COVERAGE DETAIL BY RUN
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Display evidence counts for each individual campaign run and confirm complete evidence capture
    without relying on fixed campaign size, fixed validation-row count, or fixed segment-row count.

SQL PURPOSE:
    Provide one row per active campaign registry run with:
        executive evidence count,
        parameter snapshot count,
        validation evidence counts,
        derived expected validation key count,
        segment evidence counts,
        derived expected segment count,
        and per-run evidence capture status.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    One row per active campaign registry run.

    Each row should generally show:
        executive_rows = 1
        parameter_rows = 1
        validation_rows = expected_validation_key_count
        validation_evidence_row_gap = 0
        duplicate_validation_key_rows = 0
        segment_rows = expected_segment_rows
        segment_evidence_row_gap = 0
        duplicate_segment_key_rows = 0
        evidence_capture_status = EVIDENCE_CAPTURE_READY

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH registry_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

archive_segment_expected AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            a.product_type_policy_key,
            a.score_band_policy_key,
            a.product_score_policy_segment
        )) AS expected_segment_rows

    FROM registry_runs r

    LEFT JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive a
        ON a.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND a.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND a.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND a.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND a.population_id = r.population_id

    GROUP BY r.module2_run_id
),

executive_evidence AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,
        COUNT(*) AS executive_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

parameter_evidence AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,
        COUNT(*) AS parameter_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

validation_evidence AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS validation_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            validation_area,
            validation_test_name,
            validation_category
        )) AS validation_distinct_key_count,

        COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT (
            validation_area,
            validation_test_name,
            validation_category
        )) AS duplicate_validation_key_rows

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence

    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

validation_key_catalog AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            v.validation_area,
            v.validation_test_name,
            v.validation_category
        )) AS expected_validation_key_count
    FROM registry_runs r

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence v
        ON v.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND v.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND v.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND v.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND v.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND v.population_id = r.population_id
),

segment_evidence AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS segment_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            product_type_policy_key,
            score_band_policy_key,
            product_score_policy_segment
        )) AS segment_distinct_key_count,

        COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT (
            product_type_policy_key,
            score_band_policy_key,
            product_score_policy_segment
        )) AS duplicate_segment_key_rows

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary

    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
)

SELECT
    r.module2_run_id,
    r.run_sequence_number,
    r.showcase_id,
    r.showcase_name,
    r.comparison_group_id,
    r.validation_evidence_group_id,

    r.module1_scenario_set_name,
    r.module1_scenario_name,
    r.population_id,

    r.strategy_name,
    r.strategy_version,

    COALESCE(e.executive_rows, 0) AS executive_rows,
    COALESCE(p.parameter_rows, 0) AS parameter_rows,

    COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0) AS expected_validation_key_count,
    COALESCE(v.validation_rows, 0) AS validation_rows,
    COALESCE(v.validation_distinct_key_count, 0) AS validation_distinct_key_count,

    COALESCE(v.validation_rows, 0)
        - COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0)
        AS validation_evidence_row_gap,

    COALESCE(v.duplicate_validation_key_rows, 0) AS duplicate_validation_key_rows,

    COALESCE(ase.expected_segment_rows, 0) AS expected_segment_rows,
    COALESCE(s.segment_rows, 0) AS segment_rows,
    COALESCE(s.segment_distinct_key_count, 0) AS segment_distinct_key_count,

    COALESCE(s.segment_rows, 0)
        - COALESCE(ase.expected_segment_rows, 0)
        AS segment_evidence_row_gap,

    COALESCE(s.duplicate_segment_key_rows, 0) AS duplicate_segment_key_rows,

    CASE
        WHEN COALESCE(e.executive_rows, 0) = 1
         AND COALESCE(p.parameter_rows, 0) = 1
         AND COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0) > 0
         AND COALESCE(v.validation_rows, 0) = COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0)
         AND COALESCE(v.validation_distinct_key_count, 0) = COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0)
         AND COALESCE(v.duplicate_validation_key_rows, 0) = 0
         AND COALESCE(ase.expected_segment_rows, 0) > 0
         AND COALESCE(s.segment_rows, 0) = COALESCE(ase.expected_segment_rows, 0)
         AND COALESCE(s.segment_distinct_key_count, 0) = COALESCE(ase.expected_segment_rows, 0)
         AND COALESCE(s.duplicate_segment_key_rows, 0) = 0
            THEN 'EVIDENCE_CAPTURE_READY'

        ELSE 'EVIDENCE_CAPTURE_REVIEW_REQUIRED'
    END AS evidence_capture_status

FROM registry_runs r

CROSS JOIN validation_key_catalog vkc

LEFT JOIN archive_segment_expected ase
    ON ase.module2_run_id = r.module2_run_id

LEFT JOIN executive_evidence e
    ON e.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
   AND e.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
   AND e.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
   AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND e.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
   AND e.population_id = r.population_id

LEFT JOIN parameter_evidence p
    ON p.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
   AND p.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
   AND p.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
   AND p.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND p.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
   AND p.population_id = r.population_id

LEFT JOIN validation_evidence v
    ON v.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
   AND v.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
   AND v.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
   AND v.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND v.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
   AND v.population_id = r.population_id

LEFT JOIN segment_evidence s
    ON s.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
   AND s.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
   AND s.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
   AND s.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND s.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
   AND s.population_id = r.population_id

ORDER BY r.run_sequence_number;


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.9 — ACTIVE CAMPAIGN ARCHIVE FINAL OUTPUT CONVENTION CHECKS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Apply final-output convention checks across the archived rows belonging to active campaign
    registry runs.

    Section 17.9 answers:

        "Do the archived rows for the active campaign satisfy the locked final output conventions?"

WHY THIS SECTION IS REGISTRY-SCOPED:
    The strategy archive may contain older development runs, ad hoc custom experiments, inactive
    campaign runs, or historical slices.

    Section 17 acceptance should evaluate the active campaign registry scope, not every historical
    archive row unless the user intentionally activates those runs in the campaign registry.

CONVENTIONS CHECKED:
    exactly one final decision flag per row;
    simulated_offer_exposure_flag reconciles to APPROVE / COUNTEROFFER;
    APPROVE preserves requested exposure, payment proxy, PTI, and requested Expected Loss;
    COUNTEROFFER has positive reduced exposure and satisfies target PTI / approved EL cap;
    MANUAL_REVIEW remains unresolved;
    DECLINE follows zero-exposure convention;
    simulated reason-code fields are complete;
    primary_reason_family aligns to decision_outcome.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    critical_convention_violation_count = 0
    active_campaign_archive_convention_status = ACTIVE_CAMPAIGN_ARCHIVE_CONVENTIONS_READY

READ-ONLY BOUNDARY:
    This section does not modify archive rows, latest-run rows, evidence rows, registry rows, or
    parameter rows.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_campaign_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

active_campaign_archive_rows AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,

        a.*
    FROM active_campaign_runs r

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive a
        ON a.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND a.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND a.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND a.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND a.population_id = r.population_id
),

convention_counts AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS active_campaign_archived_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE (
                COALESCE(approval_flag::INT, 0)
                + COALESCE(counteroffer_flag::INT, 0)
                + COALESCE(manual_review_flag::INT, 0)
                + COALESCE(decline_flag::INT, 0)
            ) <> 1
        ) AS final_outcome_flag_count_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag
                  IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER'))
        ) AS simulated_offer_exposure_flag_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
              AND approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_amount
        ) AS approve_amount_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND (
                    approved_amount IS NULL
                 OR approved_amount <= 0
                 OR approved_amount >= requested_amount
                 OR counteroffer_amount IS DISTINCT FROM approved_amount
              )
        ) AS counteroffer_amount_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND approved_amount IS NOT NULL
        ) AS manual_review_amount_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
              AND approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
        ) AS decline_amount_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
              AND approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS DISTINCT FROM requested_monthly_payment_proxy
        ) AS approve_payment_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND (
                    approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS NULL
                 OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS NULL
                 OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio > counteroffer_target_pti
              )
        ) AS counteroffer_affordability_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND (
                    approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS NOT NULL
                 OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS NOT NULL
              )
        ) AS manual_review_affordability_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
              AND (
                    approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
                 OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
              )
        ) AS decline_affordability_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
              AND approved_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_expected_loss_amount
        ) AS approve_expected_loss_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND (
                    approved_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
                 OR approved_expected_loss_amount < 0
                 OR approved_expected_loss_amount > requested_expected_loss_amount
                 OR approved_expected_loss_amount > product_approved_el_cap
              )
        ) AS counteroffer_expected_loss_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND approved_expected_loss_amount IS NOT NULL
        ) AS manual_review_expected_loss_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
              AND approved_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
        ) AS decline_expected_loss_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE primary_reason_code IS NULL
               OR primary_reason_family IS NULL
               OR triggered_reason_code_list IS NULL
               OR reason_code_count IS NULL
               OR reason_code_count < 1
        ) AS reason_code_completeness_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE (
                    decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                AND primary_reason_family IS DISTINCT FROM 'APPROVAL'
            )
            OR (
                    decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                AND primary_reason_family IS DISTINCT FROM 'COUNTEROFFER'
            )
            OR (
                    decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                AND primary_reason_family IS DISTINCT FROM 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
            )
            OR (
                    decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                AND primary_reason_family IS DISTINCT FROM 'POLICY_STOP'
            )
        ) AS reason_family_alignment_violation_rows

    FROM active_campaign_archive_rows
)

SELECT
    active_campaign_archived_rows,

    final_outcome_flag_count_violation_rows,
    simulated_offer_exposure_flag_violation_rows,

    approve_amount_violation_rows,
    counteroffer_amount_violation_rows,
    manual_review_amount_violation_rows,
    decline_amount_violation_rows,

    approve_payment_violation_rows,
    counteroffer_affordability_violation_rows,
    manual_review_affordability_violation_rows,
    decline_affordability_violation_rows,

    approve_expected_loss_violation_rows,
    counteroffer_expected_loss_violation_rows,
    manual_review_expected_loss_violation_rows,
    decline_expected_loss_violation_rows,

    reason_code_completeness_violation_rows,
    reason_family_alignment_violation_rows,

    (
        final_outcome_flag_count_violation_rows
        + simulated_offer_exposure_flag_violation_rows
        + approve_amount_violation_rows
        + counteroffer_amount_violation_rows
        + manual_review_amount_violation_rows
        + decline_amount_violation_rows
        + approve_payment_violation_rows
        + counteroffer_affordability_violation_rows
        + manual_review_affordability_violation_rows
        + decline_affordability_violation_rows
        + approve_expected_loss_violation_rows
        + counteroffer_expected_loss_violation_rows
        + manual_review_expected_loss_violation_rows
        + decline_expected_loss_violation_rows
        + reason_code_completeness_violation_rows
        + reason_family_alignment_violation_rows
    ) AS critical_convention_violation_count,

    CASE
        WHEN active_campaign_archived_rows = 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_NO_ACTIVE_CAMPAIGN_ARCHIVE_ROWS'

        WHEN (
            final_outcome_flag_count_violation_rows
            + simulated_offer_exposure_flag_violation_rows
            + approve_amount_violation_rows
            + counteroffer_amount_violation_rows
            + manual_review_amount_violation_rows
            + decline_amount_violation_rows
            + approve_payment_violation_rows
            + counteroffer_affordability_violation_rows
            + manual_review_affordability_violation_rows
            + decline_affordability_violation_rows
            + approve_expected_loss_violation_rows
            + counteroffer_expected_loss_violation_rows
            + manual_review_expected_loss_violation_rows
            + decline_expected_loss_violation_rows
            + reason_code_completeness_violation_rows
            + reason_family_alignment_violation_rows
        ) = 0
            THEN 'ACTIVE_CAMPAIGN_ARCHIVE_CONVENTIONS_READY'

        ELSE 'REVIEW_ACTIVE_CAMPAIGN_ARCHIVE_CONVENTIONS'
    END AS active_campaign_archive_convention_status

FROM convention_counts;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.10 — VALIDATION STATUS SUMMARY BY ACTIVE CAMPAIGN RUN
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Summarize Section 16 validation evidence by active campaign registry run.

    Section 17.10 answers:

        "For each active campaign run, what validation evidence statuses were captured?"

WHY THIS SECTION IS REGISTRY-SCOPED:
    Persistent validation evidence may contain old development or inactive run evidence.

    Section 17 evaluates active campaign registry runs.

DYNAMIC VALIDATION EVIDENCE DESIGN:
    expected_validation_key_count is derived from the distinct validation evidence keys present across
    active campaign registry runs:

        validation_area
        validation_test_name
        validation_category

EXPECTED RESULT:
    One row per active campaign registry run.

    Each row should generally show:
        validation_rows = expected_validation_key_count
        validation_distinct_key_count = expected_validation_key_count
        duplicate_validation_key_rows = 0

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_campaign_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

validation_key_catalog AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            v.validation_area,
            v.validation_test_name,
            v.validation_category
        )) AS expected_validation_key_count
    FROM active_campaign_runs r

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence v
        ON v.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND v.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND v.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND v.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND v.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND v.population_id = r.population_id
),

validation_by_run AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,

        COUNT(v.*) AS validation_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            v.validation_area,
            v.validation_test_name,
            v.validation_category
        )) AS validation_distinct_key_count,

        COUNT(v.*) - COUNT(DISTINCT (
            v.validation_area,
            v.validation_test_name,
            v.validation_category
        )) AS duplicate_validation_key_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE v.validation_status = 'PASS')
            AS validation_pass_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE v.validation_status = 'REVIEW')
            AS validation_review_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE v.validation_status = 'NOT_APPLICABLE')
            AS validation_not_applicable_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE v.validation_status NOT IN ('PASS', 'REVIEW', 'NOT_APPLICABLE')
              AND v.validation_status IS NOT NULL
        ) AS validation_unexpected_status_count

    FROM active_campaign_runs r

    LEFT JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence v
        ON v.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND v.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND v.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND v.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND v.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND v.population_id = r.population_id

    GROUP BY
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number
)

SELECT
    r.run_sequence_number,
    r.module2_run_id,
    r.showcase_id,
    r.showcase_name,
    r.comparison_group_id,
    r.validation_evidence_group_id,

    r.module1_scenario_set_name,
    r.module1_scenario_name,
    r.population_id,

    r.strategy_name,
    r.strategy_version,

    COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0) AS expected_validation_key_count,

    COALESCE(v.validation_rows, 0) AS validation_rows,
    COALESCE(v.validation_distinct_key_count, 0) AS validation_distinct_key_count,

    COALESCE(v.validation_rows, 0)
        - COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0)
        AS validation_evidence_row_gap,

    COALESCE(v.duplicate_validation_key_rows, 0) AS duplicate_validation_key_rows,

    COALESCE(v.validation_pass_count, 0) AS validation_pass_count,
    COALESCE(v.validation_review_count, 0) AS validation_review_count,
    COALESCE(v.validation_not_applicable_count, 0) AS validation_not_applicable_count,
    COALESCE(v.validation_unexpected_status_count, 0) AS validation_unexpected_status_count,

    CASE
        WHEN COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0) = 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_VALIDATION_KEY_CATALOG_MISSING'

        WHEN COALESCE(v.validation_rows, 0) = COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0)
         AND COALESCE(v.validation_distinct_key_count, 0) = COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0)
         AND COALESCE(v.duplicate_validation_key_rows, 0) = 0
         AND COALESCE(v.validation_unexpected_status_count, 0) = 0
            THEN 'VALIDATION_EVIDENCE_COMPLETE'

        ELSE 'REVIEW_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE_COMPLETENESS'
    END AS validation_evidence_status

FROM active_campaign_runs r

CROSS JOIN validation_key_catalog vkc

LEFT JOIN validation_by_run v
    ON v.module2_run_id = r.module2_run_id

ORDER BY r.run_sequence_number;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.11 — VALIDATION REVIEW / NOT_APPLICABLE CONCENTRATION
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Display validation evidence items from active campaign runs that require interpretation or
    context.

    Section 17.11 answers:

        "Which validation areas most often produced REVIEW or NOT_APPLICABLE status across the active
         campaign?"

INTERPRETATION:
    REVIEW does not automatically mean invalid.
    NOT_APPLICABLE does not automatically mean missing.

    Both should be reviewed before executive narrative, README, LinkedIn, or validation-summary
    claims are drafted.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    Zero rows is possible when all active campaign validation evidence is PASS.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_campaign_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

active_validation_evidence AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,

        v.validation_area,
        v.validation_test_name,
        v.validation_category,
        v.validation_status,
        v.observed_value,
        v.expected_behavior,
        v.interpretation
    FROM active_campaign_runs r

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence v
        ON v.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND v.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND v.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND v.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND v.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND v.population_id = r.population_id

    WHERE v.validation_status IN ('REVIEW', 'NOT_APPLICABLE')
)

SELECT
    validation_area,
    validation_test_name,
    validation_category,
    validation_status,

    COUNT(*) AS validation_item_occurrence_count,
    COUNT(DISTINCT module2_run_id) AS impacted_campaign_run_count,

    MIN(run_sequence_number) AS first_impacted_run_sequence_number,
    MAX(run_sequence_number) AS last_impacted_run_sequence_number,

    STRING_AGG(DISTINCT module2_run_id, ', ')
        AS impacted_module2_run_ids,

    MIN(observed_value) AS sample_observed_value,
    MIN(expected_behavior) AS expected_behavior,
    MIN(interpretation) AS interpretation

FROM active_validation_evidence

GROUP BY
    validation_area,
    validation_test_name,
    validation_category,
    validation_status

ORDER BY
    CASE validation_status
        WHEN 'REVIEW' THEN 1
        WHEN 'NOT_APPLICABLE' THEN 2
        ELSE 99
    END,
    impacted_campaign_run_count DESC,
    validation_area,
    validation_test_name;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.12 — ACTIVE COMPARISON REGISTRY READINESS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm each active comparison registry group has baseline and challenger archive slices that are
    ready for matched comparison.

    Section 17.12 answers:

        "For each active comparison group, do the baseline and challenger slices exist, match the
         selected Module 1 source population size, and overlap completely by application_id?"

DYNAMIC ACCEPTANCE PRINCIPLE:
    Expected comparison row count is derived from the selected Module 1 source slice in:

        credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive

    It is not hardcoded to 50,000.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    One row per active comparison group.

    Each row should generally show:
        baseline_archived_rows = expected_module1_source_rows
        challenger_archived_rows = expected_module1_source_rows
        matched_application_id_count = expected_module1_source_rows
        baseline_only_application_id_count = 0
        challenger_only_application_id_count = 0
        readiness_status = READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_comparisons AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,
        comparison_set_name,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,

        baseline_module2_run_id,
        challenger_module2_run_id,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        baseline_strategy_set_name,
        baseline_strategy_name,
        baseline_strategy_version,

        challenger_strategy_set_name,
        challenger_strategy_name,
        challenger_strategy_version
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_comparison_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

archive_counts AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

baseline_applications AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        b.application_id
    FROM active_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id
),

challenger_applications AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        ch.application_id
    FROM active_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id
),

comparison_application_union AS (
    SELECT
        COALESCE(b.comparison_group_id, ch.comparison_group_id)
            AS comparison_group_id,

        b.application_id AS baseline_application_id,
        ch.application_id AS challenger_application_id

    FROM baseline_applications b

    FULL OUTER JOIN challenger_applications ch
        ON ch.comparison_group_id = b.comparison_group_id
       AND ch.application_id = b.application_id
),

comparison_application_overlap AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_application_id IS NOT NULL
              AND challenger_application_id IS NOT NULL
        ) AS matched_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_application_id IS NOT NULL
              AND challenger_application_id IS NULL
        ) AS baseline_only_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_application_id IS NULL
              AND challenger_application_id IS NOT NULL
        ) AS challenger_only_application_id_count

    FROM comparison_application_union

    GROUP BY comparison_group_id
)

SELECT
    c.comparison_group_id,
    c.comparison_set_name,
    c.showcase_id,
    c.showcase_name,

    c.baseline_module2_run_id,
    c.challenger_module2_run_id,

    c.module1_scenario_set_name,
    c.module1_scenario_name,
    c.population_id,

    s.expected_module1_source_rows,
    s.expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count,

    c.baseline_strategy_set_name,
    c.baseline_strategy_name,
    c.baseline_strategy_version,

    c.challenger_strategy_set_name,
    c.challenger_strategy_name,
    c.challenger_strategy_version,

    (
        c.baseline_strategy_set_name IS NOT DISTINCT FROM c.challenger_strategy_set_name
        AND c.baseline_strategy_name IS NOT DISTINCT FROM c.challenger_strategy_name
        AND c.baseline_strategy_version IS NOT DISTINCT FROM c.challenger_strategy_version
    ) AS same_strategy_selected_flag,

    COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) AS baseline_archived_rows,
    COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) AS challenger_archived_rows,

    COALESCE(b.distinct_application_id_count, 0) AS baseline_distinct_application_id_count,
    COALESCE(ch.distinct_application_id_count, 0) AS challenger_distinct_application_id_count,

    COALESCE(o.matched_application_id_count, 0) AS matched_application_id_count,
    COALESCE(o.baseline_only_application_id_count, 0) AS baseline_only_application_id_count,
    COALESCE(o.challenger_only_application_id_count, 0) AS challenger_only_application_id_count,

    CASE
        WHEN s.expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
            THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNT_NOT_FOUND'

        WHEN s.expected_module1_source_rows <> s.expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count
            THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_APPLICATION_ID_GRAIN'

        WHEN (
            c.baseline_strategy_set_name IS NOT DISTINCT FROM c.challenger_strategy_set_name
            AND c.baseline_strategy_name IS NOT DISTINCT FROM c.challenger_strategy_name
            AND c.baseline_strategy_version IS NOT DISTINCT FROM c.challenger_strategy_version
        )
            THEN 'REVIEW_SAME_STRATEGY_SELECTED'

        WHEN COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) = 0
          OR COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) = 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_ARCHIVE_MISSING_SLICE'

        WHEN COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
          OR COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
            THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_ARCHIVE_ROW_COUNT_MISMATCH'

        WHEN COALESCE(b.distinct_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
          OR COALESCE(ch.distinct_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
            THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_ARCHIVE_APPLICATION_ID_GRAIN'

        WHEN COALESCE(o.matched_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
          OR COALESCE(o.baseline_only_application_id_count, 0) <> 0
          OR COALESCE(o.challenger_only_application_id_count, 0) <> 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_APPLICATION_OVERLAP'

        ELSE 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
    END AS readiness_status

FROM active_comparisons c

LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
    ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND s.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
   AND s.population_id = c.population_id

LEFT JOIN archive_counts b
    ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
   AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
   AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
   AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
   AND b.population_id = c.population_id

LEFT JOIN archive_counts ch
    ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
   AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
   AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
   AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
   AND ch.population_id = c.population_id

LEFT JOIN comparison_application_overlap o
    ON o.comparison_group_id = c.comparison_group_id

ORDER BY c.comparison_group_id;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.13 — ACTIVE COMPARISON MATCHED SOURCE-FIELD CONSISTENCY
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm matched baseline and challenger rows share the same immutable Module 1 source fields.

    Section 17.13 answers:

        "Are baseline / challenger deltas interpretable as Module 2 strategy movement rather than
         Module 1 population drift?"

WHY THIS MATTERS:
    Matched strategy comparison should isolate downstream Module 2 strategy effects.

    If Module 1 source fields differ between baseline and challenger rows, the comparison may reflect:
        population drift,
        source-selection error,
        upstream scenario mismatch,
        archive corruption,
        or incomplete rerun replacement.

SOURCE FIELDS COMPARED:
    product_type_policy_key
    score_band_policy_key
    credit_score
    annual_income
    requested_amount
    requested_monthly_payment_proxy
    requested_payment_to_income_ratio
    amount_to_income_ratio
    estimated_pd
    estimated_lgd
    requested_expected_loss_amount
    module1_scenario_set_name
    module1_scenario_name
    population_id

EXPECTED RESULT:
    One row per active comparison group.

    source_consistency_status should generally equal:
        SOURCE_FIELDS_MATCH

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_comparisons AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,
        comparison_set_name,

        baseline_module2_run_id,
        challenger_module2_run_id,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        baseline_strategy_set_name,
        baseline_strategy_name,
        baseline_strategy_version,

        challenger_strategy_set_name,
        challenger_strategy_name,
        challenger_strategy_version
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_comparison_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

matched_rows AS (
    SELECT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        c.comparison_set_name,

        c.baseline_module2_run_id,
        c.challenger_module2_run_id,

        s.expected_module1_source_rows,

        b.application_id,

        b.product_type_policy_key AS baseline_product_type_policy_key,
        ch.product_type_policy_key AS challenger_product_type_policy_key,

        b.score_band_policy_key AS baseline_score_band_policy_key,
        ch.score_band_policy_key AS challenger_score_band_policy_key,

        b.credit_score AS baseline_credit_score,
        ch.credit_score AS challenger_credit_score,

        b.annual_income AS baseline_annual_income,
        ch.annual_income AS challenger_annual_income,

        b.requested_amount AS baseline_requested_amount,
        ch.requested_amount AS challenger_requested_amount,

        b.requested_monthly_payment_proxy AS baseline_requested_monthly_payment_proxy,
        ch.requested_monthly_payment_proxy AS challenger_requested_monthly_payment_proxy,

        b.requested_payment_to_income_ratio AS baseline_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
        ch.requested_payment_to_income_ratio AS challenger_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,

        b.amount_to_income_ratio AS baseline_amount_to_income_ratio,
        ch.amount_to_income_ratio AS challenger_amount_to_income_ratio,

        b.estimated_pd AS baseline_estimated_pd,
        ch.estimated_pd AS challenger_estimated_pd,

        b.estimated_lgd AS baseline_estimated_lgd,
        ch.estimated_lgd AS challenger_estimated_lgd,

        b.requested_expected_loss_amount AS baseline_requested_expected_loss_amount,
        ch.requested_expected_loss_amount AS challenger_requested_expected_loss_amount,

        b.module1_scenario_set_name AS baseline_module1_scenario_set_name,
        ch.module1_scenario_set_name AS challenger_module1_scenario_set_name,

        b.module1_scenario_name AS baseline_module1_scenario_name,
        ch.module1_scenario_name AS challenger_module1_scenario_name,

        b.population_id AS baseline_population_id,
        ch.population_id AS challenger_population_id

    FROM active_comparisons c

    LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
        ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = c.population_id

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id
       AND ch.application_id = b.application_id
),

source_consistency_by_group AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,
        comparison_set_name,

        baseline_module2_run_id,
        challenger_module2_run_id,

        MAX(expected_module1_source_rows) AS expected_module1_source_rows,

        COUNT(*) AS matched_application_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_product_type_policy_key IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_product_type_policy_key
        ) AS product_type_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_score_band_policy_key IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_score_band_policy_key
        ) AS score_band_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_credit_score IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_credit_score
        ) AS credit_score_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_annual_income IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_annual_income
        ) AS annual_income_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_requested_amount IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_amount
        ) AS requested_amount_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_requested_monthly_payment_proxy IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_monthly_payment_proxy
        ) AS requested_payment_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_requested_payment_to_income_ratio IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_payment_to_income_ratio
        ) AS requested_pti_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_amount_to_income_ratio IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_amount_to_income_ratio
        ) AS amount_to_income_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_estimated_pd IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_estimated_pd
        ) AS estimated_pd_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_estimated_lgd IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_estimated_lgd
        ) AS estimated_lgd_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_requested_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_expected_loss_amount
        ) AS requested_expected_loss_mismatch_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_module1_scenario_set_name IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_module1_scenario_set_name
               OR baseline_module1_scenario_name IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_module1_scenario_name
               OR baseline_population_id IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_population_id
        ) AS module1_lineage_mismatch_count

    FROM matched_rows

    GROUP BY
        comparison_group_id,
        comparison_set_name,
        baseline_module2_run_id,
        challenger_module2_run_id
)

SELECT
    c.comparison_group_id,
    c.comparison_set_name,

    c.baseline_module2_run_id,
    c.challenger_module2_run_id,

    c.module1_scenario_set_name,
    c.module1_scenario_name,
    c.population_id,

    COALESCE(s.expected_module1_source_rows, 0) AS expected_module1_source_rows,
    COALESCE(r.matched_application_count, 0) AS matched_application_count,

    COALESCE(r.product_type_mismatch_count, 0) AS product_type_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.score_band_mismatch_count, 0) AS score_band_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.credit_score_mismatch_count, 0) AS credit_score_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.annual_income_mismatch_count, 0) AS annual_income_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.requested_amount_mismatch_count, 0) AS requested_amount_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.requested_payment_mismatch_count, 0) AS requested_payment_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.requested_pti_mismatch_count, 0) AS requested_pti_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.amount_to_income_mismatch_count, 0) AS amount_to_income_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.estimated_pd_mismatch_count, 0) AS estimated_pd_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.estimated_lgd_mismatch_count, 0) AS estimated_lgd_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.requested_expected_loss_mismatch_count, 0) AS requested_expected_loss_mismatch_count,
    COALESCE(r.module1_lineage_mismatch_count, 0) AS module1_lineage_mismatch_count,

    (
        COALESCE(r.product_type_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.score_band_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.credit_score_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.annual_income_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.requested_amount_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.requested_payment_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.requested_pti_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.amount_to_income_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.estimated_pd_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.estimated_lgd_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.requested_expected_loss_mismatch_count, 0)
        + COALESCE(r.module1_lineage_mismatch_count, 0)
    ) AS source_field_mismatch_count,

    CASE
        WHEN COALESCE(s.expected_module1_source_rows, 0) = 0
            THEN 'NOT_APPLICABLE_MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNT_NOT_FOUND'

        WHEN COALESCE(r.matched_application_count, 0) <> COALESCE(s.expected_module1_source_rows, 0)
            THEN 'NOT_APPLICABLE_NOT_READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'

        WHEN (
            COALESCE(r.product_type_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.score_band_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.credit_score_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.annual_income_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.requested_amount_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.requested_payment_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.requested_pti_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.amount_to_income_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.estimated_pd_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.estimated_lgd_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.requested_expected_loss_mismatch_count, 0)
            + COALESCE(r.module1_lineage_mismatch_count, 0)
        ) = 0
            THEN 'SOURCE_FIELDS_MATCH'

        ELSE 'SOURCE_FIELD_MISMATCH_REVIEW_REQUIRED'
    END AS source_consistency_status

FROM active_comparisons c

LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
    ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND s.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
   AND s.population_id = c.population_id

LEFT JOIN source_consistency_by_group r
    ON r.comparison_group_id = c.comparison_group_id

ORDER BY c.comparison_group_id;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.14 — EXECUTIVE EVIDENCE CAMPAIGN SUMMARY
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Display the one-row executive evidence summary for each active campaign registry run.

    Section 17.14 answers:

        "What is the run-level executive evidence story for each active campaign run?"

WHY THIS SECTION IS REGISTRY-SCOPED:
    Persistent executive evidence may contain historical or ad hoc evidence rows.

    Section 17 should display the active campaign registry scope.

DYNAMIC ACCEPTANCE PRINCIPLE:
    applications is compared to the selected Module 1 source population row count derived from:

        credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive

    It is not assumed to be 50,000.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    One row per active campaign registry run.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_campaign_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module1_run_id,
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

executive_evidence_ranked AS (
    SELECT
        e.*,

        COUNT(*) OVER (
            PARTITION BY
                strategy_set_name,
                strategy_name,
                strategy_version,
                module1_scenario_set_name,
                module1_scenario_name,
                population_id
        ) AS executive_evidence_rows_for_run,

        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
            PARTITION BY
                strategy_set_name,
                strategy_name,
                strategy_version,
                module1_scenario_set_name,
                module1_scenario_name,
                population_id
            ORDER BY evidence_snapshot_ts DESC NULLS LAST
        ) AS executive_evidence_row_rank
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e
)

SELECT
    r.run_sequence_number,
    r.module1_run_id,
    r.module2_run_id,
    r.showcase_id,
    r.showcase_name,
    r.comparison_group_id,
    r.validation_evidence_group_id,

    r.module1_scenario_set_name,
    r.module1_scenario_name,
    r.population_id,

    r.strategy_name,
    r.strategy_version,

    s.expected_module1_source_rows,

    COALESCE(e.executive_evidence_rows_for_run, 0) AS executive_evidence_rows_for_run,

    e.applications,
    e.applications - s.expected_module1_source_rows AS applications_minus_expected_source_rows,

    e.approval_rate,
    e.counteroffer_rate,
    e.manual_review_rate,
    e.decline_rate,
    e.simulated_offer_exposure_rate,

    e.total_requested_amount,
    e.total_approved_amount,
    e.approved_amount_capture_rate,

    e.total_requested_expected_loss_amount,
    e.total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    e.approved_expected_loss_rate,
    e.approved_amount_per_approved_expected_loss_dollar,

    e.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows,
    e.avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_offer_rows,

    e.frontier_position_type,
    e.executive_frontier_quadrant,
    e.frontier_interpretation_note,

    e.top_primary_reason_code,
    e.top_non_approval_primary_reason_code,
    e.top_policy_stop_primary_reason_code,
    e.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code,

    e.top_approved_amount_product,
    e.top_approved_expected_loss_product,
    e.top_approved_amount_score_band,
    e.top_approved_expected_loss_score_band,
    e.top_approved_el_product_score_segment,

    e.validation_pass_count,
    e.validation_review_count,
    e.validation_not_applicable_count,

    e.module3_growth_inputs_available_flag,
    e.module3_growth_input_gap_note,

    CASE
        WHEN s.expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
            THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNT_NOT_FOUND'

        WHEN COALESCE(e.executive_evidence_rows_for_run, 0) = 0
            THEN 'REVIEW_EXECUTIVE_EVIDENCE_ROW_MISSING'

        WHEN COALESCE(e.executive_evidence_rows_for_run, 0) <> 1
            THEN 'REVIEW_DUPLICATE_EXECUTIVE_EVIDENCE_ROWS'

        WHEN e.applications IS DISTINCT FROM s.expected_module1_source_rows
            THEN 'REVIEW_EXECUTIVE_EVIDENCE_APPLICATION_COUNT_MISMATCH'

        WHEN e.frontier_position_type IS NULL
          OR e.executive_frontier_quadrant IS NULL
            THEN 'REVIEW_FRONTIER_FIELDS_NOT_SYNCHRONIZED'

        ELSE 'EXECUTIVE_EVIDENCE_READY'
    END AS executive_evidence_status

FROM active_campaign_runs r

LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
    ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND s.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
   AND s.population_id = r.population_id

LEFT JOIN executive_evidence_ranked e
    ON e.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
   AND e.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
   AND e.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
   AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND e.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
   AND e.population_id = r.population_id
   AND e.executive_evidence_row_rank = 1

ORDER BY r.run_sequence_number;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.15 — BASELINE × CHALLENGER DELTA SUMMARY FOR ACTIVE COMPARISON GROUPS
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Produce the main comparison-level strategy-effect table across all active comparison groups.

    Section 17.15 answers:

        "How did each challenger strategy change access, approvals, counteroffers, manual review,
         declines, approved exposure, approved Expected Loss, approved Expected Loss rate,
         offered-population synthetic-risk profile, and approved PTI?"

WHY THIS SECTION IS DYNAMIC:
    It returns one row per active comparison registry group.

    It does not assume a fixed comparison-group count.

READINESS CONTEXT:
    comparison_readiness_status and source_consistency_status are included so deltas are interpreted
    only when matched comparison and source-field checks are clean.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_comparisons AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,
        comparison_set_name,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,

        baseline_module2_run_id,
        challenger_module2_run_id,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        baseline_strategy_set_name,
        baseline_strategy_name,
        baseline_strategy_version,

        challenger_strategy_set_name,
        challenger_strategy_name,
        challenger_strategy_version,

        expected_comparison_storyline,
        primary_metric_focus
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_comparison_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

archive_counts AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

baseline_applications AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        b.application_id
    FROM active_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id
),

challenger_applications AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        ch.application_id
    FROM active_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id
),

comparison_overlap AS (
    SELECT
        COALESCE(b.comparison_group_id, ch.comparison_group_id)
            AS comparison_group_id,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE b.application_id IS NOT NULL
              AND ch.application_id IS NOT NULL
        ) AS matched_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE b.application_id IS NOT NULL
              AND ch.application_id IS NULL
        ) AS baseline_only_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE b.application_id IS NULL
              AND ch.application_id IS NOT NULL
        ) AS challenger_only_application_id_count

    FROM baseline_applications b

    FULL OUTER JOIN challenger_applications ch
        ON ch.comparison_group_id = b.comparison_group_id
       AND ch.application_id = b.application_id

    GROUP BY COALESCE(b.comparison_group_id, ch.comparison_group_id)
),

comparison_readiness AS (
    SELECT
        c.comparison_group_id,

        s.expected_module1_source_rows,

        COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) AS baseline_archived_rows,
        COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) AS challenger_archived_rows,

        COALESCE(b.distinct_application_id_count, 0)
            AS baseline_distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(ch.distinct_application_id_count, 0)
            AS challenger_distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(o.matched_application_id_count, 0) AS matched_application_id_count,
        COALESCE(o.baseline_only_application_id_count, 0) AS baseline_only_application_id_count,
        COALESCE(o.challenger_only_application_id_count, 0) AS challenger_only_application_id_count,

        CASE
            WHEN s.expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
                THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNT_NOT_FOUND'

            WHEN COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) = 0
              OR COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) = 0
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_ARCHIVE_MISSING_SLICE'

            WHEN COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(b.distinct_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(ch.distinct_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_ARCHIVE_ROW_COUNT_OR_GRAIN'

            WHEN COALESCE(o.matched_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(o.baseline_only_application_id_count, 0) <> 0
              OR COALESCE(o.challenger_only_application_id_count, 0) <> 0
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_APPLICATION_OVERLAP'

            ELSE 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
        END AS comparison_readiness_status

    FROM active_comparisons c

    LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
        ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN comparison_overlap o
        ON o.comparison_group_id = c.comparison_group_id
),

matched_rows AS (
    SELECT
        c.comparison_group_id,

        b.application_id,

        b.product_type_policy_key AS baseline_product_type_policy_key,
        ch.product_type_policy_key AS challenger_product_type_policy_key,

        b.score_band_policy_key AS baseline_score_band_policy_key,
        ch.score_band_policy_key AS challenger_score_band_policy_key,

        b.credit_score AS baseline_credit_score,
        ch.credit_score AS challenger_credit_score,

        b.annual_income AS baseline_annual_income,
        ch.annual_income AS challenger_annual_income,

        b.requested_amount AS baseline_requested_amount,
        ch.requested_amount AS challenger_requested_amount,

        b.requested_monthly_payment_proxy AS baseline_requested_monthly_payment_proxy,
        ch.requested_monthly_payment_proxy AS challenger_requested_monthly_payment_proxy,

        b.requested_payment_to_income_ratio AS baseline_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
        ch.requested_payment_to_income_ratio AS challenger_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,

        b.amount_to_income_ratio AS baseline_amount_to_income_ratio,
        ch.amount_to_income_ratio AS challenger_amount_to_income_ratio,

        b.estimated_pd AS baseline_estimated_pd,
        ch.estimated_pd AS challenger_estimated_pd,

        b.estimated_lgd AS baseline_estimated_lgd,
        ch.estimated_lgd AS challenger_estimated_lgd,

        b.requested_expected_loss_amount AS baseline_requested_expected_loss_amount,
        ch.requested_expected_loss_amount AS challenger_requested_expected_loss_amount

    FROM active_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id
       AND ch.application_id = b.application_id
),

source_consistency AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,

        COUNT(*) AS matched_source_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_product_type_policy_key IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_product_type_policy_key
               OR baseline_score_band_policy_key IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_score_band_policy_key
               OR baseline_credit_score IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_credit_score
               OR baseline_annual_income IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_annual_income
               OR baseline_requested_amount IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_amount
               OR baseline_requested_monthly_payment_proxy IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_monthly_payment_proxy
               OR baseline_requested_payment_to_income_ratio IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_payment_to_income_ratio
               OR baseline_amount_to_income_ratio IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_amount_to_income_ratio
               OR baseline_estimated_pd IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_estimated_pd
               OR baseline_estimated_lgd IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_estimated_lgd
               OR baseline_requested_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_expected_loss_amount
        ) AS source_field_mismatch_count
    FROM matched_rows
    GROUP BY comparison_group_id
),

executive_evidence_ranked AS (
    SELECT
        e.*,

        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
            PARTITION BY
                strategy_set_name,
                strategy_name,
                strategy_version,
                module1_scenario_set_name,
                module1_scenario_name,
                population_id
            ORDER BY evidence_snapshot_ts DESC NULLS LAST
        ) AS evidence_row_rank
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary e
)

SELECT
    c.comparison_group_id,
    c.comparison_set_name,
    c.showcase_id,
    c.showcase_name,

    c.baseline_module2_run_id,
    c.challenger_module2_run_id,

    c.module1_scenario_set_name,
    c.module1_scenario_name,
    c.population_id,

    c.baseline_strategy_name,
    c.challenger_strategy_name,

    cr.expected_module1_source_rows,
    cr.matched_application_id_count,
    cr.baseline_only_application_id_count,
    cr.challenger_only_application_id_count,
    cr.comparison_readiness_status,

    COALESCE(sc.source_field_mismatch_count, 0) AS source_field_mismatch_count,

    CASE
        WHEN cr.comparison_readiness_status <> 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
            THEN 'NOT_APPLICABLE_NOT_READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'

        WHEN COALESCE(sc.source_field_mismatch_count, 0) = 0
            THEN 'SOURCE_FIELDS_MATCH'

        ELSE 'SOURCE_FIELD_MISMATCH_REVIEW_REQUIRED'
    END AS source_consistency_status,

    c.expected_comparison_storyline,
    c.primary_metric_focus,

    b.approval_rate AS baseline_approval_rate,
    ch.approval_rate AS challenger_approval_rate,
    ch.approval_rate - b.approval_rate AS delta_approval_rate,

    b.counteroffer_rate AS baseline_counteroffer_rate,
    ch.counteroffer_rate AS challenger_counteroffer_rate,
    ch.counteroffer_rate - b.counteroffer_rate AS delta_counteroffer_rate,

    b.manual_review_rate AS baseline_manual_review_rate,
    ch.manual_review_rate AS challenger_manual_review_rate,
    ch.manual_review_rate - b.manual_review_rate AS delta_manual_review_rate,

    b.decline_rate AS baseline_decline_rate,
    ch.decline_rate AS challenger_decline_rate,
    ch.decline_rate - b.decline_rate AS delta_decline_rate,

    b.simulated_offer_exposure_rate AS baseline_simulated_offer_exposure_rate,
    ch.simulated_offer_exposure_rate AS challenger_simulated_offer_exposure_rate,
    ch.simulated_offer_exposure_rate - b.simulated_offer_exposure_rate
        AS delta_simulated_offer_exposure_rate,

    b.total_approved_amount AS baseline_total_approved_amount,
    ch.total_approved_amount AS challenger_total_approved_amount,
    ch.total_approved_amount - b.total_approved_amount AS delta_total_approved_amount,

    b.total_approved_expected_loss_amount AS baseline_total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    ch.total_approved_expected_loss_amount AS challenger_total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    ch.total_approved_expected_loss_amount - b.total_approved_expected_loss_amount
        AS delta_total_approved_expected_loss_amount,

    b.approved_expected_loss_rate AS baseline_approved_expected_loss_rate,
    ch.approved_expected_loss_rate AS challenger_approved_expected_loss_rate,
    ch.approved_expected_loss_rate - b.approved_expected_loss_rate
        AS delta_approved_expected_loss_rate,

    b.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows AS baseline_avg_pd_proxy_offer_rows,
    ch.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows AS challenger_avg_pd_proxy_offer_rows,
    ch.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows
        - b.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows
        AS delta_avg_pd_proxy_offer_rows,

    b.avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_offer_rows AS baseline_avg_approved_pti_offer_rows,
    ch.avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_offer_rows AS challenger_avg_approved_pti_offer_rows,
    ch.avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_offer_rows
        - b.avg_approved_payment_to_income_ratio_offer_rows
        AS delta_avg_approved_pti_offer_rows,

    b.frontier_position_type AS baseline_frontier_position_type,
    ch.frontier_position_type AS challenger_frontier_position_type,

    b.executive_frontier_quadrant AS baseline_executive_frontier_quadrant,
    ch.executive_frontier_quadrant AS challenger_executive_frontier_quadrant,

    ch.frontier_interpretation_note AS challenger_frontier_interpretation_note,

    ch.top_reason_code_delta_driver_code AS challenger_top_reason_code_delta_driver_code

FROM active_comparisons c

LEFT JOIN comparison_readiness cr
    ON cr.comparison_group_id = c.comparison_group_id

LEFT JOIN source_consistency sc
    ON sc.comparison_group_id = c.comparison_group_id

LEFT JOIN executive_evidence_ranked b
    ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
   AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
   AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
   AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
   AND b.population_id = c.population_id
   AND b.evidence_row_rank = 1

LEFT JOIN executive_evidence_ranked ch
    ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
   AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
   AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
   AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
   AND ch.population_id = c.population_id
   AND ch.evidence_row_rank = 1

ORDER BY c.comparison_group_id;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.16 — PRODUCT GUARDRAIL STRATEGY EFFECT CHECK
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Review the product-level strategy effect for active comparison groups where the challenger is:

        PRODUCT_SPECIFIC_GUARDRAIL_STRATEGY

    Section 17.16 answers:

        "Did product-specific guardrail challengers change product-level approval, offer exposure,
         approved amount, approved Expected Loss, and decline / counteroffer behavior in an
         interpretable way?"

WHY THIS SECTION IS DYNAMIC:
    The number of product-guardrail comparisons is derived from the active comparison registry.

    It is not hardcoded to five runs.

INTERPRETATION:
    UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN and REVOLVING_LINE are the primary audited product guardrail targets.

    Other products are displayed as monitoring rows so unintended spillover can be reviewed.

READ-ONLY BOUNDARY:
    This section does not modify archive, evidence, registry, strategy-parameter, or product-policy
    rows.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH product_guardrail_comparisons AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,
        comparison_set_name,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,

        baseline_module2_run_id,
        challenger_module2_run_id,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        baseline_strategy_set_name,
        baseline_strategy_name,
        baseline_strategy_version,

        challenger_strategy_set_name,
        challenger_strategy_name,
        challenger_strategy_version
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_comparison_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
      AND challenger_strategy_name = 'PRODUCT_SPECIFIC_GUARDRAIL_STRATEGY'
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

archive_counts AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

baseline_applications AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        b.application_id
    FROM product_guardrail_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id
),

challenger_applications AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        ch.application_id
    FROM product_guardrail_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id
),

comparison_overlap AS (
    SELECT
        COALESCE(b.comparison_group_id, ch.comparison_group_id)
            AS comparison_group_id,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE b.application_id IS NOT NULL
              AND ch.application_id IS NOT NULL
        ) AS matched_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE b.application_id IS NOT NULL
              AND ch.application_id IS NULL
        ) AS baseline_only_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE b.application_id IS NULL
              AND ch.application_id IS NOT NULL
        ) AS challenger_only_application_id_count

    FROM baseline_applications b

    FULL OUTER JOIN challenger_applications ch
        ON ch.comparison_group_id = b.comparison_group_id
       AND ch.application_id = b.application_id

    GROUP BY COALESCE(b.comparison_group_id, ch.comparison_group_id)
),

comparison_readiness AS (
    SELECT
        c.comparison_group_id,

        s.expected_module1_source_rows,

        COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) AS baseline_archived_rows,
        COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) AS challenger_archived_rows,

        COALESCE(o.matched_application_id_count, 0) AS matched_application_id_count,
        COALESCE(o.baseline_only_application_id_count, 0) AS baseline_only_application_id_count,
        COALESCE(o.challenger_only_application_id_count, 0) AS challenger_only_application_id_count,

        CASE
            WHEN s.expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
                THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNT_NOT_FOUND'

            WHEN COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_ARCHIVE_ROW_COUNT_MISMATCH'

            WHEN COALESCE(o.matched_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(o.baseline_only_application_id_count, 0) <> 0
              OR COALESCE(o.challenger_only_application_id_count, 0) <> 0
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_APPLICATION_OVERLAP'

            ELSE 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
        END AS comparison_readiness_status

    FROM product_guardrail_comparisons c

    LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
        ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN comparison_overlap o
        ON o.comparison_group_id = c.comparison_group_id
),

product_metrics AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        product_type_policy_key,

        COUNT(*) AS applications,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS approval_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS counteroffer_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS manual_review_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS decline_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS simulated_offer_exposure_rate,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS total_approved_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS approved_expected_loss_rate,

        AVG(approved_amount) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
            AS avg_approved_amount_offer_rows,

        AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
            AS avg_approved_expected_loss_offer_rows,

        AVG(requested_amount) AS avg_requested_amount,

        AVG(estimated_pd) FILTER (WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag IS TRUE)
            AS avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive

    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,
        product_type_policy_key
)

SELECT
    c.comparison_group_id,
    c.comparison_set_name,
    c.showcase_id,
    c.showcase_name,

    c.baseline_module2_run_id,
    c.challenger_module2_run_id,

    c.module1_scenario_set_name,
    c.module1_scenario_name,
    c.population_id,

    cr.expected_module1_source_rows,
    cr.matched_application_id_count,
    cr.comparison_readiness_status,

    COALESCE(b.product_type_policy_key, ch.product_type_policy_key) AS product_type_policy_key,

    CASE
        WHEN COALESCE(b.product_type_policy_key, ch.product_type_policy_key)
             IN ('UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN', 'REVOLVING_LINE')
            THEN 'TARGET_PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_PRODUCT'
        ELSE 'NON_TARGET_PRODUCT_MONITORING_ROW'
    END AS product_guardrail_audit_product_type,

    b.applications AS baseline_applications,
    ch.applications AS challenger_applications,

    b.approval_rate AS baseline_approval_rate,
    ch.approval_rate AS challenger_approval_rate,
    ch.approval_rate - b.approval_rate AS delta_approval_rate,

    b.counteroffer_rate AS baseline_counteroffer_rate,
    ch.counteroffer_rate AS challenger_counteroffer_rate,
    ch.counteroffer_rate - b.counteroffer_rate AS delta_counteroffer_rate,

    b.manual_review_rate AS baseline_manual_review_rate,
    ch.manual_review_rate AS challenger_manual_review_rate,
    ch.manual_review_rate - b.manual_review_rate AS delta_manual_review_rate,

    b.decline_rate AS baseline_decline_rate,
    ch.decline_rate AS challenger_decline_rate,
    ch.decline_rate - b.decline_rate AS delta_decline_rate,

    b.simulated_offer_exposure_rate AS baseline_simulated_offer_exposure_rate,
    ch.simulated_offer_exposure_rate AS challenger_simulated_offer_exposure_rate,
    ch.simulated_offer_exposure_rate - b.simulated_offer_exposure_rate
        AS delta_simulated_offer_exposure_rate,

    b.total_approved_amount AS baseline_total_approved_amount,
    ch.total_approved_amount AS challenger_total_approved_amount,
    ch.total_approved_amount - b.total_approved_amount AS delta_total_approved_amount,

    b.total_approved_expected_loss_amount AS baseline_total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    ch.total_approved_expected_loss_amount AS challenger_total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    ch.total_approved_expected_loss_amount - b.total_approved_expected_loss_amount
        AS delta_total_approved_expected_loss_amount,

    b.approved_expected_loss_rate AS baseline_approved_expected_loss_rate,
    ch.approved_expected_loss_rate AS challenger_approved_expected_loss_rate,
    ch.approved_expected_loss_rate - b.approved_expected_loss_rate
        AS delta_approved_expected_loss_rate,

    b.avg_approved_amount_offer_rows AS baseline_avg_approved_amount_offer_rows,
    ch.avg_approved_amount_offer_rows AS challenger_avg_approved_amount_offer_rows,
    ch.avg_approved_amount_offer_rows - b.avg_approved_amount_offer_rows
        AS delta_avg_approved_amount_offer_rows,

    b.avg_approved_expected_loss_offer_rows AS baseline_avg_approved_expected_loss_offer_rows,
    ch.avg_approved_expected_loss_offer_rows AS challenger_avg_approved_expected_loss_offer_rows,
    ch.avg_approved_expected_loss_offer_rows - b.avg_approved_expected_loss_offer_rows
        AS delta_avg_approved_expected_loss_offer_rows,

    b.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows AS baseline_avg_pd_proxy_offer_rows,
    ch.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows AS challenger_avg_pd_proxy_offer_rows,
    ch.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows
        - b.avg_synthetic_estimated_pd_proxy_offer_rows
        AS delta_avg_pd_proxy_offer_rows,

    CASE
        WHEN cr.comparison_readiness_status <> 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
            THEN 'NOT_APPLICABLE_NOT_READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'

        WHEN COALESCE(b.product_type_policy_key, ch.product_type_policy_key)
             IN ('UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN', 'REVOLVING_LINE')
         AND ch.total_approved_amount <= b.total_approved_amount
         AND ch.total_approved_expected_loss_amount <= b.total_approved_expected_loss_amount
            THEN 'TARGET_PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_EFFECT_VISIBLE'

        WHEN COALESCE(b.product_type_policy_key, ch.product_type_policy_key)
             IN ('UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN', 'REVOLVING_LINE')
            THEN 'REVIEW_TARGET_PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_EFFECT'

        ELSE 'NON_TARGET_PRODUCT_MONITORING_ROW'
    END AS product_guardrail_strategy_effect_status

FROM product_guardrail_comparisons c

LEFT JOIN comparison_readiness cr
    ON cr.comparison_group_id = c.comparison_group_id

LEFT JOIN product_metrics b
    ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
   AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
   AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
   AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
   AND b.population_id = c.population_id

LEFT JOIN product_metrics ch
    ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
   AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
   AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
   AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
   AND ch.population_id = c.population_id
   AND ch.product_type_policy_key = b.product_type_policy_key

ORDER BY
    c.comparison_group_id,
    CASE COALESCE(b.product_type_policy_key, ch.product_type_policy_key)
        WHEN 'UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN' THEN 1
        WHEN 'REVOLVING_LINE' THEN 2
        WHEN 'MORTGAGE' THEN 3
        WHEN 'HELOC' THEN 4
        WHEN 'AUTO_LOAN' THEN 5
        ELSE 99
    END;


/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.17 — COUNTEROFFER-FIRST STRATEGY EFFECT CHECK
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Review the strategy effect for active comparison groups where the challenger is:

        COUNTEROFFER_FIRST_EXPOSURE_STRATEGY

    Section 17.17 answers:

        "Did counteroffer-first strategy design increase reduced-exposure treatment and create an
         interpretable counteroffer-management effect relative to its registered baseline?"

WHY THIS SECTION IS COMPARISON-REGISTRY-SCOPED:
    The active comparison registry defines the governed baseline / challenger pairs.

    This section does not infer pairings only from strategy_name.

DYNAMIC ACCEPTANCE PRINCIPLE:
    Expected matched comparison row count is derived from the selected Module 1 source population.

    It is not hardcoded to 50,000.

INTERPRETATION:
    A counteroffer-first strategy should generally:
        increase final counteroffer rate;
        increase feasible counteroffer treatment;
        increase total counteroffer exposure reduction;
        preserve comparison readiness and source consistency;
        and produce interpretable approved PTI / approved Expected Loss movement.

    The effect check is diagnostic.
    It is not a production recommendation.

READ-ONLY BOUNDARY:
    This section does not modify archive rows, evidence rows, registry rows, strategy parameters, or
    product-policy parameters.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH counteroffer_first_comparisons AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,
        comparison_set_name,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,

        baseline_module2_run_id,
        challenger_module2_run_id,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        baseline_strategy_set_name,
        baseline_strategy_name,
        baseline_strategy_version,

        challenger_strategy_set_name,
        challenger_strategy_name,
        challenger_strategy_version,

        expected_comparison_storyline,
        primary_metric_focus
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_comparison_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
      AND challenger_strategy_name = 'COUNTEROFFER_FIRST_EXPOSURE_STRATEGY'
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

archive_counts AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

baseline_applications AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        b.application_id
    FROM counteroffer_first_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id
),

challenger_applications AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        ch.application_id
    FROM counteroffer_first_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id
),

comparison_overlap AS (
    SELECT
        COALESCE(b.comparison_group_id, ch.comparison_group_id)
            AS comparison_group_id,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE b.application_id IS NOT NULL
              AND ch.application_id IS NOT NULL
        ) AS matched_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE b.application_id IS NOT NULL
              AND ch.application_id IS NULL
        ) AS baseline_only_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE b.application_id IS NULL
              AND ch.application_id IS NOT NULL
        ) AS challenger_only_application_id_count

    FROM baseline_applications b

    FULL OUTER JOIN challenger_applications ch
        ON ch.comparison_group_id = b.comparison_group_id
       AND ch.application_id = b.application_id

    GROUP BY COALESCE(b.comparison_group_id, ch.comparison_group_id)
),

comparison_readiness AS (
    SELECT
        c.comparison_group_id,

        s.expected_module1_source_rows,
        s.expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) AS baseline_archived_rows,
        COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) AS challenger_archived_rows,

        COALESCE(b.distinct_application_id_count, 0)
            AS baseline_distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(ch.distinct_application_id_count, 0)
            AS challenger_distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(o.matched_application_id_count, 0)
            AS matched_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(o.baseline_only_application_id_count, 0)
            AS baseline_only_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(o.challenger_only_application_id_count, 0)
            AS challenger_only_application_id_count,

        CASE
            WHEN s.expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
                THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNT_NOT_FOUND'

            WHEN s.expected_module1_source_rows <> s.expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count
                THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_APPLICATION_ID_GRAIN'

            WHEN COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) = 0
              OR COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) = 0
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_ARCHIVE_MISSING_SLICE'

            WHEN COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(b.distinct_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(ch.distinct_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_ARCHIVE_ROW_COUNT_OR_GRAIN'

            WHEN COALESCE(o.matched_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(o.baseline_only_application_id_count, 0) <> 0
              OR COALESCE(o.challenger_only_application_id_count, 0) <> 0
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_APPLICATION_OVERLAP'

            ELSE 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
        END AS comparison_readiness_status

    FROM counteroffer_first_comparisons c

    LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
        ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN comparison_overlap o
        ON o.comparison_group_id = c.comparison_group_id
),

counteroffer_metrics AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS applications,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS approval_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER') AS counteroffer_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER')::NUMERIC
            / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0) AS counteroffer_rate,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS preliminary_counteroffer_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
        ) AS feasible_counteroffer_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS FALSE
        ) AS failed_counteroffer_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND counteroffer_feasibility_pass_flag IS TRUE
        )::NUMERIC
        / NULLIF(
            COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE preliminary_decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'),
            0
        ) AS counteroffer_feasibility_pass_rate,

        AVG(exposure_reduction_pct) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS avg_exposure_reduction_pct_for_final_counteroffers,

        SUM(exposure_reduction_amount) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS total_counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount,

        AVG(requested_payment_to_income_ratio) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS avg_requested_pti_for_final_counteroffers,

        AVG(approved_payment_to_income_ratio) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers,

        AVG(requested_expected_loss_amount) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS avg_requested_expected_loss_for_final_counteroffers,

        AVG(approved_expected_loss_amount) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
        ) AS avg_approved_el_for_final_counteroffers,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)) AS total_approved_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            AS total_approved_expected_loss_amount,

        SUM(COALESCE(approved_expected_loss_amount, 0))
            / NULLIF(SUM(COALESCE(approved_amount, 0)), 0)
            AS approved_expected_loss_rate

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive

    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
)

SELECT
    c.comparison_group_id,
    c.comparison_set_name,
    c.showcase_id,
    c.showcase_name,

    c.baseline_module2_run_id,
    c.challenger_module2_run_id,

    c.module1_scenario_set_name,
    c.module1_scenario_name,
    c.population_id,

    cr.expected_module1_source_rows,
    cr.baseline_archived_rows,
    cr.challenger_archived_rows,
    cr.matched_application_id_count,
    cr.baseline_only_application_id_count,
    cr.challenger_only_application_id_count,
    cr.comparison_readiness_status,

    c.expected_comparison_storyline,
    c.primary_metric_focus,

    b.applications AS baseline_applications,
    ch.applications AS challenger_applications,

    b.approval_rate AS baseline_approval_rate,
    ch.approval_rate AS counteroffer_first_approval_rate,
    ch.approval_rate - b.approval_rate AS delta_approval_rate,

    b.counteroffer_count AS baseline_counteroffer_count,
    ch.counteroffer_count AS counteroffer_first_counteroffer_count,
    ch.counteroffer_count - b.counteroffer_count AS delta_counteroffer_count,

    b.counteroffer_rate AS baseline_counteroffer_rate,
    ch.counteroffer_rate AS counteroffer_first_counteroffer_rate,
    ch.counteroffer_rate - b.counteroffer_rate AS delta_counteroffer_rate,

    b.preliminary_counteroffer_count AS baseline_preliminary_counteroffer_count,
    ch.preliminary_counteroffer_count AS counteroffer_first_preliminary_counteroffer_count,
    ch.preliminary_counteroffer_count - b.preliminary_counteroffer_count
        AS delta_preliminary_counteroffer_count,

    b.feasible_counteroffer_count AS baseline_feasible_counteroffer_count,
    ch.feasible_counteroffer_count AS counteroffer_first_feasible_counteroffer_count,
    ch.feasible_counteroffer_count - b.feasible_counteroffer_count
        AS delta_feasible_counteroffer_count,

    b.failed_counteroffer_count AS baseline_failed_counteroffer_count,
    ch.failed_counteroffer_count AS counteroffer_first_failed_counteroffer_count,
    ch.failed_counteroffer_count - b.failed_counteroffer_count
        AS delta_failed_counteroffer_count,

    b.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_rate AS baseline_counteroffer_feasibility_pass_rate,
    ch.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_rate AS counteroffer_first_feasibility_pass_rate,
    ch.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_rate - b.counteroffer_feasibility_pass_rate
        AS delta_counteroffer_feasibility_pass_rate,

    b.avg_exposure_reduction_pct_for_final_counteroffers
        AS baseline_avg_exposure_reduction_pct_for_final_counteroffers,

    ch.avg_exposure_reduction_pct_for_final_counteroffers
        AS counteroffer_first_avg_exposure_reduction_pct_for_final_counteroffers,

    ch.avg_exposure_reduction_pct_for_final_counteroffers
        - b.avg_exposure_reduction_pct_for_final_counteroffers
        AS delta_avg_exposure_reduction_pct_for_final_counteroffers,

    b.total_counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount
        AS baseline_total_counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount,

    ch.total_counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount
        AS counteroffer_first_total_counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount,

    COALESCE(ch.total_counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount, 0)
        - COALESCE(b.total_counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount, 0)
        AS delta_total_counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount,

    b.avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers
        AS baseline_avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers,

    ch.avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers
        AS counteroffer_first_avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers,

    ch.avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers
        - b.avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers
        AS delta_avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers,

    b.avg_approved_el_for_final_counteroffers
        AS baseline_avg_approved_el_for_final_counteroffers,

    ch.avg_approved_el_for_final_counteroffers
        AS counteroffer_first_avg_approved_el_for_final_counteroffers,

    ch.avg_approved_el_for_final_counteroffers
        - b.avg_approved_el_for_final_counteroffers
        AS delta_avg_approved_el_for_final_counteroffers,

    b.total_approved_amount AS baseline_total_approved_amount,
    ch.total_approved_amount AS counteroffer_first_total_approved_amount,
    ch.total_approved_amount - b.total_approved_amount AS delta_total_approved_amount,

    b.total_approved_expected_loss_amount AS baseline_total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    ch.total_approved_expected_loss_amount AS counteroffer_first_total_approved_expected_loss_amount,
    ch.total_approved_expected_loss_amount - b.total_approved_expected_loss_amount
        AS delta_total_approved_expected_loss_amount,

    b.approved_expected_loss_rate AS baseline_approved_expected_loss_rate,
    ch.approved_expected_loss_rate AS counteroffer_first_approved_expected_loss_rate,
    ch.approved_expected_loss_rate - b.approved_expected_loss_rate
        AS delta_approved_expected_loss_rate,

    CASE
        WHEN cr.comparison_readiness_status <> 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
            THEN 'NOT_APPLICABLE_NOT_READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'

        WHEN ch.counteroffer_rate >= b.counteroffer_rate
         AND COALESCE(ch.total_counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount, 0)
             >= COALESCE(b.total_counteroffer_exposure_reduction_amount, 0)
         AND (
                b.avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers IS NULL
             OR ch.avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers IS NULL
             OR ch.avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers
                <= b.avg_approved_pti_for_final_counteroffers
         )
            THEN 'COUNTEROFFER_FIRST_EFFECT_VISIBLE'

        ELSE 'REVIEW_COUNTEROFFER_FIRST_EFFECT'
    END AS counteroffer_first_strategy_effect_status

FROM counteroffer_first_comparisons c

LEFT JOIN comparison_readiness cr
    ON cr.comparison_group_id = c.comparison_group_id

LEFT JOIN counteroffer_metrics b
    ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
   AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
   AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
   AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
   AND b.population_id = c.population_id

LEFT JOIN counteroffer_metrics ch
    ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
   AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
   AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
   AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
   AND ch.population_id = c.population_id

ORDER BY c.comparison_group_id;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.18 — PARAMETER SNAPSHOT PROFILE AUDIT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that every active campaign registry run has exactly one parameter snapshot and that the
    snapshot contains the strategy, product-policy, and run-story payloads needed for governance and
    documentation.

    Section 17.18 answers:

        "Did Section 16 preserve the parameter configuration for every active campaign run?"

WHY THIS SECTION IS REGISTRY-SCOPED:
    Persistent parameter snapshots may contain ad hoc or historical development runs.

    Section 17 evaluates active campaign registry runs.

EXPECTED RESULT:
    One row per active campaign registry run.

    Each row should generally show:
        parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run = 1
        strategy_params_captured_flag = TRUE
        product_policy_params_captured_flag = TRUE
        run_story_params_captured_flag = TRUE
        parameter_snapshot_hash_captured_flag = TRUE
        parameter_snapshot_status = PARAMETER_SNAPSHOT_READY

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_campaign_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module1_run_id,
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

parameter_snapshot_ranked AS (
    SELECT
        p.*,

        COUNT(*) OVER (
            PARTITION BY
                module2_run_id,
                strategy_set_name,
                strategy_name,
                strategy_version,
                module1_scenario_set_name,
                module1_scenario_name,
                population_id
        ) AS parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run,

        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
            PARTITION BY
                module2_run_id,
                strategy_set_name,
                strategy_name,
                strategy_version,
                module1_scenario_set_name,
                module1_scenario_name,
                population_id
            ORDER BY evidence_snapshot_ts DESC NULLS LAST
        ) AS parameter_snapshot_row_rank
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot p
)

SELECT
    r.run_sequence_number,
    r.module1_run_id,
    r.module2_run_id,
    r.showcase_id,
    r.showcase_name,
    r.comparison_group_id,
    r.validation_evidence_group_id,

    r.module1_scenario_set_name,
    r.module1_scenario_name,
    r.population_id,

    r.strategy_name,
    r.strategy_version,

    COALESCE(p.parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run, 0) AS parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run,

    p.evidence_snapshot_ts,
    p.evidence_snapshot_id,

    p.run_registry_match_status,

    p.strategy_params_jsonb IS NOT NULL
        AS strategy_params_captured_flag,

    p.product_policy_params_jsonb IS NOT NULL
        AS product_policy_params_captured_flag,

    CASE
        WHEN p.product_policy_params_jsonb IS NULL THEN NULL
        WHEN jsonb_typeof(p.product_policy_params_jsonb) = 'array'
            THEN jsonb_array_length(p.product_policy_params_jsonb)
        ELSE NULL
    END AS product_policy_snapshot_row_count,

    p.run_story_params_jsonb IS NOT NULL
        AS run_story_params_captured_flag,

    p.parameter_snapshot_hash IS NOT NULL
        AS parameter_snapshot_hash_captured_flag,

    p.parameter_snapshot_hash,

    CASE
        WHEN COALESCE(p.parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run, 0) = 0
            THEN 'PARAMETER_SNAPSHOT_MISSING'

        WHEN COALESCE(p.parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run, 0) > 1
            THEN 'DUPLICATE_PARAMETER_SNAPSHOT_REVIEW_REQUIRED'

        WHEN p.strategy_params_jsonb IS NULL
          OR p.product_policy_params_jsonb IS NULL
          OR p.run_story_params_jsonb IS NULL
          OR p.parameter_snapshot_hash IS NULL
            THEN 'PARAMETER_PAYLOAD_REVIEW_REQUIRED'

        WHEN jsonb_typeof(p.product_policy_params_jsonb) <> 'array'
          OR jsonb_array_length(p.product_policy_params_jsonb) = 0
            THEN 'PRODUCT_POLICY_PAYLOAD_REVIEW_REQUIRED'

        WHEN p.module2_run_id IS DISTINCT FROM r.module2_run_id
          OR p.run_sequence_number IS DISTINCT FROM r.run_sequence_number
          OR p.module1_run_id IS DISTINCT FROM r.module1_run_id
          OR p.showcase_id IS DISTINCT FROM r.showcase_id
          OR p.comparison_group_id IS DISTINCT FROM r.comparison_group_id
          OR p.validation_evidence_group_id IS DISTINCT FROM r.validation_evidence_group_id
            THEN 'PARAMETER_SOURCE_LINEAGE_REVIEW_REQUIRED'

        ELSE 'PARAMETER_SNAPSHOT_READY'
    END AS parameter_snapshot_status

FROM active_campaign_runs r

LEFT JOIN parameter_snapshot_ranked p
    ON p.module2_run_id = r.module2_run_id
   AND p.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
   AND p.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
   AND p.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
   AND p.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
   AND p.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
   AND p.population_id = r.population_id
   AND p.parameter_snapshot_row_rank = 1

ORDER BY r.run_sequence_number;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.19 — PRODUCT GUARDRAIL POLICY SNAPSHOT EXACT-VALUE AUDIT
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Confirm that active campaign PRODUCT_SPECIFIC_GUARDRAIL_STRATEGY runs captured the intended
    canonical product-guardrail values for:

        UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN
        REVOLVING_LINE

WHY THIS MATTERS:
    Structural campaign acceptance can pass even when a product-policy parameter was populated with
    the wrong value.

    This exact-value audit closes that gap.

WHY THIS SECTION IS REGISTRY-SCOPED:
    The audit starts from active campaign registry rows and then joins to parameter snapshots.

    This prevents historical ad hoc PRODUCT_SPECIFIC_GUARDRAIL_STRATEGY snapshots from inflating the
    active campaign audit.

DYNAMIC EXPECTED ROW COUNT:
    Expected audit rows are derived as:

        active PRODUCT_SPECIFIC_GUARDRAIL_STRATEGY campaign runs
        × audited product count

    The audited product count is currently two:
        UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN
        REVOLVING_LINE

CANONICAL VALUE BOUNDARY:
    The exact product-policy values below are intentionally fixed because this section validates the
    specific product-guardrail profile design.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH product_guardrail_campaign_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
      AND strategy_name = 'PRODUCT_SPECIFIC_GUARDRAIL_STRATEGY'
),

parameter_snapshots_by_run AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run,

        (ARRAY_AGG(product_policy_params_jsonb ORDER BY evidence_snapshot_ts DESC NULLS LAST))[1]
            AS product_policy_params_jsonb

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot

    GROUP BY
        module2_run_id,
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

product_guardrail_runs AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,

        r.module1_scenario_set_name,
        r.module1_scenario_name,
        r.population_id,

        r.strategy_set_name,
        r.strategy_name,
        r.strategy_version,

        COALESCE(p.parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run, 0)
            AS parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run,

        p.product_policy_params_jsonb

    FROM product_guardrail_campaign_runs r

    LEFT JOIN parameter_snapshots_by_run p
        ON p.module2_run_id = r.module2_run_id
       AND p.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND p.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND p.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND p.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND p.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND p.population_id = r.population_id
),

expected_product_guardrail_policy AS (
    SELECT *
    FROM (
        VALUES
            (
                'UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN'::TEXT,
                0.130000::NUMERIC,
                0.220000::NUMERIC,
                0.320000::NUMERIC,
                0.110000::NUMERIC,
                2500.00::NUMERIC,
                5000.00::NUMERIC,
                8500.00::NUMERIC,
                2000.00::NUMERIC,
                1000.00::NUMERIC,
                27500.00::NUMERIC,
                0.500000::NUMERIC,
                0.500000::NUMERIC
            ),
            (
                'REVOLVING_LINE'::TEXT,
                0.100000::NUMERIC,
                0.180000::NUMERIC,
                0.280000::NUMERIC,
                0.080000::NUMERIC,
                1500.00::NUMERIC,
                3200.00::NUMERIC,
                6500.00::NUMERIC,
                1400.00::NUMERIC,
                1000.00::NUMERIC,
                16000.00::NUMERIC,
                0.500000::NUMERIC,
                0.500000::NUMERIC
            )
    ) AS v(
        product_type,
        expected_product_approve_max_pti,
        expected_product_review_max_pti,
        expected_product_decline_min_pti,
        expected_counteroffer_target_pti,
        expected_product_approve_max_requested_el,
        expected_product_review_max_requested_el,
        expected_product_decline_min_requested_el,
        expected_product_approved_el_cap,
        expected_product_min_approved_amount,
        expected_product_max_approved_amount,
        expected_product_min_counteroffer_pct,
        expected_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct
    )
),

expected_run_product_rows AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,

        r.module1_scenario_set_name,
        r.module1_scenario_name,
        r.population_id,

        r.strategy_name,
        r.strategy_version,

        r.parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run,

        e.*
    FROM product_guardrail_runs r
    CROSS JOIN expected_product_guardrail_policy e
),

actual_product_guardrail_policy_raw AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,

        pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_type' AS product_type,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_approve_max_pti')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_approve_max_pti,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_review_max_pti')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_review_max_pti,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_decline_min_pti')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_decline_min_pti,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'counteroffer_target_pti')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_counteroffer_target_pti,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_approve_max_requested_el')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_approve_max_requested_el,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_review_max_requested_el')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_review_max_requested_el,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_decline_min_requested_el')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_decline_min_requested_el,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_approved_el_cap')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_approved_el_cap,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_min_approved_amount')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_min_approved_amount,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_max_approved_amount')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_max_approved_amount,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_min_counteroffer_pct')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_min_counteroffer_pct,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_max_exposure_reduction_pct')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct

    FROM product_guardrail_runs r

    CROSS JOIN LATERAL jsonb_array_elements(
        COALESCE(r.product_policy_params_jsonb, '[]'::jsonb)
    ) AS pp(product_policy_row)

    WHERE pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_type' IN (
        'UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN',
        'REVOLVING_LINE'
    )
),

actual_product_guardrail_policy AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,
        product_type,

        COUNT(*) AS actual_product_policy_rows_for_product,

        MAX(actual_product_approve_max_pti) AS actual_product_approve_max_pti,
        MAX(actual_product_review_max_pti) AS actual_product_review_max_pti,
        MAX(actual_product_decline_min_pti) AS actual_product_decline_min_pti,
        MAX(actual_counteroffer_target_pti) AS actual_counteroffer_target_pti,

        MAX(actual_product_approve_max_requested_el) AS actual_product_approve_max_requested_el,
        MAX(actual_product_review_max_requested_el) AS actual_product_review_max_requested_el,
        MAX(actual_product_decline_min_requested_el) AS actual_product_decline_min_requested_el,
        MAX(actual_product_approved_el_cap) AS actual_product_approved_el_cap,

        MAX(actual_product_min_approved_amount) AS actual_product_min_approved_amount,
        MAX(actual_product_max_approved_amount) AS actual_product_max_approved_amount,
        MAX(actual_product_min_counteroffer_pct) AS actual_product_min_counteroffer_pct,
        MAX(actual_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct) AS actual_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct

    FROM actual_product_guardrail_policy_raw

    GROUP BY
        module2_run_id,
        product_type
),

policy_comparison AS (
    SELECT
        e.*,

        COALESCE(a.actual_product_policy_rows_for_product, 0)
            AS actual_product_policy_rows_for_product,

        a.actual_product_approve_max_pti,
        a.actual_product_review_max_pti,
        a.actual_product_decline_min_pti,
        a.actual_counteroffer_target_pti,

        a.actual_product_approve_max_requested_el,
        a.actual_product_review_max_requested_el,
        a.actual_product_decline_min_requested_el,
        a.actual_product_approved_el_cap,

        a.actual_product_min_approved_amount,
        a.actual_product_max_approved_amount,
        a.actual_product_min_counteroffer_pct,
        a.actual_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct,

        CASE
            WHEN COALESCE(a.actual_product_policy_rows_for_product, 0) <> 1
                THEN NULL

            ELSE
                (
                    CASE WHEN a.actual_product_approve_max_pti IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_approve_max_pti THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_product_review_max_pti IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_review_max_pti THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_product_decline_min_pti IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_decline_min_pti THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_counteroffer_target_pti IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_counteroffer_target_pti THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_product_approve_max_requested_el IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_approve_max_requested_el THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_product_review_max_requested_el IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_review_max_requested_el THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_product_decline_min_requested_el IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_decline_min_requested_el THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_product_approved_el_cap IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_approved_el_cap THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_product_min_approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_min_approved_amount THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_product_max_approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_max_approved_amount THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_product_min_counteroffer_pct IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_min_counteroffer_pct THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                  + CASE WHEN a.actual_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct THEN 1 ELSE 0 END
                )
        END AS product_policy_field_mismatch_count

    FROM expected_run_product_rows e

    LEFT JOIN actual_product_guardrail_policy a
        ON a.module2_run_id = e.module2_run_id
       AND a.product_type = e.product_type
)

SELECT
    module2_run_id,
    run_sequence_number,

    module1_scenario_set_name,
    module1_scenario_name,
    population_id,

    strategy_name,
    strategy_version,

    parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run,

    product_type,

    actual_product_policy_rows_for_product,

    expected_product_approve_max_pti,
    actual_product_approve_max_pti,

    expected_product_review_max_pti,
    actual_product_review_max_pti,

    expected_product_decline_min_pti,
    actual_product_decline_min_pti,

    expected_counteroffer_target_pti,
    actual_counteroffer_target_pti,

    expected_product_approve_max_requested_el,
    actual_product_approve_max_requested_el,

    expected_product_review_max_requested_el,
    actual_product_review_max_requested_el,

    expected_product_decline_min_requested_el,
    actual_product_decline_min_requested_el,

    expected_product_approved_el_cap,
    actual_product_approved_el_cap,

    expected_product_min_approved_amount,
    actual_product_min_approved_amount,

    expected_product_max_approved_amount,
    actual_product_max_approved_amount,

    expected_product_min_counteroffer_pct,
    actual_product_min_counteroffer_pct,

    expected_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct,
    actual_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct,

    product_policy_field_mismatch_count,

    CASE
        WHEN parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run = 0
            THEN 'PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_PARAMETER_SNAPSHOT_MISSING'

        WHEN parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run > 1
            THEN 'PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_PARAMETER_SNAPSHOT_DUPLICATE_REVIEW_REQUIRED'

        WHEN actual_product_policy_rows_for_product = 0
            THEN 'PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_POLICY_ROW_MISSING'

        WHEN actual_product_policy_rows_for_product > 1
            THEN 'PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_POLICY_ROW_DUPLICATE_REVIEW_REQUIRED'

        WHEN product_policy_field_mismatch_count = 0
            THEN 'PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_POLICY_VALUES_MATCH'

        ELSE 'PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_POLICY_VALUE_MISMATCH'
    END AS product_guardrail_policy_value_status

FROM policy_comparison

ORDER BY
    run_sequence_number,
    product_type;



/***************************************************************************************************
SECTION 17.20 — FINAL MODULE 2 CAMPAIGN ACCEPTANCE ROLLUP
****************************************************************************************************

BUSINESS PURPOSE:
    Produce the final one-row campaign acceptance status after archive, registry, comparison,
    matched-source, evidence, convention, parameter-snapshot, and product-policy checks.

    Section 17.20 answers:

        "Is the completed active Module 2 campaign structurally ready for executive analysis,
         validation-summary drafting, README interpretation, and LinkedIn storyline development?"

DYNAMIC ACCEPTANCE DESIGN:
    Section 17.20 derives expected campaign shape from active registry and source evidence.

    It does not hardcode:
        campaign run count,
        comparison group count,
        archive rows per slice,
        total archive rows,
        validation evidence row count,
        product-guardrail campaign run count,
        or product-guardrail audit row count.

DERIVED EXPECTATIONS:
    expected_campaign_runs:
        count of active campaign registry rows.

    expected_comparison_groups:
        count of active comparison registry rows.

    expected_total_active_campaign_source_rows:
        sum of selected Module 1 source-population rows across active campaign runs.

    expected_validation_key_count:
        distinct validation_area + validation_test_name + validation_category across active campaign
        validation evidence.

    expected_product_guardrail_policy_rows:
        active PRODUCT_SPECIFIC_GUARDRAIL_STRATEGY campaign runs × audited product count.

CANONICAL PRODUCT-GUARDRAIL VALUE BOUNDARY:
    The UPL and revolving-line exact values remain fixed because the audit validates the intended
    product-guardrail profile.

FINAL STATUS VALUES:
    MODULE_2_CAMPAIGN_RESULTS_READY_FOR_ANALYSIS

    STRUCTURAL_ACCEPTANCE_PASS_BUT_PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_POLICY_REVIEW_REQUIRED

    REVIEW_MODULE_2_CAMPAIGN_RESULTS_BEFORE_ANALYSIS

READ-ONLY BOUNDARY:
    Section 17.20 does not modify archive, latest-run, evidence, registry, strategy-parameter, or
    product-policy rows.

***************************************************************************************************/

WITH active_campaign_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module1_run_id,
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,
        showcase_id,
        showcase_name,
        comparison_group_id,
        validation_evidence_group_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

campaign_registry_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS active_campaign_registry_rows,

        COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT (
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id
        )) AS duplicate_active_campaign_technical_key_rows
    FROM active_campaign_runs
),

active_comparisons AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,
        comparison_set_name,

        baseline_module2_run_id,
        challenger_module2_run_id,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        baseline_strategy_set_name,
        baseline_strategy_name,
        baseline_strategy_version,

        challenger_strategy_set_name,
        challenger_strategy_name,
        challenger_strategy_version
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_comparison_campaign_registry
    WHERE registry_active_flag IS TRUE
),

comparison_registry_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS active_comparison_registry_rows,

        COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT comparison_group_id)
            AS duplicate_active_comparison_group_rows
    FROM active_comparisons
),

module1_source_counts AS (
    SELECT
        scenario_set_name AS module1_scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name AS module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_module1_source_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.synthetic_applications_scenario_archive
    GROUP BY
        scenario_set_name,
        scenario_name,
        population_id
),

archive_counts AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS archived_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT application_id) AS distinct_application_id_count
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

active_campaign_archive_join AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,

        r.strategy_set_name,
        r.strategy_name,
        r.strategy_version,
        r.module1_scenario_set_name,
        r.module1_scenario_name,
        r.population_id,

        s.expected_module1_source_rows,
        s.expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(a.archived_rows, 0) AS archived_rows,
        COALESCE(a.distinct_application_id_count, 0) AS distinct_application_id_count

    FROM active_campaign_runs r

    LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
        ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = r.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts a
        ON a.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND a.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND a.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND a.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND a.population_id = r.population_id
),

active_campaign_archive_rows AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,
        a.*
    FROM active_campaign_runs r

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive a
        ON a.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND a.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND a.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND a.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND a.population_id = r.population_id
),

archive_grain_duplicates AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS duplicate_archive_grain_count
    FROM (
        SELECT
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id,
            application_id,
            COUNT(*) AS row_count
        FROM active_campaign_archive_rows
        GROUP BY
            strategy_set_name,
            strategy_name,
            strategy_version,
            module1_scenario_set_name,
            module1_scenario_name,
            population_id,
            application_id
        HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
    ) d
),

archive_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS active_campaign_registry_rows_for_archive_check,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
        ) AS active_runs_missing_module1_source_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
              AND expected_module1_source_rows
                    <> expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count
        ) AS active_runs_with_module1_source_application_id_grain_issue,

        SUM(COALESCE(expected_module1_source_rows, 0))
            AS expected_total_active_campaign_source_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE archived_rows > 0
        ) AS active_runs_with_archive_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE archived_rows = 0
        ) AS active_runs_missing_archive_rows,

        SUM(archived_rows) AS total_active_campaign_archived_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
              AND archived_rows <> expected_module1_source_rows
        ) AS active_runs_with_archive_row_count_mismatch,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_module1_source_rows IS NOT NULL
              AND distinct_application_id_count <> expected_module1_source_rows
        ) AS active_runs_with_archive_application_id_grain_issue
    FROM active_campaign_archive_join
),

baseline_applications AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        b.application_id
    FROM active_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id
),

challenger_applications AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT
        c.comparison_group_id,
        ch.application_id
    FROM active_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id
),

comparison_application_union AS (
    SELECT
        COALESCE(b.comparison_group_id, ch.comparison_group_id)
            AS comparison_group_id,

        b.application_id AS baseline_application_id,
        ch.application_id AS challenger_application_id

    FROM baseline_applications b

    FULL OUTER JOIN challenger_applications ch
        ON ch.comparison_group_id = b.comparison_group_id
       AND ch.application_id = b.application_id
),

comparison_application_overlap AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_application_id IS NOT NULL
              AND challenger_application_id IS NOT NULL
        ) AS matched_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_application_id IS NOT NULL
              AND challenger_application_id IS NULL
        ) AS baseline_only_application_id_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_application_id IS NULL
              AND challenger_application_id IS NOT NULL
        ) AS challenger_only_application_id_count

    FROM comparison_application_union
    GROUP BY comparison_group_id
),

comparison_readiness_by_group AS (
    SELECT
        c.comparison_group_id,

        s.expected_module1_source_rows,
        s.expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) AS baseline_archived_rows,
        COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) AS challenger_archived_rows,

        COALESCE(b.distinct_application_id_count, 0)
            AS baseline_distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(ch.distinct_application_id_count, 0)
            AS challenger_distinct_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(o.matched_application_id_count, 0)
            AS matched_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(o.baseline_only_application_id_count, 0)
            AS baseline_only_application_id_count,

        COALESCE(o.challenger_only_application_id_count, 0)
            AS challenger_only_application_id_count,

        CASE
            WHEN s.expected_module1_source_rows IS NULL
                THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_COUNT_NOT_FOUND'

            WHEN s.expected_module1_source_rows
                    <> s.expected_module1_distinct_application_id_count
                THEN 'REVIEW_MODULE1_SOURCE_APPLICATION_ID_GRAIN'

            WHEN COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) = 0
              OR COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) = 0
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_ARCHIVE_MISSING_SLICE'

            WHEN COALESCE(b.archived_rows, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(ch.archived_rows, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(b.distinct_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(ch.distinct_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_ARCHIVE_ROW_COUNT_OR_GRAIN'

            WHEN COALESCE(o.matched_application_id_count, 0) <> s.expected_module1_source_rows
              OR COALESCE(o.baseline_only_application_id_count, 0) <> 0
              OR COALESCE(o.challenger_only_application_id_count, 0) <> 0
                THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_APPLICATION_OVERLAP'

            ELSE 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
        END AS comparison_readiness_status

    FROM active_comparisons c

    LEFT JOIN module1_source_counts s
        ON s.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN archive_counts ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id

    LEFT JOIN comparison_application_overlap o
        ON o.comparison_group_id = c.comparison_group_id
),

comparison_readiness_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS comparison_group_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE comparison_readiness_status = 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
        ) AS comparison_ready_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE comparison_readiness_status <> 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
        ) AS comparison_review_count
    FROM comparison_readiness_by_group
),

matched_source_rows AS (
    SELECT
        c.comparison_group_id,

        b.application_id,

        b.product_type_policy_key AS baseline_product_type_policy_key,
        ch.product_type_policy_key AS challenger_product_type_policy_key,

        b.score_band_policy_key AS baseline_score_band_policy_key,
        ch.score_band_policy_key AS challenger_score_band_policy_key,

        b.credit_score AS baseline_credit_score,
        ch.credit_score AS challenger_credit_score,

        b.annual_income AS baseline_annual_income,
        ch.annual_income AS challenger_annual_income,

        b.requested_amount AS baseline_requested_amount,
        ch.requested_amount AS challenger_requested_amount,

        b.requested_monthly_payment_proxy AS baseline_requested_monthly_payment_proxy,
        ch.requested_monthly_payment_proxy AS challenger_requested_monthly_payment_proxy,

        b.requested_payment_to_income_ratio AS baseline_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,
        ch.requested_payment_to_income_ratio AS challenger_requested_payment_to_income_ratio,

        b.amount_to_income_ratio AS baseline_amount_to_income_ratio,
        ch.amount_to_income_ratio AS challenger_amount_to_income_ratio,

        b.estimated_pd AS baseline_estimated_pd,
        ch.estimated_pd AS challenger_estimated_pd,

        b.estimated_lgd AS baseline_estimated_lgd,
        ch.estimated_lgd AS challenger_estimated_lgd,

        b.requested_expected_loss_amount AS baseline_requested_expected_loss_amount,
        ch.requested_expected_loss_amount AS challenger_requested_expected_loss_amount,

        b.module1_scenario_set_name AS baseline_module1_scenario_set_name,
        ch.module1_scenario_set_name AS challenger_module1_scenario_set_name,

        b.module1_scenario_name AS baseline_module1_scenario_name,
        ch.module1_scenario_name AS challenger_module1_scenario_name,

        b.population_id AS baseline_population_id,
        ch.population_id AS challenger_population_id

    FROM active_comparisons c

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive b
        ON b.strategy_set_name = c.baseline_strategy_set_name
       AND b.strategy_name = c.baseline_strategy_name
       AND b.strategy_version = c.baseline_strategy_version
       AND b.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND b.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND b.population_id = c.population_id

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive ch
        ON ch.strategy_set_name = c.challenger_strategy_set_name
       AND ch.strategy_name = c.challenger_strategy_name
       AND ch.strategy_version = c.challenger_strategy_version
       AND ch.module1_scenario_set_name = c.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND ch.module1_scenario_name = c.module1_scenario_name
       AND ch.population_id = c.population_id
       AND ch.application_id = b.application_id
),

source_consistency_by_group AS (
    SELECT
        comparison_group_id,

        COUNT(*) AS matched_application_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE baseline_product_type_policy_key IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_product_type_policy_key
               OR baseline_score_band_policy_key IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_score_band_policy_key
               OR baseline_credit_score IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_credit_score
               OR baseline_annual_income IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_annual_income
               OR baseline_requested_amount IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_amount
               OR baseline_requested_monthly_payment_proxy IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_monthly_payment_proxy
               OR baseline_requested_payment_to_income_ratio IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_payment_to_income_ratio
               OR baseline_amount_to_income_ratio IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_amount_to_income_ratio
               OR baseline_estimated_pd IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_estimated_pd
               OR baseline_estimated_lgd IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_estimated_lgd
               OR baseline_requested_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_requested_expected_loss_amount
               OR baseline_module1_scenario_set_name IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_module1_scenario_set_name
               OR baseline_module1_scenario_name IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_module1_scenario_name
               OR baseline_population_id IS DISTINCT FROM challenger_population_id
        ) AS source_field_mismatch_count

    FROM matched_source_rows
    GROUP BY comparison_group_id
),

source_consistency_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS source_consistency_group_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE cr.comparison_readiness_status = 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
              AND COALESCE(sc.matched_application_count, 0) = cr.expected_module1_source_rows
              AND COALESCE(sc.source_field_mismatch_count, 0) = 0
        ) AS source_consistency_pass_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE cr.comparison_readiness_status <> 'READY_FOR_MATCHED_COMPARISON'
               OR COALESCE(sc.matched_application_count, 0) <> cr.expected_module1_source_rows
               OR COALESCE(sc.source_field_mismatch_count, 0) <> 0
        ) AS source_consistency_review_count,

        COALESCE(SUM(COALESCE(sc.source_field_mismatch_count, 0)), 0)::BIGINT
            AS total_source_field_mismatch_rows

    FROM comparison_readiness_by_group cr

    LEFT JOIN source_consistency_by_group sc
        ON sc.comparison_group_id = cr.comparison_group_id
),

executive_evidence_by_run AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS executive_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_evidence_summary
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

parameter_evidence_by_run AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS parameter_snapshot_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

validation_key_catalog AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            v.validation_area,
            v.validation_test_name,
            v.validation_category
        )) AS expected_validation_key_count
    FROM active_campaign_runs r

    JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence v
        ON v.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND v.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND v.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND v.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND v.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND v.population_id = r.population_id
),

validation_evidence_by_run AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS validation_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            validation_area,
            validation_test_name,
            validation_category
        )) AS validation_distinct_key_count,

        COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT (
            validation_area,
            validation_test_name,
            validation_category
        )) AS duplicate_validation_key_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_validation_evidence
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

archive_segment_expected AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            a.product_type_policy_key,
            a.score_band_policy_key,
            a.product_score_policy_segment
        )) AS expected_segment_rows
    FROM active_campaign_runs r

    LEFT JOIN credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_decisions_archive a
        ON a.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND a.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND a.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND a.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND a.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND a.population_id = r.population_id

    GROUP BY r.module2_run_id
),

segment_evidence_by_run AS (
    SELECT
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS segment_rows,

        COUNT(DISTINCT (
            product_type_policy_key,
            score_band_policy_key,
            product_score_policy_segment
        )) AS segment_distinct_key_count,

        COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT (
            product_type_policy_key,
            score_band_policy_key,
            product_score_policy_segment
        )) AS duplicate_segment_key_rows
    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_segment_evidence_summary
    GROUP BY
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

evidence_by_campaign_run AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,

        COALESCE(e.executive_rows, 0) AS executive_rows,
        COALESCE(p.parameter_snapshot_rows, 0) AS parameter_snapshot_rows,

        COALESCE(v.validation_rows, 0) AS validation_rows,
        COALESCE(v.validation_distinct_key_count, 0) AS validation_distinct_key_count,
        COALESCE(v.duplicate_validation_key_rows, 0) AS duplicate_validation_key_rows,

        COALESCE(vkc.expected_validation_key_count, 0) AS expected_validation_key_count,

        COALESCE(ase.expected_segment_rows, 0) AS expected_segment_rows,
        COALESCE(s.segment_rows, 0) AS segment_rows,
        COALESCE(s.segment_distinct_key_count, 0) AS segment_distinct_key_count,
        COALESCE(s.duplicate_segment_key_rows, 0) AS duplicate_segment_key_rows

    FROM active_campaign_runs r

    CROSS JOIN validation_key_catalog vkc

    LEFT JOIN archive_segment_expected ase
        ON ase.module2_run_id = r.module2_run_id

    LEFT JOIN executive_evidence_by_run e
        ON e.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND e.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND e.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND e.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND e.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND e.population_id = r.population_id

    LEFT JOIN parameter_evidence_by_run p
        ON p.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND p.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND p.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND p.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND p.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND p.population_id = r.population_id

    LEFT JOIN validation_evidence_by_run v
        ON v.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND v.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND v.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND v.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND v.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND v.population_id = r.population_id

    LEFT JOIN segment_evidence_by_run s
        ON s.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND s.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND s.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND s.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND s.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND s.population_id = r.population_id
),

evidence_summary AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS registry_run_count_for_evidence_check,

        MAX(expected_validation_key_count)
            AS expected_validation_key_count,

        COALESCE(SUM(executive_rows), 0)::BIGINT AS executive_evidence_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE executive_rows = 1
        ) AS executive_evidence_complete_run_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE executive_rows <> 1
        ) AS executive_evidence_issue_run_count,

        COALESCE(SUM(parameter_snapshot_rows), 0)::BIGINT
            AS parameter_snapshot_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE parameter_snapshot_rows = 1
        ) AS parameter_snapshot_complete_run_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE parameter_snapshot_rows <> 1
        ) AS parameter_snapshot_issue_run_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_validation_key_count > 0
              AND validation_rows = expected_validation_key_count
              AND validation_distinct_key_count = expected_validation_key_count
              AND duplicate_validation_key_rows = 0
        ) AS validation_evidence_complete_run_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_validation_key_count = 0
               OR validation_rows <> expected_validation_key_count
               OR validation_distinct_key_count <> expected_validation_key_count
               OR duplicate_validation_key_rows <> 0
        ) AS validation_evidence_incomplete_run_count,

        MIN(validation_rows) AS min_validation_rows_per_run,
        MAX(validation_rows) AS max_validation_rows_per_run,
        COALESCE(SUM(validation_rows), 0)::BIGINT
            AS total_validation_evidence_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_segment_rows > 0
              AND segment_rows = expected_segment_rows
              AND segment_distinct_key_count = expected_segment_rows
              AND duplicate_segment_key_rows = 0
        ) AS segment_evidence_complete_run_count,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE expected_segment_rows = 0
               OR segment_rows <> expected_segment_rows
               OR segment_distinct_key_count <> expected_segment_rows
               OR duplicate_segment_key_rows <> 0
        ) AS segment_evidence_issue_run_count,

        MIN(expected_segment_rows) AS min_expected_segment_rows_per_run,
        MAX(expected_segment_rows) AS max_expected_segment_rows_per_run,
        MIN(segment_rows) AS min_segment_rows_per_run,
        MAX(segment_rows) AS max_segment_rows_per_run,
        COALESCE(SUM(segment_rows), 0)::BIGINT
            AS total_segment_evidence_rows
    FROM evidence_by_campaign_run
),

convention_violations AS (
    SELECT
        COUNT(*) AS active_campaign_archived_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE (
                COALESCE(approval_flag::INT, 0)
                + COALESCE(counteroffer_flag::INT, 0)
                + COALESCE(manual_review_flag::INT, 0)
                + COALESCE(decline_flag::INT, 0)
            ) <> 1
        ) AS final_outcome_flag_count_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE simulated_offer_exposure_flag
                  IS DISTINCT FROM (decision_outcome IN ('APPROVE', 'COUNTEROFFER'))
        ) AS simulated_offer_exposure_flag_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
              AND approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_amount
        ) AS approve_amount_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND (
                    approved_amount IS NULL
                 OR approved_amount <= 0
                 OR approved_amount >= requested_amount
                 OR counteroffer_amount IS DISTINCT FROM approved_amount
              )
        ) AS counteroffer_amount_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND approved_amount IS NOT NULL
        ) AS manual_review_amount_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
              AND approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
        ) AS decline_amount_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
              AND approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS DISTINCT FROM requested_monthly_payment_proxy
        ) AS approve_payment_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND (
                    approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS NULL
                 OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS NULL
                 OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio > counteroffer_target_pti
              )
        ) AS counteroffer_affordability_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND (
                    approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS NOT NULL
                 OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS NOT NULL
              )
        ) AS manual_review_affordability_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
              AND (
                    approved_monthly_payment_proxy IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
                 OR approved_payment_to_income_ratio IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
              )
        ) AS decline_affordability_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
              AND approved_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM requested_expected_loss_amount
        ) AS approve_expected_loss_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
              AND (
                    approved_expected_loss_amount IS NULL
                 OR approved_expected_loss_amount < 0
                 OR approved_expected_loss_amount > requested_expected_loss_amount
                 OR approved_expected_loss_amount > product_approved_el_cap
              )
        ) AS counteroffer_expected_loss_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
              AND approved_expected_loss_amount IS NOT NULL
        ) AS manual_review_expected_loss_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
              AND approved_expected_loss_amount IS DISTINCT FROM 0::NUMERIC
        ) AS decline_expected_loss_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE primary_reason_code IS NULL
               OR primary_reason_family IS NULL
               OR triggered_reason_code_list IS NULL
               OR reason_code_count IS NULL
               OR reason_code_count < 1
        ) AS reason_code_completeness_violation_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE (
                    decision_outcome = 'APPROVE'
                AND primary_reason_family IS DISTINCT FROM 'APPROVAL'
            )
            OR (
                    decision_outcome = 'COUNTEROFFER'
                AND primary_reason_family IS DISTINCT FROM 'COUNTEROFFER'
            )
            OR (
                    decision_outcome = 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
                AND primary_reason_family IS DISTINCT FROM 'MANUAL_REVIEW'
            )
            OR (
                    decision_outcome = 'DECLINE'
                AND primary_reason_family IS DISTINCT FROM 'POLICY_STOP'
            )
        ) AS reason_family_alignment_violation_rows

    FROM active_campaign_archive_rows
),

convention_summary AS (
    SELECT
        active_campaign_archived_rows,

        (
            final_outcome_flag_count_violation_rows
            + simulated_offer_exposure_flag_violation_rows
            + approve_amount_violation_rows
            + counteroffer_amount_violation_rows
            + manual_review_amount_violation_rows
            + decline_amount_violation_rows
            + approve_payment_violation_rows
            + counteroffer_affordability_violation_rows
            + manual_review_affordability_violation_rows
            + decline_affordability_violation_rows
            + approve_expected_loss_violation_rows
            + counteroffer_expected_loss_violation_rows
            + manual_review_expected_loss_violation_rows
            + decline_expected_loss_violation_rows
            + reason_code_completeness_violation_rows
            + reason_family_alignment_violation_rows
        ) AS critical_convention_violation_count
    FROM convention_violations
),

product_guardrail_campaign_runs AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,
        run_sequence_number,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
    FROM active_campaign_runs
    WHERE strategy_name = 'PRODUCT_SPECIFIC_GUARDRAIL_STRATEGY'
),

parameter_snapshots_by_run AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,

        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,

        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id,

        COUNT(*) AS parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run,

        (ARRAY_AGG(product_policy_params_jsonb ORDER BY evidence_snapshot_ts DESC NULLS LAST))[1]
            AS product_policy_params_jsonb

    FROM credit_decisioning_sim.strategy_run_parameter_snapshot

    GROUP BY
        module2_run_id,
        strategy_set_name,
        strategy_name,
        strategy_version,
        module1_scenario_set_name,
        module1_scenario_name,
        population_id
),

product_guardrail_runs AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.run_sequence_number,

        r.strategy_set_name,
        r.strategy_name,
        r.strategy_version,

        r.module1_scenario_set_name,
        r.module1_scenario_name,
        r.population_id,

        COALESCE(p.parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run, 0)
            AS parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run,

        p.product_policy_params_jsonb

    FROM product_guardrail_campaign_runs r

    LEFT JOIN parameter_snapshots_by_run p
        ON p.module2_run_id = r.module2_run_id
       AND p.strategy_set_name = r.strategy_set_name
       AND p.strategy_name = r.strategy_name
       AND p.strategy_version = r.strategy_version
       AND p.module1_scenario_set_name = r.module1_scenario_set_name
       AND p.module1_scenario_name = r.module1_scenario_name
       AND p.population_id = r.population_id
),

expected_product_guardrail_policy AS (
    SELECT *
    FROM (
        VALUES
            (
                'UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN'::TEXT,
                0.130000::NUMERIC,
                0.220000::NUMERIC,
                0.320000::NUMERIC,
                0.110000::NUMERIC,
                2500.00::NUMERIC,
                5000.00::NUMERIC,
                8500.00::NUMERIC,
                2000.00::NUMERIC,
                1000.00::NUMERIC,
                27500.00::NUMERIC,
                0.500000::NUMERIC,
                0.500000::NUMERIC
            ),
            (
                'REVOLVING_LINE'::TEXT,
                0.100000::NUMERIC,
                0.180000::NUMERIC,
                0.280000::NUMERIC,
                0.080000::NUMERIC,
                1500.00::NUMERIC,
                3200.00::NUMERIC,
                6500.00::NUMERIC,
                1400.00::NUMERIC,
                1000.00::NUMERIC,
                16000.00::NUMERIC,
                0.500000::NUMERIC,
                0.500000::NUMERIC
            )
    ) AS v(
        product_type,
        expected_product_approve_max_pti,
        expected_product_review_max_pti,
        expected_product_decline_min_pti,
        expected_counteroffer_target_pti,
        expected_product_approve_max_requested_el,
        expected_product_review_max_requested_el,
        expected_product_decline_min_requested_el,
        expected_product_approved_el_cap,
        expected_product_min_approved_amount,
        expected_product_max_approved_amount,
        expected_product_min_counteroffer_pct,
        expected_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct
    )
),

expected_product_guardrail_rows AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,
        r.parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run,
        e.*
    FROM product_guardrail_runs r
    CROSS JOIN expected_product_guardrail_policy e
),

actual_product_guardrail_policy_raw AS (
    SELECT
        r.module2_run_id,

        pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_type' AS product_type,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_approve_max_pti')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_approve_max_pti,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_review_max_pti')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_review_max_pti,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_decline_min_pti')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_decline_min_pti,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'counteroffer_target_pti')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_counteroffer_target_pti,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_approve_max_requested_el')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_approve_max_requested_el,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_review_max_requested_el')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_review_max_requested_el,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_decline_min_requested_el')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_decline_min_requested_el,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_approved_el_cap')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_approved_el_cap,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_min_approved_amount')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_min_approved_amount,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_max_approved_amount')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_max_approved_amount,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_min_counteroffer_pct')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_min_counteroffer_pct,

        (pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_max_exposure_reduction_pct')::NUMERIC
            AS actual_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct

    FROM product_guardrail_runs r

    CROSS JOIN LATERAL jsonb_array_elements(
        COALESCE(r.product_policy_params_jsonb, '[]'::jsonb)
    ) AS pp(product_policy_row)

    WHERE pp.product_policy_row ->> 'product_type' IN (
        'UNSECURED_PERSONAL_LOAN',
        'REVOLVING_LINE'
    )
),

actual_product_guardrail_policy AS (
    SELECT
        module2_run_id,
        product_type,

        COUNT(*) AS actual_product_policy_rows_for_product,

        MAX(actual_product_approve_max_pti) AS actual_product_approve_max_pti,
        MAX(actual_product_review_max_pti) AS actual_product_review_max_pti,
        MAX(actual_product_decline_min_pti) AS actual_product_decline_min_pti,
        MAX(actual_counteroffer_target_pti) AS actual_counteroffer_target_pti,

        MAX(actual_product_approve_max_requested_el) AS actual_product_approve_max_requested_el,
        MAX(actual_product_review_max_requested_el) AS actual_product_review_max_requested_el,
        MAX(actual_product_decline_min_requested_el) AS actual_product_decline_min_requested_el,
        MAX(actual_product_approved_el_cap) AS actual_product_approved_el_cap,

        MAX(actual_product_min_approved_amount) AS actual_product_min_approved_amount,
        MAX(actual_product_max_approved_amount) AS actual_product_max_approved_amount,
        MAX(actual_product_min_counteroffer_pct) AS actual_product_min_counteroffer_pct,
        MAX(actual_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct) AS actual_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct

    FROM actual_product_guardrail_policy_raw

    GROUP BY
        module2_run_id,
        product_type
),

product_guardrail_policy_audit_summary AS (
    SELECT
        (
            SELECT COUNT(*)
            FROM product_guardrail_campaign_runs
        ) AS product_guardrail_campaign_run_count,

        (
            SELECT COUNT(*)
            FROM expected_product_guardrail_policy
        ) AS audited_product_count,

        (
            SELECT COUNT(*)
            FROM product_guardrail_runs
            WHERE parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run = 1
        ) AS product_guardrail_parameter_snapshot_complete_run_count,

        (
            SELECT COUNT(*)
            FROM product_guardrail_runs
            WHERE parameter_snapshot_rows_for_run <> 1
        ) AS product_guardrail_parameter_snapshot_issue_run_count,

        COUNT(*) AS expected_product_guardrail_policy_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE a.product_type IS NULL
        ) AS missing_product_guardrail_policy_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE COALESCE(a.actual_product_policy_rows_for_product, 0) <> 1
        ) AS product_guardrail_policy_row_count_issue_rows,

        COUNT(*) FILTER (
            WHERE COALESCE(a.actual_product_policy_rows_for_product, 0) = 1
              AND (
                    a.actual_product_approve_max_pti IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_approve_max_pti
                 OR a.actual_product_review_max_pti IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_review_max_pti
                 OR a.actual_product_decline_min_pti IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_decline_min_pti
                 OR a.actual_counteroffer_target_pti IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_counteroffer_target_pti
                 OR a.actual_product_approve_max_requested_el IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_approve_max_requested_el
                 OR a.actual_product_review_max_requested_el IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_review_max_requested_el
                 OR a.actual_product_decline_min_requested_el IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_decline_min_requested_el
                 OR a.actual_product_approved_el_cap IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_approved_el_cap
                 OR a.actual_product_min_approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_min_approved_amount
                 OR a.actual_product_max_approved_amount IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_max_approved_amount
                 OR a.actual_product_min_counteroffer_pct IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_min_counteroffer_pct
                 OR a.actual_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct IS DISTINCT FROM e.expected_product_max_exposure_reduction_pct
              )
        ) AS product_guardrail_policy_mismatch_rows

    FROM expected_product_guardrail_rows e

    LEFT JOIN actual_product_guardrail_policy a
        ON a.module2_run_id = e.module2_run_id
       AND a.product_type = e.product_type
),

acceptance_inputs AS (
    SELECT
        /*******************************************************************************************
        Dynamic expected campaign shape.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        cr.active_campaign_registry_rows AS expected_campaign_runs,
        cmpr.active_comparison_registry_rows AS expected_comparison_groups,

        ar.expected_total_active_campaign_source_rows,
        ev.expected_validation_key_count,

        pga.product_guardrail_campaign_run_count
            AS expected_product_guardrail_campaign_runs,

        pga.audited_product_count,
        pga.expected_product_guardrail_policy_rows,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Registry and archive.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        cr.active_campaign_registry_rows,
        cr.duplicate_active_campaign_technical_key_rows,

        cmpr.active_comparison_registry_rows,
        cmpr.duplicate_active_comparison_group_rows,

        ar.active_campaign_registry_rows_for_archive_check,
        ar.active_runs_missing_module1_source_count,
        ar.active_runs_with_module1_source_application_id_grain_issue,
        ar.active_runs_with_archive_rows,
        ar.active_runs_missing_archive_rows,
        ar.total_active_campaign_archived_rows,
        ar.active_runs_with_archive_row_count_mismatch,
        ar.active_runs_with_archive_application_id_grain_issue,

        agd.duplicate_archive_grain_count,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Comparison and source consistency.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        cmp.comparison_group_count,
        cmp.comparison_ready_count,
        cmp.comparison_review_count,

        src.source_consistency_group_count,
        src.source_consistency_pass_count,
        src.source_consistency_review_count,
        src.total_source_field_mismatch_rows,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Evidence.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        ev.registry_run_count_for_evidence_check,

        ev.executive_evidence_rows,
        ev.executive_evidence_complete_run_count,
        ev.executive_evidence_issue_run_count,

        ev.parameter_snapshot_rows,
        ev.parameter_snapshot_complete_run_count,
        ev.parameter_snapshot_issue_run_count,

        ev.validation_evidence_complete_run_count,
        ev.validation_evidence_incomplete_run_count,
        ev.min_validation_rows_per_run,
        ev.max_validation_rows_per_run,
        ev.total_validation_evidence_rows,

        ev.segment_evidence_complete_run_count,
        ev.segment_evidence_issue_run_count,
        ev.min_expected_segment_rows_per_run,
        ev.max_expected_segment_rows_per_run,
        ev.min_segment_rows_per_run,
        ev.max_segment_rows_per_run,
        ev.total_segment_evidence_rows,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Final-output conventions.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        cv.active_campaign_archived_rows,
        cv.critical_convention_violation_count,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Product guardrail policy exact-value audit.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        pga.product_guardrail_campaign_run_count,
        pga.product_guardrail_parameter_snapshot_complete_run_count,
        pga.product_guardrail_parameter_snapshot_issue_run_count,
        pga.expected_product_guardrail_policy_rows AS actual_product_guardrail_policy_rows_checked,
        pga.missing_product_guardrail_policy_rows,
        pga.product_guardrail_policy_row_count_issue_rows,
        pga.product_guardrail_policy_mismatch_rows,

        /*******************************************************************************************
        Gate-level flags.
        *******************************************************************************************/
        (
            cr.active_campaign_registry_rows > 0
            AND cr.duplicate_active_campaign_technical_key_rows = 0
        ) AS campaign_registry_ready_flag,

        (
            cmpr.duplicate_active_comparison_group_rows = 0
        ) AS comparison_registry_ready_flag,

        (
            cr.active_campaign_registry_rows > 0
            AND ar.active_campaign_registry_rows_for_archive_check = cr.active_campaign_registry_rows
            AND ar.active_runs_missing_module1_source_count = 0
            AND ar.active_runs_with_module1_source_application_id_grain_issue = 0
            AND ar.active_runs_missing_archive_rows = 0
            AND ar.active_runs_with_archive_row_count_mismatch = 0
            AND ar.active_runs_with_archive_application_id_grain_issue = 0
            AND agd.duplicate_archive_grain_count = 0
        ) AS archive_ready_flag,

        (
            cmp.comparison_group_count = cmpr.active_comparison_registry_rows
            AND cmp.comparison_review_count = 0
        ) AS comparison_ready_flag,

        (
            src.source_consistency_group_count = cmpr.active_comparison_registry_rows
            AND src.source_consistency_review_count = 0
            AND src.total_source_field_mismatch_rows = 0
        ) AS source_consistency_ready_flag,

        (
            ev.registry_run_count_for_evidence_check = cr.active_campaign_registry_rows
            AND ev.expected_validation_key_count > 0
            AND ev.executive_evidence_complete_run_count = cr.active_campaign_registry_rows
            AND ev.executive_evidence_issue_run_count = 0
            AND ev.parameter_snapshot_complete_run_count = cr.active_campaign_registry_rows
            AND ev.parameter_snapshot_issue_run_count = 0
            AND ev.validation_evidence_complete_run_count = cr.active_campaign_registry_rows
            AND ev.validation_evidence_incomplete_run_count = 0
            AND ev.segment_evidence_complete_run_count = cr.active_campaign_registry_rows
            AND ev.segment_evidence_issue_run_count = 0
        ) AS evidence_ready_flag,

        (
            cv.active_campaign_archived_rows > 0
            AND cv.critical_convention_violation_count = 0
        ) AS final_output_conventions_ready_flag,

        (
            pga.product_guardrail_campaign_run_count = 0
            OR (
                pga.product_guardrail_parameter_snapshot_complete_run_count
                    = pga.product_guardrail_campaign_run_count
                AND pga.product_guardrail_parameter_snapshot_issue_run_count = 0
                AND pga.expected_product_guardrail_policy_rows
                    = pga.product_guardrail_campaign_run_count * pga.audited_product_count
                AND pga.missing_product_guardrail_policy_rows = 0
                AND pga.product_guardrail_policy_row_count_issue_rows = 0
                AND pga.product_guardrail_policy_mismatch_rows = 0
            )
        ) AS product_guardrail_policy_ready_flag

    FROM campaign_registry_summary cr
    CROSS JOIN comparison_registry_summary cmpr
    CROSS JOIN archive_summary ar
    CROSS JOIN archive_grain_duplicates agd
    CROSS JOIN comparison_readiness_summary cmp
    CROSS JOIN source_consistency_summary src
    CROSS JOIN evidence_summary ev
    CROSS JOIN convention_summary cv
    CROSS JOIN product_guardrail_policy_audit_summary pga
),

acceptance_status AS (
    SELECT
        ai.*,

        (
            campaign_registry_ready_flag
            AND comparison_registry_ready_flag
            AND archive_ready_flag
            AND comparison_ready_flag
            AND source_consistency_ready_flag
            AND evidence_ready_flag
            AND final_output_conventions_ready_flag
        ) AS structural_acceptance_ready_flag,

        CASE
            WHEN campaign_registry_ready_flag
             AND comparison_registry_ready_flag
             AND archive_ready_flag
             AND comparison_ready_flag
             AND source_consistency_ready_flag
             AND evidence_ready_flag
             AND final_output_conventions_ready_flag
             AND product_guardrail_policy_ready_flag
                THEN 'MODULE_2_CAMPAIGN_RESULTS_READY_FOR_ANALYSIS'

            WHEN campaign_registry_ready_flag
             AND comparison_registry_ready_flag
             AND archive_ready_flag
             AND comparison_ready_flag
             AND source_consistency_ready_flag
             AND evidence_ready_flag
             AND final_output_conventions_ready_flag
             AND product_guardrail_policy_ready_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                THEN 'STRUCTURAL_ACCEPTANCE_PASS_BUT_PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_POLICY_REVIEW_REQUIRED'

            ELSE 'REVIEW_MODULE_2_CAMPAIGN_RESULTS_BEFORE_ANALYSIS'
        END AS module2_campaign_acceptance_status,

        CONCAT_WS(
            ' | ',

            CASE
                WHEN campaign_registry_ready_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                    THEN 'REVIEW_CAMPAIGN_REGISTRY'
            END,

            CASE
                WHEN comparison_registry_ready_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                    THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_REGISTRY'
            END,

            CASE
                WHEN archive_ready_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                    THEN 'REVIEW_ARCHIVE_INVENTORY_OR_ARCHIVE_GRAIN'
            END,

            CASE
                WHEN comparison_ready_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                    THEN 'REVIEW_COMPARISON_READINESS'
            END,

            CASE
                WHEN source_consistency_ready_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                    THEN 'REVIEW_MATCHED_SOURCE_FIELD_CONSISTENCY'
            END,

            CASE
                WHEN evidence_ready_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                    THEN 'REVIEW_SECTION_16_EVIDENCE_COMPLETENESS'
            END,

            CASE
                WHEN final_output_conventions_ready_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                    THEN 'REVIEW_FINAL_OUTPUT_CONVENTIONS'
            END,

            CASE
                WHEN product_guardrail_policy_ready_flag IS DISTINCT FROM TRUE
                    THEN 'REVIEW_PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_POLICY_EXACT_VALUES'
            END
        ) AS acceptance_review_focus

    FROM acceptance_inputs ai
)

SELECT
    /***********************************************************************************************
    Final status.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    module2_campaign_acceptance_status,

    CASE
        WHEN acceptance_review_focus IS NULL
          OR acceptance_review_focus = ''
            THEN 'ALL_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_GATES_PASSED'
        ELSE acceptance_review_focus
    END AS acceptance_review_focus,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    Gate flags.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    campaign_registry_ready_flag,
    comparison_registry_ready_flag,
    archive_ready_flag,
    comparison_ready_flag,
    source_consistency_ready_flag,
    evidence_ready_flag,
    final_output_conventions_ready_flag,
    product_guardrail_policy_ready_flag,
    structural_acceptance_ready_flag,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    Dynamic expected campaign shape.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    expected_campaign_runs,
    expected_comparison_groups,
    expected_total_active_campaign_source_rows,
    expected_validation_key_count,
    expected_product_guardrail_campaign_runs,
    audited_product_count,
    expected_product_guardrail_policy_rows,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    Registry and archive evidence.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    active_campaign_registry_rows,
    duplicate_active_campaign_technical_key_rows,

    active_comparison_registry_rows,
    duplicate_active_comparison_group_rows,

    active_campaign_registry_rows_for_archive_check,
    active_runs_missing_module1_source_count,
    active_runs_with_module1_source_application_id_grain_issue,
    active_runs_with_archive_rows,
    active_runs_missing_archive_rows,
    total_active_campaign_archived_rows,
    active_runs_with_archive_row_count_mismatch,
    active_runs_with_archive_application_id_grain_issue,
    duplicate_archive_grain_count,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    Comparison and source-consistency evidence.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    comparison_group_count,
    comparison_ready_count,
    comparison_review_count,

    source_consistency_group_count,
    source_consistency_pass_count,
    source_consistency_review_count,
    total_source_field_mismatch_rows,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    Section 16 evidence completeness.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    registry_run_count_for_evidence_check,

    executive_evidence_rows,
    executive_evidence_complete_run_count,
    executive_evidence_issue_run_count,

    parameter_snapshot_rows,
    parameter_snapshot_complete_run_count,
    parameter_snapshot_issue_run_count,

    validation_evidence_complete_run_count,
    validation_evidence_incomplete_run_count,
    min_validation_rows_per_run,
    max_validation_rows_per_run,
    total_validation_evidence_rows,

    segment_evidence_complete_run_count,
    segment_evidence_issue_run_count,
    min_expected_segment_rows_per_run,
    max_expected_segment_rows_per_run,
    min_segment_rows_per_run,
    max_segment_rows_per_run,
    total_segment_evidence_rows,


    /***********************************************************************************************
    Convention and product-guardrail policy audit evidence.
    ***********************************************************************************************/
    active_campaign_archived_rows,
    critical_convention_violation_count,

    product_guardrail_campaign_run_count,
    product_guardrail_parameter_snapshot_complete_run_count,
    product_guardrail_parameter_snapshot_issue_run_count,
    actual_product_guardrail_policy_rows_checked,
    missing_product_guardrail_policy_rows,
    product_guardrail_policy_row_count_issue_rows,
    product_guardrail_policy_mismatch_rows

FROM acceptance_status;


/***************************************************************************************************
END OF SECTION 17 — POST-CAMPAIGN ACCEPTANCE, EXPORT, PARAMETER AUDIT, AND STRATEGY EFFECT REVIEW

If execution reaches this point:
    1. Active campaign archive inventory has been reviewed.
    2. Active campaign archive slice detail has been displayed.
    3. Archive grain duplicates have been checked.
    4. Active campaign registry rows have been reconciled to archive slices.
    5. Registry/archive missing or mismatch detail has been displayed.
    6. Archive slices without active campaign registry rows have been surfaced for review.
    7. Section 16 evidence coverage has been summarized.
    8. Section 16 evidence detail has been displayed by run.
    9. Active-campaign archive final-output conventions have been checked.
    10. Validation status has been summarized by active campaign run.
    11. Validation REVIEW / NOT_APPLICABLE concentration has been reviewed.
    12. Active comparison registry readiness has been checked.
    13. Matched comparison source-field consistency has been checked.
    14. Executive evidence campaign summary has been displayed.
    15. Baseline × challenger deltas have been displayed.
    16. Product guardrail strategy effects have been reviewed.
    17. Counteroffer-first strategy effects have been reviewed.
    18. Parameter snapshot completeness has been reviewed.
    19. Product guardrail policy snapshots have been compared to intended canonical values.
    20. Final campaign acceptance has been summarized in one status row.

Dynamic acceptance basis:
    Section 17 acceptance is derived from active registry and evidence state.

    It does not assume:
        a fixed number of campaign runs,
        a fixed number of comparison groups,
        a fixed Module 1 source population size,
        a fixed total archive row count,
        a fixed Section 14 validation evidence row count,
        a fixed product × score segment count,
        or a fixed number of product-guardrail strategy runs.

    Instead, Section 17 derives expected values from:
        active campaign registry rows,
        active comparison registry rows,
        selected Module 1 source-population counts,
        active campaign archive slices,
        persisted validation evidence keys,
        archived product × score segment keys,
        Section 16 evidence tables,
        and audited product-policy expectations.

Interpretation of final acceptance:
    MODULE_2_CAMPAIGN_RESULTS_READY_FOR_ANALYSIS:
        Active campaign archive, registry, evidence, convention, comparison, source-consistency,
        parameter snapshot, and audited product-policy checks are clean.

        This means the campaign SQL evidence is structurally ready for executive interpretation,
        README drafting, LinkedIn storytelling, and written Validation Summary drafting within the
        documented simulation boundaries.

    STRUCTURAL_ACCEPTANCE_PASS_BUT_PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_POLICY_REVIEW_REQUIRED:
        Structural, archive, evidence, convention, comparison, source-consistency, and parameter
        snapshot checks are clean, but at least one audited product-guardrail policy snapshot check
        requires review.

        This status may reflect a missing product-policy row, duplicate product-policy row, missing
        parameter snapshot, duplicate parameter snapshot, or product-policy value mismatch.

        The campaign may be structurally complete, but product-guardrail parameter evidence should be
        reviewed before final interpretation.

    REVIEW_MODULE_2_CAMPAIGN_RESULTS_BEFORE_ANALYSIS:
        One or more structural, archive, registry, evidence, convention, comparison, source-field,
        validation, parameter, or product-policy checks require review.

        This status means final documentation should pause until the specific Section 17 diagnostic
        query identifying the issue has been reviewed.

Recommended post-Section 17 workflow:
    If module2_campaign_acceptance_status = MODULE_2_CAMPAIGN_RESULTS_READY_FOR_ANALYSIS:
        1. Preserve the Section 17 outputs.
        2. Use Section 17.20 as the final campaign acceptance row.
        3. Use Section 17.14–17.17 for executive narrative development.
        4. Use Section 17.18–17.19 for parameter governance evidence.
        5. Proceed to written Validation Summary / README / LinkedIn drafting.

    If module2_campaign_acceptance_status = STRUCTURAL_ACCEPTANCE_PASS_BUT_PRODUCT_GUARDRAIL_POLICY_REVIEW_REQUIRED:
        1. Review Section 17.19.
        2. Confirm whether the product-guardrail parameter evidence issue is expected or erroneous.
        3. Rerun affected campaign slices or evidence capture if needed.
        4. Rerun Section 15 if archive-changing corrections were made.
        5. Rerun Section 16.9 after a fresh Section 15 run.
        6. Rerun Section 17.

    If module2_campaign_acceptance_status = REVIEW_MODULE_2_CAMPAIGN_RESULTS_BEFORE_ANALYSIS:
        1. Identify which Section 17 diagnostic query produced the review condition.
        2. Correct archive, registry, comparison, evidence, source-consistency, validation, parameter,
           or product-policy issues as needed.
        3. Rerun affected campaign slices only if the issue affects accepted strategy output.
        4. Rerun Section 15 after archive-changing corrections.
        5. Rerun Section 16.9 after a fresh Section 15 run.
        6. Rerun Section 17.

Read-only boundary:
    Section 17 did not insert archive rows.
    Section 17 did not delete archive rows.
    Section 17 did not update archive rows.
    Section 17 did not modify latest-run rows.
    Section 17 did not modify evidence rows.
    Section 17 did not modify campaign registry rows.
    Section 17 did not modify comparison registry rows.
    Section 17 did not modify strategy parameter rows.
    Section 17 did not modify product-policy parameter rows.
    Section 17 did not synchronize frontier evidence.
    Section 17 did not recalculate decision outcomes.
    Section 17 did not recalculate approved exposure values.
    Section 17 did not recalculate approved Expected Loss values.
    Section 17 did not reassign simulated reason codes.
    Section 17 did not implement revenue logic.
    Section 17 did not implement earnings logic.
    Section 17 did not implement pricing optimization logic.
    Section 17 did not implement funding-cost logic.
    Section 17 did not implement profitability logic.
    Section 17 did not implement capital logic.
    Section 17 did not implement risk-adjusted margin logic.

Final documentation boundary:
    Section 17 provides SQL evidence acceptance.

    It does not itself draft:
        BRD text,
        written Validation Summary conclusions,
        README narrative,
        LinkedIn posts,
        production policy recommendations,
        model validation approval,
        fair-lending conclusions,
        customer communications,
        or operational implementation instructions.

Final campaign workflow checkpoint:
    Full-campaign SQL workflow is complete only after:

        all planned runs through Section 16.8
        → fresh Section 15
        → Section 16.9 synchronization
        → Section 17 final acceptance

***************************************************************************************************/
